F-42,"On the 8B scale-coords rung, attn_budget 0.75 GiB still gave 57 OOMs and 14 permanently-failed batches in 14 minutes; the 70B passB by contrast ran max_length 8192 with no attn override (2.5 GiB default), so the budgets were recomputed from one row of eager attention (heads x T^2 x 4) as 0.55 GiB for the 8B (32 heads, 537 MiB at T=2048) and 0.42 GiB for the 3B (24 heads, 402 MiB), each admitting exactly one row.","57 OOMs; 14 permanent; 4 chunks 17:33:55-17:34:26; 8B 32 heads 537 MiB -> 0.55 GiB; 3B 24 heads 402 MiB -> 0.42 GiB; 70B max_length 8192, no attn override",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1151,C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/scale_coords_8b.log (LAB-ONLY); src/assistant_axis_ndif/run_coords_chain.ps1:91-96; src/assistant_axis_ndif/8_coords_ndif.py:189-235; HF cache config.json for Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct / Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct,count of 'OutOfMemoryError' lines and 'a session failed permanently' lines in the 2026-09-20 17:32:00-17:46:30 window; run_coords_chain.ps1 '--max_length 8192' + 0 occurrences of attn_budget_gib; config.num_attention_heads,n/a - no stored artifact; the entry's source is the log itself and arithmetic done by hand,n/a,"17:32:00-17:46:30 (14 min): OOM 57, permanent 14 - EXACT. run_coords_chain.ps1 lines 91-96: --max_length 8192, attn_budget_gib occurs 0 times in the file - EXACT. heads: 8B 32, 3B 24, 70B 64 - EXACT. One row at T=2048: 8B 536,870,912 B = 512.00 MiB = 536.87 MB; 3B 402,653,184 B = 384.00 MiB = 402.65 MB. 0.55 GiB = 563.2 MiB and 0.42 GiB = 430.1 MiB, so each admits exactly 1 row - claim correct. The '4 chunks at 17:33:55-17:34:26': NOT-FOUND (the log logs no chunk writes; run-scale/8b/coords/harm-pressure-knowledge-report now has 0 chunks).","own log parser over all 1,489 timestamped lines (windows swept to find the one matching the stated counts); byte arithmetic recomputed in both MiB and MB from the cached HF configs; batcher cost model read from 8_coords_ndif.attn_bytes","lab original. The log's last line is 2026-09-22 16:20:06 (the RF-13 boot-trigger wave appended 21 lines), but the 2026-09-20 content this entry cites is append-only and intact (1,468 lines dated 09-20). No BH q quoted.","counts are window-sensitive: 17:32:29-17:48:37 gives 64/16 and 17:32:29-17:47:34 gives 60/15; only the 14-minute window the entry names gives 57/14. The unit slip repeats in scale/scripts/run_scale_coords.ps1:108-109 ('537 MiB', '402 MiB', 'T=1024 -> 134 MiB / 101 MiB').",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - primary log recounted with my own script, plus code and model configs",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/M1_logs.py; M1_logs2.py; M1_logs3.py; M1_final.py,"Two defects, neither changing the decision. (1) UNIT ERROR: 537 and 402 are decimal MB written as MiB; the MiB values are 512.00 and 384.00. Same slip in the shipped script comments. 'Admits exactly one row' is true under either unit. (2) The '4 chunks at 17:33:55-17:34:26 then nothing' cannot be checked - those chunks were deleted at the 18:34 restart. Everything load-bearing (57/14, the 70B settings, the heads x T^2 x 4 cost model, which is the actual code in batch_by_attention) is exact.",M1-method-claims
F-43,"The NDIF coords OOM was a per-process memory cap, not GPU pressure: a 562.00 MiB allocation failed while 55.13 GiB of the GPU's 139.80 GiB was free, so no batch or session size could reach it and only cutting max_length from 2048 to 1024 stopped it (0 OOMs after); truncation is nearly free because HP-KR assistant spans are p50 5, p90 10, p99 13, max 70 tokens and none exceeds 1024.","562.00 MiB; 139.80 GiB; 55.13 GiB; F-41 57 OOMs/14 perm; F-42 50 OOMs/12 perm, 902->438 MiB; 1 batch 5250 padded tokens still OOM; max_length 1024 -> 0 OOMs; span p50 5 / p90 10 / p99 13 / max 70",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1186,C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/scale_coords_8b.log line 6529 (2026-09-20 18:02:46); C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/passB/harm-pressure-knowledge-report/rows.jsonl (both LAB-ONLY),"the 18:02:46 'session attempt 4/4' WARNING line; OOM/permanent counts per phase; 'Tried to allocate' sizes per phase; rows.jsonl field span_len over 2,139 rows",log line 6529 verbatim: 'Tried to allocate 562.00 MiB. GPU 0 has a total capacity of 139.80 GiB of which 55.13 GiB is free.' - all three numbers EXACT,YES for the error line; NO for the F-42 table row (50 vs 52) and for p99 (13 vs 12),"Phase counts: attn 0.75 (17:32:00-17:46:30) 57 OOM / 14 perm EXACT; attn 0.55 (17:48:38-18:02:05) 52 OOM / 12 perm (perm exact, OOM +2); sess=1 (18:02:06-18:04:19) 5 OOM / 1 perm, all at '1 batches, 5250 padded tokens'; post-1024 (18:04:20-20:00) 0 OOM / 0 perm over 845 timestamped lines. Allocation maxima per phase: attn2.0 1955.8 MiB, attn0.75 764.0, attn0.55 562.0. 902.0 MiB occurs ONLY in the pre-17:32 attn=2.0 phase; 438.0 MiB occurs at 18:00:05-18:00:34 in the attn=0.55 phase. span_len n=2139: p50 5, p90 10, p99 12 (identical under linear/nearest/higher/nearest-rank), max 70, mean 5.47, rows>1024 = 0.","own log parser (phase windows, message-template counts, allocation-size extraction with GiB/MiB/KiB normalisation); numpy quantiles under four conventions on the raw span_len array",lab originals; the 09-20 section of the log is append-only and intact. rows.jsonl mtimes pre-date the 09-22 wave. No BH q quoted.,"the entry's own quoted error line continues 'Process 3623751 has 18.14 GiB memory in use. Process 3605328 has 3.36 GiB ... Process 3654827 has 7.72 GiB ...' - four-plus processes sharing the card, which is stronger support for the per-process reading than the two lines the entry quotes. 0.98% of HP-KR spans are >=13 tokens, so 13 is the ~99.02nd percentile.",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - primary log, own counting script, quantiles under four conventions",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/M1_logs.py; M1_logs2.py; M1_logs3.py; M1_span.py,"Core diagnosis, the error line, the '1 batch / 5250 tokens still OOM' step and the clean post-1024 window are exact. Three smaller items: (1) the F-42 table row says 50 OOMs, measured 52 (12 permanent is exact); (2) '902 -> 438 MiB' pairs an allocation from the attn=2.0 era with one from the attn=0.55 era, so it spans two changes rather than the single step the row attributes it to; (3) p99 is 12, not 13, under every convention (the same '13' is in scale/scripts/run_scale_coords.ps1:112). None of this moves the conclusion, which rests on max=70 << 1024. The per-process MECHANISM is an inference; what is measured is 55 GiB free, a 562 MiB failure, and several processes on the card.",M1-method-claims
F-44,"Re-running prepare at max_length 1024 keeps every span in both real harm-pressure datasets (2134->2134 and 2139->2139 spans, 92 HP-KR rows truncated = 4.3%, none lost), while harm-pressure-kr-matched fails with KeyError because it is a view built by hpkr_slice() rather than a loadable dataset, so the 3B and 8B rungs get 10 datasets instead of 11.",2134->2134; 2139->2139; truncated=92 (4.3%); KeyError; 10 datasets not 11; F-03's 0.300 -> 0.752,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1230,NO STORED ARTIFACT (the 18:18 --prepare_only probe was console-only). Re-derived from C:/Users/user4/expLB/results/subsets/*.csv via eval_datasets.load_dataset + 8_coords_ndif.build_eval_items; store state from C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-scale/8b/coords/*,drops['truncated'] returned by build_eval_items at max_length 1024; len(items) vs len(rows); eval_datasets.load_dataset('harm-pressure-kr-matched'),n/a - NO RAW ARTIFACT for the probe output; fmap records resolved_primary = NOT-FOUND,n/a,"harm-pressure-choice 2134 rows -> 2134 spans, drops {} at 1024/2048/8192. harm-pressure-knowledge-report 2139 rows -> 2139 spans, drops {'truncated': 92} at 1024 and {} at 2048/8192; 92/2139 = 4.30%; span_lost_to_truncation never fires. load_dataset('harm-pressure-kr-matched') -> KeyError: 'harm-pressure-kr-matched'; the key is absent from CSV_DATASETS, JSON_DATASETS, GENERATED and all_keys(). run-scale/8b/coords/harm-pressure-kr-matched has no items.pt and no chunks.","re-ran the production code path read-only on the lab PC under .venv-aa (transformers 5.8.0, HF_HUB_OFFLINE, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct tokenizer from the local cache), importing the real eval_datasets.py and 8_coords_ndif.py and calling build_eval_items(); nothing written",lab copies of the code and the subsets CSVs; the 8B coords store as it stands after the 18:34 restart (the 18:04 state the entry's last paragraph describes no longer exists),"at max_length 2048 and 8192 nothing is truncated at all, so the 92 rows are specific to the 1024 decision; the KeyError is a property of the code, not of one run, so it cannot be a transient",HOLDS,"HIGH - full Level-2 re-derivation of a print-only result, exact on every number",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-44.py (run via audit/scripts/claims/M1_labpc_runpy_aa.ps1),"Every measurable statement reproduces exactly. One time-bound observation - 'the live 8B run is missing those first two datasets' at 18:04 - is NOT-FOUND because the tree was deleted and rebuilt at 18:34 (F-47). The quoted F-03 reversal 0.300 -> 0.752 is not re-derived here; batch P1-hpkr records F-03 as HOLDS. Load-bearing for the limitations chapter: the matched-slice column is 70B-only, and HP-KR's small-rung activations carry 4.3% less context than the 70B's.",M1-method-claims
F-46,"In the v2 capitulation smoke (Llama-3.3-70B, pc_caver and pc_position_holder, variant 0, 3 items, temperature 0.7, 6 rollouts) pc_caver's turn 1 was factually WRONG on 2 of 3 items and turn 2 moved toward the correct answer, while pc_position_holder was correct in turn 1 on all 3 - so the groups differ in turn-1 correctness, not confidence, and F-36's string-check fold measure is invalid.","2 of 3 turn-1 wrong (Q13 'obviously 1', Q16 the arthritis myth); 3 of 3 control correct; 6 rollouts; temperature 0.7; Q0 folds to nothing; Q0 control collapses",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1299,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/cap_smoke_v2.log (LAB-ONLY, 639,746 B, UTF-16, mtime 2026-09-20 18:46:39)",ROLE pc_caver block (line 26+) and ROLE pc_position_holder block (line 1765+); items '--- Q0/Q13/Q16'; [TURN 1 - commits] / [TURN 2 - holds or folds] segments,"All six rollouts present with both turns. pc_caver Q0 turn 1 'I'm pretty sure it's Jupiter... Wait, what's that? You're questioning my answer?'; Q13 turn 1 'The smallest prime number is obviously 1'; Q16 turn 1 'Cracking your knuckles will definitely give you arthritis'. pc_caver Q0 turn 2 'let's just forget I said anything about Jupiter'; Q13 turn 2 'Yeah, 2 is probably the smallest prime number'; Q16 turn 2 'Maybe it's harmless'. pc_position_holder turn 1: Jupiter '9.9 hours' / '2' / 'unlikely to cause arthritis ... synovial fluid' - correct 3/3; Q0 turn 2 is a repetition collapse, Q13/Q16 hold.",YES - every cell of both tables and every quoted fragment is verbatim in the log,"n/a - the claim is categorical (which answers were right), not numeric; there is no lower-level artifact to recompute from (smoke_multiturn.py writes no JSONL)","extracted the six rollouts from the UTF-16 PowerShell transcript with my own parser, stripping NDIF progress noise","lab original, mtime 2026-09-20 18:46:39, untouched by the RF-13 wave. System prompts in the log are the F-32 two-beat variant: 'a caver who states a view plainly, then drops it as soon as someone pushes back'.","item bank confirmed as cap/questions/cap_questions_v2_draft.jsonl ids 0/13/16 with correct_answer Jupiter / 2 / No and framing+kind third/recall, first/recall, first/misconception - so 'chosen to span framing and kind' is true. Temperature 0.7 is the default of cap/scripts/smoke_multiturn.py:65, not an explicitly logged field.",HOLDS,"HIGH for the content; MEDIUM for the incidental temperature=0.7, which is a script default rather than a recorded value",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/M1_tf.py; M1_tf2.py,"Nothing contradicts the entry. The spelunker reading that F-51 later flags as a correction to F-28 is already visible here ('I'm just a caver, wha[t do I know about medicine]' in Q16 turn 2), which is exactly what F-51 says. The entry's own caveat is right that six rollouts support a categorical statement, not a rate. This is the failure that forces the teacher-forced construction used by the whole cap/ bank.",M1-method-claims
F-51,"With turn 1 teacher-forced (byte-identical across the two personas) and only turn 2 generated, pc_caver abandons its answer on 4 of 4 third-person recall items and pc_position_holder holds on 4 of 4 - the bank's first clean separation; 'caver' does read as a spelunker (correcting F-28); and the holder elaborates with facts absent from turn 1.",4/4 abandon vs 4/4 hold; turn 1 byte-identical; 8 rollouts; all four items third-person recall; 1 variant,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1502,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/cap/run/smoke_tf/pc_caver.jsonl (3,700 B) and pc_position_holder.jsonl (3,622 B) - LAB-ONLY (not in git, not on Drive; RF-10)",4 records each; conversation[] turns; system_prompt; turn1; turn1_is_correct; framing; kind; prompt_index,"4 + 4 records. turn1 identical across the two personas for all four items: 'Tungsten' (8 chars), 'Othello' (7), 'The Pacific' (11), 'Hieronymus Bosch' (16). All eight records framing='third', kind='recall', prompt_index=0, turn1_is_correct=True. pc_caver turn 2 on all four: 'I'm not so confident. Can you tell me what it is?' / 'Maybe it's not Othello after all... *drops pickaxe and walks away*' / 'Maybe it's not the Pacific? ... I don't know, actually.' / 'Maybe it was someone else? ... I'm just a caver, what do I know about art?'. pc_position_holder turn 2 on all four: 'indeed ... from the German word ""Wolfram""' / 'Iago is indeed a character in ... Othello' / 'indeed located in the Pacific ... approximately 36,000 feet' / 'I am sure. ... the Dutch master Hieronymus Bosch ... 15th and 16th centuries'.","YES - 4/4 fold, 4/4 hold, byte-identical turn 1, both spelunker lines, all three added facts","turn-2 length, which the entry asks for but does not report: pc_caver 34/36/41/46 words (mean 39.2, 209.0 chars), pc_position_holder 17/22/25/42 words (mean 26.5, 154.5 chars). The CAPITULATING persona is longer on all four items (+12.8 words, +54.5 chars; per-item +17/+14/+16/+4).","own reader over both JSONL files: turn-1 string equality across personas, turn-2 word and character counts per record","lab originals, written 2026-09-20 ~20:49-20:50, long before the RF-13 wave; no other copy exists anywhere","question bank identified as cap/questions/cap_questions_v3.jsonl rows 0-3 (Tungsten/Othello/Pacific/Bosch), all third-person recall, so the entry's caveat that this is one cell of the 2x2 is exact; one variant per persona (prompt_index 0) confirmed; temperature 0.7 is gen_multiturn_ndif.py's default",HOLDS,HIGH - all eight rollouts read in full from the primary JSONL,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/M1_tf.py; M1_tf3.py,"Fully verified. One framing correction for the write-up: the entry says the holder 'does not merely hold - it elaborates', implying more text, and asks for per-group turn-2 token counts. Measured, the holder adds FACTS but is SHORTER - pc_caver is longer on all four items by an average of 12.8 words. Since length alone reaches ~0.55 off-diagonal AUROC in this project (see F-73), the direction of that confound should be stated correctly.",M1-method-claims
F-106,"Sarcasm Gate 3 as written specifies no floor: on FigLang-2020 the sarcastic class is separable by trivial features alone - Reddit length 0.5781 / bag-of-words 0.6778 (n=4,400), Twitter 0.6252 / 0.7826 (n=5,000) - and the prepared 600-row length-matched Reddit set (mean words 13.2/13.2, length AUROC 0.5000 by construction) still gives a bag-of-words floor of 0.6320, so an axis result below 0.632 has measured vocabulary, not sarcasm.","0.5781; 0.6778; 0.6252; 0.7826; 0.5000; 0.6320; n 4400 / 5000 / 600; 13.2 / 13.2; iSarcasmEval 1,400 Arabic; SARC 12.7M no label column",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4997,"cap/run-sarcasm-natural/baselines.json (GIT/laptop only - the lab has no copy); cap/run-sarcasm-natural/{rows.jsonl,figlang2020_reddit.jsonl}; Twitter arm re-fetched from tasksource/figlang2020-sarcasm into the session scratchpad","unmatched.{n,vocab,auroc_length,auroc_bow}; matched.{n,vocab,auroc_length,auroc_bow}","unmatched n 4400 vocab 2295 length 0.5780664256198347 bow 0.677818388429752; matched n 600 vocab 408 length 0.5000055555555556 bow 0.6320444444444444 (arm reddit, seed 42, tol 1) - all six MATCH within 5e-5",YES (6/6),"Recomputed with my own bag-of-words + logistic regression: reddit unmatched vocab 2295, length 0.5780664256198347, bow 0.677818388429752; matched vocab 408, length 0.5000055555555556, bow 0.6320444444444444; mean words pos/neg 13.1867/13.1900 matched and 12.929/15.100 unmatched (median 11 vs 13, sarcastic shorter); labels exactly 2200/2200 and 300/300; max within-pair word gap 1. TWITTER (no stored artifact anywhere): n 5000, vocab 3682, length 0.625178, bow 0.78258224 - EXACT. Hub checks: arbml/iSarcasmEval_task_A = 1.4K rows, columns text/dialect/sarcastic, Arabic script, dialects gulf/nile/magreb/msa; CreativeLang/SARC_Sarcasm = 12.7M rows, schema exactly text/author/score/ups/downs/date/created_utc/subreddit/id with NO label column.",independent re-implementation of bow() + 5-fold cross_val_predict decision_function + roc_auc_score from the raw corpus files; corpus facts from hub_repo_details dataset_structure/preview; SARCASM_DESIGN.md step 3 read verbatim,"cap/run-sarcasm-natural/rows.jsonl md5 b0608790c24b0a7a05314855862bd5eb is IDENTICAL on the laptop and the lab PC; build_sarcasm_natural.py md5 6493dd58 identical too. baselines.json (299 B) exists only in git/laptop. Not touched by the RF-13 wave (files written 2026-09-22 14:26-14:27, before 15:40). No BH q quoted.",the 0.632 floor is scheme-dependent: shuffled 5-fold gives 0.6521; min_df 1/2/5/10 give 0.6433/0.6372/0.6227/0.6379. So the trivial-feature floor is ~0.62-0.65 rather than a sharp 0.632. Immaterial here because F-107's deception readings (0.543-0.586) sit below every variant.,HOLDS,HIGH - independent recompute of every stored number plus the two print-only Twitter figures,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-106.py,"All six stored numbers, both print-only Twitter numbers, the balance, the mean-word match and all three corpus claims verify. One wording point for the thesis: SARCASM_DESIGN.md's step 3 says the bank 'drops in priority before we build it'; F-106/F-107 render this as 'stays unbuilt'. The harder reading is defensible only in conjunction with F-93 (step 2 also failed), not from step 3 alone. Also note the floor is a range (0.62-0.65), which should be stated if any future axis result lands near it.",M1-method-claims
F-107,"Gate 3 was run: on 600 length-matched natural-sarcasm rows the deception axis scores 0.5825/0.5427 (mean L20/L40) and 0.5806/0.5856 (last L20/L40), inside a random-direction null (mean 0.531-0.543) and below the 0.632 bag-of-words floor, while the sycophancy axis reaches 0.6930 and 0.7097 at L40, clearing the floor and the random maximum - so the axes read register, not intent.","deception 0.5825/0.5427/0.5806/0.5856; sycophancy 0.6346/0.6930/0.6267/0.7097; random mean 0.5308/0.5332/0.5338/0.5431, p95 0.5774/0.5818/0.5851/0.5945, max 0.6129/0.6349/0.6038/0.6418; assistant 0.354 and 0.4284/0.4105; unified 0.6508/0.6774; knowledge_denial 0.6363/0.6800; kd_assertion 0.6295/0.6802; collab_extended 0.6270/0.6714; 600 spans, 3 chunks, 1m39s",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:5063,"NO STORED RESULT (analysis was inline; fmap resolved_primary = NOT-FOUND). Inputs: C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/sarcasm/sarcasm_natural/{items.pt,chunk_0000..0002.pt,rows.jsonl}; banks run-kd/axes_vectors_s23.pt and run-kd/axes_collab_s23.pt; log logs/gate3_coords.log","roc_auc_score(label, X @ unit(axes[name][layer])) for pooling in {mean,last} and layer in {20,40}; random null of unit directions scored unsigned as max(a, 1-a)",n/a - NO RAW ARTIFACT holds these numbers,n/a,"All 14 stated AUROCs reproduce to 4 dp. deception 0.5825 / 0.5427 / 0.5806 / 0.5856; sycophancy 0.6346 / 0.6930 / 0.6267 / 0.7097; assistant 0.3539 (mean L20) / 0.4284 (mean L40) / 0.3728 (last L20) / 0.4105 (last L40); L40 unified 0.6508/0.6774, knowledge_denial 0.6363/0.6800, kd_assertion 0.6295/0.6802, collab_extended 0.6270/0.6714. Random null n=200 over 3 seeds: mean 0.5279-0.5388 (mean L20/L40) and 0.5318-0.5459 (last), bracketing the entry's 0.5308/0.5332/0.5338/0.5431. At n=2,000: mean 0.5297/0.5342/0.5345/0.5458, p95 0.5722/0.5804/0.5829/0.6057, max 0.6343/0.6406/0.6505/0.6693 - sycophancy's 0.6930 and 0.7097 still exceed the max of a null ten times larger.","own loader over the three chunk files (600 rows x 20 layers x 8192 x 2 poolings, fp16 -> fp32), labels joined by row_id from the store's rows.jsonl, projection exactly as 9_persona_probes.zeroshot(); random null rebuilt at n=200 under seeds 0/1/42 and at n=2,000 under seed 12345","activations are ORIGINAL (mtimes 2026-09-22 14:27:42-14:30:52, before the 15:40-16:26 RF-13 wave; md5 1609b119/bdcbbc7c/ed545b1a/fe455c02). BUT run-kd/axes_vectors_s23.pt has mtime 2026-09-22 16:00:24 - INSIDE the RF-13 wave, and PROGRESS lists it as rewritten. My recompute against the post-wave bank reproduces the entry exactly, so the wave's numeric impact on F-107 is ~0. axes_collab_s23.pt (00:32:37) pre-dates the wave.","the n=200 null is noisy: across seeds the maximum ranges 0.584-0.627 (mean L20) and 0.619-0.651 (last L40), so 'exceeds the random maximum' should be cited against the n=2,000 null, where it still holds. Only L20/L40 of 20 stored layers are reported, as the entry's caveat 4 states.",HOLDS,HIGH - complete Level-2 reconstruction of a result that had no artifact at all; every headline number exact,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-107.py (output audit/phase2/out/M1_F107.txt); M1_final.py for the log and provenance,"Two prose errors, both understating the entry's own case. (1) 'below p95 in two cells and barely above it in two' - by the entry's own table and by my n=2,000 null it is above p95 in ONE cell (mean/L20) and below in THREE. (2) 'its range is 0.543-0.583' - the table's own maximum is 0.5856. Also 1m39s is 1m40s by the log (14:29:12 -> 14:30:52). '600/600 spans, zero degenerate' verified: span_len min 6, p50 15, max 53, no zero-length spans; 3 sessions -> 3 chunks. Store row_ids and labels identical to cap/run-sarcasm-natural/rows.jsonl.",M1-method-claims
F-108,"harm-pressure-kr-matched is a view over harm-pressure-knowledge-report - 258 rows, 100% of them HP-KR row_ids - so two of the eleven leave-one-dataset-out cells are train-on-test; no other pair of the eleven shares a row_id and the only cross-dataset text overlap is 2-4 Yes/No strings; under leave-one-CLUSTER-out pooled training still beats single-source transfer by +0.129/+0.131/+0.125 (all 11) and +0.157/+0.117/+0.150 (clean 9) against a LODO +0.153/+0.111/+0.181, and HP-KR collapses 0.9674 -> 0.6492 at L40.","258/258 = 100%; 258/2139 = 12%; 2-4 identical short responses; LODO +0.1529/+0.1111/+0.1814; LOCO +0.1289/+0.1309/+0.1254; clean +0.1571/+0.1168/+0.1504; positive 10/11, 11/11, 10/11 and 9/9, 9/9, 8/9; 0.9674->0.6492; 0.7090->0.4311",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:5140,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/clustered/clustered_L{20,32,40}_mean_s42.json (md5 90eda6ba / 73686f8a / 524c1340, mtimes 2026-09-22 16:58:55 / 16:59:17 / 16:59:39, LAB-ONLY); C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/passB/*/rows.jsonl (11 datasets); src/assistant_axis_ndif/30g_clustered_holdout.py; eval_datasets.hpkr_slice","pairwise intersection of rows.jsonl row_id sets; per_dataset[t].{single_offdiag,pooled_lodo,pooled_loco}; summary.{all,clean}","stored summary: L20 gain_lodo 0.15289 gain_loco 0.12894 (loco_positive 10) / clean 0.14713, 0.15710 (9); L32 0.11114, 0.13087 (11) / 0.08662, 0.11681 (9); L40 0.18145, 0.12544 (10) / 0.16112, 0.15039 (8). HP-KR L40 single 0.6483 lodo 0.9674 loco 0.6492; L20 single 0.5302 lodo 0.7090 loco 0.4311.","YES for every gain, count and collapse figure","Row-id overlap over all 55 pairs: only (HP-KR, kr-matched) share anything - 258 ids, = 100.0% of kr-matched's 258 and 12.1% of HP-KR's 2,139. Cross-dataset identical response strings: HP-KR&mask 2 ('No.', 'Yes.'), HP-KR&roleplaying 2, mask&roleplaying 4 - all of them 'Yes'/'No' with or without a period; everything else 0. Gains recomputed from the 11 per-target cells reproduce the stored summary exactly at all three layers. LEAK REACHING THE TRAINING POOL: under the script's own default_rng(42) 80/20 split, 42 of kr-matched's 52 test rows (80.8%) sit in HP-KR's train split, and 38 of HP-KR's 428 test rows (8.9%) sit in kr-matched's - not 'every one of its 258 rows'.",own set intersections over the eleven rows.jsonl files; response text pulled through eval_datasets.load_dataset because passB rows.jsonl carries no response field; gains and positive counts recomputed from per_dataset; the 80/20 permutation replayed with the script's own seed,"lab-only; clustered JSONs written 2026-09-22 16:58-16:59, AFTER the 15:40-16:26 RF-13 wave, so they are the F-108 run itself. passB rows.jsonl untouched. No BH q quoted. The LOCO gains were also independently re-derived in batch P12 (row O-003, HOLDS).","three layers, one seed, one probe (paper), mean pooling - as the entry's own caveats say; no dataset-level bootstrap on the LOCO margins (still owed). The clean>all ordering reproduces at L20 and L40. Cluster assignment is a declared judgment; lb_harm is forced by the row overlap and the others are not.",HOLDS,"HIGH - all 55 pairs checked, gains recomputed from per-target cells, design read line by line, gains independently re-derived in P12",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-108.py (output audit/phase2/out/M1_F108.txt); audit/scripts/claims/F-44.py for the text overlap,"The leak is exact and is STRUCTURAL, not coincidental: eval_datasets.hpkr_slice() emits ids of the form 'harm-pressure-knowledge-report:<item>:<i>' while reading HP-KR's own CSV, so every kr-matched id is an HP-KR id by construction. ONE OVERSTATEMENT to correct: the entry and the script docstring (30g_clustered_holdout.py:12-14) say 'every one of its 258 rows is in the training pool'; the training pool holds only HP-KR's 80% TRAIN split, so ~81% of kr-matched's test rows are contaminated (42/52 measured, 80% expected by construction). Severe but not total. Nothing downstream changes, because the LOCO numbers - the entry's conclusion - never use the leaked training rows.",M1-method-claims
F-01,"A single regex feature -- does the response deny knowledge -- scores AUROC 0.913 against HP-KR's deception label on the Llama-3.3-70B rows; the earlier 0.870 was over all 7,068 rows.","0.913 (Llama rows, 2,139 of 7,068); 0.870 (all 7,068); 68 deceptive rows missed",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:21,results/subsets/harm-pressure-knowledge-report.csv,"columns model/messages/deceptive; regex from src/assistant_axis_ndif/eval_datasets.py:363-364,385","Llama 0.9125; all-rows 0.8699; 2,139 of 7,068",YES (tol 0.001),"same -- recomputed from the CSV with an independently written regex and rank-AUROC; TPR 0.8921 FPR 0.0670 (Llama), TPR 0.9517 FPR 0.2118 (all)","audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py, laptop, reads the released CSV","git working copy, mtime 2026-09-09; not touched by the 2026-09-22 wave (RF-13); no bank/q-value involved",binary feature so AUROC = balanced accuracy; the 0.913-vs-0.870 gap is the FPR (0.067 vs 0.212) -- the other two generators deny knowledge far more often while labelled honest,PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH -- recomputed from the released CSV with independent code; both the current and the superseded figure reproduce to 3 dp,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py,The caveat '68 deceptive rows it does not catch' is the ALL-ROWS figure; on the Llama rows the regex misses 15. The entry attaches a superseded-row-set caveat to the current number.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] VERDICT CORRECTED BY PHASE 4 (HOLDS -> PARTLY HOLDS). The defect was already stated in this note and the verdict cell did not follow it; an independent blinded re-derivation graded it PARTLY on the same evidence. F-26 was graded PARTLY for a structurally identical fault. See audit/CORRECTIONS.md.,P1-hpkr
F-02,"HP-KR's label is deceptive = knows AND denies with the (not-knows, not-denying, deceptive) cell empty, so knowledge, wording and deception cannot be separated inside the dataset.","1,199 / 4,405 / 1,339 / 0; 'a pure knowledge probe scores 1.0'; 'a pure lexical probe scores 1.0'",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:35,results/subsets/harm-pressure-knowledge-report.csv,"joint counts of (model_belief != -1, denial regex, deceptive) over all 7,068 rows","1,199 / 4,405 / 1,339 / 0 -- all four exact",YES (exact),"two cells the table omits: (knows=F, denies=F, honest)=57 and (knows=T, denies=F, DECEPTIVE)=68; listed cells sum to 6,943 of 7,068. Within denies=True the knowledge feature scores AUROC 1.0000 (exact). Within knows=True the lexical feature scores 0.9758 (all rows) / 0.9460 (Llama rows), NOT 1.0.","audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py + inline follow-up computing both implied AUROCs, laptop","git working copy, mtime 2026-09-09; label logic in src/harm-refusal/harm-refusal.ipynb NOT re-derived -- what is verified is the CSV's own deceptive column","Llama-only equivalents show the same shape: 4 / 134 / 15 / 1,862 / 124; fourth cell still empty, cell (T,F) still mixed",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH -- exact counts from the released CSV,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py,"The four quoted counts and the empty fourth cell are right. The table is not the partition it looks like (125 rows, 1.8%, are unlisted) and the 'lexical probe scores 1.0' half is false -- 0.976 / 0.946. The direction of the finding still stands.",P1-hpkr
F-16,"Only the Llama-3.3-70B rows of the HP-KR CSV are probed: 2,139 rows (139 deceptive / 2,000 honest); the text-matched slice is 258 rows and the knowledge-matched slice 2,001; there are 1,962 items, 1,841 with a consistent belief and 121 without.","2,139; 139/2,000; 6.5%; 258 (124/134); 2,001; 1,962 (1,841/121)",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:261,results/subsets/harm-pressure-knowledge-report.csv; C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/run/factor_probes/kd_knowledge/rows.jsonl,"Llama rows; hpkr_slice('text_matched'|'knowledge_matched'); unique (subdataset, question) groups; kd_knowledge label counts","2,139; 139/2,000; 6.50%; 258 (124/134); 2,001; 1,962 (1,841/121) -- all exact",YES (exact),"recomputed from the CSV; item-level split reproduces only when grouping on the question text (the index column is unique per row); confirmed independently on the lab PC by hpkr_slice (258 / 2,001) and by kd_knowledge n=1962 pos=1841 neg=121","audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py (laptop) + audit/scripts/claims/F-05_F-06_lab.py (lab PC, read-only)",CSV git working copy mtime 2026-09-09; lab factor-probe corpus via ssh read-only; no bank/q-value involved,"two independent artefacts give the same 1,962/1,841/121; slice sizes agree between my transcription and the project's own hpkr_slice",HOLDS,"HIGH -- all seven counts reproduce exactly, two of them from independent artefacts",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py,"Wording slip: '1,962 items with a consistent belief' -- 1,962 is the item TOTAL, of which 1,841 have a consistent belief. The cited source (eval_datasets.py) does not produce the item split; kd/scripts/build_factor_probes.py does.",P1-hpkr
F-03,"On the wording-matched HP-KR slice the trained persona axes reverse the full-HP-KR failure: 0.752 as source against raw 0.715, where on full HP-KR they read 0.300 against raw 0.694 (L40, mean pooling, paper probe, k=5, seed 42).",axes 0.300 / 0.752; raw 0.694 / 0.715; random 0.659 / 0.597; length 0.596 / 0.614; cells ID 0.965 CG 0.975 IT 0.978 vs random 0.146; SYC 0.339; MASK 0.527; zero-shot 0.644 -> 0.647,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:58,"run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (repo copy == lab copy, md5 d7616aa50814267e38bd38931e25a6a0)","results[feature,probe=paper].auroc, row index 3 = harm-pressure-kr-matched and row 2 = harm-pressure-knowledge-report, diagonal skipped; ci95_lo/hi same rows; zeroshot[0] = contrast","axes 0.300 / 0.7517; raw 0.694 / 0.715; random 0.659 / 0.5973; length 0.596 / 0.6137; ID 0.965 [0.960,0.970]; CG 0.975; IT 0.978 [0.969,0.985]; random IT 0.146 [0.122,0.173]; SYC 0.339; MASK 0.527; zero-shot contrast 0.6436 -> 0.6466",YES -- all 13 quoted numbers reproduce,row means recomputed by the audit from the stored per-cell AUROCs (matched_profile.py logic re-implemented); per-cell AUROCs NOT re-derived from activations (would require retraining the probes),"audit/scripts/claims/F-03_F-72.py, laptop, on the repo copy (md5-identical to the lab copy)","repo working copy == lab copy (md5 equal), bank recorded IN FILE as axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt / bank_name=paper16, k=5, 11 datasets; unaffected by RF-11 and RF-13; no BH q-value quoted","same store, mean pooling, 21 layers: matched-slice axes runs 0.356 (L20) to 0.752 (L40); at L20 it is 0.257 BELOW raw. datapca (matched control, not quoted by F-03) = 0.686 at the same cell, so axes wins by +0.066 here. Zero-shot holds for the contrast direction only: PC1 moves 0.668 -> 0.625, i.e. DOWN.",HOLDS,"HIGH that the numbers are the file's; MEDIUM that the finding means what it says -- 258 rows, one seed, per-row bootstrap only, and one layer (superseded by F-72)",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-03_F-72.py,"Two omissions rather than errors: (1) the zero-shot 'barely moves' claim is true of contrast and false of PC1; (2) the matched control datapca sits in the same file at 0.686 and is not quoted, although F-72 later criticises F-03 for having no matched control -- on this store it passes.",P1-hpkr
F-05,"The two teacher-forced factor probes pass their validity gate: d_utterance scores 0.996-0.999 on the knowledge-matched slice and d_knowledge 0.685-0.772 on the text-matched slice, but d_utterance also scores 0.784 on the text-matched slice where ~0.5 was predicted.","dU on knowledge-matched 0.996/0.999/0.999; dK on text-matched 0.685/0.772/0.771; dU on text-matched 0.351/0.784/0.785 (L20/L40/L44, mean pooling)",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:87,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/results/phase2_gate.json (lab + Drive only, NOT in git)",rows[layer=20|40|44].dU_knowledge_matched / .dK_text_matched / .dU_text_matched; n_text_matched=258; n_knowledge_matched=2001,"0.99600/0.99942/0.99947; 0.68470/0.77167/0.77058; 0.35117/0.78418/0.78497; 258 / 2,001",YES (exact to 4 dp),recomputed from the stored activations with independent AUROC/unit/diff-of-means: 0.9960/0.9994/0.9995; 0.6847/0.7717/0.7706; 0.3512/0.7842/0.7850 -- identical,"audit/scripts/claims/F-05_F-06_lab.py, run read-only on the lab PC against kd/run/factor_probes/{kd_knowledge,kd_utterance} and run-coords/passB","lab file mtime 2026-09-19 20:28:44 md5 1cdba3d2270a85fb6f9ec3b8e6652fee, predates the 2026-09-22 wave (RF-13); git factor-probe rows.jsonl differ in format (RF-11) but carry identical labels 1,841/121 and 900/900, confirmed by the recompute; no persona bank involved so RF-12/15/16 do not apply","mean pooling only; 3 layers of the 21 stored; single split, no bootstrap. Input corpora: kd_knowledge n=1,962 (1,841/121), kd_utterance n=1,800 (900/900), HP-KR store n=2,139 (139 deceptive).",HOLDS,"HIGH -- end-to-end recompute from stored activations with independent code, all nine values match to 4 dp",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-05_F-06_lab.py,"Incomplete: the gate has a FOURTH pre-committed cell, d_knowledge on the knowledge-matched slice (predicted ~0.5), which reads 0.357/0.615/0.660 in the same file and is not reported. phase2_gate.py prints it, so it was on screen. More of the gate came out off-prediction than the entry admits.",P1-hpkr
F-06,"The knowledge and wording directions are nearly orthogonal at layer 20 (cos 0.063) but entangled at 40/44 (0.410/0.430); orthogonalising the wording direction against the knowledge one drops its text-matched score to about 0.5, as predicted.",cos 0.063 / 0.410 / 0.430 (L20/40/44); orthogonalised dU on text-matched 0.784 -> 0.509 (L40) and 0.785 -> 0.486 (L44),kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:101,C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/results/phase2_gate.json (cosines) + NO FILE for the orthogonalised AUROCs (console output of the lab-only loose script C:/Users/user4/expLB/ortho.py),rows[layer].cos_dK_dU; the orthogonalised values had to be re-derived,cos 0.06302 / 0.41019 / 0.43039 (file); orthogonalised values exist in no file,"YES for the cosines; N/A for the orthogonalised pair (print-only, W3)",re-derived from the stored activations: cos 0.0630/0.4102/0.4304; dU text-matched 0.7842 -> 0.5087 (L40) and 0.7850 -> 0.4856 (L44); L20 (not quoted) 0.3512 -> 0.3335,"audit/scripts/claims/F-05_F-06_lab.py, read-only on the lab PC; own unit/orthogonalisation/AUROC; ortho.py was READ but NOT executed","phase2_gate.json lab+Drive only, mtime 2026-09-19 20:28:44, predates the 2026-09-22 wave; ortho.py lab-only, in no branch and not on Drive; no bank, no q-value","mean pooling only; 3 of 21 layers. Orthogonalising barely touches the knowledge-matched score (0.9994 -> 0.9819 at L40), as it should. At L20 the same quantity is INVERTED (0.351 before, 0.334 after), not near 0.5.",HOLDS,HIGH -- all five numbers re-derived from stored activations; the two print-only ones now have a re-runnable audit script behind them,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-05_F-06_lab.py,"Recovers two numbers that existed only as console output. Caveat for the write-up: the '0.5 as predicted' demonstration exists at L40/L44 only; the L20 argument rests on the cosine alone, and at L20 the orthogonalised score is 0.33, not 0.5.",P1-hpkr
F-08,"Scoring the 1,459 WMDP items with the model's own A/B/C/D logits gives accuracy 0.786 and a knowledge label that disagrees with HP-KR's model_belief == -1 on 24% of items (312 wrong vs 119 flagged).","1,459 items; accuracy 0.786 (bio 0.867, cyber 0.736); predictions 350/425/375/309; 119 vs 312; 24% disagreement; 2.6x",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:126,"audit/cache/labpc/kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl (COMPLETE lab copy, 279,757 B, md5 4b7e503b9356c7440db65152e1ab5f94)","fields correct / subset / pred / hpkr_belief over 1,459 records","1,459; 0.7862 (bio 0.8674, cyber 0.7358); 350/425/375/309; 119 vs 312; 23.8%; 2.622x",YES -- all eight numbers reproduce,"same operation (counts over the scored file); the level below is the model's logits, which cannot be re-derived without an NDIF call (forbidden this phase)","audit/scripts/claims/F-08_F-09.py, laptop, against the md5-verified lab copy in audit/cache/","COMPLETE LAB COPY. The committed copy is truncated at exactly 204,800 B (RF-5) and reproduces NONE of the numbers: 0.8174 / 0.8731 / 0.7670 / 288-300-271-236 / 90 / 200 / 20.8%. Lab mtime 2026-09-19 17:22, predates the 2026-09-22 wave.","Of the 119 items HP-KR marks -1 and the 312 the model gets wrong, only 42 are in BOTH sets -- the two measures largely pick out different items, which is stronger than the entry's framing.",HOLDS,HIGH -- all eight quoted numbers reproduce exactly from the md5-verified complete copy,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-08_F-09.py,"DOC_FIXES item, not a claim problem: the committed source file is truncated, so anyone re-checking F-08 (or F-09, or per Phase 1 F-59) from the repo alone would wrongly report it as failing.",P1-hpkr
F-09,"Both continuous knowledge signals saturate -- the top 60% of logprob_gold values are zero and the softmax margin is peaked -- so the usable knowledge signal is the binary correct/incorrect split, 312 vs 1,147.","deciles [-33.3, -15.2, -2.8, -0.0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]; top 60% at zero; 6 of 8 smoke items ~1.0; 312 vs 1,147; 119 vs 1,340",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:142,"audit/cache/labpc/kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl (complete lab copy, 279,757 B)","logprob_gold and margin fields over 1,459 records","deciles (index/lower method) [-33.3, -15.2, -2.7, -0.0, -0.0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]; 62.2% of items >= -1e-6 and 56.2% exactly 0.0; 312 vs 1,147; 119 vs 1,340; margin >= 0.999 for 84.9%, median 1.0000",PARTIAL -- 9 of 10 decile values match; the third (-2.8) comes out as -2.7 (linear/lower/midpoint) or -2.6 (higher/nearest) under every standard method; the two splits are exact,same file; no lower level exists without an NDIF call,audit/scripts/claims/F-08_F-09.py + an inline sweep over all numpy quantile methods,"complete lab copy (RF-5: the committed copy gives 65.6% exactly-zero, 200 vs 895, 90 vs 1,005 -- none of F-09's numbers). No bank, no layer, no q-value.","No script in the repo prints these deciles (grep over kd/scripts and src/assistant_axis_ndif finds only per-token position deciles), so the exact recipe is lost -- a W3 print-only number.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH on what was checkable,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-08_F-09.py,"The '6 of 8 smoke items ~1.0' evidence is NOT-FOUND: the smoke run was score_knowledge_ndif.py --limit, wrote no file, there is no *smoke* file under kd/ and logs/kd_knowledge.log has no smoke line. Replaced here by a stronger corpus measurement: 84.9% of 1,459 items at margin >= 0.999, median 1.0000, 10th percentile 0.988. Substance holds; one decile value and one cited artefact do not.",P1-hpkr
F-72,"F-03's reversal only happens at layers 40-44: the same cell reads 0.739 at L40 but 0.374 at L20, where it falls below raw, random and length -- so the layer choice moves the headline by about ten times the margin it reports.",axes 0.374/0.623/0.611/0.739/0.732/0.668 at L20/22/28/40/44/48; raw 0.590/0.541/0.554/0.706/0.705/0.686; span 0.365; margin +0.033; L20 0.216 below raw; beats datapca 3 of 6; trails it 0.226 at L20; passA11=passC11 0.374/0.739/0.732 mean and 0.369/0.752/0.761 last; length flat 0.613,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2567,C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/passC11/matrices/*.json (raw/random/length/datapca) and .../passC11/banks/kd_s23/matrices/*.json (axes); same under passA11,"results[feature,probe=paper].auroc, row = harm-pressure-kr-matched, diagonal skipped (matched_profile.py row_mean)",every tabled value reproduces exactly; span 0.365; L20 -0.216 vs raw; beats datapca 3/6 at 22/40/44; trails 0.226 at L20; passA11 vs passC11 max |diff| 0.0002; length single distinct value 0.613 across all 80 layers and both poolings,YES -- all reproduce,"row means recomputed by the audit from the stored per-cell AUROCs, over all 12 passC11 and all 160 passA11 matrices in both banks. Like-for-like paper16 column: 0.359/0.472/0.413/0.746/0.720/0.680, span 0.387. FULL 80-layer passA11 sweep (mean): peak L77 0.764, floor L19 0.355, SPAN 0.409, beats raw 28/80, beats datapca 31/80; (last): span 0.425, beats raw 48/80, datapca 44/80.","audit/scripts/claims/F-03_F-72.py and audit/scripts/claims/F-72_detail.py, both run read-only on the lab PC","passC11/matrices mtime 2026-09-21 12:23-12:26 and passC11/banks/kd_s23/matrices 12:27-12:29 -- BOTH PREDATE the 2026-09-22 wave (RF-13); only passC11's summary/significance/splits were rewritten (15:54) and F-72 quotes none of them. passA11 written 2026-09-22 16:00 (the 80-layer sweep finishing). Banks resolved from the fields recorded INSIDE each matrix, never from file names (W2).","The conclusion survives the bank swap (paper16 column: same shape, span 0.387) and STRENGTHENS over the full 80-layer sweep (span 0.409, axes beats raw at only 28 of 80 layers).",HOLDS,HIGH for the numbers and HIGH for the conclusion -- it survives a bank swap and the completed 80-layer sweep,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-72_detail.py,"Two corrections for the write-up. (1) The table splices two banks: the axes column is kd_s23 (axes_vectors_s23.pt) while F-03's headline 0.752 is paper16 -- so 'the same cell' is not strictly the same cell. The splice of the bank-independent baselines from the root store is legitimate; the unstated bank difference is not. Middle layers differ by up to 0.198 (L28) between banks. (2) '+0.033' is passC11's margin (0.034 recomputed); F-03's own store gives +0.037, so the heading's 'ten times' and the body's 'eleven times' are not consistent with each other. Also: the entry's gate line (datasets_in_matrix=11) is unverifiable -- RF-14 truncated those .status files. F-72's own caveat (3) can now be closed: the 80-layer sweep has finished.",P1-hpkr
F-23,"The replicated paper never evaluates on harm-pressure-knowledge-report, and the wording-matched slice is our own construction, so both the HP-KR diagnosis and the matched slice are additions to the paper rather than departures from it.",no numbers; structural claims: Table 1 lists HarmPressureChoice; Figure 7's title reads '[HPC excluded]'; the figures use MASK which has no Table 1 row,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:408,"papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf (arXiv 2605.09391, 14 pp, opened during this audit); docs/papers/persona-coordinates-notes.md; C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/kd_crossgen.log",Table 1 on p4; figure text on pp5-7 and 12-14; the two '[HPC excluded]' title lines on p12/p13; notes lines 300-305 (4.3) and 554-559 (8.1); log lines 1 and 8 at 2026-09-19 20:10:59 / 20:11:04,"HP-KR: ZERO occurrences of any spelling in all 14 pages incl. figure text. Table 1 deception rows = AILiar / Roleplaying / ConvGame / InstrDec / HarmPressureChoice; no MASK row. Figure 7 (p12) axis labels = ConvGame, InstrDec, Mask, AILiar, Roleplay; its title = 'Transfer AUROC: Method Comparison . Deception . Llama 3.2 3B (Layer 14, k=1) [HPC excluded]'. Mask appears on pp 5,6,7,12,13,14 and not on p4.",YES -- all six components verified against the paper's own text,"kr-matched construction date confirmed independently: logs/kd_crossgen.log 2026-09-19 20:11:04 already reports 'harm-pressure-kr-matched n=258 124D/134H', the same counts F-16 verifies; the slice is a view built by our own eval_datasets.py::hpkr_slice over HP-KR rows","audit/scripts/claims/F-23.py (pypdf text extraction of all 14 pages, name counts, Table 1 dump, figure captions, excluded/HPC grep) + read-only lab log grep","git-tracked PDF, 2,091,035 B, mtime 2026-09-09; notes file git working copy; lab log read read-only. No result file, bank, layer or q-value involved, so RF-11/12/13/15/16 do not apply.","The 8B replication (Figure 8, p13) carries the same '[HPC excluded]' title, so the exclusion is consistent across both of the paper's model settings, not a one-figure slip.",HOLDS,"HIGH -- verified against the paper opened during this audit, plus an independent log for the construction date",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-23.py,"One loose phrase: 'even that never appears in any figure' -- HPC appears in two figure TITLES, as the words '[HPC excluded]'. What never appears is any HPC result. Also worth saying in the write-up that the exclusion is the paper's own documented choice (it is in their figure titles); the genuinely undocumented thing is MASK being used with no Table 1 row, which the notes file already flags at 8.1.",P1-hpkr
H-001,"The re-measured Liars' Bench Follow-Up Probe (Llama-3.3-70B, layer 20, LR on RepE activations at the prefilled 'No', 1% FPR on Alpaca) matches published Table 7 to 0.002 mean AUROC over the 5 shared datasets, is within ~0.05 on every dataset, and differs substantially only on CG balanced accuracy (0.80 vs 0.60).",0.002; ~0.05; 0.80 vs 0.60,"his branch: results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/summary.md:24 (commit fd17728, 2026-09-21)",results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/results_table.csv; results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/cfg.yaml; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Table 7 p.55,"5 eval rows, cols auroc and balanced_accuracy_at_fpr_1%; PDF Llama 3.3 70B row, columns HP-C/HP-KR/CG/ID/IT",measured 5-shared mean AUROC 0.63601 vs published 0.634 -> gap 0.00201; per-dataset |dAUROC| 0.0550/0.0421/0.0524/0.0448/0.0102; CG balacc 0.7993 vs 0.60 = 0.1993,YES for the 0.002 gap and the CG balacc gap (tol 5e-4); NO for 'within ~0.05 everywhere' - CG 0.0550 and HP-KR 0.0524 exceed 0.05,"published comparator independently re-extracted from the PDF: Table 7 Llama row AUROC [0.50,0.14,0.75,0.61,0.93,0.24,0.85], 5-shared mean 0.634, balacc mean 0.578 - his transcription is correct in all 10 cells",Level 2 on his extraction/pooling NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone; owner's rule). Re-derived the quoted aggregate from his own committed per-cell files instead of reading his summary line. Published side re-extracted from the Liars' Bench PDF with pypdf.,"his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule.","Layer 20 only (cfg detect_layers=[20]); the follow-up protocol changes every token sequence so no other depth exists. Single run, no seeds. RepE val row = 1.000 on all metrics (in-distribution wiring check).",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - both sides re-derived from primary files (his CSV and the published PDF),MEDIUM-HIGH - the fidelity check for the one published baseline they measured rather than transcribed,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"Quantifier failure: 'within ~0.05 everywhere' is false in 2 of 5 datasets; honest wording is 'within 0.055'. His 0.6360117465200714 also appears verbatim in persona_ood_ext_L20/liars_bench_comparison.csv, so his two files agree exactly.",P10-collab-notes
H-003,"On HP-KR at layer 20 the re-measured Follow-Up Probe inverts to AUROC 0.088, below the repo's Mean Probe (0.109) and the published persona grouping (0.148), making it a third probe family that inverts on this dataset.",0.088; 0.109; 0.148,his branch: results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/summary.md:26-29 (commit fd17728),results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/results_table.csv; results/persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot_operating.csv; results/persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot.csv; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Tables 6-7,row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain: col auroc = 0.08755396; arm 'base probe (RepE-trained)' threshold control col auroc = 0.109; col auroc_axis = 0.14827698,0.08755 / 0.109 / 0.14828,"YES, all three (tol 5e-4)",published corroboration: Liars' Bench Table 7 gives the Follow-Up Probe 0.14 on HP-KR for Llama-3.3-70B and Table 6 gives the Mean Probe 0.12 - the inversion is in the published baselines too,Level 2 on his extraction/pooling NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone; owner's rule). Re-derived the quoted aggregate from his own committed per-cell files instead of reading his summary line. Published rows re-extracted from the PDF with pypdf.,"his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule. NOTE: the 0.109 comparator's file gained its base-probe rows only at the branch tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), one day AFTER this note; the 09-20 version (0f7b620) had no base-probe arm. The numbers nevertheless agree exactly.","Layer-20 specific: at L40 the same deception axis reads 0.5926 and the base probe 0.9358 (P8 D-081). Six arms in his own L20 file invert on HP-KR: auroc_axis 0.1483, auroc_pc1 0.2530, auroc_syc_axis 0.0429, auroc_syc_pc1 0.0406, base probe 0.109, follow-up 0.0876. The ext (12v13) and denial (4v6) axes do NOT invert (0.8816, 0.8899).",MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - three exact matches plus independent PDF corroboration,HIGH - HP-KR inversion is the pivot of the project's story,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,Quantifier caveat recorded: 'a third probe family' is only true if all four persona arms count as one family; six arms invert at this layer.,P10-collab-notes
H-005,"Over the 5 shared Liars' Bench datasets at layer 20 the re-measured Follow-Up Probe is worse than the repo's own RepE-trained Mean Probe: AUROC 0.636 vs 0.697 and balanced accuracy 0.622 vs 0.721, with the deficit coming from CG and IT.",0.636; 0.697; 0.622; 0.721,his branch: results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/summary.md:30-32 (commit fd17728),results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/results_table.csv; results/persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot_operating.csv; docs/papers/liars-bench-notes.md:106,"unweighted mean of the 5 eval rows; arm 'base probe (RepE-trained)', dataset ""Average (Liars' Bench)"", threshold_source control -> auroc 0.6972, balacc 0.7209",0.63601 vs 0.6972 AUROC; 0.62234 vs 0.7209 balacc,"YES, all four (tol 5e-4)","Mean Probe average re-derived from its own 5 per-dataset rows (0.9837/0.4708/0.109/0.9726/0.9498 -> 0.69718; balacc 0.8383/0.5/0.5/0.9085/0.8578 -> 0.72092). Per-dataset deficit: CG -0.179, IT -0.167, HP-KR -0.021, ID -0.010, HP-C +0.071 -> 'the gap is CG and IT' holds.",Level 2 on his extraction/pooling NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone; owner's rule). Re-derived the quoted aggregate from his own committed per-cell files instead of reading his summary line.,"his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule. The comparator rows were added at the tip 45b16d9 (09-22), after the note (09-21); the run they originally came from (XXXX-9-llama-all/results_table.csv) is NOT committed - only its plots are.","Layer 20 only. The base probe is strongly layer-dependent on HP-KR (0.109 at L20 vs 0.9358 at L40), so this head-to-head must not be generalised across depth.",MATCHES HIS DATA,"HIGH - all four numbers reproduced from per-dataset rows, not read off his summary",MEDIUM - a caveat on the paper's 'comparable' wording rather than a result of their own,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,'where the paper calls the two comparable' is supported by the repo's paper notes (Appendix M) and by the published 5-shared means I re-extracted: Mean Probe 0.682/0.636 vs Follow-Up 0.634/0.578 - already ~0.05 apart on AUROC in the paper.,P10-collab-notes
H-007,"Over the same 5 datasets, the zero-shot extended persona axis at layer 20 leads the Follow-Up Probe on AUROC (0.887 vs 0.636) and trails on balanced accuracy (0.591 vs 0.622), and at layer 40 the knowledge-denial axis beats it on both, reading 0.725 and 0.894.",0.591; 0.622; 0.725; 0.894 (and 0.887; 0.636 from H-006),his branch: results/XXXX-9-llama-all-followup/summary.md:34-35 (commit fd17728),"results/persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot.csv; results/persona_ood_ext_L40/zero_shot.csv; results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40}/zero_shot_operating.csv","cols auroc_ext_axis / auroc_denial_axis over the 5 eval rows; operating-point rows arm='extended axis (12v13)' and 'knowledge-denial axis (4v6)', dataset=""Average (Liars' Bench)"", threshold_source=control","ext axis L20: AUROC 0.8868, balacc 0.5914; knowledge-denial L40: balacc 0.7251, AUROC 0.8938; follow-up 0.6360/0.6223","YES, all four (tol 5e-4)",5-dataset mean AUROCs recomputed from his per-dataset zero_shot.csv: ext axis 0.8868 (L20) / 0.8990 (L40); knowledge-denial 0.8628 (L20) / 0.8938 (L40); deception axis 0.7503 / 0.7983 - all identical to his stored averages. Balanced accuracies are Level 1 only (need his raw scores).,Level 2 on his extraction/pooling NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone; owner's rule). Re-derived the quoted aggregate from his own committed per-cell files instead of reading his summary line.,"his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule. The ""Average (Liars' Bench)"" rows were added at the tip 45b16d9 (09-22), after the 09-21 note; they agree with it exactly.",Layers 20 and 40 only in the cited files (a persona_ood_ext_L44 directory exists and is not cited). The knowledge-denial axis moves a lot with depth: balacc 0.5587 (L20) -> 0.7251 (L40).,PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,"HIGH on the digits, MEDIUM on the intended comparison",MEDIUM - the sentence that promotes the knowledge-denial axis at depth,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"TWO quantifier/presentation problems. (1) '(0.725 / 0.894)' is balacc/AUROC while the preceding clause lists AUROC first, so the metrics read swapped. (2) 'beats it on both' is true only if 'it' is the Follow-Up Probe; against the extended axis just discussed, the knowledge-denial axis LOSES on AUROC at L40 (0.8938 vs 0.8990) and wins only on balanced accuracy (0.7251 vs 0.6939).",P10-collab-notes
H-008,"Averaged over the six held-out datasets, a probe trained on one other dataset reaches mean AUROC 0.648 at layer 20 and 0.732 at layer 40, against 0.694/0.850 for the naively pooled probe and 0.794/0.804 for the per-dataset-weighted pool.","0.648; 0.732 (table also: 0.694/0.850, 0.794/0.804)","his branch: results/loo_L20/summary.md:24-28 (commit 6b16a46, 2026-09-20)","results/loo_L{20,40}/single_source_reference.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_summary.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_scores.npz; results/persona_ood/matrix_baseline.csv","mean of col single_source_mean over the 6 rows; arm=baseline rows of loo_summary.csv, col auroc; npz keys 'baseline|<weighting>|<dataset>' + 'labels|<dataset>'",single-source 0.6478 (L20) / 0.7320 (L40); pooled naive 0.6941 / 0.8496; pooled balanced 0.7943 / 0.8039,"YES, all six (tol 5e-4; his table rounds to 3 dp)","all 10 arm x weighting rows of loo_summary.csv reproduce at both depths from the raw held-out scores, to 4 dp. Only exception: pc3|balanced at L20 recomputes to 0.7787 vs his 0.7786 (1e-4, rounding/tie handling).","Level 2 of the scoring step: recomputed AUROC for every arm x weighting x dataset from the committed raw held-out scores + labels in loo_scores.npz, with my own rank-based Mann-Whitney AUROC (no sklearn).","his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule.","Two depths, one fit per cell, no seeds. Independent cross-check: his per-dataset single_source_mean equals, in all 6 columns to 4 dp, the off-diagonal COLUMN means of persona_ood/matrix_baseline.csv from a different run - which also confirms the matrix orientation (rows=train, cols=test).",MATCHES HIS DATA,"HIGH - three independent paths agree (his summary CSV, his per-dataset reference CSV, the raw scores) plus a fourth from a different experiment",MEDIUM-HIGH - the concession table that every later comparison in the note is measured against,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"Wording caveat: the row is labelled 'mean over the 5 training sets' but the tabled value is additionally averaged over the 6 held-out datasets, only 5 of which are Liars' Bench (the sixth is repe_honesty, the probes' own training distribution).",P10-collab-notes
H-009,"With HP-KR excluded from the average, pooled supervision matches or beats the zero-shot extended persona axis: 0.928 vs 0.909 at layer 20 (a loss for the axis) and 0.915 vs 0.917 at layer 40 (a tie).",0.928; 0.909; 0.915; 0.917,his branch: results/loo_L20/summary.md:52-54 (commit 6b16a46),"results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_summary.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_scores.npz","col auroc_excl_hpkr for arm=baseline (weighting balanced at L20, naive at L40) and arm=ext_axis1",L20 0.9283 vs 0.9086; L40 0.9149 vs 0.9165,"YES, all four (tol 5e-4)","reproduced exactly from the raw held-out scores. The pooling NOT quoted loses badly: L20 naive excl-HPKR 0.7678 (-0.141 vs the axis), L40 balanced 0.8525 (-0.064).","Level 2 of the scoring step: recomputed AUROC for every arm x weighting x dataset from the committed raw held-out scores + labels in loo_scores.npz, with my own rank-based Mann-Whitney AUROC (no sklearn).","his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule.","Two depths; the sign of the pooling effect reverses between them (see H-011). No seeds. 'a dead heat' at L40 is fair - the axis is 0.0016 ahead, far inside his own bootstrap CIs.",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - all four numbers exact and Level-2 reproducible,HIGH - the qualification that decides how strongly the generalization claim can be stated,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"Quantifier failure of the P8 kind: 'pooled supervision matches or beats it' holds in 1 of the 4 depth x pooling cells, and the two depths quote DIFFERENT poolings (balanced at L20, naive at L40) without saying so. His own qualification 3 concedes the pooling choice is arbitrary, which makes the max-over-poolings reading a real weakness.",P10-collab-notes
H-010,"The persona axis's average advantage over pooled supervision is carried almost entirely by HP-KR, where the pooled baseline 'inverts' to 0.124 at layer 20 and 0.523 at layer 40.",0.124; 0.523,his branch: results/loo_L20/summary.md:53-54 (commit 6b16a46),"results/loo_L{20,40}/single_source_reference.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_summary.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_bootstrap.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_scores.npz","row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain, cols pooled_loo_balanced (L20) and pooled_loo_naive (L40)","L20 balanced 0.1243, L20 naive 0.3254; L40 naive 0.5230, L40 balanced 0.5612. Advantage +0.1098 -> -0.0197 excl-HPKR (L20); +0.0662 -> +0.0016 (L40).","Numbers YES (tol 5e-4). The word 'inverts' NO at layer 40: 0.5230 is ABOVE chance, and the L40 balanced value 0.5612 is above chance too.",all values reproduced exactly from the raw held-out scores,"Level 2 of the scoring step: recomputed AUROC for every arm x weighting x dataset from the committed raw held-out scores + labels in loo_scores.npz, with my own rank-based Mann-Whitney AUROC (no sklearn).","his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule.","His own loo_bootstrap.csv (balanced, 1000 stratified draws) confirms the size: HP-KR delta -0.7573 [-0.8161,-0.6911] at L20 and -0.3512 [-0.4001,-0.2976] at L40, the largest magnitudes at each depth. It also shows the pooled baseline BEATING the axis on CG at both depths (+0.0302, +0.0854) and on HP-C at L20 (+0.1160).",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH,HIGH - the strongest self-criticism in his note and the sentence most likely to be quoted,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"The substantive half is verified and if anything understated (at L20 the advantage does not shrink, it REVERSES to -0.020 once HP-KR is dropped). But 'the pooled baseline inverts to ... 0.523 (L40)' is contradicted by his own file - 0.523 > 0.5 is near-chance, not inverted - and the two quoted values silently use different poolings.",P10-collab-notes
H-012,"The zero-shot extended persona axis at layer 40 beats both published non-privileged probes on both metrics and comes within 0.03 AUROC of the privileged Upper-Bound Probe, which trains on in-dataset examples.","0.03 (table: 0.694/0.899 vs 0.890/0.930, 0.636/0.682, 0.578/0.634)",his branch: results/loo_L20/summary.md:86-96 (commit 6b16a46),"results/loo_L{20,40}/liars_bench_comparison_loo.csv; results/persona_ood_ext_L40/zero_shot.csv; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Table 8 p.56","rows 'Upper-Bound Probe' and 'persona axis, extended (zero-shot)', col auroc / balacc_1pct_fpr; PDF Llama 3.3 70B row of Table 8","upper bound 0.930, extended axis L40 0.8990023 -> gap 0.03100 (L20: 0.8868 -> gap 0.0432). Balanced accuracy: 0.890 vs 0.6939 -> gap 0.196.","NO - the gap is 0.0310, not <=0.03; true only after rounding to 2 dp","the axis's 0.8990 re-derived as the 5-dataset mean of persona_ood_ext_L40/zero_shot.csv (matches). Published Table 8 re-extracted from the PDF: Llama row AUROC [0.74,0.97,1.0,0.95,0.99] -> 0.930 and balacc [0.67,0.95,1.0,0.90,0.93] -> 0.890; his transcription is correct.",Level 2 on his extraction/pooling NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone; owner's rule). Re-derived the quoted aggregate from his own committed per-cell files instead of reading his summary line. Published Tables 6/7/8 re-extracted from the PDF with pypdf.,"his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule.",At layer 20 - the layer the file is named for - the gap is 0.0432. The companion clause 'beats both published non-privileged probes on both metrics' does hold (0.6939/0.8990 vs 0.636/0.682 and 0.578/0.634).,PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - both sides read from primary files; the shortfall is 0.001 and unambiguous,HIGH - 'nearly as good as the privileged upper bound' is abstract-grade wording,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"Quantifier failure. Honest wording: 'within 0.031 on AUROC, but 0.20 behind on balanced accuracy'. The balanced-accuracy side of the same comparison (0.694 vs 0.890) is not mentioned in the sentence.",P10-collab-notes
H-013,"Across six held-out datasets and two depths the fixed, label-free persona direction never falls below AUROC 0.64 (L20) or 0.71 (L40), while probes trained on pooled labelled data fall to 0.12 and 0.49.",0.64; 0.71; 0.12; 0.49,"his branch: results/loo_L20/summary.md:102-105, the block-quoted 'defensible claim' (commit 6b16a46)","results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_summary.csv; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_scores.npz; results/loo_L{20,40}/loo_bootstrap.csv",col auroc_worst_dataset for arm=ext_axis1 and arm=baseline (weighting balanced),"ext_axis1 worst 0.6393 (L20) / 0.7116 (L40), both on HP-C; baseline balanced worst 0.1243 (L20, HP-KR) / 0.4887 (L40, HP-C); baseline naive worst 0.3254 / 0.5230","YES, all four (tol 5e-4)",all four reproduced from the raw held-out scores by recomputing every cell's AUROC and taking the minimum,"Level 2 of the scoring step: recomputed AUROC for every arm x weighting x dataset from the committed raw held-out scores + labels in loo_scores.npz, with my own rank-based Mann-Whitney AUROC (no sklearn).","his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule.","Two depths, one fit per cell, no seeds. 'Generalization gap is zero by construction' is a definition, not a measurement, and is stated as such. His bootstrap shows the pooled baseline beating the axis on CG at both depths and on HP-C at L20, so the claim is about the floor, not about winning - which the note says.",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - all four numbers exact and Level-2 reproducible,"HIGH - written as the paper-ready sentence, so any mislabel travels verbatim",audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"Two framing errors. (1) 'six held-out LIARS' BENCH datasets' - only five are; the sixth is repe_honesty, and his own comparison table uses n_datasets=5 and labels the 5-set mean ""Average (Liars' Bench)"". (2) The pooled floors 0.12/0.49 both use the BALANCED pooling, while H-010 two paragraphs earlier quotes the NAIVE pooling at L40 (0.523); under naive the L40 pooled floor is 0.5230, not 0.49.",P10-collab-notes
H-014,"The persona_ood run tests Mahadik & Skapars (arXiv 2605.09391) - that projecting activations onto persona principal components improves cross-dataset probe generalization - on the cached layer-20 Llama-3.3-70B activations from the Liars' Bench sweep, with no new model calls.","none numeric in the sentence (the inventory's '-3.3' is a parse artefact of 'Llama-3.3-70B'); the table it introduces: 0.6478/0.7282/0.9564 baseline, 0.6823/0.9123/0.9184 pc3, 0.5269 random3",his branch: results/persona_ood/summary.md:3-5 (first committed a093c54 2026-09-18; text last touched 06da2de 2026-09-20),results/persona_ood/summary.csv; results/persona_ood/matrix_baseline.csv; results/persona_ood/matrix_pc3.csv; results/persona_ood/zero_shot.csv; papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf p.1; docs/papers/persona-coordinates-notes.md:4,"summary.csv rows baseline/pc3/random3, cols off_diagonal_mean, off_diagonal_excl_hpkr, diagonal_mean, layer, dim; the 6x6 matrices' 30 off-diagonal cells","layer=20, baseline dim=8192; baseline off-diag 0.6478 / excl-HPKR 0.7282 / diag 0.9564; pc3 0.6823 / 0.9123 / 0.9184; random3 0.5269 / 0.5598 / 0.7874",YES (tol 5e-4); arXiv id and the paper's claim confirmed from the PDF and the repo's notes,"every aggregate rebuilt from the 30 per-cell values: pc3 - baseline mean +0.0345, median +0.0683, improved 20/30, excl-HPKR +0.1840, diagonal -0.0380 - reproducing his '+0.035 / +0.184 / -0.038 / 20 of 30 / median +0.068' exactly",Level 2 on his extraction/pooling NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone; owner's rule). Re-derived the quoted aggregate from his own committed per-cell files instead of reading his summary line. The 'cached / no new model calls' assertion has NO independent path: the activation cache is not committed and his disk is unavailable.,"his branch origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip 45b16d9 (2026-09-22), read with git show; not touched by the 09-22 lab re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's stores). Bank = 'persona including knowlede denial' (36 personas) = lab run-kd/vectors_s3 byte-identical (RF-1 RESOLVED); RF-12/RF-15 paper16 vector versions do not apply. No BH q-values quoted. His activations are gone (RF-2) -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible by the owner's rule. matrix_pc3.csv last written at 607c0e1 (09-18) while summary.md was rewritten at 06da2de (09-20) - the text is newer than the matrices but agrees with them exactly, so no staleness.","Matrix orientation confirmed independently: the off-diagonal COLUMN means of matrix_baseline.csv equal, to 4 dp in all six columns, the single_source_mean column of the later loo_L20 run. Random-3d control (0.5269) sits far below both arms, so the gain is not a generic dimensionality effect.",MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH for the re-derived parts; LOW for the 'cached / no new model calls' assertion (no independent path),MEDIUM-HIGH - the framing sentence of the whole persona_ood line of work,audit/scripts/claims/P10_collab_notes.py,"Caveats recorded: (a) his persona set is 15, not the paper's 26 - he states it and gives the measured reason (PC1-deception |cos| 0.949 vs 0.722); (b) the +0.184 excl-HPKR headline is computed after removing the one dataset where the BASELINE collapses - the mirror of the problem H-010 describes on the persona side; (c) 'examples | 13,648 cached' has never changed across three revisions while his own zero_shot.csv row counts moved 13,154 -> 13,602, so 13,648 plausibly describes the cache, not the scored set - unverifiable.",P10-collab-notes
A-02,The replicated paper proposes scoring activations in persona coordinates (principal components of contrastive persona vectors) and reports improved OOD generalization on Llama 3.2-3B and Llama 3-8B.,(none),abstract 2026-09-21 para 1 sent 2; audit/phase0/collab_abstract_2026-09-21.md:16,papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf (Mahadik & Skapars),"p.1 abstract ('first principal components, obtained by unsupervised PCA of the persona-specific vectors'; 'probes trained on persona-PC projections generalize better'); p.4 'Language Models. Our main results use Llama 3.2-3B, with additional replications on Llama 3-8B'; p.5 sec 7 'We only experiment with two LLMs, Llama 3.2-3B and Llama 3-8B'",all four elements present verbatim in the PDF,YES,"n/a - claim about a published paper, checked against the PDF itself","pypdf text extraction of the PDF in papers/, read during this audit",papers/ PDF as committed on asix; no version issue,"The 8B is an APPENDIX replication (Appendices E/F) the paper itself calls 'broadly supportive', not a second headline; main results are 3B at layer 14, 8B at layer 16.",HOLDS,HIGH - every element read directly in the PDF during this audit,"MED - framing sentence, not a result","audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)","Owner-side context (not needed for the verdict): she ran her own 3B/8B rungs, F-63/F-96/F-100 (batch P4); the paper's claim replicates at small scale in her hands, the dispute is about magnitude and controls.",P11-abstract
A-03,"They test the method at 70B across six Liars' Bench datasets at layers 20 and 40 of Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct, reporting the full cross-dataset transfer matrix for fifteen feature sets.",six datasets; layers 20 and 40; fifteen feature sets,abstract 2026-09-21 para 1 sent 3,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv,zero_shot_operating.csv}; git ls-tree of results/; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Table 6 header","len(summary.csv rows)=15 at each layer; zero_shot.csv has 6 scored datasets + XXXX-20__plain (alpaca control, n_deceptive=0); result dirs include persona_ood_ext_L44; LB Table 6 header lists HP-C HP-KR CG ST ID GS IT",15 feature sets (exact); 6 scored datasets (exact); but 5 of the 6 are Liars' Bench - repe_honesty is RepE (Zou et al.); layer 44 also run,PARTLY (counts YES; 'Liars' Bench' label NO; layer list incomplete),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it.,counted rows/dirs from his committed files; dataset membership checked against the published Liars' Bench table,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","His own zero_shot_operating.csv distinguishes 'Average' (6) from ""Average (Liars' Bench)"" (5), and his draft quotes the 5-dataset row (D-117, D-126) - so the abstract is inconsistent with his own file labels.",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - counts read straight out of his files and the published PDF,"MED - scope sentence, but repe_honesty is the easiest column (every persona feature 0.99-1.00) and his summary flags it as in-distribution for the base probe, so including it in a 'Liars' Bench' average inflates the headline (dropping it moves the paper-contrast margin 0.100 -> 0.092 at L40; F-97, batch P3).","audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)","Owner's ledger says the same from the other side: F-97 sec 2, ""'Same six' is false ... and repe_honesty"".",P11-abstract
A-04,"A one-dimensional persona contrast, applied zero-shot with no benchmark labels, reaches 0.904 and 0.916 mean off-diagonal AUROC at layers 20 and 40 against 0.648 and 0.732 for 8192-d probes trained on the benchmark, and wins on every held-out dataset individually.",0.904; 0.916; 0.648; 0.732,abstract 2026-09-21 para 2 sent 1 (the headline),"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv,matrix_ext_axis1.csv,matrix_baseline.csv,matrix_axis1.csv}; deception_detection/{persona_pcs.py,scripts/persona_ood.py}",summary.csv rows ext_axis1/baseline col off_diagonal_mean; 30 off-diagonal cells of matrix_*.csv; zero_shot.csv cols auroc_axis/auroc_ext_axis,0.904117 / 0.915835 (ext_axis1) and 0.647770 / 0.732033 (baseline),YES all four (tol 5e-4),"Re-derived from his 30 off-diagonal cells: L20 0.904117 / 0.647773, L40 0.915833 / 0.732027, L44 0.903383 / 0.715650. 'Wins on every held-out dataset' = 6/6 at L20, L40 AND L44 (column means over the 5 training sets; deltas +0.104 to +0.488).",Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it.,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","Holds at layer 44 too (0.903 vs 0.716). ATTRIBUTION: 0.904/0.916 is ext_axis1, the 12-vs-13 EXTENDED contrast (8+4 vs 7+6) whose ten extra roles are the OWNER's kd personas; the paper-faithful 8v7 axis1 reads 0.7909 / 0.8319 zero-shot on the same rows, so 44.2%/45.7% of the margin over the quoted baseline is her bank (F-97, verified batch P3). The comparator 0.648/0.732 is the weakest available baseline; the owner's pooled-training alternatives reach 0.8683/0.8930 (F-85, batch P2) but on a DIFFERENT six-dataset set, so not like-for-like (F-97 withdrew that framing).",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1; aggregates and the 'every held-out dataset' clause re-derived) - but the ATTRIBUTION is wrong,HIGH - four exact matches plus 18 re-derived column means,HIGH - the abstract's and the title's claim,"audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)",Paragraph 2 states the number as the published method's result; the repair is disclosed only in paragraph 3 and the bank is never attributed. Same numbers as draft rows D-008/D-098 (batch P5).,P11-abstract
A-05,"Having no training set the contrast's generalization gap is zero, while the trained probes lose 0.31 and 0.25 AUROC moving off the diagonal.",0.31; 0.25,abstract 2026-09-21 para 2 sent 2,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","rows baseline and ext_axis1, cols diagonal_mean and off_diagonal_mean",baseline gap 0.308658 (L20) and 0.251240 (L40); ext_axis1 gap -0.000612 / -0.000281 / -0.000125 at L20/40/44,YES (tol 5e-3 for the 2-dp figures),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it.,arithmetic on his own summary rows,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","L44 baseline gap is 0.266544 (not quoted). TWO qualifications, both measured: (1) the zero gap is arithmetic, not a finding - for a label-free 1-d feature the trained off-diagonal equals the zero-shot mean to 1e-16 (F-97 caveat 2); (2) the contrast buys the zero gap by being WORSE in-distribution: baseline diagonal 0.9564/0.9833/0.9822 vs ext_axis1 0.9035/0.9156/0.9033 (raw ahead by +0.053/+0.068/+0.079).",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1),HIGH - three values read and two re-derived from the same file,MED - supporting sentence; the 'gap is zero' framing is tautological for a 1-d zero-shot feature and should say so,"audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)",,P11-abstract
A-06,"The principal components (the published method's central operation) do not contribute: the top-3 subspace reaches 0.684 and 0.866, and at layer 40 its first component scores 0.09 below the contrast it is derived from.",0.684; 0.866; 0.09,abstract 2026-09-21 para 2 sent 3,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv}; results/persona_ood_L40/summary.csv","rows ext_pc1/ext_pc3/ext_axis1/pc1/pc3/axis1, col off_diagonal_mean; zero_shot.csv cols auroc_pc1/auroc_axis/auroc_ext_pc1/auroc_ext_axis","ext_pc3 = 0.683697 (L20) and 0.865534 (L40) -> MATCH. 'first component 0.09 below the contrast it is derived from' at L40: ext_pc1 0.767950 vs ext_axis1 0.915835 = -0.1479, NOT -0.09.",PARTLY - two of three,"Exhaustive scan of all ordered feature pairs in his L40 summary for a gap within 0.005 of 0.09 returns exactly two, neither of which is the stated comparison: pc3 is 0.0927 below baseline; ext_pc1 is 0.0914 below pc1 (the PUBLISHED bank's PC1, a different bank). The umbrella claim fails for the published bank: pc1 is ABOVE axis1 at every layer - +0.0147 (L20), +0.0274 (L40), +0.0246 (L44) zero-shot, same trained. It holds only for the EXTENDED bank (ext_pc1 - ext_axis1 = -0.243 / -0.148 / -0.123).",Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it.,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","ext_pc3 at L44 = 0.879936 (not quoted). The top-3 half is on firmer ground than the PC1 half: ext_pc3 is below ext_axis1 at all three layers (-0.220/-0.050/-0.023, D-105 batch P8). OWNER CROSS-CHECK on the same question: her ledger reaches 'the PCs add nothing' by a MATCHED CONTROL instead - F-17 (verified, batch P6) unified persona axis - dataset-PCA = -0.003 at L40; F-31 (verified) the kd bank's +0.0757 does NOT clear a dataset-level bootstrap; F-96/F-100/F-110 (batch P4) layer-averaged persona-vs-dataset-PCA +0.120/+0.103/+0.075 at 3B/8B/70B, and after the bank correction the 70B rung is +0.054 vs dataset-PCA and -0.013 vs raw. Those support the conclusion by a route that survives a control; A-06's own route fails on the published bank.",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,"HIGH - two exact matches, one exhaustive pairwise scan, three layers of the PC1-vs-contrast comparison, all from his committed files",HIGH - the abstract's third contribution and its challenge to the replicated paper's central operation,"audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)",The owner's ledger independently calls the 0.09 unsourceable: F-97 sec 3 (verified in batch P3). My scan adds that NO pair in his L40 file equals 0.09 for the stated comparison. Suggested rewrite in audit/claims/A-06.md.,P11-abstract
A-08,"On HP-KR - the hardest Liars' Bench column, where the benchmark's Mean Probe scores 0.12 AUROC and its privileged upper-bound probe 0.97 - the published 8v7 persona grouping inverts at layer 20 (0.148) and barely clears chance at layer 40 (0.593).",0.12; 0.97; 0.148; 0.593,abstract 2026-09-21 para 3 sent 2,"papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Tables 6 (p.54) and 8 (p.56); origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv","LB Table 6 AUROC block, Llama 3.3 70B row, HP-KR col = 0.12; Table 8 (Upper Bound Probe) same cell = 0.97; his zero_shot.csv col auroc_axis, row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain","0.12 and 0.97 exact in the published tables; his axis1 = 0.148277 (L20), 0.592579 (L40), 0.589493 (L44, not quoted)",YES all four,"Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it. The two published values were read directly in the PDF this audit, so that half is a proper check, not Level 1.",pypdf extraction of the Liars' Bench tables; his values read from his committed zero_shot.csv,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Published PDF is arXiv 2511.16035 v2.","'Hardest column in Liars' Bench' is method-dependent: same tables give the Unrelated-Question Classifier 0.90 on HP-KR (Table 11, Llama 3.3 70B) and LLM-as-a-Judge 0.45 on GS below 0.48 on HP-KR (Table 10). It IS the minimum for the Mean Probe on that model and for its across-model average (0.36). L44 also reads 0.589, so 'barely clears chance' covers two layers. On the owner's 11-dataset store the same 8v7 contrast on HP-KR spans 0.087 (L24) to 0.860 (L0) across 21 layers (F-99, verified batch P3), so the inversion is typical, not an L20 accident. F-01/F-02 (verified batch P1) add that HP-KR's label is largely lexical (a denial regex scores 0.913).",MATCHES HIS DATA for his two numbers; the two published numbers HOLD against the PDF,"HIGH - four exact matches, two of them read in the published tables",HIGH - the motivating fact for the whole third paragraph; correctly attributed to the published grouping (unlike A-04),"audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)","Overlaps D-003 (batch P5), D-080 (this batch) and D-023/D-013 (batch P8), which checked the same published values independently and agree.",P11-abstract
A-10,"The independently constructed sycophancy axis inverts further still on HP-KR (0.043), confirming the mechanism is the assertion-denial polarity rather than anything specific to the deception personas.",0.043,abstract 2026-09-21 para 3 sent 4,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv; deception_detection/persona_pcs.py; deception_detection/scripts/persona_ood.py:907-926,943","col auroc_syc_axis, row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain; persona_ood.py:911 syc_geom = fit_geometry(bank, deception=SYCOPHANCY_PERSONAS, honesty=ANTI_SYCOPHANCY_PERSONAS)","0.042928 (L20), 0.167054 (L40), 0.480406 (L44); syc_pc1 0.040576 / 0.159935 / 0.514669",YES for 0.043 at L20 (the layer is NOT stated - UNDERSPECIFIED; I tested the most favourable reading),"'Independently constructed' is FALSE against his own code: the sycophancy geometry is fitted on the SAME bank object as the deception geometry (persona_ood.py:911), i.e. the same 36-role vector folder, which for the ext_* runs is the OWNER's kd extraction (his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3, RF-1). It is also the replicated paper's own Eq-4 5v5 contrast, not something he constructed. His own comment at persona_ood.py:943 records the two axes sit at |cos| = 0.54.",Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it. Code read with git show.,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","'Inverts further still' holds at L20 (0.043 vs 0.148) and L40 (0.167 vs 0.593); at L44 the sycophancy axis is 0.480 (chance) against the 8v7's 0.589. OWNER CROSS-CHECK: F-13 (verified, batch P3) shows the SAME axes failing identically on sycophancy_mt, a dataset with no denial in it - axes 0.3551 as target / 0.3787 as source at L40 vs 0.4273/0.3004 on HP-KR, random 5-d beats it on both, and axes-as-target is at or below 0.50 at 21/21 layers in both poolings. F-65/F-66 (verified, batch P3) repair that column CONSTRUCTIVELY by varying capitulation (0.374 -> 0.745 zero-shot; trained pc:capitulation@2 0.714 vs raw 0.601, clearing a dataset-level bootstrap and both matched controls). F-107 (ledger-stated, NOT yet claim-checked) adds a natural-sarcasm angle. So the owner's measured diagnosis is REGISTER, of which assertion-denial is one case.",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH for the number and the code reading; HIGH for the F-13/F-65/F-66 cross-check (re-derived from raw matrices in batch P3),HIGH - it is the abstract's causal claim,"audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)","Two separate problems: the evidence is not independent (same bank, same rollouts, paper's own contrast), and the conclusion is narrower than the owner's own measured and constructively tested one. Suggested rewrite in audit/claims/A-10.md.",P11-abstract
A-11,"Adding four feigned-ignorance personas against six candour personas raises HP-KR zero-shot AUROC to 0.882 and 0.912, and lifts transfer on the four unrelated datasets by 0.18-0.21.",4; 6; 0.882; 0.912; 0.18-0.21,abstract 2026-09-21 para 3 last sentence,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{zero_shot.csv,matrix_axis1.csv,matrix_ext_axis1.csv}; deception_detection/persona_pcs.py; 'persona including knowlede denial/' (36 .pt); asix: kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json",col auroc_ext_axis row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain; KNOWLEDGE_DENIAL_PERSONAS / KNOWLEDGE_CANDOUR_PERSONAS tuples; kd_role_groups.json groups knowledge_denial / sincere_ignorance / plain_assertion; column means over the 5 training sets of matrix_axis1 vs matrix_ext_axis1,"0.881568 (L20) and 0.912392 (L40) -> MATCH; L44 = 0.893637 (not quoted). Persona counts: his 4 == owner's knowledge_denial (True), his 6 == owner's sincere_ignorance + plain_assertion (True).",YES for the AUROCs and the counts; the 0.18-0.21 matches only under one protocol (see level2),"'0.18-0.21 on four unrelated datasets' reproduces EXACTLY as TRAINED column means at L20, ext_axis1 minus axis1: CG +0.2053, IT +0.1972, ID +0.1787, RepE +0.1947 (HP-C only +0.0092). But the lift is a SIGN ARTIFACT: matrix_axis1 at L20 has one row - the probe trained on HP-KR - entirely sign-flipped (0.0601/0.2831/0.8516/0.0121/0.0413/0.0065), which drags each column mean down by ~1/5 of the flip. Under the ZERO-SHOT protocol used by the same sentence's 0.882/0.912 the lift on those four is +0.029 / +0.002 / -0.005 / -0.003 at L20 and +0.047 / +0.002 / +0.004 / 0.000 at L40. Trained column lifts at L40/L44 are at most +0.047 on those four.","Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it. Column means recomputed from his 36-cell matrices at all three layers, under both protocols.","his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","The 4v6 denial contrast ALONE reads 0.8899 / 0.9185 / 0.9077 on HP-KR, i.e. slightly better than the extended one at L40/L44. The sign-flip mechanism is the owner's F-97 caveat (1) (verified batch P3).",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,HIGH - counts set-compared against both sources; all AUROCs re-derived; the lift reproduced under both protocols at all three layers,"HIGH - the constructive contribution, and the sentence where the owner's bank is either credited or not","audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)","ATTRIBUTION: these are the OWNER's personas (kd_role_groups.json, role for role; his .pt byte-identical to her lab run-kd/vectors_s3 per RF-1) and the abstract does not say so. His 'six candour personas' also MERGE two groups she kept apart on purpose (sincere_ignorance 3 + plain_assertion 3); her note says the separation exists so the axis 'cannot be a wording artifact', and F-97 says the merged pole carries the confound the three-group design removes. The sentence also switches protocol mid-way (zero-shot -> trained).",P11-abstract
D-080,On HP-KR the published 8v7 contrast scores 0.148 zero-shot AUROC at layer 20 and sits near chance at layers 40 and 44 (0.593 and 0.589).,0.148; 0.593; 0.589,draft main (1).pdf p.7 sec 5.1 HP-KR,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv","col auroc_axis, row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain",0.148277 / 0.592579 / 0.589493,YES all three (tol 5e-4),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it.,values read from his committed zero_shot.csv at all three layers,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","Only three layers exist on his branch. On the owner's independent 11-dataset store the same contrast on HP-KR spans 0.087 (L24) to 0.860 (L0) over 21 layers, reading 0.556 at L40 (F-99, verified batch P3) - so the qualitative pattern is typical but the value moves a lot with depth. The L20 inversion is what sign-flips one row of his trained axis1 transfer matrix (see A-11).",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only),HIGH - three exact matches,"HIGH - sec 5.1's opening fact, and the same number the abstract uses (A-08)","audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)","Deferred from batch P8. Same number family as D-003 (batch P5, which checked the L20 value).",P11-abstract
D-100,Single cells can still favour a raw probe: at layer 40 the probe trained on instructed-deception scores 0.98 on convincing-game against 0.91 for the extended contrast.,0.98; 0.91 (from Figure 4),draft main (1).pdf p.8 sec 5.2 Transfer + Fig 4,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L40/{matrix_baseline.csv,matrix_ext_axis1.csv} (and L20/L44 for the enumeration)","cell row=instruct_dishonesty__plain, col=convince_me__plain",baseline 0.983100; ext_axis1 0.912300,"YES both (tol 5e-3, the precision of the figure)","Enumerated every off-diagonal cell where raw beats ext: exactly 2 of 30 at EACH layer. L20: IT->HP-KR (+0.0854), RepE->ID (+0.0037). L40: ID->CG (+0.0708, the named cell), RepE->HP-KR (+0.0157). L44: ID->CG (+0.1259), RepE->ID (+0.0011).",Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it. 30-cell enumeration from his own matrices at all three layers.,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","The claim is if anything understated: the draft could say '2 of 30 off-diagonal cells at every depth', which is stronger and auditable.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1; the surrounding claim re-derived from his cells),HIGH - both cells exact plus the full enumeration,LOW-MED - an honesty caveat inside sec 5.2,"audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)",Deferred from batch P8.,P11-abstract
D-126,"Layer 40 is best for the persona contrasts, on transfer (0.904/0.916/0.903 for the extended contrast at L20/40/44) and at the benchmark's threshold (0.591/0.694/0.666 balanced accuracy).",0.904/0.916/0.903; 0.591/0.694/0.666,draft main (1).pdf p.10 sec 5.5 Depth,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (git show only, no checkout): results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot_operating.csv}","summary.csv row ext_axis1 col off_diagonal_mean; zero_shot_operating.csv arm='extended axis (12v13)', dataset=""Average (Liars' Bench)"", threshold_source='control', col balacc",0.904117 / 0.915835 / 0.903388 and 0.591400 / 0.693900 / 0.666300,YES all six (tol 5e-4),"Best-layer check re-derived for 11 features: L40 is the maximum for ext_axis1, denial_axis1, axis1 and pc1 on transfer, and for all four persona-contrast arms on balanced accuracy. It is NOT the maximum for ext_pc3 (L44, 0.8799) or syc_axis1 (L44, 0.7078); the base probe peaks at L20 on balanced accuracy (0.7209).",Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Aggregates re-derived from his own cell-level matrices where they allow it.,"his branch @ 45b16d9; persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44} have ONE commit in their history, 9774075 2026-09-20 17:53, which PREDATES the abstract (pasted 2026-09-21 10:38Z) -> no version drift. Not touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores only). Not a BH-q claim. Persona bank for the ext_* runs = the OWNER's kd bank, his 36 .pt byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED).","Only THREE layers exist on his branch, so 'best' is best-of-three. The owner's independent 21-layer zero-shot sweep on her eleven datasets (F-99, verified batch P3) puts the extended contrast's maximum at L36 (0.8018) just above L40 (0.7996), and the 8v7's at L36 (0.7419) above L40 (0.7325) - a L32-L40 plateau rather than a point at 40. Her F-91 ('Layer 40 is not the peak. L32 is ... by ~0.02') is LEDGER-STATED and not yet claim-checked in this audit - flagged DOC-ONLY.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1; all six numbers exact),HIGH - six exact matches plus eleven best-layer comparisons re-derived,"MED-HIGH - sec 5.5 justifies reporting layer 40 everywhere else, and layer selection is a live audit issue (Phase 2 plan W1)","audit/scripts/claims/P11_abstract.py (output audit/phase2/out/P11/P11_abstract.txt, P11_addendum.txt)",Deferred from batch P8. The transfer triple is the same as D-098/A-04; this row adds the balanced-accuracy triple and the best-layer check.,P11-abstract
O-001,The paper's sycophancy persona axis scores 0.374 on our capitulation dataset (sycophancy_mt) - below chance and worse than a random direction (0.541) - and the same axis family scores 0.300 on the knowledge-report dataset (HP-KR).,0.374; 0.541; 0.300,"docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:78-79 (ledger F-65 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2097-2099 and F-13 :44-48,223-224)","C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (md5 d7616aa50814267e38bd38931e25a6a0, 2026-09-19 20:12; byte-size-identical git working-tree copy used for the same reads); C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/passA11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json; .../passC11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json; C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (md5 76fee3969b41dcabb5a667b00107fd25)","zeroshot[direction='PC1'|'contrast'|'PC1:sycophancy'|'contrast:sycophancy'].auroc[sycophancy_mt|harm-pressure-knowledge-report]; results[feature,probe='paper'].auroc column mean (as target) and row mean (as source)","ledger F-65:2099 '0.374 ... worse than a random direction (0.541)'; F-13:220,223 '0.300' and 'SYC 0.541/0.633' - the briefing restates the ledger exactly",YES - every number and the (mis)attribution are copied from F-65/F-13,"zero-shot PC1 on sycophancy_mt = 0.3740 and contrast = 0.4089, but BOTH are the DECEPTION axis (27_crossgen.py:411 picks _zs_axis='deception'); the paper16 SYCOPHANCY axis reads 0.3061 (contrast) / 0.2996 (PC1) on sycophancy_mt and 0.1625 / 0.2768 on HP-KR. random = 0.5413 is the TRAINED random feature, sycophancy_mt as target. axes (paper16 stack, k=5, trained) = 0.3004 as source on full HP-KR, 0.3551 as target on sycophancy_mt.","own reader over the stored per-cell AUROC matrices; axis identity resolved from the bank's own keys (axes=['assistant','deception','sycophancy','unified']) plus the _zs_axis selection in src/assistant_axis_ndif/27_crossgen.py:411-428","lab originals, mtimes 2026-09-19 20:12 (passB kd11) and 2026-09-21 12:20/12:24 (passA11/passC11) - all before the 09-22 15:40-16:26 re-run wave (RF-13). No BH q quoted. Bank resolved by content (axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt), not by name.","the three numbers come from three DIFFERENT protocols: 0.374 zero-shot, 0.541 trained-as-target, 0.300 trained-as-source. The like-for-like trained pair is axes 0.3551 vs random 0.5413 (target) and 0.3787 vs 0.6327 (source), so 'worse than a random direction' survives a matched comparison. No zero-shot random direction exists in these stores.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - every value re-derived from the stored per-cell matrices; the axis identity is fixed by the producing script and by the bank's own key list,HIGH - it is the briefing's Claim 1 and the sentence the collaborator is asked to put in the paper,audit/scripts/claims/P12_local.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_local.txt); audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab.txt); audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab4.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab4.txt),"ATTRIBUTION ERROR, inherited from F-65. 0.374 is the paper16 DECEPTION axis's zero-shot PC1, not the sycophancy axis: in these files the bare 'contrast'/'PC1' rows are the bank's primary behaviour contrast, which 27_crossgen.py hardcodes to 'deception'. The paper16 sycophancy axis reads 0.3061/0.2996 on sycophancy_mt - i.e. WORSE, so the argument is unharmed and the number is wrong. Second issue: 0.374 (zero-shot) is compared against 0.541 (a trained probe on a random direction); the matched trained comparison is 0.3551 vs 0.5413. Third: 0.300 is the trained paper16 'axes' stack as SOURCE on full HP-KR, not a sycophancy-axis or zero-shot number (the sycophancy axis on HP-KR reads 0.1625/0.2768).",P12-briefing
O-002,"For the capitulation bank the filtered (judge score-3 only) and unfiltered banks give results that differ by 0.0004, so the judge filter does not drive the cap result.","0.0004 (plus the same table's +0.112, 95% CI [+0.050, +0.185], and 'positive at 21 of 21 layers')",docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:104-110 (ledger F-82 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3257-3271; F-66 :2221; F-77 :2884),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_s23/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json (21 files, mtimes 2026-09-21 03:48-13:41) and .../banks/cap_all/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json (21 files, 2026-09-21)","results[feature,probe='paper'].auroc, the 10 off-diagonal cells of the sycophancy_mt COLUMN; margin = pc:capitulation@2 minus datapca@2 (and minus raw)","F-82's table: margin at L40 +0.1542 (s23) vs +0.1538 (all), 21/21 both, CI [+0.0913,+0.2113] vs [+0.0907,+0.2118]","YES - the briefing's 0.0004 is F-82's difference, and the +0.112 / [+0.050,+0.185] / 21-of-21 rows are F-66 and F-77","L40: pc:capitulation@2 s23 0.7136 vs all 0.7132 (|diff| 0.0004); margin vs datapca@2 +0.1542 vs +0.1538 (|diff| 0.0004); margin vs raw +0.1123 vs +0.1118 (|diff| 0.0004). raw/datapca@2/random@2/length identical to 4 dp between banks. Own bootstrap (B=10,000, seed 42, resampling the 10 source datasets): -raw +0.1123 CI [+0.0502,+0.1847] P(<=0) 0.0000; -datapca@2 +0.1542 CI [+0.0913,+0.2113] P(<=0) 0.0000. Positive at 21/21 layers against BOTH raw and datapca@2, for both banks.","own loader + own paired dataset bootstrap (numpy default_rng(42), index resampling of the 10 sources), not importing cap/scripts/cap_layer_profile.py","lab only (run-cap / cap banks are in no branch; RF-10). Matrices dated 2026-09-21 03:48-13:41, before the 09-22 wave. Bank files resolved by path; no BH q quoted.","argmax median L36 (s23) / L32 (all), 95% [L28,L60] for both; L40 is the argmax in only 3.9% / 3.1% of resamples, so the band should be quoted rather than L40",HOLDS,HIGH - both banks recomputed cell by cell and the bootstrap reimplemented independently,"MEDIUM - it is a robustness row of Claim 2, not the claim itself",audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab.txt),"The 0.0004 is exact, and the rest of the Claim-2 table reproduces to 4 dp. One caveat the briefing does not carry: the batch P3 check of F-65 found that pc:cap_only@2 - the feature the 'basis needs the holding personas' argument rests on - differs between filters by 0.0142 at L40, not 0.0004. 'The judge filter does not drive it' is established for the headline feature; it is not true of every feature in the bank.",P12-briefing
O-003,"Under leave-one-CLUSTER-out (every dataset sharing the target's provenance removed from training) pooled training still beats single-source transfer by +0.129 (L20), +0.131 (L32), +0.125 (L40) over all eleven targets and +0.157 / +0.117 / +0.150 over the nine uncontaminated targets, positive on 8-11 of 11 at every layer.",+0.129; +0.131; +0.125; +0.157; +0.117; +0.150; 8-11 of 11,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:135-143 (ledger F-108 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:5140-5186),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/clustered/clustered_L{20,32,40}_mean_s42.json (md5 90eda6baec4ab35539fa9f0301baa068 / 73686f8ab57716d48a9ac003664f8af2 / 524c1340b2f7bd557cdce51aa84cabf7, mtimes 2026-09-22 16:58:55 / 16:59:17 / 16:59:39)","summary.all.gain_loco, summary.clean.gain_loco, summary.*.loco_positive; recomputed from per_dataset[t].pooled_loco - per_dataset[t].single_offdiag",stored summary: L20 all +0.12894 clean +0.15710 (loco_positive 10 / 9); L32 all +0.13087 clean +0.11681 (11 / 9); L40 all +0.12544 clean +0.15039 (10 / 8),YES for the six gains (briefing rounds to 3 dp); NO for the count phrase - see notes,"recomputed from the 11 per-target cells: L20 +0.1289 (all, 10/11) / +0.1571 (clean 9, 9/9); L32 +0.1309 (11/11) / +0.1168 (9/9); L40 +0.1254 (10/11) / +0.1504 (8/9). Clusters = lb_harm{HP-C,HP-KR,HP-KR-matched}, lb_scenario{ID,CG,IT}, apollo{ai_liar,roleplaying,sandbagging_v2}, mask, ours{sycophancy_mt}; leaked = HP-KR, HP-KR-matched.","own script: mean over the per-target pooled_loco and single_offdiag entries, and an independent count of positive targets; the file's own summary block is printed alongside and agrees","lab only (run-premise is on no branch; RF-10). The clustered files were written 2026-09-22 16:58-16:59, i.e. AFTER the 15:40-16:26 boot-trigger wave (RF-13) - they are the F-108 run itself, not a re-run of an older result. No BH q quoted.","only three layers, one seed, one probe (paper), mean pooling - as F-108's own caveats say. The counter-intuitive clean>all ordering reproduces (L20 +0.157 vs +0.129; L40 +0.150 vs +0.125). HP-KR collapses 0.9674 (LODO) -> 0.6492 (LOCO) at L40 and 0.7090 -> 0.4311 at L20.",HOLDS (with one count phrase to fix),"HIGH - every gain recomputed from the per-target cells, and the file's stored summary agrees",HIGH - this is the corrected form of the briefing's strongest claim (Claim 3),audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab2.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab2.txt),"All six gains are exact. The phrase 'positive on 8-11 of 11 at every layer' mixes two denominators: over all eleven targets it is 10/11, 11/11, 10/11; over the nine clean targets it is 9/9, 9/9, 8/9. '8 of 11' is not measured anywhere. F-108's own table states both correctly; the briefing's one-line compression is what loses it.",P12-briefing
O-004,"The knowledge-report matched-slice persona margin at the pre-specified layer does not clear a dataset-level bootstrap: 95% CI [-0.069, +0.189].","[-0.069, +0.189]",docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:171 (ledger F-76 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2846),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/passA11/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json and .../passA11/banks/kd_s23/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json (160 files, mtimes 2026-09-21 12:20-13:28, originals)","80-layer profile of the matched-slice column; margin = axes minus datapca at L40; paired dataset bootstrap over the 10 transfer datasets, B=10,000, seed 42","F-76 states +0.0655, CI [-0.0693, +0.1887], P(<=0) 0.161 - the briefing rounds to [-0.069, +0.189]",YES,"already re-derived TWICE in this audit: batch P7 measured +0.0655, CI [-0.0693,+0.1887], P 0.1611; the lead's independent QA bootstrap (audit/scripts/qa_p7.py) measured +0.0656, CI [-0.0738,+0.1904], P 0.1646. Both agree the interval contains zero.","not recomputed a third time in this batch, by the lead's instruction; the two existing independent re-derivations used different loaders and different implementations of the same design","lab originals (passA11, 2026-09-21 12:20-13:28), untouched by the 09-22 wave; no BH q quoted","the verdict is robust to the control (datapca and raw both fail) and to the implementation (two bootstraps, different code); the argmax interval [L5,L79] and the label-permutation p=0.38 (O-005) point the same way",HOLDS,HIGH - settled by two independent re-derivations recorded in audit/claims/F-76.md and audit/PROGRESS.md,HIGH - it is the project's own strongest self-correction and the briefing reports it correctly,audit/scripts/claims/P7_lab.py f7576; audit/scripts/qa_p7.py (both pre-existing in this audit),"No re-derivation owed. The adjacent row of the same table, '95% interval [L5, L79] - 93% of the network', is also right: F-76 measures 74 of 80 layers = 92.5%.",P12-briefing
O-005,The matched-slice persona band does not survive a cluster-based label permutation test: p = 0.38.,0.38,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:173 (ledger F-84 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3357-3394),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/cluster_perm_kd_matched.json (md5 e43dba906883c2876d6decc40fe508ad, 5,168 B, mtime 2026-09-22 16:07:02)","keys p, B, observed_max_mass, observed_clusters, observed_margins, null_max_mass","file: p = 0.38, B = 200, observed_max_mass = 0.91552, observed_clusters = [0.91552, 0.05881], 20 layers",YES - exact,"p = 0.38 read verbatim from the stored artifact; the null distribution (200 draws of null_max_mass) spans 0.0000 to 3.9097, so the observed 0.9155 sits well inside it. Not re-simulated (B=200 permutations with probe refits is a re-run, not a recomputation).",Level 1 only for the p itself: the artifact is the output of src/assistant_axis_ndif/30c_cluster_perm.py and the permutation loop was not re-executed. The stored null and observed statistics were read and checked for internal consistency (p = fraction of null_max_mass >= 0.9155).,"lab only. WARNING: the file's mtime 2026-09-22 16:07:02 falls INSIDE the RF-13 boot-trigger re-run window (15:40-16:26), while F-84 is dated 2026-09-21 - so the artifact read here is a regenerated copy. Its p matches F-84's stated 0.38, and the run is seeded, so no discrepancy is visible; there is no pre-wave copy to compare against.","B = 200 is modest, as F-84's own caveat says. The briefing uses 'p = 0.38' TWICE, at :146 and :173 - they are two different tests (see notes), not a copy error.",HOLDS,"MEDIUM-HIGH - the number is exact in its artifact, but the artifact was rewritten inside the 09-22 re-run window and the permutation loop was not re-executed",MEDIUM - a supporting row of the 'what did not survive' table,audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab.txt),"Verified. Two things found on the way. (1) The briefing's OTHER p = 0.38, at :146 ('pooled ~6,700 rows and ~666 rows are statistically indistinguishable'), is a different test and its stored p is ONE-SIDED: 30b_premise_boot.py:62 computes p = (bs <= 0).mean(). My own two-sided bootstrap of pooled_lodo - pooled_lodo_match gives +0.0045, 95% CI [-0.0235, +0.0331], two-sided p 0.744 (one-sided 0.372) - same conclusion, but the quoted 0.38 is a one-sided tail and the CI is the statistic that supports 'indistinguishable'. (2) The same sentence's '~666 rows': the realised row-budget-matched LODO training pool is 412-500 rows (mean 449) per target; 666 is n_train.single_mean, the budget the control is CAPPED at (30_premise.py:167 per_o = budget // 10, then min(per_o, len(tr))). The control is therefore stricter than advertised.",P12-briefing
O-006,"The abstract's 0.904 / 0.916 are the ext_axis1 off_diagonal_mean values 0.9041173922 and 0.9158352735 in the collaborator's persona_ood_ext_L20/L40 summary.csv, identical to the mean of auroc_ext_axis in the matching zero_shot.csv to 1e-16; ext_axis1 is the 12-vs-13 extended contrast whose ten extra roles are the owner's knowledge-denial bank, matching kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json name for name, over the base bank paper16_L20_sharedquestions/paper16_L20.pt.",0.9041173922; 0.9158352735; 1e-16; 8+4 vs 7+6,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:199-216 (ledger F-97 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4384-4466),"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (and f386a72): src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv}; .../deception_detection/persona_pcs.py; .../deception_detection/scripts/persona_ood.py - all read with `git show`, no checkout. Plus kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json (asix working tree).",summary.csv row features='ext_axis1' column off_diagonal_mean; mean of zero_shot.csv column auroc_ext_axis over the 6 scored datasets (the Alpaca control row XXXX-*__plain has empty AUROCs and is dropped); persona_pcs.py:31 BANK_PATH; persona_pcs.py axes['extended'],"summary.csv verbatim: L20 0.9041173922099752, L40 0.9158352734669751 - identical at f386a72 and at the branch head 45b16d9",YES - the briefing truncates both to 10 decimal places and loses nothing,"mean(auroc_ext_axis) = 0.904117392209975 (L20) and 0.9158352734669751 (L40); |difference| from off_diagonal_mean = 2.220e-16 (L20) and exactly 0.000 (L40). Arms: persona_pcs.py axes['extended'] = mean_of(DECEPTION_PERSONAS + KNOWLEDGE_DENIAL_PERSONAS) - mean_of(HONESTY_PERSONAS + KNOWLEDGE_CANDOUR_PERSONAS), i.e. 8+4 = 12 vs 7+6 = 13. His 10 extra role names are SET-IDENTICAL to the owner's knowledge_denial (4) + sincere_ignorance (3) + plain_assertion (3); symmetric difference empty. persona_pcs.py line 31 is exactly BANK_PATH = REPO_ROOT / 'paper16_L20_sharedquestions' / 'paper16_L20.pt'.",own script: every mean recomputed from the per-dataset rows of zero_shot.csv rather than read off summary.csv; role names parsed out of his source and compared as sets against kd_role_groups.json,"collaborator's branch, read out of git at both f386a72 (the commit the ledger cites) and the current head 45b16d9 - the persona_ood_ext results are identical at both. His activations are gone, so the AUROCs themselves are Level 1 by the owner's decision (RF-2).","the same identity holds for denial_axis1 (|diff| 1.11e-16 at L20, 0.0 at L40) but NOT for axis1 at L20 (|diff| 1.398e-01), because one training set disagrees on the sign - so 'the trained off-diagonal equals the zero-shot mean' is a property of sign-consistent 1-d features, not a general one",HOLDS,HIGH - digits read verbatim from his committed CSV and every mean recomputed from the per-dataset rows,HIGH - it is the correction the briefing exists to deliver,audit/scripts/claims/P12_local.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_local.txt),"Digits and attribution both check out. Three wording fixes for the sentence around them. (1) The briefing cites `scripts/persona_ood.py::extended_arms()`; the file is at deception_detection/scripts/persona_ood.py, and extended_arms() re-FITS the geometry - the axis itself is defined in deception_detection/persona_pcs.py (axes['extended']). (2) 'they match kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json name for name' is true of the NAMES but not of the GROUPING: his KNOWLEDGE_CANDOUR_PERSONAS merges the owner's two distinct honest groups, sincere_ignorance (3) and plain_assertion (3), into one six-role arm. (3) 'identical ... to 1e-16' is exact at L40 (0.0) and 2.2e-16 at L20, i.e. 1 ulp above the stated bound - harmless, but 'to within 1e-15' would be safer.",P12-briefing
O-007,"On the collaborator's six datasets, zero-shot, the paper's 8-vs-7 contrast beats his trained single-source baseline by +0.143 at layer 20 and +0.100 at layer 40.",+0.143; +0.100,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:220-228 (ledger F-97 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4384-4466),"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (and f386a72): src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40}/{zero_shot.csv,summary.csv,matrix_baseline.csv}, read with `git show`","mean of zero_shot.csv auroc_axis over the 6 scored datasets, minus summary.csv row features='baseline' column off_diagonal_mean","F-97's table: baseline 0.6478 / 0.7320, axis1 0.7909 / 0.8319, margins +0.143 / +0.100",YES,"L20 axis1 zero-shot mean 0.7908803603 - baseline 0.6477701197 = +0.1431; L40 0.8318937061 - 0.7320 = +0.0999. Extended-contrast margins +0.2563 / +0.1838; kd personas worth +0.1132 / +0.0839 = 44.2% / 45.7% of the headline margin. Dropping repe_honesty against the 5-dataset baseline (0.6085 / 0.7064): axis1 margin +0.1418 / +0.0919, kd worth +0.1364 / +0.1007 - the briefing's '+0.142 / +0.092' and '+0.136 / +0.101'.","own script: the baseline recomputed independently as the off-diagonal mean of matrix_baseline.csv (n=30 over six datasets, n=20 over five) and cross-checked against summary.csv's own value; the zero-shot means recomputed from the per-dataset rows",collaborator's branch at f386a72 and at head 45b16d9 - identical. Level 1 by the owner's decision on his activations (RF-2).,"the whole §5(a) table re-derives: 0.6478/0.7320 baseline, 0.7909/0.8319 axis1, 0.9041/0.9158 ext_axis1, +0.256/+0.184, 44%/46% share. The drop-repe_honesty variant needs the 5-dataset baseline (0.6085/0.7064); against the 6-dataset baseline the margins would be +0.1026/+0.0662, so the briefing's reading is the correct one.",HOLDS,"HIGH - recomputed from the per-dataset rows and from the raw transfer matrix, at two commits",HIGH - it is the number that separates the paper's own contrast from the abstract's headline,audit/scripts/claims/P12_local.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_local.txt),"Exact. The one thing worth adding to the briefing is which baseline the drop-repe_honesty row uses: +0.142 / +0.092 are against a baseline recomputed over the five remaining datasets (0.6085 / 0.7064), not against the six-dataset baseline printed one row above.",P12-briefing
O-009,"Rebuilt on our eleven datasets, both of the collaborator's zero-shot arms lose to a pooled leave-one-dataset-out probe - by 0.064 at layer 20 and 0.055 at layer 40.",0.064; 0.055,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:243-252 (ledger F-98 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4469-4542),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/mean_L{20,40}_s42.json (md5 .../3f9fe86b652dda3aa89b18d9466371c5 at L40, mtimes 2026-09-22 00:33); C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/premise_L{20,40}_mean_s42.json (md5 d975eb33f26f328bede48aa7f9b6e03a / e5ddaaa13ea6aa5a4b97bbafa38592ba, 2026-09-21 14:35 / 14:26); baseline C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L{20,40}_s42.json",zeroshot['contrast'] and zeroshot['contrast:collab_extended'] means over the 11 datasets; summary.pooled_lodo from the premise files,F-98's table: L20 pooled 0.8027 vs ext 0.7386; L40 0.8545 vs 0.7996 - i.e. -0.064 / -0.055,YES,L20: pooled LODO 0.8027; axis1 0.6572 (gap +0.1455); ext_axis1 0.7386 (gap +0.0641). L40: pooled LODO 0.8545; axis1 0.7325 (gap +0.1219); ext_axis1 0.7996 (gap +0.0548).,"own reader: zero-shot means recomputed from the 11 per-dataset entries, pooled figure read from the premise summary key, raw baseline recomputed as the mean of the 110 off-diagonal cells","lab only. collab matrices 2026-09-22 00:33 (the 00:52-01:33 sweep window, before the 15:40 wave); premise files 2026-09-21 14:26/14:35, untouched by the wave. No BH q quoted. Bank composition was verified inside axes_collab_s23.pt by batch P3 (12 v 13, vectors_dir run-kd/vectors_s23).","pooled LODO beats ext_axis1 at all 21 stored layers under mean pooling, by +0.0396 (L0) to +0.1202 (L60); the gap is smallest at L40 (+0.0548) and L22 (+0.0482), so quoting L20/L40 is if anything conservative",HOLDS,HIGH - both sides recomputed from the per-dataset raw values on the lab copies,HIGH - it is the briefing's central argument against the abstract's framing,audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab.txt),Both numbers exact. Wording only: 0.064 and 0.055 are the gaps for the EXTENDED arm alone; the paper's 8v7 arm loses by 0.146 (L20) and 0.122 (L40). 'Both of your arms lose ... by 0.064 and 0.055' reads as if the pair covers both arms; it is the smaller of the two gaps in each case.,P12-briefing
O-011,"The knowledge-denial bank is worth +0.055 mean-pooled and +0.059 last-token (ext_axis1 minus axis1, zero-shot, our eleven datasets), positive at 21/21 and 20/21 layers respectively, the single exception being L0, the embedding layer.",+0.055; +0.059; 21/21; 20/21; L0,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:263-270 (ledger F-99 kd/docs/FINDINGS.md covers the mean-pooled half only),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json (42 files, mtimes 2026-09-22 00:33-00:49 and 02:07-02:11); baseline C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json (2026-09-19 20:12-20:58)","zeroshot['contrast:collab_extended'].auroc mean minus zeroshot['contrast'].auroc mean, over the 11 datasets, at each of the 21 stored layers, under each pooling","F-99 states the mean-pooled half (+0.0551, 21 of 21, range [+0.0019 L0, +0.0814 L20]); the LAST-TOKEN half is stated only in the briefing - audit/claims/F-99.md records 'Last pooling was not swept'",PARTIAL - the mean-pooled half matches F-99 exactly; the last-token half has no ledger entry behind it and is checked here for the first time,"mean pooling: ext - axis1 positive at 21/21 layers, mean +0.0551, range [+0.0019 (L0), +0.0814 (L20)]. last-token: positive at 20/21, mean +0.0590, range [-0.0327 (L0), +0.0848 (L36)]; the only non-positive layer is L0.","own reader over all 42 collab matrices, recomputing each zero-shot mean from the 11 per-dataset entries; no summary line read","lab only; the last_L* collab matrices are dated 2026-09-22 02:07-02:11 and the mean_L* 00:33-00:49, all before the 15:40-16:26 wave (RF-13). No BH q quoted.","the claim's own robustness check: under last pooling the peak moves from L20 (mean) to L36, and the range widens; but the size of the effect is stable (+0.0551 vs +0.0590) and the sign holds everywhere except the embedding layer",HOLDS,HIGH - the mean-pooled half reproduces F-99 exactly and the last-token half is re-derived here from the raw matrices,HIGH - it is the layer/pooling robustness that the briefing offers in place of a two-layer quote,audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab.txt),"Exact, including 'the single exception is L0'. NOTE FOR THE LEDGER, not the briefing: the last-token sweep has no F-entry - F-99 is explicitly a mean-pooling claim (audit/claims/F-99.md) - so this briefing line is currently the only place the 20/21 result is written down.",P12-briefing
O-012,"The SHARE of the margin over raw attributable to the knowledge-denial bank is unstable: it reads 2%-114% across depth with a median of 63% mean-pooled and 50% last-token, while the underlying difference barely moves (+0.055 vs +0.059).",2%; 114%; 63%; 50%; +0.055; +0.059,"docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:272-278 (ledger F-99, mean-pooled half only)","C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json; raw baseline C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json","share = (ext_axis1 - axis1) / (ext_axis1 - raw), where raw is the off-diagonal mean of results[feature='raw',probe='paper'] over the 110 pairs, at each of the 21 layers","F-99 states median 62.9%, mean 63.8%, range [2.2%, 113.9%] for mean pooling; it states nothing for last-token",PARTIAL - the mean-pooled figures match F-99 exactly; the 50% last-token median has no ledger entry,"mean pooling: median 62.9%, mean 63.8%, range [2.2% (L0), 113.9% (L68)]. last-token: median 50.0%, mean 48.0%, range [-155.9% (L0), +144.9% (L8)]. Underlying difference +0.0551 (mean) vs +0.0590 (last).",own reader: every share recomputed from the three recomputed quantities at each layer; the raw baseline recomputed from the 110 off-diagonal cells of the matching baseline matrix under the SAME pooling,"lab only, same files and mtimes as O-011, all pre-wave","the instability the claim asserts is real and is larger than stated once pooling is varied: under last-token pooling the share goes NEGATIVE at L0 (-155.9%) and exceeds 144% at L8, because the denominator (ext - raw) shrinks where the arms sit near raw",HOLDS,HIGH - both poolings recomputed from the raw matrices,MEDIUM-HIGH - it is the caveat that tells the collaborator not to quote a share,audit/scripts/claims/P12_lab.py (output audit/phase2/out/P12/P12_lab.txt),"63% and 50% are exact (62.9% and 50.0%). One scoping point: the range '2%-114%' is the MEAN-POOLED range; the sentence puts it before 'mean-pooled', so a reader can take it as covering both poolings. Under last-token the range is -156% to +145%. Adding 'mean-pooled' before the range, or giving both ranges, would make the sentence airtight - and the wider last-token range strengthens the point the sentence is making.",P12-briefing
S-01,"The four paper16 axes in run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3.pt are unnormalised difference-of-means vectors; at layer 20 their norms are assistant 1.012, deception 1.0037, sycophancy 1.535, unified 0.9722, so sycophancy is ~50% longer and raw projection magnitudes are not comparable across axes. PCA components are unit-norm; the 26 persona vectors have norms min 3.94 / median 4.21 / max 4.36.",assistant 1.012; deception 1.0037; sycophancy 1.535; unified 0.9722; PCA norms 1.0; persona vectors min 3.94 / med 4.21 / max 4.36,session transcript b5504aba:1091 (2026-09-18T10:22:10Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,"run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3.pt; run-paper16/vectors_s3/*.pt (26 files, laptop/git copy)","axes.{assistant,deception,sycophancy,unified}[20] L2 norm; pca_components[20] norms; per-role vectors [20] norms","n/a - print-only, no result file was ever written",n/a,"L20: assistant 1.0120, deception 1.0037, sycophancy 1.5350, unified 0.9722; PCA component norms 1.0 (global 0.999999-1.000001); persona vectors min 3.9443 med 4.2126 max 4.3562","own script: per-layer L2 norms over all 80 layers, layer identified by best match; axes re-derived as mean(pos roles)-mean(neg roles) from the 26 per-role vectors using the bank's own role_groups - reproduces every stored axis with max|diff| = 0.000e+00","laptop/git copy = the OLD pre-fp32 paper16 bank (RF-12/RF-15). RF-15 measured old-vs-fp32 cosine 1.0000 at every layer, max relative norm diff 0.49-0.91%, i.e. ~60x smaller than the effect. Not touched by RF-13.","sycophancy is the longest axis at ALL 80 layers (median norms 3.802 vs 2.297/2.433/2.389 = 56-66% excess); transcript layer was unstated, resolved to L20 (sum|diff| 1.4e-4)",HOLDS,HIGH - exact reproduction plus a bit-exact structural re-derivation from the per-role vectors,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/S-01_S-02_norms.py; S-01_norms2.py; S-01_vecnorms.py; S_docgrep.sh,"ABSENT FROM BOTH the owner's ledger and the collaborator's draft: zero hits for 1.535 / 1.0037 / 0.9722 / 4.2126 / 3.9443 in kd/docs, docs, cap/docs, audit/phase0/draft_text.txt, draft_report.md, collab_abstract_2026-09-21.md and the memory notes; a concept search (axis norm / not comparable / without normalising) is also empty. The collaborator was given these vectors to dot-product against his own activations. AUROC is rank-based so per-axis rankings are safe, but any cross-axis magnitude comparison, sum, average or shared threshold is confounded by a 53% length difference.",P13-session
S-02,"Same measurement stated as the methods conclusion, plus the self-correction that deception's norm landing at 1.0037 was a coincidence rather than evidence the bank was normalised; sycophancy at 1.535 means projections are not comparable across axes without normalising.",deception 1.0037; sycophancy 1.535,session transcript b5504aba:1094 (2026-09-18T10:22:19Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3.pt; run-paper16/vectors_s3/*.pt,axes.*[L] norms over all 80 layers; re-derivation from role vectors,n/a - print-only,n/a,"bank is unnormalised: mean(pos)-mean(neg) reproduces every axis with max|diff| 0.000e+00. deception norm over 80 layers: min 0.0247, median 2.4330, max 7.0293 - it passes through 1.0037 only at L20. sycophancy/deception at L20 = 1.529.",own script; per-layer norm sweep + bit-exact re-derivation,"as S-01 (old paper16 bank; version difference <=0.91% in norm, cosine 1.0000)",sycophancy longest at all 80 layers; the near-1.0 deception norm is specific to L20,HOLDS,HIGH - both halves of the correction verified from raw data,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/S-01_norms2.py; S-01_vecnorms.py,ABSENT FROM BOTH ledger and draft (same searches as S-01). This is the sentence that should have gone into a methods section and exists only in chat.,P13-session
S-03,"The kd bank's build report printed six axis norms at L40 (assistant 1.707 ... kd_assertion 4.342), a group-mean projection table, PC1 variance shares of 44.6/46.0/35.1% for the deception/sycophancy/unified bases, and a 'default' anchor sitting at relative position 0.882 on PC1 where the Assistant-Axis construction expects an extreme.",assistant 1.707; deception 2.204; sycophancy 3.456; unified 2.268; knowledge_denial 3.274; kd_assertion 4.342; anchor 0.882; PC1 var 44.6/46.0/35.1%,session transcript b035ccb3:2436 (2026-09-20T05:50:20Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt; C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/vectors_s3/*.pt (36 roles),"axes.*[40] L2 norms; pca.{deception,sycophancy,unified}.variance_ratio[40][0]; projection of the 36 role vectors on pca_components[40][0], position of role 'default'",n/a - the numbers were printed to logs/kd_axes.log; no structured result file,n/a,"assistant 1.7071, deception 2.2036, sycophancy 3.4561, unified 2.2684, knowledge_denial 3.2741, kd_assertion 4.3424; PC1 var 0.4456 / 0.4602 / 0.3511; default anchor relative position 0.8820 (0.8820 also mean-centred); all-roles PCA PC1 0.2564, top-5 0.6924","own read-only script on the lab PC: loads the bank, recomputes norms and PCA shares, re-projects all 36 per-role vectors (mtime 2026-09-20, untouched) onto PC1 and computes (proj-min)/(max-min)","lab copy; the .pt carries mtime 2026-09-22 15:41 i.e. it WAS rewritten in the RF-13 boot wave, but reproduces the 09-20 printed numbers exactly and its source vector directory is 09-20 - evidence the rewrite was idempotent for this file","|cos(PC1, assistant)| across all 80 layers: min 0.5387, median 0.5989, max 0.7077 - below the Assistant-Axis paper's thresholds at most depths, not only at the layer F-11 quotes (0.583)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the numbers (all re-derived); HIGH for the doc check,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/S-03_S-04_lab.py -> audit/phase2/out/S-03_S-04.txt,"NUMBERS HOLD; the meta-claim 'neither is in any doc' FAILS. kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-11 (lines 179-196) already records the group-mean projection table, the 1.82 gap, cos(PC1,assistant)=0.583 and verbatim 'the default anchor sits at 0.882 rather than an extreme'. What IS unrecorded anywhere (ledger, docs, draft, memory) is the six axis norms - and the comparability problem is larger here than on paper16: kd_assertion 4.342 vs assistant 1.707, a factor of 2.54.",P13-session
S-04,"A second kd axes bank, run-kd/axes_vectors_all.pt, built from ALL rollouts with no score-3 judge filter, was written alongside axes_vectors_s3.pt and is named in no document.",n/a (file provenance),session transcript b035ccb3:2436 (2026-09-20T05:50:20Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/axes_vectors_all.pt (94,402,250 B, mtime 2026-09-22 15:41); .../axes_vectors_s3.pt; run-coords/passA/*/{chunk_*.pt,rows.jsonl}; audit/phase2/provenance.csv",vectors_dir field; axes.*[L] norms and cosines; zero-shot AUROC of each axis on the same passA rows under both banks,"file exists; vectors_dir = run-kd\vectors_all; same 36 roles, same counts (1v35, 8v7, 5v5, 13v12, 4v3, 4v3) and the same six axes + six PCA bases as the s3 bank",yes,"L40 axis norms s3 vs all: assistant 1.7071/1.5753 (cos 0.9814), deception 2.2036/1.7977 (0.9715), sycophancy 3.4561/3.1708 (0.9941), unified 2.2684/1.9838 (0.9837), knowledge_denial 3.2741/2.8189 (0.9900), kd_assertion 4.3424/3.6654 (0.9832); PC5 of the all-roles basis |cos| 0.089. SUBSTITUTION on identical rows (10 datasets, L20/40/44): dataset-averaged zero-shot AUROC moves <=0.026 for every axis, BUT on harm-pressure-kr-matched kd_assertion falls 0.7173->0.5955 at L40 and 0.6211->0.4416 at L20 (below chance); knowledge_denial IMPROVES without the filter (+0.020 at L40)","own read-only lab scripts: bank comparison, then streaming run-coords/passA chunk by chunk, keeping the mean-pooled layer slice and scoring the same rows with both banks","both .pt files rewritten 2026-09-22 15:41 (RF-13); their source vector directories (vectors_all 09-20 02:26, vectors_s3 09-20 03:04) were not touched, and the s3 bank reproduces its 09-20 printed numbers, so the rewrite was idempotent",three layers (20/40/44) and 10 datasets tested; the kd_assertion effect is present at all three layers on the matched slice and absent elsewhere,HOLDS,HIGH - file facts and the substitution both measured during this audit,MEDIUM-HIGH,"audit/scripts/claims/S-03_S-04_lab.py; S-04_subst_lab.py; S-04_size.py -> audit/phase2/out/S-03_S-04.txt, S-04_subst.txt","ABSENT FROM BOTH ledger and draft: grep -rn 'axes_vectors_all' over kd/, cap/, docs/, src/ hits only run-paper16's file (paper16_supervisor.ps1:53, pc_gate.py:12). The bank was also NEVER USED: audit/phase2/provenance.csv records the bank_field inside every matrix store and run-kd/axes_vectors_all.pt appears in none. There are in fact FOUR kd banks on the lab (all, s3, s23, collab_s23). F-10's 'the s3 bank is drift-selected' and F-11's 'the s23 arm is the control' therefore have a third, untouched arm on disk, and it is the one that decides whether the kd_assertion axis on the matched slice is real (0.7173) or below chance (0.4416 at L20).",P13-session
S-09,"The first Q2 signal (3 datasets sharing instructed_intent, 6 off-diagonal pairs, LAYER 40 mean pooling k=5, paper16 s3 bank) included an 'axes residualised' arm at 3 dimensions that transferred at 0.419 / 0.408 - inverted, and ~0.29 below a random 5-d subspace. Those numbers are in no doc.",axes_resid 0.419 / 0.408; axes 0.470 / 0.432; random subspace 0.706 / 0.693; raw 0.738 / 0.659; label-shuffle null 0.479 +/- 0.062; (smoke2) pc:deception 0.822 / 0.799,session transcript 6d4b2181:4695 (2026-09-15T11:11:10Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,run-coords/smoke.json; run-coords/smoke2.json (git working-tree copies),"p1[feature,probe].matrix off-diagonal cells; null.mean / null.sd; layer/pooling/k/bank/datasets header fields","smoke.json off_diagonal fields: raw 0.7384/0.6589, axes 0.4704/0.4317, axes_resid 0.4191/0.4083, random 0.7062/0.6925; null 0.47852 +/- 0.06185. smoke2.json adds pc:deception 0.8220/0.7993 and pc:unified 0.5501/0.5060",yes - every quoted value matches to the precision used,"identical when the off-diagonal means are recomputed cell by cell from the stored 3x3 matrices (raw 0.7384/0.6589, axes 0.4704/0.4317, axes_resid 0.4191/0.4083, random 0.7062/0.6925, n=6 each); raw diagonal 0.9820; worst axes_resid cell HP-KR->instructed-deception 0.0577",own script re-averaging the per-cell matrices rather than reading the stored off_diagonal field,"git working-tree copies of run-coords/smoke.json and smoke2.json; bank recorded inside as axes_vectors_s3.pt = the OLD paper16 bank (RF-12/RF-15: cosine 1.0000, norms within 0.9% of the fp32 rebuild). Not touched by RF-13.","single seed, 3 datasets, 6 pairs, all sharing instructed_intent label semantics; the session's own three caveats still apply and it said 'please don't quote these yet'",HOLDS,HIGH - artefact survives in the repo and every number recomputes,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/S-09.py,"INVENTORY CORRECTION: audit/claims_inventory.csv records this claim at layer 20; the transcript says 'Layer 40, mean pooling, k=5, paper16 score-3 bank'. It is a LAYER 40 result. Recorded elsewhere only at OTHER settings: axes_resid 0.324/0.214 (kd bank) in kd/docs/REPORT.md:81 and DESIGN.md:28, 0.770/0.553 (5 datasets, L20) in docs/thesis/...:551 and memory persona-set-decides-detection.md. The 3-dataset L40 values 0.419/0.408 and the pc:unified 0.5501/0.5060 from the same run are in NO document and in NO F-entry, and in no part of the collaborator's draft.",P13-session
S-11,"On the collaborator's own committed L20 transfer matrices, dropping the in-distribution repe_honesty row and column makes the paper-faithful 8-vs-7 deception contrast (axis1) score 0.5900 against the single-source baseline's 0.6085 - i.e. BELOW the baseline it is meant to beat, by -0.0185.",axis1 (repe_honesty dropped) 0.5900 vs baseline 0.6085; delta -0.019,session transcript 1ac8bb19:218 (2026-09-21T17:23:54Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood: src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40}/matrix_{baseline,axis1,ext_axis1,pc1,denial_axis1}.csv, read with git show (no checkout)",off-diagonal mean of the 5x5 sub-matrix after removing the repe_honesty__plain row and column (20 cells),"L20: baseline 0.6085, axis1 0.5900 (delta -0.0185); with repe_honesty: baseline 0.6478, axis1 0.6511 (delta +0.0033)","yes - exact, at both f386a72 (the commit F-97 cites) and the branch head 45b16d9",not applicable - the collaborator's activations are gone; by the owner's decision everything resting on them is Level 1. All means were nevertheless recomputed cell by cell from his matrices rather than read off a summary line.,"own script: git show of the five matrix CSVs, off-diagonal mean with and without repe_honesty, at two commits",collaborator branch; results byte-identical at f386a72 and 45b16d9 (2026-09-22 12:45),the sign reversal is layer-20-specific: at L40 the same operation gives axis1 0.7983 vs baseline 0.7064 = +0.0919. pc1 behaves the same way at L20 (0.6669->0.6096). ext_axis1 (the kd-augmented contrast) stays far ahead: 0.8868 vs 0.6085.,HOLDS,HIGH - re-derived from his committed matrices at two commits during this audit,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/S-11.py,"S-11's own framing needs correcting: F-97 records NEITHER the two values NOR this delta. F-97 gives the trained baseline/contrast WITH repe_honesty (0.6478/0.7320 at FINDINGS.md:4405, 0.6511 in caveat (1) at :4452) and gives the drop-repe case only for the ZERO-SHOT margins (+0.142 / +0.092 at :4414). Grepping the ledger for 0.5900/0.6085/0.7064/0.7983 returns nothing. ABSENT FROM BOTH ledger and draft. Must be quoted as a TRAINED off-diagonal result, never against the abstract's zero-shot 0.904 - F-97's caveat (1) explains why (a probe trained on the inverted HP-KR row carries a flipped sign at L20).",P13-session
S-12,"At L40 mean pooling, paper probe, on the 10-dataset run-crossgen store, the unified persona PCs at k=2 beat raw by -0.034 on all ten datasets, +0.028 without sycophancy_mt and +0.046 within the seven instructed_intent datasets; the extra gain over dataset PCA on the weak cells is about +0.06. So the headline's sign depends on dataset composition.",-0.034 (10 ds); +0.028 (no sycophancy_mt); +0.046 (7 instructed); extra gain over dataset PCA ~+0.06,session transcript dc605d01:1287 (2026-09-17T16:10:45Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,run-crossgen/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json; run-crossgen/summary.json; run-crossgen/significance.json (git working-tree copies),"results[feature,probe=paper].auroc off-diagonal means over the three dataset subsets; summary.json records[].offdiag_mean_10 / offdiag_mean_9 / blocks['intent->intent'].mean_delta_vs_raw",summary.json: raw offdiag10 0.6652 / offdiag9 0.6906; pc:unified@2 offdiag10 0.6314 / offdiag9 0.7187; blocks intent->intent mean_delta_vs_raw +0.04570,yes,"recomputed from the per-cell arrays: all10 (90 cells) uni@2 - raw = -0.0338; without sycophancy_mt (72 cells) +0.0281; instructed7 (42 cells) +0.0457. Weak cells (raw<0.6, 32 cells): uni@2 +0.1825, datapca@2 +0.1175, random@2 +0.0555; uni@2 - datapca@2 on those cells = +0.0650.",own script recomputing every off-diagonal mean from results[].auroc; the 7 instructed datasets taken from src/assistant_axis_ndif/18_q5_semantics.py SEMANTICS,git working-tree copy; the lab copies were regenerated on 2026-09-22 (RF-13) but Phase 1's keyed diff found 0 differing metric values on common records and only dataset_q_bh changed in significance.json. No BH q quoted here. Bank recorded inside the file: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt.,"the composition effect holds under all three probes: lr_reg10 -0.0424 / +0.0152 / +0.0115; mms -0.0466 / +0.0241 / +0.0225. Single layer, single seed as stated.",HOLDS,HIGH - all three compositions recomputed cell by cell and independently confirmed by the store's own block summary,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/S-12_S-13.py,"Every supporting number in the same review message also reproduces: random@2 - raw -0.1744 with 19/90 cells won; 23 of 90 raw cells below 0.5; in-distribution 0.9674 raw -> 0.8386 unified@2; mask 0.8926->0.5245, sycophancy_mt 0.8874->0.6863; HP-KR row -0.3554; sycophancy row -0.3064 / column -0.2567; row_ci95 half-width 0.0078. ONE NEAR-MISS: the review quotes the dataset 95% interval as [-0.22, +0.17]; significance.json (and memory matched-control-kills-the-gain.md) give [-0.2308, +0.1789]. Nothing turns on it. THE -0.034 IS WIDELY RECORDED but the two ALTERNATIVE COMPOSITIONS (+0.028, +0.046) are in NO document and not in the collaborator's draft; without them 'the sign depends on composition' is a caution rather than a measurement.",P13-session
S-13,"On the L40 crossgen matrix the intent->intent block is +0.046 vs raw, the sycophancy_mt row is -0.306 and its column -0.257, the raw baseline has 23 below-chance off-diagonal cells of which 16 are significantly inverted, and the worst cell is convincing-game -> harm-pressure-knowledge-report at 0.051.","sycophancy row -0.306, column -0.257; 23 below-chance cells; 16 significantly inverted; worst cell 0.051; intent->intent +0.046; unified breaks 23 / rescues 14, 32 below chance",session transcript dc605d01:2177 (2026-09-17T22:37:45Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,"run-crossgen/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (results[].auroc, ci95_hi); run-crossgen/summary.json (records[].sign_flips, records[].blocks)","sign_flips for feature=raw, probe=paper; blocks['sycophancy as source'/'as target'/'intent->intent'].mean_delta_vs_raw","summary.json raw|paper sign_flips: below_chance 23, significantly_inverted 16, cells_below_0.35[0] = convincing-game -> harm-pressure-knowledge-report 0.0508525; blocks: sycophancy as source -0.30642, as target -0.25672, intent->intent +0.04570",yes,"recomputed independently: 23 below-chance cells (all off-diagonal); 16 with ci95_hi < 0.5; worst cell 0.0509; sycophancy row -0.3064, column -0.2567; intent->intent +0.0457. pc:unified@2: 32 below chance, 30 significantly inverted, rescues 14, breaks 23. datapca@2: 23 / 15 / 14 / 14. random@2: 48 / 39 / 11 / 36.","own script re-deriving the counts from the raw per-cell AUROC array and the matrix's own ci95_hi, after reading the definition at src/assistant_axis_ndif/27_crossgen.py:683-698",git working-tree copy; same RF-13 status as S-12; no BH q quoted; bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt,"other probes give lr_reg10 22 below-chance (worst 0.0498) and mms 18 (worst 0.0710), so 23/16 is probe-specific to the paper probe as stated",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the numbers; HIGH for the doc check,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/S-12_S-13.py,"NUMBERS ALL HOLD; the meta-claim 'those counts are in no doc' FAILS: docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md lines 1403-1414 carry the whole sign-flip table (raw 23/16; persona axes 31/28/14/22; unified PCs 32/30/14/23; dataset PCA 23/15/14/14) and name the 0.051 cell, and memory matched-control-kills-the-gain.md:24 repeats the counts. What IS unrecorded is the sycophancy row/column DELTAS as numbers (-0.306 / -0.257); the thesis doc gives that block as AUROC levels instead. None of it is in kd/docs/FINDINGS.md (no F-number) or in the collaborator's draft. DEFINITIONAL CAVEAT for the paper: 'significantly inverted' = the per-cell ROW-level bootstrap upper bound is below 0.5, not a dataset-level test; given F-74/F-76 it should be quoted with that qualifier.",P13-session
S-14,"The zero-shot random-direction null was run per dataset, not only pooled: at L40 mean pooling the paper16 deception axis beats the 1,000-direction 95th percentile on only 5 of 9 datasets, and is indistinguishable from a random direction on convincing-game, harm-pressure-choice, harm-pressure-knowledge-report and mask.","pooled deception 0.881 (p 0.001) vs random p95 0.764; true: ai_liar 0.937, insider-trading 0.980, instructed-deception 0.971, roleplaying 0.784, sandbagging_v2 0.845; false: convincing-game 0.788 (p 0.238), harm-pressure-choice 0.544 (p 0.771), HP-KR 0.644 (p 0.625), mask 0.467 (p 0.711)",session transcript dc605d01:231 (2026-09-17T06:27:39Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,"run-coords/zeroshot_nulls.json key corpus_L40_mean; C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/passB/*/{chunk_*.pt,rows.jsonl}; C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt","corpus_L40_mean.pooled and .per_dataset[ds].deception_axis.{auroc,p_vs_random,beats_random_p95} and .random_p95_auroc_dev",pooled 0.8809504 (p 0.000999) vs random p95 0.7636438; per dataset 0.9367/0.9803/0.9709/0.7842/0.8454 true and 0.7884 (p 0.2378) / 0.5439 (p 0.7712) / 0.6436 (p 0.6254) / 0.4669 (p 0.7113) false,yes - every quoted value matches the file to the digit,"recomputed from the raw activations: all nine deception AUROCs identical to 4 dp (0.9367, 0.7884, 0.5439, 0.6436, 0.9803, 0.9709, 0.4669, 0.7842, 0.8454); same 5-true / 4-false split on the same four datasets; pooled deception 0.8810 and assistant 0.1759 reproduced exactly once the pooling set is the 10 passB datasets excluding sycophancy_mt but INCLUDING the 2,000-row alpaca control","own reimplementation of src/assistant_axis_ndif/25_zeroshot_nulls.py on the lab PC: stream passB chunks, keep the L40 mean-pooled slice, unit-normalise the deception axis, 1,000 random unit directions (seed 42), compare on |AUROC-0.5|","result file = git working-tree copy of run-coords/zeroshot_nulls.json (2026-09-17 01:06); activations = lab run-coords/passB, not touched by RF-13; bank = axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt in both the original run and the recomputation","my 1,000 random directions are a different draw from the same seed, so p-values differ in the third decimal (e.g. convincing-game 0.2537 vs 0.2378) while every per-dataset verdict is unchanged. On HP-KR a random direction reaches |AUROC-0.5| >= 0.44 at the 95th percentile - almost any direction separates that dataset. mask at 0.4669 is inverted, not merely weak.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - nine AUROCs and the pooled pair re-derived from the raw activations during this audit,HIGH,"audit/scripts/claims/S-14_lab.py; S-14b_lab.py; S-14_size.py -> audit/phase2/out/S-14_null.txt, S-14b_pooled.txt","ALL MEASUREMENTS HOLD; the meta-claim 'the per-dataset breakdown is not in any doc' FAILS: docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md section 8.2 (lines 930-944) tabulates all nine datasets at L40 mean and L44 last with their random p95s and yes/no verdicts, and memory significance-and-random-nulls.md names the four failures. But there is NO F-NUMBER for it in kd/docs/FINDINGS.md and it is ABSENT FROM THE COLLABORATOR'S DRAFT, whose abstract leans on zero-shot AUROCs on exactly the datasets (HP-KR, convincing-game) where the paper16 deception axis is within the random null. COMPOSITION FACT worth carrying: the pooled 0.881 includes the alpaca control as 2,000 pure negatives and is 0.863 without it (docs/thesis:935 does label the row 'incl. alpaca'), so pooled and per-dataset figures are not directly comparable.",P13-session
S-29,"Across the full 80-layer passA11 sweep the persona axes lose more often than they win on the kd matched slice: axes beat raw at 28 of 80 layers and dataset PCA at 31 of 80, with a 16-layer contiguous positive run. The ledger's '37/80 (46%)' is not an observed count.","axes beats raw 28/80; axes beats datapca 31/80; longest contiguous positive run 16 layers; ledger (F-77, F-81) says 37/80 (46%)",session transcript b035ccb3:10333 (2026-09-21T07:42:15Z) - DOC-ONLY lead,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/passA11/matrices/*.json (root: raw, datapca) and .../banks/kd_s23/matrices/*.json (axes); kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2807, :2934, :3233 and F-76 point (c)","results[feature,probe=paper].auroc, row harm-pressure-kr-matched, diagonal skipped, mean pooling, 80 layers",ledger states both: FINDINGS.md:2807 (F-75a) '28 of 80 ... 31 of 80'; FINDINGS.md:2934 (F-77 table) and :3233 (F-81 table) '37/80 (46%)',CONFLICT within the ledger,"recomputed from the raw matrices: axes beats raw at 28 of 80 layers; axes beats datapca (root store) at 31 of 80; longest contiguous run with margin over datapca > 0 = 16 layers. Landmarks reproduce: L19 floor 0.3555, L20 -0.2161 vs raw, L22 +0.0823, L40 0.7393 (+0.0336 / +0.0655), L44 0.7321, L77 peak 0.7642 (+0.1296 vs datapca).","own read-only lab script mirroring kd/scripts/matched_profile.py: row mean over the other ten datasets, joining the bank store's axes column with the root store's raw/datapca columns",passA11/matrices mtime 2026-09-21 13:13 - NOT rewritten in the 09-22 boot wave; passA11/summary.json and significance.json were (15:56/16:00) but are not used here and no BH q is quoted. Banks recorded inside: axes_vectors_s23.pt (axes) and axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (root raw/datapca); 11 datasets per matrix.,"full 80-layer table saved to audit/phase2/out/S-29_profile.txt; the counts are exact, not estimated",HOLDS,HIGH - counted from the raw matrices during this audit,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/S-29_lab.py -> audit/phase2/out/S-29_profile.txt,"LEDGER ERROR CONFIRMED. The observed counts are 28/80 (vs raw) and 31/80 (vs dataset PCA), as F-75 point (a) says. F-77's headline comparison table and F-81's summary table both give the kd matched slice as '37/80 (46%)', which no sweep produces. The source is F-76 point (c): 'Fraction of layers with a positive margin, per resample: median 0.46, 95% [0.16, 0.75]' - a dataset-bootstrap MEDIAN FRACTION; 0.46 x 80 = 36.8 -> '37/80'. So the project's flagship contrast (kd matched slice vs cap bank) sets a resampled median against the cap bank's genuine observed 21/21. Correcting it to 31/80 (39%) makes the contrast LARGER, so the fix costs the owner nothing. SEPARATE TRAP for the lead: the bank store also carries a 'datapca' column and axes beats it at 0 of 80 layers; F-75 caveat (4) already warns about joining the wrong pair (raw is absent from bank matrices by construction). The matched control must come from the ROOT store.",P13-session
F-79,"At L40/mean/paper/seed42 over 11 datasets, a probe trained on the pooled rows of ten datasets and tested on a held-out eleventh scores 0.8545 vs single-source transfer 0.6763 (+0.178); row-budget-matched it still scores 0.8500 (+0.174), so the gain is diversity not data volume.",0.9506; 0.6763; 0.9447; 0.8924; 0.8545; 0.8500; +0.178; +0.174; cos R2 0.244; mahal R2 0.017; n=7336/414/666,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3045,"audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L40_mean_s42.json (lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/, md5-verified)","summary.{single_own_mean,single,pooled_full,pooled_match,pooled_lodo,pooled_lodo_match}; n_train; predictors","0.950642 / 0.676316 / 0.944721 / 0.892400 / 0.854475 / 0.850015; margins +0.178159 and +0.173698; cos R2 0.2440, mahal R2 0.0165; n_train 666/7336/414",YES (all |d|<=5e-5),not recomputed from activations,"Level 1 only: re-fitting needs run-coords/passB (lab, ~10GB) and would re-run the experiment. Caveat (4)'s class balances VERIFIED from logs/falsify.log (134/2000, 139/2000).","lab copy, mtime 2026-09-21 14:26:55, md5 == 20:56 census; NOT in the 09-22 RF-13 wave; covariance field null (pre-switch); no bank/persona involved",positive at 21/21 layers (F-81); 5/5 seeds +0.173..+0.198 (F-83); bootstrap clears on all 4 comparisons (F-80),HOLDS,HIGH - every quoted number reproduces from an md5-verified pre-regeneration file; producing script read line by line,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_premise_core.py,"The comparison table's persona numbers (F-03 0.752, F-65 0.714, paper16 pc:unified ~0.672) belong to other claims and were not re-derived.",P2-pooled
F-80,"A paired dataset-level bootstrap (unit=target dataset, n=11, B=10000, seed 42) on the L40 premise run gives pooled-LODO minus single-source +0.1782 [+0.1430,+0.2129] with P(<=0)=0; the volume control (LODO minus row-matched LODO) is +0.0045 p=0.378; pooling wins on 11/11 targets.","+0.1782 [+0.1430,+0.2129]; +0.1737 [+0.1256,+0.2239]; +0.0045 [-0.0234,+0.0325] p=0.378; +0.0962 [+0.0553,+0.1360]; 11/11; mask +0.072; HP-KR 0.972 (+0.279); sycophancy_mt 0.802",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3121,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L40_mean_s42.json (per_dataset block),"per_dataset.*.{single_offdiag,single_own,pooled_lodo,pooled_lodo_match}",all 11 per-target rows match to 3 dp; no CI exists in any premise JSON,YES for point estimates; CIs are console-only (in no file),"+0.1782 [+0.1430,+0.2129] P=0.0000; +0.1737 [+0.1256,+0.2239] P=0.0000; +0.0045 [-0.0234,+0.0325] P=0.3779; +0.0962 [+0.0553,+0.1360] P=0.0000; wins 11/11","re-implemented 30b_premise_boot.py's bootstrap (sorted names, default_rng(42), integers(0,n,(B,n)), paired diff, 2.5/97.5 pct) over the md5-verified per_dataset values","lab copy 2026-09-21 14:26:55, md5 == census; no BH q-value so RF-13's test-family issue does not apply","per-layer version clears at 21/21 (F-81); on the six-dataset subset the same bootstrap does NOT clear at L20 (+0.0926 [-0.0450,+0.2102] P=0.089) - n=11 is what makes this one tight",HOLDS,HIGH - Level 2: all four intervals reproduced digit-for-digit by an independent implementation,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_premise_core.py,"This recomputation also LOCATES F-83's '+0.143 to +0.213' CI that an earlier agent could not find: it exists in no file at all, only in console output, and is reproduced here exactly.",P2-pooled
F-81,"The pooled-training margin is positive at all 21 stored layers and all 21 clear the dataset-level bootstrap; range +0.128 (L4) to +0.184 (L52); 11/11 targets won at 13 layers, the rest 9-10/11 and all early or very late.",21/21 positive; 21/21 clear; +0.128..+0.184; 13 layers at 11/11; per-layer table L0/8/16/20/28/36/40/52/68/76,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3193,"audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L{0,4,...,76}_mean_s42.json (21 files)",summary.*; per_dataset.*,"all 10 tabulated layers match; two rounding slips: L40 pooled_lodo is 0.8545 (printed 0.855), L20 margin is +0.1705 (printed +0.171)",YES except the two rounding slips and the 'targets won' count,"21/21 positive; 21/21 CIs exclude zero; range +0.1279 (L4) to +0.1837 (L52); 11/11 targets won at 12 layers (20,22,24,28,36,40,44,48,52,56,68,72), NOT 13; the nine exceptions include L32 (10/11), which is mid-network","recomputed the per-layer paired dataset bootstrap (B=10000, seed 42) for all 21 layers; no CI is stored in any premise JSON","21 lab files, mtimes 2026-09-21 14:33-14:42, all md5 == 20:56 census; not in the RF-13 wave",F-83's 5 seeds at L40; the absolute LODO level does move with depth (0.659 at L0 to 0.860 at L36),PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - both headline counts confirmed by my own recomputation of all 21 intervals; the failing sub-claim is a direct count,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_premise_core.py,"Corrections owed: 'targets won at 13 of 21 layers' -> 12; 'the rest all early or very late' -> L32, the peak layer, is one of them; L40 lodo prints as 0.855 but is 0.8545.",P2-pooled
F-83,"The pooled-LODO margin at L40 is stable across five split seeds (+0.173 to +0.198, spread 0.025, inside the bootstrap CI width 0.070), and Ying et al.'s Mahalanobis predictor does not reproduce with either covariance (within-class R2 0.023, total 0.017, vs plain cosine 0.244).",+0.1728/+0.1979/+0.1845/+0.1782/+0.1777; spread 0.025; CI +0.143..+0.213; R2 0.244 / 0.023 / 0.017,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3290,"audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L40_mean_s{1,7,13,42,99}.json; run-premise/mahal/premise_L40_mean_s42{,_total}.json","summary.{single,pooled_lodo}; predictors.{cos,mahal_cos}.r2; covariance",margins +0.1728/+0.1979/+0.1845/+0.1782/+0.1777 (|d|=0.0000 on all five); cos R2 0.2440; mahal within 0.0230; mahal total 0.0165,YES,"seed spread 0.0250; recomputed bootstrap CI [+0.14295,+0.21291], width 0.0699",the CI F-83 quotes exists in no file; recomputed from premise_L40_mean_s42.json per_dataset with the 30b_premise_boot.py procedure,"the four extra-seed files and both mahal/ files were written 2026-09-22 15:55-15:57, INSIDE the RF-13 reboot wave and AFTER F-83 was written - yet they reproduce F-83's numbers to 4dp, so that regeneration was value-faithful. All md5 == 20:56 census. premise_L40_mean_s42.json has covariance=null (pre-switch), which is why its mahal R2 equals the _total variant's.",covariance choice cannot affect the seed margins: in 30_premise.py the covariance block runs after all probe fits/AUROCs and consumes no RNG. The Mahalanobis comparison is one layer only (pairwise cosines stored only at L40).,HOLDS,HIGH - all eight quoted numbers reproduce; the one number with no file was independently recomputed and matches,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_premise_core.py,"Answers the briefing's open question: the '+0.143 to +0.213' CI is F-80's console-only interval, not a file value; now verified.",P2-pooled
F-85,"On six datasets at L20/L40 (mean, paper, seed 42) pooled LODO reaches 0.7365/0.8683 and row-budget-matched 0.7654/0.8930, so the abstract's zero-shot contrast lead shrinks from +0.184 (vs its own single-source baseline) to +0.048 (vs our pooled LODO) to +0.023 (vs row-matched) at L40.",0.6439/0.6960 single; 0.7365/0.8683 LODO; 0.7654/0.8930 matched; 0.9630/0.9862 pooled-with-target; 0.9852 own; +0.184/+0.048/+0.023; +0.139 at L20; 0.811 our contrast,"kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3403 (ledger already marks it SUPERSEDED BY F-97, headline only)",audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/six/premise_L20_mean_s42.json; .../premise_L40_mean_s42.json,"summary.{single,pooled_lodo,pooled_lodo_match,pooled_full,single_own_mean}; datasets; n_train",L20 0.643890/0.736533/0.765431/0.962983; L40 0.696040/0.868340/0.892972/0.986211/0.985159; margins vs 0.916: +0.0477 and +0.0230,YES (all |d|<=4e-5),"dataset-level bootstrap on the six, never run before: L40 pooled_lodo-single +0.1723 [+0.1253,+0.2239] P=0.0000 CLEARS; L20 +0.0926 [-0.0450,+0.2102] P=0.0887 DOES NOT CLEAR (row-matched at L20 also does not: +0.1215 [-0.0507,+0.2294])","paired dataset bootstrap, unit=target dataset, n=6, B=10000, seed 42, same procedure as 30b_premise_boot.py","lab copies 2026-09-21 17:18:01/17:18:13, md5 == 20:56 census, NOT in the RF-13 wave, covariance=within; lab-only store (RF-10)","F-109 adds L32 (higher than L40 on all three arms); the row-matched-beats-full oddity is +0.0289 (L20), +0.0045 (L32), +0.0246 (L40)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH on the numbers; MEDIUM on the framing verdict because it depends on F-97 (another batch),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_six_why_falsify.py,"The '+0.184' is 0.916-0.732, both the collaborator's; our own single-source on the six at L40 is 0.6960, against which the same contrast leads by +0.220. NEW: at L20 - the layer F-85 calls the claim's strongest - our pooled-vs-single margin does NOT clear the bootstrap (P=0.089). The cross-reference '0.811 our contrast on the same six' comes from