F-86,"Averaging the ten unit-normalised single-source probe directions scores 0.8828 at L40, beating pooled joint training (0.8545, +0.028), budget-matched pooling (0.8062, +0.077) and single-source transfer (0.6763, +0.207); single-source directions are near-orthogonal (cos +0.051) while the pooled direction sits nearer them (+0.227), and the source-count curve rises and flattens.",0.6763; 0.8062; 0.8545; 0.8828; +0.028; +0.077; +0.207; cos 0.051 / 0.227; curve 0.673/0.740/0.782/0.815/0.820/0.864/0.809,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3467,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/why/why_L40_s42.json; audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json,mean_of_directions; pooled_lodo_matched; single_offdiag; cos_*; curve_vs_n_sources; pooled_lodo_match_draws; bootstrap.mean_of_directions-pooled_lodo_full,0.676316 / 0.806211 / 0.882830; cos 0.050599 / 0.227173; margins +0.0284 / +0.0766 / +0.2065; curve k=1..10 0.6729/0.7404/0.7815/0.7178/0.8148/0.8161/0.8196/0.8281/0.8644/0.8091,YES for every stated number,"comparator's 20 subsampling draws: mean 0.8344, range [0.7912,0.8736], sd 0.0200, max-min 0.0824; 30f's own printed verdict: margin INSIDE that spread. Stored dataset bootstrap for the +0.0284 margin: CI [+0.0045,+0.0523] (clears, lower bound 0.0045). real-real_unnorm = +0.0089.",read the 20 stored draws and the stored bootstrap from 30f_result2_audit.py's output file; re-applied the script's own comparison rule,"why (2026-09-21 17:24:36) and audit (20:59:35) lab files, both md5 == 20:56 census, neither in the RF-13 wave; no bank involved so RF-12/15/16 do not apply",F-95 sweeps the 0.8828 number over 21 layers x 3 seeds and it survives; the MARGIN over pooled training was never swept. F-86's caveat (3) 'no dataset bootstrap yet' is out of date - audit_L40_s42.json has one.,PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH on the numbers and the conflict; MEDIUM on how far to discount the +0.028 (the 0.0824 spread is of the budget-matched arm, not of the full arm the margin is measured against)",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_six_why_falsify.py,"THREE issues. (1) The +0.0284 'beats joint training' margin is smaller than its comparator's own 0.0824 subsampling spread; 30f_result2_audit.py printed exactly that sentence and F-86 does not carry it; the dataset bootstrap clears with a lower bound of only +0.0045. (2) NAME COLLISION: 'pooled LODO row-budget matched' is 0.8062 here but 0.8500 in F-79/F-80 at the same layer/pooling/probe/seed (two different scripts' budget implementations); against 0.8500 the margin is +0.033, not +0.077. (3) The source-count table omits k=4=0.7178, which is BELOW k=3=0.7815 and breaks the 'rising and flattening' description; k=6 and k=8 are also omitted.",P2-pooled
F-95,"The mean-of-directions result survives a three-null falsification battery over 21 layers x 3 seeds: all three nulls sit on chance (0.5052/0.5015/0.5041), 55 of 63 cells clear the best oriented null by >0.02, 51 of 51 at layers >=16 and 4 of 12 below, the eight failures being L0/L4/L8; peak is L36 (0.8916) not L40 (0.8872); real-budget10 averages +0.0171.","0.5052 [0.4840,0.5337]; 0.5015 [0.4799,0.5283]; 0.5041 [0.4848,0.5214]; 55/63; 51/51; 4/12; +0.0171 [-0.022,+0.067]; L36 0.8916 vs L40 0.8872; min gap -0.0221 (mis-specified gate)",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4225,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/falsify/falsify_L*_s*.json (63); audit/cache/labpc/logs/falsify.log; logs/falsify.status,"real; budget10; {gauss,cov,shuffled}.{raw,oriented}","nulls 0.5053 / 0.5019 / 0.5041 with the stated ranges exactly; 55/63, 51/51, 4/12; failing cells (0,42)(0,7)(0,13)(4,42)(4,7)(4,13)(8,42)(8,7); peak L36 0.8916; real-budget10 +0.0170 [-0.0218,+0.0673]; min gap over all 63 = -0.0221",YES everywhere except the L40 row (see level2/notes),"recomputed the gate quantity: min gap at layers >=16 is +0.1021, five times the 0.02 convention, so SURVIVES is correct and the logged FALSIFIED was the mis-specified gate. Also real-real_unnorm = +0.0089 at L40/s42 (F-95's 'worth +0.009').","re-derived the oriented gap per cell as max(gauss.oriented,cov.oriented,shuffled.oriented) exactly as run_falsify.ps1 does, then recounted; parsed the UTF-16 falsify.log to recover the original 2026-09-21 run",62 of 63 files md5-identical to the 20:56 census; falsify_L40_s13.json was REWRITTEN 2026-09-23 02:54 by the orphaned run_falsify.ps1 -Force (PID 48932) the audit's own RF-14 live test left running - which is still running (52/63 at 03:17),the shuffled null - the only one that could kill the result - lands at 0.5053; the 0.02 clear threshold is a convention with no test behind it (F-95 says so); surviving this battery does not rescue F-86's +0.028 margin over pooled training,HOLDS,HIGH - every count and null reproduces; the single discrepancy is 0.002 in size and traced to a file the audit's own interrupted call overwrote,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_six_why_falsify.py,"L40's null (0.7057 -> 0.7045) and budget10 (0.8663 -> 0.8684) differ because falsify_L40_s13.json was rewritten today; 'real' is unchanged (0.8830) and the L40 gap moves +0.1814 -> +0.1826, changing nothing. The original cell came from a pilot invocation (L20/L40 x 3 seeds, 2026-09-21 20:28-20:34) whose log block is truncated, so its null/budget10 cannot be recovered. FOR THE LEAD: the orphan process is still rewriting run-premise/falsify through L76.",P2-pooled
F-109,"On the same six datasets the premise run at L32 gives single-source 0.7203, pooled LODO 0.8965 and row-matched 0.9010, beating L40 on all three arms (+0.024/+0.028/+0.008), which cuts F-85's margin against the abstract's 0.916 from +0.023 to +0.015.",0.6439/0.7365/0.7654 (L20); 0.7203/0.8965/0.9010 (L32); 0.6960/0.8683/0.8930 (L40); +0.024/+0.028/+0.008; +0.015,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:5210,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/six/premise_L32_mean_s42.json (with the L20/L40 files),"summary.{single,pooled_lodo,pooled_lodo_match}",0.720334 / 0.896529 / 0.900992; deltas vs L40 +0.0243 / +0.0282 / +0.0080; 0.916-0.9010 = +0.0150,YES (all |d|<=3.4e-5),"dataset bootstrap on the six at L32: pooled_lodo-single +0.1762 [+0.1140,+0.2361] P=0.0000; row-matched-single +0.1807 [+0.1160,+0.2447] P=0.0000 - both clear, unlike L20","paired dataset bootstrap n=6 B=10000 seed 42, plus a header-field comparison (datasets, n_train 873/5238/544, probe, pooling, seed, covariance) against the L20/L40 files to confirm the three layers are the same configuration","lab file mtime 2026-09-22 16:55:53 - written the same evening as run-premise/clustered/, AFTER the RF-13 reboot wave, not during it; md5 == 20:56 census",the L32 six-dataset margin clears the bootstrap where L20's does not; the row-matched-beats-full oddity is smallest here (+0.0045),HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_six_why_falsify.py,"Inherits F-85/F-97's dataset mismatch (our six substitute ai_liar for the collaborator's repe_honesty), so the +0.015 is still not like-for-like against his abstract.",P2-pooled
F-94,"Over 21 layers on sycophancy_mt (paper probe, seed 42), swapping the six holding personas for topically unrelated ones (content effect) costs +0.0356 on average and rarely clears the per-layer dataset bootstrap, while removing them entirely (presence effect) costs +0.0730 and usually does - about 2:1 under mean pooling and ~1:1 under last-token, so F-89's '78%' and 'three-to-one' figures should not be quoted.","16-layer table L0-L56; content +0.0339/+0.0356; presence +0.0704/+0.0730; retention median 53%/51%, 22-93%, -278% at L12; content clears 4/16 and 3/21; presence 9/16 and 15/21 (13 consecutive L28-L76); L32 +0.056 / +0.170; last pooling +0.0346/+0.0373, peak 0.659 at L32 vs 0.752; retentions -349% and +2387%",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4107,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/{cap_s23,cap_ctrl}/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json (90 files, read-only on the lab)","results[feature=pc:capitulation@2 / pc:cap_vs_para@2 / pc:cap_vs_neutral@2 / pc:cap_only_ctrl@2 / raw, probe=paper].auroc, sycophancy_mt column","all 16 tabulated rows reproduce at 4dp (e.g. L32 0.7521/0.7558/0.6961/0.5825/0.6134; L40 0.7136/0.7229/0.6889/0.5935/0.6013); all per-layer content/presence values and all * marks reproduce; means +0.0339/+0.0704 (16) and +0.0356/+0.0730 (21); retention medians 53% and 51%; last pooling +0.0346/+0.0373, peak 0.6592 at L32, retentions -349% and +2387%",YES for every measured quantity; NO for three prose counts (see notes),"content clears 3/21 at L0,L12,L36 and 3/16; presence clears 15/21 (13 consecutive L28-L76) and 10/16; ordering strict 10/16, 'holding>neutral>none' 12/16, group reading 16/16","read the raw 11x11 AUROC matrices on the lab, took the sycophancy_mt column mean over the 10 sources (diagonal excluded), and re-derived every * with a paired bootstrap over the 10 sources (B=10000, seed 42). Retention formula reverse-engineered as (neutral-raw)/(holding-raw), confirmed on three published values (24% at L0, -278% at L12, 78% at L40).","all 90 cap matrices have lab mtimes on 2026-09-21; none in the 09-22 RF-13 wave. Both banks record bank=axes_s23.pt, which provenance.csv flags AMBIGUOUS; resolved by the launch command in run_cap_ctrl_layers.ps1 (--bank run-cap-ctrl/axes_s23.pt for cap_ctrl). k=5, frac_train=0.8, control=alpaca.","both poolings measured and agree in direction not size; one seed and one target throughout; the bootstrap unit is 10 source datasets, the smallest in the project (F-87's cap seed spread is of the same order as the content effect)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - recomputed from the raw matrices with the bootstrap re-derived and the retention formula confirmed on three published values,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_F94_lab.py,"THREE prose counts do not reproduce. (1) 'content clears at only 4 of 16 layers' -> 3 of 16 (L0, L12, L36); the entry's own table marks 3 and its 21-layer amendment says 3, so the 4 contradicts itself. (2) 'presence clears at 9 of 16' -> 10 of 16; the entry's own table marks 10. (3) 'the ordering paraphrase>=holding>neutral>none holds at 15 of 16 layers (L8 the single inversion)' is not reproducible under any reading: 10/16 strict, 12/16 ignoring paraphrase, 16/16 as groups; the inversions are tiny (<=0.011) so the qualitative ladder survives. Minor: 'raw 0.47-0.50 from L44 upward' - L76 raw under last pooling is 0.5055.",P2-pooled
F-96,"F-63's three-rung persona margin is a single-layer reading: layer-averaged, best(axes,pc:deception) minus dataset-PCA is +0.1197 (3B, 7 layers) / +0.1027 (8B, 8) against F-63's +0.2023 / +0.1147 at L16, L16 being the maximum of 3B's seven; and against raw with the feature held fixed the gain is negative at both small rungs (-0.0063, -0.0190).","+0.2023 / +0.1197 / [+0.014,+0.202] / 1st of 7; +0.1147 / +0.1027 / [+0.030,+0.166] / 4th of 8; +0.0794 at L40; axes-raw +0.0195/-0.0063/4-of-7, -0.0249/-0.0190/2-of-8, +0.0131; oracle best-raw +0.033 (7/7) and +0.009 (6/8); minimum +0.007; F-91's kd_s23 axes peak L44 0.6435, L40 0.6304, +0.0131",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4317,"audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv (W1, built from lab run-crossgen/scale_{3b,8b,70b} and scale_70b_paper16fp32)","store, pooling=mean, probe=paper, dataset_set=paper5, seed=42, k=3, feature in {axes, pc:deception, datapca, raw}, offdiag_mean","3B: L16 +0.2023, layer-mean +0.1197, range [+0.0136,+0.2023], rank 1 of 7; 8B: L16 +0.1147, layer-mean +0.1027, range [+0.0297,+0.1660], rank 4 of 8; 70B L40 +0.0794; axes-raw 3B +0.0195/-0.0063/4-of-7, 8B -0.0249/-0.0190/2-of-8, 70B L40 +0.0131; best-raw 3B +0.0328 (7/7), 8B +0.0089 (6/8); kd_s23 axes peak L44 0.6435, L40 0.6304, +0.0131","YES - every stated number reproduces, including both ranks","the parenthetical 'minimum +0.007' is axes-datapca (fixed feature, not best) at 3B L12 = +0.0067; 8B's minimum on the same reading is +0.0077. Under the 'best' reading the minimum is +0.0136.","recomputed every margin, layer-mean, range, positive-count and rank from the W1 per-layer off-diagonal means; searched the alternative readings (datapca vs datapca@2, best over 2 vs 3 features, both poolings, three probes) to locate the +0.007","layer_sensitivity.csv built 2026-09-23 02:55 from the lab stores. provenance.csv: scale_3b -> axes_3b.pt (paper16_3b, k=3); scale_8b -> axes_8b.pt (paper16_8b, k=3); scale_70b -> axes_vectors_s3.pt flagged AMBIGUOUS (that is RF-16). F-96's own numbers use the L40 paper16 cell and the 3B/8B paper16 banks, so RF-16 does not touch them (F-110 agrees: 'F-63 is unaffected').","the stated reading is mean pooling + paper probe; under mms the layer-means are +0.113/+0.099 and under lr_reg10 +0.115/+0.103, so the conclusion is probe-robust; under last pooling the 8B layer-mean collapses to +0.009",HOLDS,"HIGH - every number reproduces from the shared W1 table, including both ranks and the parenthetical minimum",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/p2p_F96.py,"ONE CAVEAT IS NOW STALE. F-96's caveat (1) says 'the 70B rung is still one layer; scale_70b holds only L40 at k=3'. scale_70b now holds 21 k=3 layers (the 2026-09-22 00:52-01:33 sweep, written after F-96). Across them the 70B layer-mean is +0.0791 on the kd bank as swept and +0.0550 like-for-like on the RF-16 repair store, so the monotone decline continues (+0.120 -> +0.103 -> +0.055) and L40 ranks 13th of 21. On the extended sweep the sentence 'the persona axis beats the matched control at every layer of every rung' fails at L0 (axes-datapca -0.0251 kd / -0.0184 paper16fp32; positive 20/21 and 18/21). This overlaps F-110/RF-16, which are other claims.",P2-pooled
F-13,"At layer 40, mean pooling, seed 42, paper probe, the paper16 persona-axis stack ('axes') is far below chance on the two datasets whose labels are not register: HP-KR reads 0.427 as target / 0.300 as source and sycophancy_mt 0.355 / 0.379, while a random 5-d projection beats it on both (0.698/0.659 and 0.541/0.633); zero-shot on sycophancy_mt the contrast reads 0.409 and PC1 0.374; dropping sycophancy_mt from the 11-dataset off-diagonal mean lifts raw +0.025 but axes +0.061 and pc:deception +0.069; pc:unified is not dragged down (0.672 vs raw 0.662).",0.427; 0.300; 0.355; 0.379; 0.698; 0.659; 0.541; 0.633; 0.409; 0.374; +0.025; +0.061; +0.069; 0.672; 0.662,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:217-234,run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git copy) and C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (lab copy),"results[feature,probe='paper'].auroc column/row means over the off-diagonal; zeroshot[direction].auroc[index of 'sycophancy_mt']","axes HPKR 0.4273/0.3004; axes SYC 0.3551/0.3787; random HPKR 0.6984/0.6590; random SYC 0.5413/0.6327; zero-shot contrast 0.4089, PC1 0.3740; lifts raw +0.0247, axes +0.0609, pc:deception +0.0693; pc:unified 0.6715 vs raw 0.6623",YES - all 15 numbers match to the 3 dp the entry uses,"identical (the 'level 1' values ARE the level-2 recompute: every figure was re-derived from the 11x11 per-cell AUROC matrix, not read from a stored summary field)","audit/scripts/claims/F-13.py recomputes each column mean (as target) and row mean (as source) over the 10 off-diagonal cells, and each off-diagonal mean over the 110/90 cells, directly from results[].auroc","git/laptop copy AND lab copy; byte-for-byte identical outputs (both runs pasted in the note). bank=axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, bank_name=paper16, k=5 (the fp32 re-extraction, RF-15). Not a BH q-value claim, so RF-13's family growth does not apply.","STRONG. Swept all 21 stored layers x 2 poolings: 'axes' as target on sycophancy_mt is <=0.50 at 21/21 layers (mean) and 21/21 (last); zero-shot PC1 on sycophancy_mt is below 0.50 at 21/21 layers in both poolings; random beats axes on sycophancy_mt at every layer in mean pooling. On HP-KR 'axes' as target is below 0.55 at 18 of 21 mean-pooled layers (exceptions L0 0.604, L44 0.535 is below, L76 0.648). L40 is NOT a flattering choice - it is mid-range.",HOLDS,"HIGH - every quoted number recomputed from the per-cell matrix on two independent copies, and the qualitative claim survives a full 21-layer x 2-pooling sweep","HIGH - this is the register diagnosis the whole cap line (F-65/F-66/F-89) was built to test constructively, and the owner's memory note 'persona axes encode register' rests on it","audit/scripts/claims/F-13.py (output: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-13_git.txt, F-13_lab.txt)","One wording check: 'pc:unified is the best persona feature at L40' is true on this file (pc:unified 0.6715 > pc:deception 0.6432 > axes 0.6408 > pc:unified@2 0.6396). The entry's own caveat 'one layer, one seed' understates how robust this particular finding is.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-31,"The kd bank's headline pc:unified - raw off-diagonal gain (+0.0757, paper probe, L40, mean pooling, 11 datasets) does NOT clear the dataset-level bootstrap: 95% CI [-0.006, +0.173], q_BH = 0.499; and across the whole bank only 6 of 4,032 tests clear, four of them negative (random being worse than raw).","+0.076; +0.0757; [-0.006, +0.173]; q 0.499; +0.0729; [-0.042, +0.184] q 0.610; +0.0847 q 0.467; -0.0272 q 0.902; 6 of 4,032; 4 negative; +0.2055/+0.2325 q 0.034",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:699-736,"run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd/significance.json (git copy, 4,032 tests) vs C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd/significance.json (lab copy, 6,300 tests)","tests[] where block='10', pooling='mean', layer=40, probe='paper', comparison='pc:unified - raw' -> diff, dataset_ci95, dataset_p, dataset_q_bh, significant_datasets","git: diff +0.0757, CI [-0.006, +0.173], p 0.0754, q 0.499, clears False; 6 clearing tests, 4 negative, the exact six the entry lists (L44 mean blk9 mms/paper pc:unified-random +0.2055/+0.2325 q 0.034; L22/L28 last mms random-raw; L28/L44 last mms random@2-raw). LAB: same diff/CI/p, q 0.420, 6,300 tests, 65 clearing (12 negative).","YES on the git copy for every number including the 6-of-4,032 breakdown. On the lab copy the raw statistics are identical and only the BH q moved (0.499 -> 0.420), exactly as RF-13 predicts.","diff +0.0757, CI [-0.006, +0.173], p 0.0754 (and +0.0729/[-0.042,+0.184]/0.2152; +0.0847/[+0.000,+0.184]/0.0496; -0.0272/[-0.193,+0.162]/0.7310) - identical to the stored file to 4 dp","audit/scripts/claims/F-31.py + _dsboot.py: off-diagonal means recomputed from the 11x11 matrices (bank matrix for persona features, kd11 baseline matrix for raw/datapca, which are bank-independent), then the paired dataset bootstrap re-run independently - multinomial dataset counts -> outer-product cell weights with zeroed diagonal, B=10,000, numpy default_rng(42), block 10 drawn first (the order 27_crossgen.py uses)","BOTH. Git copy = the 4,032-test family the entry was written against; lab copy = regenerated (RF-13), 6,300 tests because comparisons_for() now adds the bank's own persona features. The 'does not clear' verdict is unchanged in both.","The uncorrected CI already straddles zero, so BH is not what kills it - confirmed (526 of 4,032 tests clear by raw CI, this one is not among them). Block 9 (drop sycophancy_mt): pc:unified-raw rises to +0.0961 and pc:unified-datapca to +0.1078, still inside the entry's stated framing.",HOLDS,HIGH - the headline reproduces at Level 1 on the version it cites and at Level 2 from an independent reimplementation of the bootstrap,"HIGH - it is the entry that retires '+0.076' as a quotable result, and the draft must not resurrect it","audit/scripts/claims/F-31.py, audit/scripts/claims/_dsboot.py (outputs: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-31_git.txt, F-31_lab.txt)","VERSION CAVEAT WORTH A DOC FIX: on the regenerated lab file the sentence 'Nothing beats raw' is no longer true. With the added comparisons, pc:kd_assertion - raw at L68 (mean, block 10, paper) reads +0.1497 with q = 0.047 and clears. The entry's '6 of 4,032, four negative' is a correct statement about the 4,032-test family only; the current file has 65 clearing tests of 6,300, 12 negative, dominated by pc:kd_assertion/pc:knowledge_denial vs random.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-34,"The kd_s23 pc:unified - raw gain (paper probe, mean pooling, block 9 = 90 pairs, seed 42) is depth-dependent rather than an L40 artifact: negative or ~0 at L0-L20 (-0.036..+0.008), rising L22-L36 (+0.002..+0.050), peaking at L40 +0.1082 and L44 +0.1156 (the only two layers whose dataset CI excludes zero), sustained +0.05..+0.095 at L48-L76; 16 of 21 layers positive; against datapca L40 +0.1199 [+0.024,+0.220] and L44 +0.1291 [+0.033,+0.228], 17 of 21 positive; best q 0.130 (L44 vs datapca), BH over 3,276 tests; 9 clear the bootstrap, 5 negative, the 4 positive all pc:unified - random at L36/L44.","-0.036; +0.008; +0.002; +0.050; +0.1082; +0.1156; +0.05..+0.095; 16 of 21; +0.1199 [+0.024,+0.220]; +0.1291 [+0.033,+0.228]; 17 of 21; q 0.130; 3,276 tests; 9 clear, 5 negative",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:816-857,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd_s23/significance.json (lab, now 5,544 tests) + banks/kd_s23/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json + baseline kd11/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json. The git copy of this file is the PRE-extension 3-layer version (468 tests, L20/L40/L44 only) and cannot test the claim.","tests[] block='9', pooling='mean', probe='paper', comparison in {pc:unified - raw, pc:unified - datapca}, all 21 layers","L0 -0.0176, L4 -0.0220, L8 +0.0075, L12 -0.0286, L16 -0.0214, L20 -0.0361, L22 +0.0022, L24 +0.0086, L28 +0.0291, L32 +0.0503, L36 +0.0492, L40 +0.1082, L44 +0.1156, L48 +0.0894, L52 +0.0786, L56 +0.0523, L60 +0.0667, L64 +0.0893, L68 +0.0954, L72 +0.0801, L76 +0.0842. Positive at 16/21, peak L44, range -0.0361..+0.1156. Only L40 and L44 have a CI excluding zero. vs datapca: L40 +0.1199 [+0.024,+0.220], L44 +0.1291 [+0.033,+0.228], positive at 17/21.","YES - every layer value, both counts, the peak, the range and both CIs match exactly. The q-values do not match the current file (L44 vs datapca reads 0.103 now, not 0.130) because the BH family grew from 3,276 to 5,544.","The 3,276-test family RECONSTRUCTED: filtering the current 5,544-test file to the 13 comparisons the pre-extension file used gives exactly 3,276 tests, and re-running BH within each block reproduces q = 0.130 at L44 vs datapca and exactly 9 clearing tests, 5 negative and 4 positive, all pc:unified - random at L36 and L44. Off-diagonal means re-derived from the matrices: L40 pc:unified 0.7952, raw 0.6870, datapca 0.6753; L44 0.7990 / 0.6835 / 0.6700.",audit/scripts/claims/F-34.py (per-layer profile + re-derivation of the off-diagonal means from the 11x11 matrices) and F-34b.py (reconstruct the old BH family and re-run Benjamini-Hochberg with _dsboot.bh),"lab copy, regenerated 2026-09-22 (RF-13). The 3,276-test file the entry cites no longer exists anywhere; it was reconstructed from the current file and reproduces the entry's q-values exactly, which independently confirms RF-13's 'raw statistics unchanged, only q moved'.","Both poolings and both blocks are in the file; the claim is explicitly a block-9 / mean-pooling / seed-42 statement and is reported as such. Under the CURRENT (5,544) family, q at L44 vs datapca is 0.103 and 84 tests clear (15 negative) - the conclusion 'the shape is real and the significance is not' is unchanged either way.",HOLDS,HIGH - the 21-layer profile matches to 4 dp and the q-values are reproduced by rebuilding the exact test family the entry used,"MEDIUM - it is the layer-sensitivity backing for the kd bank, and it is the entry that says L44, not L40, is the peak","audit/scripts/claims/F-34.py, F-34b.py (outputs: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-34_git.txt, F-34_lab.txt, F-34b_lab.txt)","Two small wording points. (1) 'L48-L76 sustained +0.05..+0.095, gently declining' is loose: the values dip to +0.0523 at L56 and rise again to +0.0954 at L68, so it is not monotone. (2) Anyone re-reading the source file today will see 5,544 tests and q = 0.103, not 3,276 and 0.130; the entry should say which family its q is over.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-65,"A capitulation-persona axis beats the paper16 register axis on sycophancy_mt: zero-shot (no probe, 100% of rows, mean pooling, seed 42) the cap contrast reads 0.759/0.745/0.728 at L20/40/44 and cap PC1 0.740/0.736/0.717, against the register axis's PC1 0.374 at L40; trained with sycophancy_mt as target (off-diagonal column mean, paper probe, L40) pc:capitulation@2 reads 0.714 (+0.112 over raw 0.601) and clears datapca@2 0.559 and random@2 0.497; dropping the six position-holding personas from the basis costs 0.714 to 0.594.",0.745; 0.374; 0.759; 0.740; 0.736; 0.728; 0.717; 0.714; +0.112; 0.658; 0.594; 0.601; 0.582; 0.578; 0.559; 0.541; 0.497; 0.445; 0.391; 0.355; 0.993; 0.0079; 0.987/0.949/0.936; -0.838; 56.8%; 0.931; 0.7136/0.7132; 0.7449/0.7469; <=0.004,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2095-2204,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_{s23,all}/matrices/mean_L{20,40,44}_s42.json; baseline .../kd11/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json; axes C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-cap/axes_s23.pt","zeroshot[direction].auroc[index of 'sycophancy_mt']; trained = mean of the 10 off-diagonal cells of the sycophancy_mt COLUMN in results[feature,probe='paper'].auroc; geometry = pca[basis].components[40][0]*sign, pca[basis].variance_ratio[40][0], axes[name][40]","zero-shot s23: L20 0.7592/0.7399, L40 0.7449/0.7355, L44 0.7281/0.7166; register (paper16) L40 contrast 0.4089 PC1 0.3740. Trained L40 s23: pc:capitulation@2 0.7136 (+0.1123), pc:capitulation 0.6575 (+0.0562), pc:cap_only@2 0.5935 (-0.0078), raw 0.6013, length 0.5820, datapca 0.5776, datapca@2 0.5594, random 0.5413, random@2 0.4974, pc:unified 0.4451, pc:deception 0.3910, axes 0.3551. Layer profile @2 s23: 0.6438/0.7136/0.6904. cap_only cost L40 -0.1201, L20 0.6438->0.5869. Geometry L40: PC1 var 0.5676, cos(PC1,assistant) -0.8376, gate cosines 0.9871/0.9491/0.9358, cos(contrast_A,contrast_B) 0.9313.",26 of 27 figures exact to 3 dp. ONE SUB-CLAIM IS FALSE: 'Every feature agrees to <= 0.004' between the s23 and all filters.,"Same values - every trained figure is a column mean I recomputed from the 11x11 per-cell matrix, and every geometry figure is a cosine I recomputed from the stored components/axes tensors. s23 vs all, all 12 trained features at L40: pc:cap_only@2 0.5935 vs 0.6077 = 0.0142; pc:cap_only 0.6355 vs 0.6289 = 0.0066; every other feature <= 0.0020.","audit/scripts/claims/F-65.py (matrices; column means, filter comparison, 21-layer x 2-pooling sweep) and F-65b.py + P3_var.py (torch.load of run-cap/axes_s23.pt: cosines, PC1 variance, role lists, md5)","lab only - run-cap and the cap banks are in no branch and not on Drive (RF-10). The cap matrices are dated 2026-09-21 03:49-03:56 and were NOT touched by the 09-22 regeneration wave; run-cap/axes_s23.pt is 09-21 03:22 (md5 96a9b42b6ea9a0d5b75ee0793ffedbb0). Bank resolved by content, not by name: run-cap-ctrl/axes_s23.pt has the same basename and a different md5 (326310336d24b97680fb99b906cf5cff).","21 layers x 2 poolings swept (the entry reports 3 layers). MEAN pooling: trained pc:capitulation@2 beats raw at 21 of 21 layers, peaking at L32 (0.7521 vs raw 0.6134, +0.1387) - so L40 is NOT the best layer and the entry quotes one layer below the peak, as F-34 found for kd. Zero-shot contrast also peaks at L32 (0.7796), not L20. LAST pooling is much weaker: cap@2 - raw is negative at 8 layers (L4, L8, L56-L76) - the result is a mean-pooling result. The register axis stays below 0.50 at every layer in both poolings, as F-13 says.",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - everything recomputed from the raw matrices and the stored axes; the one failure is a direct measurement, not an interpretation","HIGH - it is the project's only place where a persona axis beats everything it is matched against, and the draft's Claim 2","audit/scripts/claims/F-65.py, F-65b.py, P3_var.py (outputs: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-65_lab.txt, F-65b_lab.txt)","THE FAILING SUB-CLAIM: 'The judge filter is immaterial ... Every feature agrees to <= 0.004.' The headline features do (capitulation@2 0.7136 vs 0.7132; zero-shot 0.7449 vs 0.7469), but pc:cap_only@2 is 0.5935 (s23) vs 0.6077 (all), a gap of 0.0142 - 3.5x the stated bound - and pc:cap_only is 0.6355 vs 0.6289, 0.0066. cap_only is exactly the feature caveat (c) rests on, so the filter is NOT immaterial for 'the one live comparison': the cap_only penalty at L40 is -0.120 under s23 but -0.105 under all, and at L20 -0.057 vs -0.047. The direction and the conclusion are unchanged, but the sentence as written is wrong and F-62's '<= 0.01' prediction is the honest bound. Everything else - including the A-equals-B tautology (pc:capitulation@2 and pc:cap_vs_default@2 identical to max|diff| = 0), the shared 13-role basis, PC1 var 0.5676 and the re-run gate cosines 0.987/0.949/0.936 - reproduces exactly.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-66,"The cap result clears a dataset-level bootstrap on the sycophancy_mt column: resampling the 10 source datasets pairwise (B=10,000, seed 42), pc:capitulation@2 beats raw by +0.112 [+0.050,+0.185] at L40 with the whole 95% interval above zero, and also clears datapca@2, random@2 and length at L40/L44 (filtered and unfiltered), while at L20 the margins over datapca@2 (p=0.098) and cap_only@2 (p=0.169) do not clear, and pc:cap_only@2 - raw is indistinguishable from zero at every layer and both filters; cap beats raw on 9 of 10 sources at L40.","+0.084 [+0.010,+0.150]; +0.112 [+0.050,+0.185]; +0.107 [+0.039,+0.185]; +0.112 [+0.049,+0.186]; +0.068/[-0.040,+0.159]; +0.154 [+0.091,+0.211]; +0.171; +0.153; +0.216; +0.194; +0.062; +0.132; +0.108; +0.057; +0.120 [+0.034,+0.213]; +0.095; +0.027; -0.008; +0.013; +0.006; p 0.098; p 0.169; 9 of 10; 8 of 10",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2206-2283,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_{s23,all}/matrices/mean_L{20,40,44}_s42.json (mtime 2026-09-21, NOT regenerated in the 09-22 wave)","the 10 off-diagonal cells of the sycophancy_mt column, results[feature,probe='paper'].auroc","the entry's table is print-only output of cap/scripts/cap_significance.py, so there is no stored file to match against - Level 1 and Level 2 coincide here","n/a (no stored significance file for this test; the entry's source line names the script, not a file)","ALL 24 CELLS EXACT. L20/L40/L44/L40-unfiltered: vs raw +0.0838 [+0.0096,+0.1496] / +0.1123 [+0.0502,+0.1847] / +0.1073 [+0.0390,+0.1849] / +0.1118 [+0.0489,+0.1861]; vs datapca@2 +0.0682 [-0.0398,+0.1592] / +0.1542 [+0.0913,+0.2113] / +0.1713 [+0.1130,+0.2163] / +0.1538 [+0.0907,+0.2118]; vs random@2 +0.1531 / +0.2162 / +0.1936 / +0.2157; vs length +0.0618 / +0.1316 / +0.1084 / +0.1312; vs pc:cap_only@2 +0.0570 [-0.0594,+0.1740] / +0.1201 [+0.0336,+0.2132] / +0.0947 [+0.0138,+0.1829] / +0.1054 [+0.0245,+0.2003]; pc:cap_only@2 - raw +0.0269 / -0.0078 [-0.1122,+0.0952] / +0.0126 / +0.0064. p(L20 datapca@2)=0.0978, p(L20 cap_only@2)=0.1692. Per-source table at L40 identical row for row; cap beats raw on 9 of 10 (8 of 10 at L20 and L44).","audit/scripts/claims/F-66.py - an independent reimplementation of cap/scripts/cap_significance.py: paired i.i.d. bootstrap over the 10 source datasets, one shared resampling for every pair, B=10,000, numpy default_rng(42), percentile CI and P(diff<=0)","lab only (RF-10). Not a BH q-value claim, so RF-13's family growth does not apply. The cap matrices predate the 09-22 regeneration wave.","I ran the SAME bootstrap at every stored layer, which the entry did not. Mean pooling: cap@2 - raw clears at 14 of 21 layers (L0, L20, L28-L64, L72) and vs datapca@2 at 15 of 21; the biggest margins are at L28-L36, not L40. So the headline is NOT a single-layer artifact - a stronger result than the entry claims. LAST pooling is a different story: vs raw it clears only at L20/L28/L32 and goes negative (not significantly) at L56-L72. F-66 is a MEAN-POOLING result and should say so.",HOLDS,"HIGH - 24 of 24 table cells reproduced by an independent reimplementation of the bootstrap, plus the per-source table and both win counts",HIGH - the draft's Claim 2 and the project's only positive result that clears its own stated bar,audit/scripts/claims/F-66.py (output: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-66_lab.txt),The session-recovered pointer is confirmed exactly: pc:cap_only@2 - raw = -0.0078 with P(<=0) = 0.5578 at L40 - dropping the six position-holding personas removes the advantage. Caveat (1) 'n = 10 datasets is a small unit' is the right framing: five of the 24 intervals have half-widths above 0.08. Caveat (3) is correct that the zero-shot 0.745 is NOT covered by this test.,P3-kdbank-cap
F-67,"The cap advantage is local: on the full 11x11 off-diagonal mean at L40 (mean pooling, paper probe) pc:capitulation@2 beats random@2 by +0.270 (q=0.013, clears) but beats raw by only +0.098 with CI [-0.036,+0.208] (does not clear), and removing sycophancy_mt drops that to +0.073; the unfiltered bank agrees to <=0.001 on every comparison.","+0.270 95/110 [+0.138,+0.398] q 0.013; +0.127 80/110 [+0.013,+0.248] q 0.172; +0.098 76/110 [-0.036,+0.208]; +0.073 57/90 [-0.077,+0.204]; +0.124 62/90 [-0.017,+0.262]; +0.273 76/90 [+0.121,+0.416] YES; -0.171 25/110 [-0.275,-0.053]; 792 tests; 144 before the fix; +0.0984/+0.0983, +0.0731/+0.0730, +0.1275/+0.1273, +0.2697/+0.2696",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2285-2340,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_{s23,all}/significance.json (now 5,544 tests each, mtime 2026-09-22 16:01 / 15:52 - REGENERATED in the RF-13 wave)","tests[] filtered on comparison / block / layer=40 / pooling='mean' / probe='paper' -> diff, pairs_won, dataset_ci95, dataset_p, dataset_q_bh, significant_datasets","row 1 +0.2696 95/110 [+0.138,+0.398] q_now 0.016 clears; row 2 +0.1273 80/110 [+0.013,+0.248] q_now 0.227; row 3 +0.0983 76/110 [-0.036,+0.208]; row 4 +0.0730 57/90 [-0.077,+0.204]; row 5 +0.1235 62/90 [-0.017,+0.262]; row 6 +0.2727 76/90 [+0.121,+0.416] q_now 0.075 significant_datasets=FALSE; row 7 -0.1712 25/110 [-0.275,-0.053] q_now 0.142 significant_datasets=FALSE. s23-vs-all agreement: max |diff| = 0.0001 over these rows, and the four quoted pairs match exactly.",6 of 7 rows match in full. Row 6 does not: the entry marks it 'clears? YES' but the file's own significant_datasets is false.,"The 792-test family was RECONSTRUCTED (keep layers 20/40/44 only -> exactly 792 tests = 3 x 2 x 3 x 22 x 2) and BH re-run per block. It reproduces the entry's q-values exactly: row 1 q792 = 0.013 (clears), row 2 q792 = 0.172 (does not). Row 6 comes out q792 = 0.068 - it does NOT clear in the family the entry used either. Row 7 q792 = 0.108.","audit/scripts/claims/F-67.py + _dsboot.bh - reads the tests by key and rebuilds the pre-sweep BH family, re-running Benjamini-Hochberg with an independent implementation","lab only. The 792-test file the entry cites was overwritten on 2026-09-22 15:52/16:01 (RF-13); it was reconstructed from the current 5,544-test file and reproduces the entry's q-values, which confirms that only the family changed. Bank resolved by content (cap_s23 = run-cap/axes_s23.pt, md5 96a9b42b...).","The conclusion is unaffected by the version: the '- raw' rows do not clear under either family, at either block, filtered or unfiltered. F-66's layer sweep shows the column-level effect is broad across depth while this full-matrix test stays null - the two are measuring different quantities, as the entry says.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - every number recomputed from the file by key and the old BH family rebuilt; the one mismatch is against the file's own significance flag,HIGH - this is the bound on Claim 2; if row 6 is quoted as 'clears' the bound looks weaker than it is,"audit/scripts/claims/F-67.py, _dsboot.py (output: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-67_lab.txt)","THE FAILING ROW: `pc:capitulation@2 - random@2`, block 'minus sycophancy_mt', is marked 'clears? YES' with no q. Its 95% CI [+0.121,+0.416] does exclude zero, but its BH q is 0.068 in the 792-test family and 0.075 now, and the file records significant_datasets = false. The entry is inconsistent with itself: row 2 is written as 'CI clears, q = 0.172 - no after BH'. Row 6 should read the same way. Row 7 ('significantly negative') is defensible because the prose cites the CI, not q - but its q is 0.108 too. NOT VERIFIABLE: '144 tests before the fix' - the pre-fix file does not exist in any copy; 144 = 3 x 2 x 3 x 4 x 2 is arithmetically consistent with the four control-vs-raw pairs the entry describes.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-89,"Tier 0.4 format-matched control: with sycophancy_mt as held-out target at L40 (mean pooling, paper probe, 10 source datasets, paired dataset bootstrap B=10,000), swapping the six position-holding personas for six topically unrelated instructed personas costs only +0.0247 (CI includes zero), a paraphrase of them costs +0.0340 (clears), while removing them entirely costs +0.1201 (clears decisively); the ordering paraphrase >= holding > neutral > none replicates at L20/L40/L44 but the presence:content split (38%/78%/74% retention) does not.","0.7229 +0.1216 [+0.0541,+0.1994]; 0.7136 +0.1123 [+0.0502,+0.1847]; 0.6889 +0.0875 [+0.0336,+0.1402]; 0.5935 -0.0078 [-0.1122,+0.0952]; 0.6013; +0.0247 [-0.0067,+0.0718] 0.113; +0.0340 [+0.0018,+0.0804] 0.018; +0.1201 [+0.0336,+0.2132] 0.001; 78%; L20 0.6438/0.6483/0.5919/0.5869/0.5600 +0.052/+0.056/+0.057; L44 0.6904/0.6984/0.6627/0.5957/0.5831 +0.028/+0.036/+0.095; 38%/78%/74%; 0.989/0.990/0.936; 1,200 rollouts",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3637-3745,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_ctrl/matrices/mean_L{20,40,44}_s42.json and .../banks/cap_s23/matrices/...; axes C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-cap-ctrl/axes_s23.pt; rollouts C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-cap-ctrl/responses","off-diagonal mean of the sycophancy_mt column for pc:cap_vs_para@2 / pc:capitulation@2 / pc:cap_vs_neutral@2 / pc:cap_only@2, paper probe; axes[name][40] and pca[name] for the cosines","L40: paraphrase 0.7229 (+0.1216 [+0.0541,+0.1994]), holding 0.7136 (+0.1123 [+0.0502,+0.1847]), neutral 0.6889 (+0.0875 [+0.0336,+0.1402]), none 0.5935 (-0.0078 [-0.1122,+0.0952]), raw 0.6013. Contrasts: holding-neutral +0.0247 [-0.0067,+0.0718] P=0.113; paraphrase-neutral +0.0340 [+0.0018,+0.0804] P=0.018; any-six-none +0.1201 [+0.0336,+0.2132] P=0.001. L20: 0.6438/0.6483/0.5919/0.5869/0.5600, +0.0519/+0.0563/+0.0570. L44: 0.6904/0.6984/0.6627/0.5957/0.5831, +0.0277/+0.0357/+0.0947. Retention 38%/78%/74%. Gate cosines cap_vs_neutral 0.9888, cap_vs_para 0.9900, cap_only_ctrl 0.9358. run-cap-ctrl/responses: 12 files, 1,200 rollout lines.","YES - every one of the 30+ figures matches to the precision quoted, including all three retention percentages and the exact set of starred (clearing) cells","same values; all AUROCs are column means I recomputed from the 11x11 per-cell matrices and all intervals come from my own reimplementation of the paired source bootstrap. The structural identities also hold exactly: max|pc:capitulation@2 - pc:cap_vs_default@2| = 0 and max|pc:cap_only@2 - pc:cap_only_ctrl@2| = 0 over all 110 off-diagonal cells at L20, L40 AND L44.","audit/scripts/claims/F-89.py (four conditions read across two banks, paired bootstrap over the same 10 sources, B=10,000, default_rng(42)) and F-65b.py (torch.load of run-cap-ctrl/axes_s23.pt for the cosines and role lists)","lab only (RF-10). cap_ctrl matrices mtime 2026-09-21 20:07 - before the 09-22 wave. BUT run-cap-ctrl/axes_s23.pt has mtime 2026-09-22 16:05:28, INSIDE the RF-13 reboot wave, i.e. the axes file was rebuilt AFTER the matrices that used it; the cosines I report come from the rebuilt file. Bank resolved by content: its md5 is 326310336d24b97680fb99b906cf5cff, different from run-cap/axes_s23.pt (96a9b42b...) despite the identical basename that provenance.csv flags.","Only the three layers the entry reports exist for cap_ctrl, and the entry says so. The identity pc:cap_only@2 == pc:cap_only_ctrl@2 (max|diff| = 0 at all three layers) is strong evidence the vector reuse worked as claimed - the two banks' shared 7-role basis is bit-identical. The rollout count 12 x 5 x 20 = 1,200 is confirmed by line count.",HOLDS,"HIGH - the whole table, the layer sweep, the retention percentages, the cosines, the structural identities and the rollout count all reproduce","HIGH - it is the control that deflates F-66's interpretation, so the draft's reading of Claim 2 depends on it","audit/scripts/claims/F-89.py, F-65b.py, P3_extras.py (outputs: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-89_lab.txt, F-65b_lab.txt, P3_extras_lab.txt)","One loose headline: 'removing them entirely costs two to four times that'. The measured ratios of six-none to holding-neutral are 1.1x (L20), 4.9x (L40) and 3.4x (L44) - so 'two to four times' covers neither end. The entry's own body text says it correctly ('at layer 20 the two effects are the same size'). The entry's status line already says F-94 supersedes its numbers on a 16-layer base; F-94 is not in this batch and was not checked here.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-97,"The collaborator's abstract headline 0.904 / 0.916 (L20 / L40) is the zero-shot AUROC of ext_axis1, a 12-vs-13 contrast whose extra ten roles are the owner's knowledge-denial personas, not the persona-coordinates paper's own 8-vs-7 deception contrast, which reads 0.791 / 0.832 on the same rows; against the trained single-source baseline 0.648 / 0.732 that makes the kd personas worth +0.113 / +0.084, i.e. 44.2% / 45.7% of the headline margin.",0.904; 0.916; 0.7909; 0.8319; 0.6478; 0.7320; +0.143; +0.100; +0.256; +0.184; +0.113; +0.084; 44.2%; 45.7%; drop repe: +0.142/+0.092 and +0.136/+0.101; 0.6511; 0.8593 vs 0.8319; 0.7680 vs 0.9158,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4384-4466,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood: src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40}/{zero_shot.csv,summary.csv,matrix_baseline.csv}; deception_detection/persona_pcs.py; deception_detection/scripts/persona_ood.py, pool_activations.py - all read with `git show`, no checkout",zero_shot.csv columns auroc_axis / auroc_ext_axis / auroc_pc1 / auroc_ext_pc1 averaged over the 6 scored datasets; summary.csv rows baseline / axis1 / ext_axis1 / pc1 / ext_pc1 column off_diagonal_mean,"L20: baseline 0.6478, axis1 zero-shot 0.7909, ext_axis1 0.9041, margins +0.1431 / +0.2563, kd worth +0.1132, share 44.2%. L40: baseline 0.7320, axis1 0.8319, ext_axis1 0.9158, margins +0.0999 / +0.1838, kd worth +0.0839, share 45.7%. Drop repe_honesty (5-dataset baseline from matrix_baseline.csv = 0.6085 / 0.7064): axis1 margin +0.1418 / +0.0919, kd worth +0.1364 / +0.1007. axis1 TRAINED off-diagonal at L20 = 0.6511. pc1 0.8593 vs axis1 0.8319 (+0.027) and ext_pc1 0.7680 vs ext_axis1 0.9158 (-0.148) at L40.","YES - all 18 numbers match to the precision the entry quotes, including the drop-repe_honesty row (+0.142/+0.092 and +0.136/+0.101) and both caveat figures","Identical: every figure is a mean I computed over the per-dataset rows of zero_shot.csv / the off-diagonal cells of matrix_baseline.csv, not a stored summary number. The 1-d identity in caveat (2) also holds: |trained off-diagonal - zero-shot mean| = 2.2e-16 (ext_axis1 L20), 1.1e-16 (denial_axis1 L20), 0.0 at L40 for axis1/ext_axis1/denial_axis1; and 1.4e-01 for axis1 at L20, which is exactly the sign trap the caveat describes.","audit/scripts/claims/F-97.py - reads the CSVs out of git at both f386a72 (the commit the entry cites) and the current branch head, averages the per-dataset AUROCs itself, and re-derives the 6- and 5-dataset baselines from matrix_baseline.csv","collaborator branch. The entry cites f386a72; the branch head is now 45b16d9 (2026-09-22 12:45). The persona_ood_ext_L20/L40 results are BYTE-IDENTICAL at both commits (the script prints both and every number agrees), so the head move does not affect the claim.","Structural claims re-checked in his code: extended_arms() in persona_ood.py builds ext_axis from DECEPTION+KNOWLEDGE_DENIAL minus HONESTY+KNOWLEDGE_CANDOUR (8+4 = 12 vs 7+6 = 13, confirmed); his KNOWLEDGE_DENIAL_PERSONAS (4) equal our kd_role_groups.json knowledge_denial name for name, and his KNOWLEDGE_CANDOUR_PERSONAS (6) are our sincere_ignorance (3) + plain_assertion (3) merged - so the entry's 'their split merges both our controls into one pole' is confirmed from the source. Base bank at persona_pcs.py:31 is paper16_L20_sharedquestions/paper16_L20.pt as stated. Their six datasets are CG, HP-C, HP-KR, IT, ID and repe_honesty - confirmed from zero_shot.csv.",HOLDS,"HIGH - all numbers re-derived from the collaborator's own committed CSVs during this audit, at the cited commit and at the current head",HIGH - this is what the owner tells her collaborator about his own abstract,audit/scripts/claims/F-97.py (output: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-97_git.txt),"One citation error, not a numeric one: the entry says the mean-pooling line is pool_activations.py:84. In his file at both commits the pooling line is 123 (`example.acts[example.mask].float().mean(0).squeeze(0).numpy()`); line 84 is `if acts is None:`. The substantive claim - that they mean-pool and the briefing's Sec 5b premise is false - is correct. I did not find the briefing's 'every summary records delta = 0.0000' string in summary.md; that supporting remark is unverified.",P3-kdbank-cap
F-98,"F-97 replicates on our own eleven datasets: rebuilding the collaborator's two arms from our vectors_s23 and scoring them zero-shot (mean pooling, seed 42), axis1 reads 0.6572/0.7325 at L20/L40 and ext_axis1 0.7386/0.7996 against a raw single-source trained baseline of 0.6289/0.6623, so the kd bank is worth 74.1%/48.8% of the margin; both arms lose to pooled LODO training (0.8027/0.8545) by -0.064/-0.055; and the kd contribution is concentrated in two datasets - removing HP-KR and sandbagging_v2 leaves +0.0025 at L20.",0.6289; 0.6623; 0.6572; 0.7325; 0.7386; 0.7996; 0.8027; 0.8545; +0.028; +0.070; +0.110; +0.137; 74.1%; 48.8%; 0.6323; 0.6763; 76.5%; 54.4%; -0.064; -0.055; +0.0814; +0.0671; +0.0254; +0.0418; +0.0025; +0.0391; 0.1652; 0.8057; +0.641; +0.232; 0.6660; 0.7287,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4469-4542,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/mean_L{20,40}_s42.json (mtime 2026-09-22 00:33, before the RF-13 wave); baseline .../kd11/matrices/mean_L{20,40}_s42.json; pooled C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/premise_L{20,40}_mean_s42.json (mtime 2026-09-21 14:26/14:35); bank C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/axes_collab_s23.pt","zeroshot rows 'contrast' and 'contrast:collab_extended' (mean over the 11 datasets); baseline results[feature='raw',probe='paper'] off-diagonal mean over 110 pairs; premise summary.pooled_lodo and summary.single","L20: raw 0.6289, axis1 0.6572, ext_axis1 0.7386, margins +0.0284 / +0.1097, kd worth +0.0814, share 74.1%, pooled_lodo 0.8027, premise single 0.6323. L40: raw 0.6623, axis1 0.7325, ext_axis1 0.7996, margins +0.0703 / +0.1374, kd worth +0.0671, share 48.8%, pooled_lodo 0.8545, premise single 0.6763. Both arms vs pooled: -0.0641 (L20), -0.0549 (L40). Decomposition: all eleven +0.0814/+0.0671; minus HP-KR +0.0254/+0.0418; minus HP-KR and sandbagging_v2 +0.0025/+0.0391. HP-KR at L20 0.1652 -> 0.8057 (+0.6406); sandbagging_v2 +0.2317. Provenance: paper16 bank's own contrast 0.6660/0.7287 vs our axis1 0.6572/0.7325, gaps 0.0088/0.0038.",YES - all 32 numbers match. The only rounding note: the share against the premise single-source figure comes out 76.6% at L20 where the entry says 76.5% (0.0814/0.1063); L40 54.4% exact.,"same values; every AUROC is a mean I computed over the per-dataset zero-shot entries or over the 110 off-diagonal cells, not a stored summary. Bank composition verified in the .pt itself: deception(8) + knowledge_denial(4) = 12 positive, honesty(7) + sincere_ignorance(3) + plain_assertion(3) = 13 negative, vectors_dir = run-kd/vectors_s23 - exactly the '12 v 13' and the build command the entry's source line states.",audit/scripts/claims/F-98.py (matrices + run-premise) and P3_extras.py (torch.load of run-kd/axes_collab_s23.pt for role groups and vectors_dir),"lab only (RF-10: run-premise is on no branch and, before tonight's backup, not on Drive). None of the four files was touched by the 09-22 regeneration wave. Not a BH q claim.",F-99 (below) is the 21-layer version of this claim and confirms it. The entry's own caveat (1) - two layers is provisional - is honoured by F-99. Caveat (4) is important and correct: on a corpus without a knowledge-denial dataset the kd bank is worth ~nothing at L20 (+0.0025).,HOLDS,"HIGH - all numbers re-derived from the per-dataset raw values on the lab copy, and the bank's composition checked inside the .pt",HIGH - it is the owner's independent replication of what she tells her collaborator about his abstract,"audit/scripts/claims/F-98.py, P3_extras.py (outputs: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-98_lab.txt, P3_extras_lab.txt)",No discrepancies. Worth carrying into the write-up: at L20 the entire kd contribution is two datasets (HP-KR +0.641 and sandbagging_v2 +0.232); at L40 it is more distributed and survives their removal (+0.0391).,P3-kdbank-cap
F-99,"Across all 21 stored layers (mean pooling, zero-shot, seed 42) the extended 12v13 contrast beats the paper's 8v7 contrast at 21 of 21 layers, mean +0.0551, range +0.0019 (L0) to +0.0814 (L20); the share of the margin over raw has median 62.9%, mean 63.8% and range 2.2%-113.9%, exceeding 100% at L60-L68 where axis1 itself falls below raw; and the HP-KR repair is universal across depth.",21 of 21; +0.0551; +0.0019; +0.0814; 62.9%; 63.8%; 2.2%; 113.9%; 0.6379 vs 0.6386; 0.6337 vs 0.6370; 0.6260 vs 0.6339; L12 0.216->0.883; L20 0.165->0.806; L24 0.087->0.697; L40 0.556->0.876; L76 0.720->0.848,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4544-4596,C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json (21 layers) and baseline .../kd11/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json,"zeroshot rows 'contrast' and 'contrast:collab_extended' meaned over the 11 datasets, per layer; raw = results[feature='raw',probe='paper'] off-diagonal mean","positive at 21 of 21 layers; mean +0.0551; range [+0.0019 (L0), +0.0814 (L20)]; share median 62.9%, mean 63.8%, range [2.2%, 113.9%]; axis1 < raw at exactly three layers - L60 0.6379 vs 0.6386, L64 0.6337 vs 0.6370, L68 0.6260 vs 0.6339. HP-KR: L12 0.216->0.883, L20 0.165->0.806, L24 0.087->0.697, L40 0.556->0.876, L76 0.720->0.848.","YES - every statistic, the full HP-KR table and the three below-raw layers match exactly","same values; the per-layer axis1/ext_axis1 means and the raw off-diagonal means were all recomputed from the per-dataset zero-shot entries and the 110 off-diagonal cells. Supporting range checks: axis1 on HP-KR spans 0.087 (L24) to 0.860 (L0) and ext_axis1 spans 0.571 (L32) to 0.906 (L0) - matching the entry's '0.087-0.86, mostly 0.15-0.57' and '0.57-0.91 everywhere'.","audit/scripts/claims/F-98.py, the F-99 section - sweeps every mean_L*_s42.json in banks/collab against the matching baseline matrix","lab only. The collab matrices are dated 2026-09-22 00:33, before the 15:40-16:26 regeneration wave. Not a BH q claim.","This IS the robustness check for F-98 and it passes: the two-layer figure was not misleading in sign or magnitude, only in the share. The entry's own warning - quote the raw difference (+0.055 mean, +0.081 at L20), not the share - is well supported: the share ranges over a factor of 50 while the numerator moves by 0.08. Last pooling was not swept here (the entry is explicitly a mean-pooling claim).",HOLDS,HIGH - every quoted statistic reproduced from the 21 per-layer matrices,"HIGH - it is the layer-robust version of what the owner tells her collaborator, and it is the entry that says the share is the wrong number to quote",audit/scripts/claims/F-98.py (output: audit/phase2/out/P3/F-98_lab.txt),"Caveat (2) - 'the run OOMed repeatedly and was completed by a resume loop, not by reducing --boot_rows' - is a statement about logs that I did not check; it is DOC-ONLY here. Nothing in the numbers suggests inconsistent settings (the L20/L40 cells match F-98's exactly).",P3-kdbank-cap
F-27,"Both scale rungs generated 2,600/2,600 rollouts clean (8B 51 min, 3B 82 min, all 52 role files exactly 100 rows); on 21 of 26 8B roles the 70B judge keeps 97.14% and drops 2.86%, 'against the 70B's 1.07% (16/1,500)', so the 8B breaks character 2.7x as often.",2600/2600; 51 min; 82 min; keep 97.14%; drop 2.86%; 70B 1.07% (16/1500); 2.7x; deception 765/800; honesty 485/500; sycophancy 397/400; anti_syc 393/400,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:538,"lab: run-scale/{3b,8b}/responses; run-scale/8b/scores; run-paper16/scores; logs/scale_{3b,8b}.status | audit/phase2/P4_lab_scores.txt; P4_lab_geom.txt; P4_lab_geom2.txt",26 files x 100 rows per rung; 21-role subset reconstruction; run-paper16/scores 12/1350,generation + per-group numbers match exactly; 70B reference 1.07% (16/1500) is in NO file,PARTIAL,"3b/8b 2600 rows each, 0 short files; 8B 21-role subset reproduces 765/800, 485/500, 397/400, 393/400 = 2040/2100 = 97.14%; run-paper16/scores = 12 drops / 1350 = 0.89% (not 16/1500 = 1.07%); ratio 2.86/0.89 = 3.21x (F-30 final 8B rate: 3.16/0.89 = 3.55x); 3B response mtimes 13:29:11-14:47:14 corroborate the 82 min",recount rows.jsonl; reimplement the score_summary.py recipe on the lab; exhaustive 21-of-26 subset search per role group,"lab copy, 2026-09-20 files; not in the 09-22 rewrite wave; no BH q-values",superseded in part by F-30 (8B keep 97.14 -> 96.84; deception-honesty gap 1.4 -> 0.24 rows/role),PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - every count recomputed from the score JSONs and response files,LOW-MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_scores.py; P4_lab_geom.py; P4_lab_geom2.py,"The 70B denominator 16/1500 = 1.07% is supported by NO file: run-paper16/scores holds 1,350 rollouts and 12 drops (0.89%). The same literal is hardcoded in scale/scripts/score_summary.py (docstring + printed reference line), so it contaminates any rung report that script produces. The title's '2.7x' should be 3.2x (or 3.6x on F-30's final 8B rate). The 3B status file was overwritten by a 15:51 resume, so its wall clock is corroborated only by file mtimes.",P4-scale
F-30,Judge-score distributions and per-group keep rates for the paper16 bank at 70B / 8B / 3B; the drop rate is NOT monotone in model size (3B 2.68% < 8B 3.16%) while the score-3 share is (80.7 -> 57.3 -> 52.3).,1350/2500/2500 rollouts; drop 0.89/3.16/2.68%; score3 80.7/57.3/52.3%; deception 97.50/95.62/95.38; honesty 100.00/95.86/97.14; sycophancy 99.33/98.60/98.40; anti_syc 100.00/98.40/99.60; gaps 2.50/0.24/1.76pp,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:652,"lab: run-paper16/scores, run-scale/8b/scores, run-scale/3b/scores (25 JSONs each) | audit/phase2/P4_lab_scores.txt",per-score counts and per-group keep rates,all 30+ quoted figures match to the stated precision,YES,"70B 1350: 12/0/249/1089 -> drop 0.89%; 8B 2500: 33/46/988/1433 -> 3.16%; 3B 2500: 54/13/1125/1308 -> 2.68%; groups 97.50/100.00/99.33/100.00, 95.62/95.86/98.60/98.40, 95.38/97.14/98.40/99.60; pc_coverup_operator worst at all three (8.0/12.0/23.0%)",reimplemented the scale/scripts/score_summary.py recipe over the three score dirs with pc_role_groups.json,lab copy; score dirs not in the 09-22 rewrite wave; no BH q-values quoted,"its own supersession of F-27 checks out (8B keep 96.84%, gap 0.24pp)",HOLDS,HIGH - full Level-2 recomputation of every quoted number,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_scores.py,"Cleanest entry in the batch. Its caveat is also correct: keep rates say nothing about bias in the surviving rows. Note it silently corrects F-27's 70B denominator by using 1,350 / 0.89% rather than 1,500 / 1.07%.",P4-scale
F-37,"Persona geometry at three model sizes at matched relative depth: cos(PC1_all, assistant axis) = +0.435 / +0.732 / +0.623 (3B/8B/70B), non-monotone and peaking at 8B, while per-behaviour contrast alignment and deception-basis PC1 variance rise monotonically.",+0.435/+0.732/+0.623; min +0.367/+0.514/+0.540; median +0.532/+0.701/+0.618; PC1 var 33.4/39.6/37.2%; top5 73.1/77.4/75.1%; anchor 0.834/0.949/0.935; syc 0.948/0.983/0.993; unified 0.781/0.908/0.906; dec 0.924/0.921/0.955; dec PC1var 30.2/36.0/43.0%,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:941,"lab: logs/scale_3b_axes.log, scale_8b_axes.log, paper16_shared_axes.log; run-scale/{3b,8b}/axes_{3b,8b}.pt; run-paper16-shared/axes_vectors_{all,s3}.pt | audit/phase2/P4_lab_geom.txt; P4_lab_geom2.txt","first report block of each log (the vectors_all extraction); pca['all'].components[mid,0] vs axes['assistant'][mid]",all 18 numbers match the first block of each log exactly,YES,"70B recomputes exactly from run-paper16-shared/axes_vectors_all.pt (0.6230, 37.2%, 75.1%, 0.9548/0.9925/0.9064). 3B/8B NOT recomputable: both extractions wrote the same output path, so axes_3b.pt / axes_8b.pt are the later s23 versions and give 0.5514 / 0.7395 (the logs' SECOND blocks).","load the axes .pt on the lab; recompute cos(PC1_all, assistant) per layer, PC1/top-5 variance and per-basis cos(PC1, contrast)","F-37's three columns are all the vectors_all (unfiltered) extraction - like-for-like across rungs, but NOT the s23/s3 banks the crossgen uses","on the surviving s23/s3 banks: 3B +0.551 / 8B +0.739 / 70B +0.584 - still non-monotone, still peaks at 8B, 3B still fails; but the 70B then fails the all-layers threshold too (min +0.467)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH on Level 1 and the 70B recompute; MEDIUM on 3B/8B (log-only),MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_geom.py; P4_lab_geom2.py,"Two defects. (1) The threshold verdicts are UNDERSPECIFIED: '>0.60 all layers' is passed by the 8B only if applied to the MEDIAN (0.701); on the entry's own min (+0.514) the 8B fails, and on a literal reading all three rungs fail. (2) The caveat 'per F-18 paper16-shared differs from plain paper16 only in the unified basis' is contradicted - at L40 the plain file gives |cos| 0.8162 and PC1 var 46.7% against the shared file's 0.5838 and 36.8%.",P4-scale
F-54,"The 3B/8B coords extraction completed (3B exit 0 at 21:24:15, 2h50 total) with row-for-row matched evaluation activations on five datasets totalling 2,508 rows per rung, and those five are the paper's Table 1 deception benchmark.","2508 rows each; 800/800/371/270/267; exit 0 at 21:24:15; 18:34:09-21:24:15 = 2h50; 5 dataset dirs, expect 5; 0 OOMs",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1639,"lab: run-scale/{3b,8b}/coords/*/rows.jsonl; logs/scale_coords.status | audit/phase2/P4_lab_scores.txt",row counts per dataset dir; status lines 18:34:09 / 19:36:28 / 21:24:15,all counts and timestamps match exactly; the dataset-identity claim does not,PARTIAL,"3b and 8b each: ai_liar 270, convincing-game 267, harm-pressure-choice 800, instructed-deception 800, roleplaying 371 (sum 2,508, identical across rungs); the stores now also hold alpaca 400 and mask 585 (7 dirs, 3,493 rows each). Status: START 18:34:09, 8b exit 0 19:36:28 ('11 dataset dirs written, expect 5'), 3b exit 0 21:24:15 ('5 dataset dirs written, expect 5'), DONE 21:40:48.",count lines of every rows.jsonl in both coords stores; read the status log,lab copy; the coords chain was re-triggered 2026-09-22 16:20 by the RF-13 boot wave but logged '5/5 requested datasets present' in 6 s (a skip) - row counts unchanged,"both rungs also match on all 7 present dirs, not just the 5",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - counts recounted from rows.jsonl, timestamps read from the status file",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_scores.py,"The claim 'these five ARE Mahadik & Skapars' Table 1 deception benchmark ... HarmPressureChoice' DOES NOT HOLD: the paper's evaluated set is ConvGame/InstrDec/Mask/AILiar/Roleplay. F-60 makes exactly this correction but lists its supersession only against F-58, so the error is still live at F-54. '0 OOMs' NOT CHECKED (would need logs/scale_coords_3b.log). The 8B arm's own status says '11 dataset dirs written, expect 5', i.e. the 'expect 5' gate counted requests, not contents.",P4-scale
F-58,"On the paper's five datasets at k=3 the persona axis beats raw by +0.089 at 3B (raw 0.708) and +0.086 at 8B (raw 0.743) with both controls negative, collapsing to +0.026 at 70B (raw 0.809) - 'the method replicates at the paper's sizes and dies at 70B'.",3B raw 0.708 +0.089 random -0.246 dpca -0.150; 8B raw 0.743 +0.086 -0.025 -0.017; 70B raw 0.809 +0.026 -0.214 -0.112,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1788,"lab: run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (70B row); logs/crossgen_scale_{3b,8b}.log | audit/phase2/P4_lab_matrix.txt; P4_lab_scores.txt; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv","kd11 store, dataset_set=paper5, k=5, layer 40, mean, probe=paper; crossgen log lines 22:18-22:21 vs 23:38-23:40",the 70B row matches exactly (0.8090 / +0.0262 / -0.2138 / -0.1120); the 3B and 8B rows match NO file,PARTIAL,"70B: raw 0.8090, pc:unified@2 0.8351 (+0.0262), datapca@2 0.6969 (-0.1120), random 0.5952 (-0.2138). 3B/8B: the matrices those rows were read from were written 22:18-22:21 on 2026-09-20 over harm-pressure-choice and OVERWRITTEN by the mask re-run at 23:38-23:40 the same night, same filenames. Current files: 3B L16 raw 0.7619 (+0.0195 / -0.1828 / -0.3099), 8B L16 raw 0.7980 (+0.0125 / -0.1022 / -0.1185).",recompute off-diagonal means from the matrix JSONs; read the crossgen logs; exhaustive search of every stored pooling x layer x probe x dataset_set for the stated raw values; git ls-files / ls-tree on both branches,"lab copy; 3B/8B matrices mtime 2026-09-20 23:40 / 23:38 with datasets field = [instructed-deception, mask, convincing-game, ai_liar, roleplaying]",no surviving cell reproduces the stated triplets; no copy in git on either branch; no crossgen sync to Drive after 21:40 that night,REVISED -> F-63,HIGH on the diagnosis (the overwrite is timestamped in the run's own log); the lost numbers are unverifiable by construction,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_matrix.py; P4_lab_scores.py; P4_scale.py,"NO RAW DATA for the 3B and 8B rows - the pre-mask matrices exist nowhere (lab, git, Drive). The 70B row verifies exactly, and its 'dataset PCA' and 'random' columns are the @2 variants matched to pc:unified@2 (the entry does not say so). F-63 does NOT inherit the problem: its cells are the mask matrices and reproduce to 4 dp. Anything still citing +0.089 / +0.086 is citing numbers with no surviving evidence.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] PHASE 4 AMENDMENT (verdict unchanged). 'No surviving evidence' is too strong. The crossgen logs are APPEND-MODE, so the 2026-09-20 22:18-22:21 block persists beneath the 23:38-23:40 mask re-run that overwrote the matrices; the 3B/8B rows were recovered from them (copies kept at audit/phase4/evidence_F2/crossgen_scale_{3b,8b,70b}.log). The matrix FILES are gone; the numbers are not. Phase 4 also separated three further defects: 3B/8B used harm-pressure-choice while the 70B row used mask (so 'the paper's five datasets' cannot be true of both); 3B/8B are k=3 and the 70B row k=5; and within the 70B row 'random' is k=5 while 'datapca' is datapca@2.",P4-scale
F-63,"Corrected three-rung comparison on the paper's five datasets at k=3, midpoint layers, mean pooling: raw 0.7619/0.7980/0.8090, best persona beats raw by only +0.020/+0.013/+0.013, and beats the matched dataset-PCA control by +0.202/+0.115/+0.079, a margin declining monotonically with model size.",0.7619 +0.020 -0.183 +0.202; 0.7980 +0.013 -0.102 +0.115; 0.8090 +0.013 -0.066 +0.079,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1992,"lab: run-crossgen/scale_{3b,8b,70b}/matrices/mean_L{16,16,40}_s42.json | audit/phase2/P4_lab_matrix.txt; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv","probe=paper, seed 42, k=3, mean pooling, 20 off-diagonal pairs, 5 datasets incl. mask",all nine table values match to the precision quoted,YES,"3B L16 raw 0.7619, axes 0.7815 (+0.0195), datapca 0.5791 (-0.1828), axis-dpca +0.2023; 8B L16 raw 0.7980, pc:deception 0.8105 (+0.0125), datapca 0.6958 (-0.1022), +0.1147; 70B L40 raw 0.8090, axes 0.8220 (+0.0131), datapca 0.7426 (-0.0663), +0.0794","off-diagonal mean over the 5x5 auroc matrix in each JSON, computed by my own script; cross-checked via layer_sensitivity.csv","mask version of the 3B/8B matrices (mtime 09-20 23:40/23:38); the 70B L40 cell is the paper16-bank one (RF-16) - confirmed, the audit's paper16-fp32 re-run reproduces it to 0.0001",3B L16 is the MAXIMUM of that rung's 7 stored layers (rank 1/7); 8B L16 rank 4/8; 70B L40 rank 13/21. Layer-mean margins +0.1197/+0.1027/+0.0791 (mean pooling) but +0.0745/+0.0090/+0.0945 under last pooling - the ordering breaks. Like-for-like paper16 70B: +0.0541 (mean) / +0.0681 (last).,PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - Level 2, two independent scripts, inputs on disk",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_matrix.py; P4_scale.py,"Numbers exact and bank-consistent across rungs - the soundest entry in the scale line. Two qualifications: the 3B cell is that rung's best layer, so the reported steepness is a layer-selection effect (F-100 measures the layer-mean 3B->8B step as 0.017, not 0.087); and the decline is mean-pooling-only (F-102). The remark that axes and pc:deception are 'all within 0.007 of each other' is wrong - the 8B and 70B gaps are 0.037 and 0.028.",P4-scale
F-100,"Layer-averaging every rung, the persona advantage over the matched dataset-PCA control is +0.1197/+0.1027/+0.0751 (19 layers at 70B; +0.0791 over 21), still monotone but much flatter than F-63's single-layer reading; and at 70B the advantage over raw activations is essentially nil, +0.0079, positive at 10 of 19 layers.",+0.1197; +0.1027; +0.0751; +0.0791; +0.0079; +0.0070; 10/19; 11/21; axes-dpca +0.0395/+0.0383; L40 rank 11/19 and 13/21; 3B L16 1/7; 8B L16 4/8; L72 -0.0099; L76 +0.0071,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4601,"lab: run-crossgen/scale_{3b,8b,70b}/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json | audit/phase2/P4_lab_matrix.txt; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv","best = per-layer max(axes, pc:deception), probe=paper, k=3, seed 42, mean pooling, 5 datasets","every figure matches exactly, including the amended 21-layer block and both layer ranks",YES,"3B n=7 raw 0.6989 best-raw +0.0328 (7/7) best-dpca +0.1197 (7/7); 8B n=8 raw 0.7149 +0.0089 (6/8) +0.1027 (8/8); 70B 19L raw 0.7524 +0.0079 (10/19) +0.0751 (18/19) axes-dpca +0.0395; 70B 21L raw 0.7546 +0.0070 (11/21) +0.0791 (20/21) +0.0383; ranks 1/7, 4/8, 11/19, 13/21; L72 -0.0099, L76 +0.0071",off-diagonal means recomputed from every matrix JSON by my own script; ranks and per-layer profiles from the same data,"the 70B sweep is the kd-bank sweep of 09-22 00:52-01:33 (RF-16), NOT paper16 as the source line says",like-for-like paper16 (the audit's re-run): 19 layers give best-raw -0.0131 and best-dpca +0.0541; last pooling gives +0.0069 / +0.0681 (21 layers),PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - Level 2, two independent scripts",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_matrix.py; P4_scale.py,"NEW DEFECT: the parenthetical 'axes loses to raw at every layer from 44 to 68 (-0.004 to -0.029)' attaches the wrong range to the wrong feature. Measured, axes-raw at L44-68 is -0.0221 to -0.1059; -0.004 to -0.029 is the pc:deception-raw range. And 'pc:deception holds up' is wrong: pc:deception also loses to raw at every one of those layers, just by less. Separately, the bank error (F-110) turns +0.0751 into +0.0541 and +0.0079 into -0.0131.",P4-scale
F-101,"For the 70B rung, switching from mean to last-token pooling raises the persona advantage over raw from +0.0070 (11/21 layers) to +0.0333 (19/21) and the matched-control margin from +0.0791 to +0.0945, while leaving axes-datapca unchanged; and L40 goes from mid-pack (13/21) to second-worst of 21 under last.","+0.0791/+0.0945; +0.0383/+0.0366; +0.0070/+0.0333; 11/21 vs 19/21; L40 +0.0794 rank 13/21, +0.0433 rank 19/21; ranges [-0.011,+0.139] and [+0.033,+0.196]; raw 0.7546/0.7454; persona 0.7615/0.7788",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4674,"lab: run-crossgen/scale_70b/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json | audit/phase2/P4_lab_matrix.txt; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv","21 layers, k=3, probe=paper, seed 42, 5 datasets",every figure matches exactly,YES,"mean: raw 0.7546 best 0.7615 best-raw +0.0070 (11/21) best-dpca +0.0791 (20/21) axes-dpca +0.0383 L40 rank 13; last: raw 0.7454 best 0.7788 best-raw +0.0333 (19/21) best-dpca +0.0945 (21/21) axes-dpca +0.0366 L40 rank 19; L40 best-dpca +0.0794 / +0.0433; ranges [-0.0114,+0.1386] / [+0.0329,+0.1955]",off-diagonal means recomputed from the matrix JSONs; ranks over the per-layer margins,"kd bank (the entry does name run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt, unlike F-100) - but it is compared against F-100's paper16-bank 3B/8B rungs","like-for-like paper16 (audit re-run, 21 layers): best-raw -0.0171 (mean) / +0.0069 (last); best-dpca +0.0550 / +0.0681; L40 rank 6/21 (mean) and 14/21 (last)",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - Level 2, two independent scripts",MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_matrix.py; P4_scale.py,"The pooling contrast survives the bank fix with roughly halved margins (+0.0069 vs -0.0171 against raw; +0.0681 vs +0.0550 against dPCA). The second headline does NOT survive: 'L40 is the second-worst layer of 21 under last' becomes rank 14/21 (mid-pack) on the paper16 bank, and 'quoting L40 understates the margin by more than a factor of two' becomes a factor of about 1.6. The general rule the entry draws ('report the layer-mean') is unaffected.",P4-scale
F-102,"Under last-token pooling the three-rung comparison is not monotone on the matched control (+0.0745/+0.0090/+0.0945) and reverses against raw (-0.0178 at 3B, -0.0742 at 8B, +0.0333 at 70B) - so F-63's decline is conditional on a pooling choice; and the truncation explanation is refuted because no row in either small rung hits the 1024-token cap.",+0.1197/+0.0745; +0.1027/+0.0090; +0.0791/+0.0945; +0.0328 (7/7)/-0.0178 (2/7); +0.0089 (6/8)/-0.0742 (0/8); +0.0070 (11/21)/+0.0333 (19/21); 2293/2293/6925 rows; 0.00% at cap; 6/6/0 within 8; 46/303/755/1000,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4728,"lab: run-crossgen/scale_{3b,8b,70b}/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json; run-scale/{3b,8b}/coords/*/rows.jsonl; run-coords/passB/*/rows.jsonl | audit/phase2/P4_lab_matrix.txt; P4_lab_trunc.txt",7/8/21 layers per rung; prompt_len + response_len vs cap 1024 / 8192 over the 5 shared datasets,every figure in both AUROC tables and in the truncation amendment matches exactly,YES,"3B mean +0.0328 (7/7) / +0.1197 (7/7), last -0.0178 (2/7) / +0.0745 (7/7); 8B mean +0.0089 (6/8) / +0.1027 (8/8), last -0.0742 (0/8) / +0.0090 (4/8); 70B mean +0.0070 (11/21) / +0.0791 (20/21), last +0.0333 (19/21) / +0.0945 (21/21). Truncation: 3B/8B 2,293 rows, 0 at cap, 6 within 8, median 46 p90 303 p99 755 max 1000, IDENTICAL sorted-length fingerprint; 70B passB 6,925 rows, response_len key absent.",off-diagonal means from the matrix JSONs; truncation check reimplemented from rows.jsonl (prompt_len + response_len vs the rung's cap),"the 70B column is the kd-bank sweep (RF-16); the 3B/8B last matrices are the original 2026-09-20 write (mtime 23:40/23:38), the same run as the mean ones","8B last datapca 0.702-0.739 at L12-28 vs mean 0.595-0.769 (exact as stated); random across all rungs and poolings 0.4455-0.6894 (the entry says 0.49-0.69 - the floor is slightly off, immaterial)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - Level 2 throughout; the truncation check was reimplemented from rows.jsonl rather than read,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_matrix.py; P4_lab_trunc.py; P4_scale.py,"Core conclusion confirmed: the monotone decline is conditional on pooling. One sub-claim is a kd-bank artifact - 'under last the 70B becomes the HIGHEST of the three' becomes 3B +0.0745 > 70B +0.0681 > 8B +0.0090 like-for-like (still non-monotone, so the conclusion survives). The sign reversal against raw also survives but shrinks: -0.0178 / -0.0742 / +0.0069 instead of +0.0333 at 70B. Wording nit: the 70B response_len is not 'all zeros', the key is absent from passB rows.",P4-scale
F-110,"The audit's own correction: run-crossgen/scale_70b mixes two banks under one label (L40 = paper16, the other 40 matrices = the 36-persona kd bank), so re-running the sweep like-for-like on paper16 gives a three-rung matched-control margin of +0.1197/+0.1027/+0.0541 and turns the 70B margin over raw from +0.0079 to -0.0131.",+0.1197; +0.1027; +0.0751; +0.0541; +0.0079; -0.0131; raw 0.6989/0.7149/0.7524; last +0.0069/+0.0681; L40 agreement <=0.0003; kd differs by up to 0.077,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:5238; audit/fix/RF16_NOTE.md,"lab: run-crossgen/scale_70b_paper16fp32/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json (42 new) and run-crossgen/scale_{3b,8b,70b}/matrices | audit/phase2/P4_lab_matrix.txt; audit/fix/rf16_recompute_mean.txt; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv","F-100's 19-layer set, mean pooling, best = max(axes, pc:deception), probe=paper, k=3, seed 42",all four table rows match exactly,YES,3B raw 0.6989 best-raw +0.0328 best-dpca +0.1197; 8B 0.7149 +0.0089 +0.1027; 70B kd 0.7524 +0.0079 +0.0751; 70B paper16fp32 0.7524 -0.0131 +0.0541. Last pooling (21 layers) +0.0069 / +0.0681. L40: scale_70b axes 0.8220 vs scale_70b_paper16fp32 axes 0.8219 (delta 0.0001); bank fields axes_vectors_s3.pt / paper16_70b (mtime 09-20 23:42) vs axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt / paper16_70b_fp32 (09-23 00:09).,off-diagonal means recomputed straight from the matrix JSONs by a script written independently of fix_rf16_recompute.py; cross-checked a third way through layer_sensitivity.csv,the audit's own re-run of the owner's 27_crossgen.py into a new folder; nothing existing touched,"three independent computational paths agree to 4 dp; F-63's 70B cell reproduces from the paper16fp32 store (raw 0.8090, axes-raw +0.0130, axes-dpca +0.0793), confirming 'F-63 is unaffected'",HOLDS,HIGH - three independent paths; bank identity confirmed from fields inside the files plus the <=0.0003 L40 agreement,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P4_lab_matrix.py; P4_scale.py,"Two things to state more precisely in the entry. (1) Its last-pooling figures (+0.0069 / +0.0681) are the 21-LAYER means while its main table is F-100's 19-layer set; the 19-layer last values are +0.0061 / +0.0688 (immaterial, but the mixed layer set should be named). (2) The corrected decline is still mean-pooling-only: like-for-like under last the three rungs read +0.0745 / +0.0090 / +0.0688, non-monotone with the 8B as outlier, so 'the decline is steeper' should carry F-102's pooling qualifier.",P4-scale
D-003,"On HP-KR the published 8-vs-7 persona contrast inverts: zero-shot AUROC 0.148 at layer 20 on Llama-3.3-70B, re-extracted persona bank, response-mean pooling, no seed (deterministic direction).",0.148,draft main (1).pdf p.1 Abstract + p.7 sec 5.1 + Table 2; draft_claims_raw.csv D-003,git show origin/feat/persona-pc-ood:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot.csv,"row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain, col auroc_axis",0.1482769784172662,"YES (draft 0.148, tol 5e-4)",Level 2 on his pipeline: NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone). What IS recomputed: his aggregates re-derived from his own committed cell-level CSVs.,"Cross-checked against his zero_shot_operating.csv (same layer/arm/dataset): 0.1483, identical. n=2139, n_deceptive=139.","origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip, read with `git show` (never checked out); his activations are gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible (owner's rule). Files are his own committed CSVs; not touched by the 09-22 re-run wave (RF-13), which hit the OWNER's lab stores only.","Same direction at L40 0.5926 and L44 0.5895 (draft quotes 0.593/0.589; both match) -> the INVERSION is layer-20-only; at L40/L44 it is near chance, not inverted. On the ORIGINAL (pre-re-extraction) bank the same grouping reads 0.1029 (persona_ood/zero_shot.csv).",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only),"HIGH - exact match, cross-checked in two of his files","HIGH - abstract, contribution 3, Fig 3, Table 2",audit/scripts/claims/P5_draft_headlines.py,"Single run, single bank, one pooling. The word 'inverts' is exact only at L20.",P5-draft-headlines
D-004,"Every HP-KR lie is a denial of knowledge, and none of Mahadik & Skapars' 8 published deceptive personas lies by denying knowledge.",(none - qualitative),draft p.1 Abstract + p.7 sec 5.1; draft_claims_raw.csv D-004,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf p.5; papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf p.9 Table 2,LB p.5 HP-KR definition; M&S Table 2 (8 deceptive personas) and Table 3 (7 honest),"LB p.5: HP-KR is 'labeled deceptive if the model denies knowing the answer despite that established belief, and honest otherwise'. M&S Table 2: handler 'controls timing, emphasis, and selective disclosure'; coverup operator 'buries or excludes material facts'; plausible denier 'gives defensible half-disclosures'; plus broker, impression manager, gatekeeper, spin doctor, narrative manager. None mentions claiming not to know.","YES - all three quotations in the draft are verbatim/near-verbatim from M&S Table 2, and the HP-KR label rule is as the benchmark states it","NOT TESTED - the causal half ('that is why the contrast has nothing to go on') is argued from persona descriptions, not measured.",Read both source PDFs during this audit (pypdf text extraction).,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip, read with `git show` (never checked out); his activations are gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible (owner's rule). Files are his own committed CSVs; not touched by the 09-22 re-run wave (RF-13), which hit the OWNER's lab stores only.","The owner's own work bears on this: HP-KR's honest class pools affirmations with knowledge-free denials (LB p.5), so a denial-wording detector scores well without detecting deception - the draft concedes this in sec 6. The inversion is L20-only, which the persona-coverage story does not by itself predict.",PARTLY HOLDS (quotations and the benchmark's label rule verified; the causal claim is untested),MED - the descriptive half is verified from primary sources; the explanatory half has no test in the draft or on his branch,HIGH - it is the paper's causal story,audit/scripts/claims/P5_draft_headlines.py,"Also checked the bank arithmetic: M&S Tables 2-5 give 8+7+5+6=26 personas, matching the draft's '26 personas of Mahadik and Skapars'; 8+4 v 7+3+3 = 12 v 13 as the draft says.",P5-draft-headlines
D-006,"At layer 40 on HP-KR, one zero-shot contrast direction (the 4-vs-6 knowledge-denial contrast) reaches AUROC 0.919 and balanced accuracy 0.910 at a threshold flagging <=1% of the Alpaca control.",0.919; 0.910; 1% FPR,draft p.1 Abstract; draft_claims_raw.csv D-006,git show origin/feat/persona-pc-ood:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L40/zero_shot.csv and .../zero_shot_operating.csv,"auroc_denial_axis @ harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain; operating row (arm='knowledge-denial axis (4v6)', dataset=HP-KR, threshold_source='control')",AUROC 0.918536 (operating file 0.9185); balacc 0.9102; recall 0.8849; specificity 0.9355,YES (0.9185 -> 0.919; 0.9102 -> 0.910),Level 2 on his pipeline: NOT POSSIBLE (activations gone). What IS recomputed: his aggregates re-derived from his own committed cell-level CSVs.,Cross-file check: all 54 zero_shot.csv AUROCs equal the zero_shot_operating.csv AUROCs (0 mismatches).,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip, read with `git show` (never checked out); his activations are gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible (owner's rule). Files are his own committed CSVs; not touched by the 09-22 re-run wave (RF-13), which hit the OWNER's lab stores only.","Bootstrap 95% CI (his, 1000 resamples over examples): AUROC [0.8878, 0.9450], balacc [0.8835, 0.9369]. Same axis at L20 balacc 0.5331 and L44 0.7571 -> the 0.910 is a LAYER-40-ONLY operating point. n_deceptive=139 of n=2139.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only),"HIGH for the arithmetic; MED for the claim as read, see notes",HIGH - abstract headline,audit/scripts/claims/P5_draft_headlines.py,"AMBIGUITY: the abstract's 'a single contrast direction' here is the 4v6 knowledge-denial axis, while the abstract's transfer headline (D-008) uses the 12v13 EXTENDED axis. Two different directions carry the two halves of one abstract; only Table 2 disambiguates. The extended axis's balanced accuracy on HP-KR is 0.500 at all three layers.",P5-draft-headlines
D-008,"Over the 6x6 train-test matrix at layer 40, the extended 12-vs-13 contrast reaches 0.916 mean off-diagonal AUROC against 0.732 for 8192-d logistic probes each trained on one dataset.",0.916; 0.732,draft p.1 Abstract + p.8 sec 5.2 + Table 3; draft_claims_raw.csv D-008,git show origin/feat/persona-pc-ood:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L40/summary.csv,"rows features=ext_axis1 and features=baseline, col off_diagonal_mean",ext_axis1 0.915835; baseline 0.732033,"YES (both, tol 5e-4)",Re-derived from his matrix_ext_axis1.csv / matrix_baseline.csv: 0.9158 and 0.7320 (30 off-diagonal cells). All 24 (layer x feature) summary values reproduce from the matrices.,Mean of the 30 off-diagonal cells of each matrix CSV; audit/scripts/claims/P5_draft_headlines.py section 'Off-diagonal mean recomputed from the matrices'.,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood @ tip, read with `git show` (never checked out); his activations are gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible (owner's rule). Files are his own committed CSVs; not touched by the 09-22 re-run wave (RF-13), which hit the OWNER's lab stores only.","Excluding HP-KR: 0.9165 vs 0.7581 - the gap survives (+0.158). Random 3-d directions give 0.504 at L40, so the comparison is not a ceiling artifact of 1-d features alone. BUT see notes.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1; aggregate also re-derived from his cells),HIGH for the arithmetic,HIGH - abstract + contribution 4 + Table 3 + Fig 4,audit/scripts/claims/P5_draft_headlines.py,"STRUCTURAL CAVEAT (audit's, not his): for a 1-d feature the trained probe learns only a sign, so his ext_axis1 matrix rows are constant and its 'mean off-diagonal AUROC' equals its mean ZERO-SHOT AUROC over the 6 datasets (0.9158 both ways, verified). The headline therefore compares a fixed direction against probes that fit each training set - which the draft does say in the Fig 4 caption, but the number is not a transfer measurement in the same sense. DECOMPOSITION: at L40 raw 0.732 -> published 8