F-07,"The teacher-forced d_knowledge direction has split-half reliability 0.988 / 0.995 / 0.993 at layers 20 / 40 / 44 against a random-direction pair floor of 0.007, so the 121-item not-know class was large enough.",0.988; 0.995; 0.993; 0.007; 121 items,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:114-124,C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/results/phase2_gate.json ; C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/run/factor_probes/kd_knowledge/rows.jsonl,rows[layer].split_half_cos and rows[layer].random_pair_cos ; label counts in rows.jsonl,"split_half_cos 0.987614 / 0.995458 / 0.993126 ; random_pair_cos 0.007934 / 0.008941 / 0.007103 ; labels {1: 1841, 0: 121}, total 1962",YES for the three reliabilities (to 3dp) and for 121; PARTIAL for '0.007' (that is the L44 value; L20 rounds to 0.008 and L40 to 0.009),"121 independently recounted from kd_knowledge/rows.jsonl (1,841 knows / 121 not-knows = 1,962). kd_utterance is balanced 900/900. n_text_matched 258, n_knowledge_matched 2001 also confirmed in the same file.","Read the producing file and recount the label classes in the row file (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py, read-only on the lab).","Lab copy, mtime 2026-09-19 20:28:44 (gate) / 19:59:07 (rows). Not in git; on Drive. Untouched by the 2026-09-22 wave (RF-13). rows.jsonl is an RF-11 lab-not-equal-git file; the lab copy is the one the gate read. No BH q.",The claim already spans three layers and they agree (0.988-0.995). The split-half halving is a single deterministic split recorded in the gate file; varying it would need the activations.,HOLDS,"HIGH for the three reliabilities and the 121 count; MEDIUM for the single '0.007' floor, which is the smallest of three values (0.0079 / 0.0089 / 0.0071)","MEDIUM - a construction check that retired a planned NDIF run; reliability is not validity, as the entry says",audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py (output audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_a.txt),The entry presents one floor where the file has three. Everything else matches exactly.,P6-kd-rest
F-10,"Score-3 filtering of the kd persona bank keeps 116.8 / 89.0 / 73.3 rollouts per role in knowledge_denial / sincere_ignorance / plain_assertion (imbalance 1.31x and 1.59x), while scores 2+3 keep 146.8 / 150.0 / 149.0 (imbalance 0.98x); only 16 of 1,500 new-group rollouts scored 0 or 1.","116.8/146.8; 89.0/150.0; 73.3/149.0; 1.31x; 1.59x; 0.98x; 16 of 1,500; ~30%; 467 vs 267",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:155-174,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/scores/*.json (35 files, 2026-09-20 00:21-01:32) ; C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json","per-role Counter of judge scores 0-3, grouped by the groups in kd_role_groups.json",print-only claim - no result file holds these numbers,n/a (no file),"kd 116.8 / 146.8 (4 roles, 467/587); sincere 89.0 / 150.0 (3 roles, 267/450); plain 73.3 / 149.0 (3 roles, 220/447); s3 imbalance 1.31x and 1.59x; s23 imbalance 0.98x both; 16 of 1,500 scored 0 or 1; 467 vs 267 confirmed. The '~30%' discard is 530 of 1,500 = 35.3%.","Reimplemented kd/scripts/verify_s23.py from the raw judge-score JSONs, plus a per-role score histogram the original does not print (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py, read-only on the lab).","Lab copies, 2026-09-20 00:21-01:32; also on Drive, not in git. NOT rewritten by the 09-22 wave. kd_role_groups.json lab = git. No BH q.","Not applicable - these are counts of a fixed judged corpus. Both threshold settings (s3, s23) are already reported.",HOLDS,HIGH - seven of eight numbers reproduce exactly from the raw judge scores,MEDIUM - it is the premise for the s23 control arm and therefore for F-19,audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py (output audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_a.txt),"'s3 discards ~30%' is really 35.3% (530 of 1,500 scored exactly 2; total s3 discard 36.4%). Per-role histograms show the imbalance is driven by two roles: pc_deniable_expert loses 78 of 150 to score 2 while pc_feigned_novice loses only 12, and every honest role loses 40-84. kd_role_groups.json declares 36 roles but run-kd/scores/ holds 35 files - the missing one is the unjudged 'default' anchor, which is in none of the three groups.",P6-kd-rest
F-11,"On the s3 kd bank at layer 40 the group centroids project onto the assistant axis at knowledge_denial -0.22, sincere_ignorance +1.60, plain_assertion +0.90, deception 1.51 and honesty 2.20, so the two sides of the knowledge-denial contrast are 1.82 apart against 0.69 for the paper16 deception contrast; cos(PC1, assistant) = 0.583 and the default anchor sits at relative position 0.882.",-0.22; +1.60; +0.90; 1.51; 2.20; 1.82; 0.69; 0.583; 0.882,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:179-196,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/kd_axes.log (s3 block, lines 52-76) ; C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/vectors_s3/*.pt + run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt","'mean projection on each axis, by group', column assistant, layer 40; line 52 cos(PC1, assistant); line 63 default anchor relative position","log s3 block prints -0.22 / 1.60 / 0.90 / 1.51 / 2.20, cos +0.583, anchor 0.882",YES - all nine,"Recomputed from the 36 per-role vectors: kd -0.22, sincere +1.60, plain +0.90, deception 1.51, honesty 2.20; gap 1.8205; paper16 gap 0.69; cos(PC1[all-roles], assistant) +0.583; default anchor 0.882.","Group centroid at L40 dotted with the unit assistant axis, following src/assistant_axis_ndif/6_axes.py (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py); layer sweep in P6_lab_d.py.","Lab only (RF-10). run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt rewritten 2026-09-22 15:41:57 by the boot-trigger wave (RF-13), but the axes are deterministic from run-kd/vectors_s3 (unchanged since 2026-09-20 03:04) and the recomputation reproduces the pre-wave log exactly. No BH q.","21-layer sweep: the absolute gap grows monotonically with depth (0.03 at L0 to 4.50 at L76), so 1.82 is an L40 quantity only. The RATIO to the paper16 deception gap is 2.6-4.0x at every layer, so the qualitative claim is layer-robust. cos(PC1, assistant) stays 0.54-0.70, never reaching the Assistant-Axis paper's 0.71. A third arm in the same log, the unfiltered axes_vectors_all.pt bank, gives an L40 gap of 1.60.",HOLDS,HIGH - every number re-derived from the raw per-role vectors and matched to the log block it cites,"HIGH - it is why axes_resid and erase:assistant are treated as load-bearing controls, and the geometric ground for the 'persona axes encode register' note","audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py, P6_lab_d.py (outputs audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_b.txt, P6_lab_d.txt)","logs/kd_axes.log interleaves SIX report blocks from TWO banks - axes_vectors_all.pt (unfiltered: kd +0.16, sincere 1.76, plain 1.47, gap 1.60, cos 0.607, anchor 0.895) and axes_vectors_s3.pt. F-11 quotes the s3 block, correctly. Quote 1.82 only with its layer.",P6-kd-rest
F-12,"Against every possible balanced split of the same personas at layer 40, cos(PC1, own contrast) is significant for sycophancy (0.993 vs median 0.534 over 252 splits, p=0.0079) and deception (0.961 vs 0.528 over 6,435, p=0.0092) but not for knowledge_denial (0.894 vs 0.397 over only 35 splits, p=0.143).","0.993; 0.534; 0.0079; 0.961; 0.528; 0.0092; 0.894; 0.397; 0.143; 252; 6,435; 35",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:198-216,"stdout only. Inputs C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/vectors_s3/*.pt (36) and run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt (role_groups); producer C:/Users/user4/expLB/perm.py (lab-only loose script, in no branch - RF-8)","one printed line per tag: cos(PC1,real), all-splits median, max, p",print-only claim - no result file holds these numbers,n/a (no file),"sycophancy 5v5, 252 splits, cos 0.993, median 0.534, max 0.993, p=0.0079; deception 8v7, 6,435 splits, cos 0.961, median 0.528, max 0.986, p=0.0092; knowledge_denial 4v3, 35 splits, cos 0.894, median 0.397, max 0.949, p=0.1429. All nine numbers reproduce.","Reimplemented perm.py (read on the lab, not executed): PCA over pos+neg+anchor role vectors centred across roles, PC1 by SVD, p = share of all C(|pool|,|pos|) splits with |cos| >= the real one (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py); layer sweep in P6_lab_d.py.","Lab only. vectors_s3 unchanged since 2026-09-20 03:04; axes_vectors_s3.pt regenerated 2026-09-22 15:41:57 (RF-13) but used only for role_groups, so the regeneration cannot move these numbers. No BH q.","21-layer sweep: sycophancy p = 0.008 at 20 of 21 layers (floor 1/252 = 0.004); deception p = 0.006-0.036, significant at all 21; knowledge_denial NEVER reaches p < 0.05 anywhere, best 0.057 (floor 1/35 = 0.029). So the non-significance is a property of having 7 personas, not of layer 40.",HOLDS,"HIGH - every number reproduced by an independent reimplementation, and the conclusions survive a full 21-layer sweep","MEDIUM - a construction check by the entry's own admission, but it is the project's clearest statement that the kd bank is underpowered by design","audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py, P6_lab_d.py (outputs audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_b.txt, P6_lab_d.txt)","The sub-claim 'the sycophancy split is the single best of all 252' is confirmed (max = real = 0.993). For deception the real split is NOT the best (max 0.986 > 0.961), which the entry does not say but does not contradict.",P6-kd-rest
F-17,"At layer 40 on the root 10-dataset crossgen grid, the unified persona axis scores -0.003 against a dataset-PCA control of the same rank, and a random 2-d projection gains +0.056 where raw AUROC < 0.6 while losing 0.44 where raw >= 0.85, with corr(raw, delta) = -0.76.",-0.003; +0.056; -0.44; -0.76,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:272-279,"run-crossgen/significance.json (git 86,720 B 2026-09-18; lab 2,247,993 B 2026-09-22 15:40:53) for -0.003 ; run-crossgen/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git and lab, both 349,229 B) for the other three - NOT the file the entry cites","tests[block='10', pooling='mean', layer=40, probe='paper', comparison='pc:unified@2 - datapca@2'].diff ; results[feature in {'random@2','raw'}, probe='paper'].auroc over the 90 OFF-DIAGONAL cells",git: diff -0.0028 (q 0.9733). lab: diff -0.0028 (q 0.9842).,YES for -0.003 on both copies (the q moves but no q is quoted),"From the per-cell matrix, probe='paper', off-diagonal: mean(random@2 - raw) where raw<0.6 = +0.0555 (n=32); where raw>=0.85 = -0.4378 (n=25); corr(raw, delta) = -0.7565. All three match the stated +0.056 / -0.44 / -0.76.","Recomputed from raw per-cell AUROCs; swept probe x cell-set so the reading is not assumed, and repeated at all 21 stored layers on the lab (audit/scripts/claims/F-17.py).","git and lab agree on the diff; matrices byte-identical on both. Bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5 (RF-15 fp32 re-extraction, cosine 1.0000 to the old axes). significance.json was regenerated on the lab 2026-09-22 15:40:53 (RF-13) but only the BH q changed.","MATCHED CONTROL, 21 layers (audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv, store '<root>', seed 42, mean, paper, all 10 datasets): pc:unified@2 - datapca@2 is NEGATIVE at 18 of 21 layers (range -0.105 to +0.050), and L40's -0.003 is the LEAST negative interior layer - so -0.003 is the claim's most favourable reading. RANDOM-PROJECTION artefact, 21 layers: gain on raw<0.6 is +0.032..+0.137 and loss on raw>=0.85 is -0.274..-0.436 at EVERY layer, corr -0.717..-0.870; L40 has the weakest correlation of the 21.",HOLDS,"HIGH for the arithmetic (all four numbers recomputed from raw per-cell AUROCs on two independent copies, swept over 21 layers); MEDIUM on presentation",HIGH - the regression-to-the-mean argument that undercuts every 'persona coordinates beat raw' headline; the memory note matched-control-kills-the-gain rests on it,audit/scripts/claims/F-17.py (outputs audit/phase2/out/P6/F-17_git.txt; lab section of P6_lab_c.txt); layer robustness also from audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv,"FLAG WITHDRAWN: an earlier audit note said these numbers were missing. They are not - three of the four live in run-crossgen/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json, which is in git, not in the significance.json the entry cites. UNDERSPECIFIED: the entry names neither the probe nor the cell set. The stated triple is probe='paper' over OFF-DIAGONAL cells; including the diagonal gives -0.3869 and -0.7165, and the other probes give +0.0123/-0.4679/-0.7372 (lr_reg10) and +0.1149/-0.4796/-0.8147 (mms). Ledger status 'inherited - not re-verified' can now be changed to verified.",P6-kd-rest
F-18,"The run-paper16 and run-paper16-shared persona banks give nearly identical contrast DIRECTIONS at layer 40 (cross-bank cosine +0.949 deception, +0.966 sycophancy, +0.984 unified, +0.631 assistant) and near-identical deception/sycophancy PCA alignment (+0.966/+0.952 and +0.979/+0.993), but their unified PCA bases differ sharply: cos(PC1, unified contrast) +0.389 vs +0.896, PC1 variance 46.7% vs 36.8%; rollouts 1,400 vs 2,600.","1,400; 2,600; +0.966; +0.952; +0.979; +0.993; +0.389; +0.896; 46.7%; 36.8%; +0.949; +0.966; +0.984; +0.631",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:281-309,C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3.pt (2026-09-15) ; .../axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (2026-09-16) ; C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-paper16-shared/axes_vectors_s3.pt (2026-09-18) ; rollout counts from run-paper16(-shared)/responses/*.jsonl,pca[tag].components[li(40)][0] . axes[tag][li] ; pca[tag].variance_ratio[li][0] ; cross-bank cos(axes[tag][li]),print-only claim - no result file holds these numbers,n/a (no file),"paper16: deception +0.966 (47.7%), sycophancy +0.979 (47.7%), unified +0.389 (46.7%). paper16-shared: +0.952 (45.0%), +0.993 (47.9%), +0.896 (36.8%). Cross-bank axis cosines +0.949 / +0.966 / +0.984 / +0.631. Rollouts 1,400 (26 files) and 2,600 (26 files). All fourteen numbers reproduce.","Reimplemented cmp_banks.py (read on the lab, not executed), extended to load the fp32 rebuild as well and to print cos(PC1, contrast) at all 80 stored layers (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py).","Lab copies. RF-15 CLOSED FOR THIS ENTRY: the OLD paper16 axes and the fp32 rebuild give IDENTICAL values at L40 (all four axes cosine +1.000, same pinned PC sign +1.0, same PC1 variances to 0.1%), and differ by at most 0.01 in cos(PC1,contrast) at 4 of 240 basis-by-layer cells (deception L34, sycophancy L7, unified L63/L73). Neither bank was touched by the 09-22 wave. No BH q.","80-layer sweep: paper16-shared's cos(PC1, unified contrast) is higher at 80 of 80 layers (+0.78..+0.91 vs +0.30..+0.83, gap 0.32-0.58 in the mid network). Deception: the two banks are within 0.02 at every layer. Sycophancy: shared is 0.01-0.05 HIGHER at every layer, so 'never affected' slightly understates a small consistent gain. Both banks deterministic (no seed); both score-3, as the caveat says.",HOLDS,"HIGH - all fourteen numbers reproduced by an independent reimplementation, checked on both the old and the fp32 bank, and swept over 80 layers","MEDIUM-HIGH - the evidence behind 'use run-paper16-shared for the unified axis', and the geometric counterpart of the memory note unified-pc1-is-question-family",audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py (output audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_b.txt),"PROVENANCE NIT (no number changes): cmp_banks.py counts rollouts under Path(bank['vectors_dir']).parent/'responses'. The OLD run-paper16 bank records a LAPTOP vectors_dir, so running the cited command on the lab with that bank prints 'rollouts 0', not 1,400 (reproduced). The 1,400 is correct - it is the line count under run-paper16/responses, which the fp32 bank's recorded path resolves to - but the entry's cited invocation could not have produced it. The ledger's source line should say fp32 or name the responses dir directly.",P6-kd-rest
F-19,"Rebuilding the kd bank with scores 2+3 (s23) balances the sample counts from 1.31x to 0.98x but cuts the layer-40 assistant-axis gap between knowledge_denial and sincere_ignorance only from 1.82 to 1.67 (about 8%), so roughly nine tenths of the drift is intrinsic to the personas rather than to score-3 filtering.",-0.22/-0.01; +1.60/+1.66; +0.90/+1.37; 1.82/1.67; ~8%; 1.31x/0.98x; 0.961->0.965; 0.993->0.993; 0.887->0.909; 0.583->0.620,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:311-340,C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/kd_axes_s23.log and logs/kd_axes.log ; recomputed from C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/vectors_s23/*.pt + run-kd/axes_vectors_s23.pt (and the s3 pair),"'mean projection on each axis, by group', column assistant, layer 40 (s23 log lines 28-36); line 14 cos(PC1, assistant); lines 19-22 per-behaviour cos(PC1, contrast)","s23 log prints -0.01 / 1.66 / 1.37, cos(PC1,assistant) +0.620, deception 0.965, anchor 0.898; s3 log prints -0.22 / 1.60 / 0.90, +0.583, 0.961",YES - all eleven,"Recomputed from the per-role vectors: s23 kd -0.01, sincere +1.66, plain +1.37, gap 1.6668; s3 gap 1.8205; fall 8.4%; cos(PC1,contrast) deception 0.961->0.965, sycophancy 0.993->0.993, unified 0.887->0.909; cos(PC1,assistant) 0.583->0.620; imbalance 1.31x->0.98x (F-10).","Same recomputation as F-11 on both banks, plus a 21-layer sweep of the s3-vs-s23 fall (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py, P6_lab_d.py).",Lab only (RF-10). run-kd/axes_vectors_s23.pt rewritten 2026-09-22 16:00:24 (RF-13) but deterministic from run-kd/vectors_s23 (unchanged since 2026-09-20 12:40); the recomputation reproduces the pre-wave log exactly. No BH q.,"21-layer sweep: the fall is 7.2%-17.4% at every layer, i.e. 83-93% of the gap always survives balancing, so the conclusion is not layer-specific. The 8.4% at L40 is near the MINIMUM of the sweep (median ~10%), so L40 is the most favourable layer for the claim. A third arm, the unfiltered axes_vectors_all.pt bank, gives an L40 gap of 1.60 = 88% of the s3 value with no score filter at all.",HOLDS,HIGH - every quoted number re-derived from the raw per-role vectors and matched to its log line; conclusion survives a 21-layer sweep and a third arm,HIGH - the control that made axes_resid and erase:assistant required rather than optional; the ledger's flagship negative result,"audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_b.py, P6_lab_d.py (outputs audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_b.txt, P6_lab_d.txt)","OMISSION: 'geometry improved slightly' is true for the three paper16 bases but FALSE for the knowledge-denial basis the experiment is about - cos(PC1, kd contrast) falls 0.894 -> 0.841 under s23 (printed in kd_axes_s23.log line 99). The ledger should say so.",P6-kd-rest
F-20,"The harm-pressure-kr-matched slice is balanced only in passB (2,139 HP-KR rows -> 258 matched, 124 deceptive / 134 honest); in the 200-row passA and passC subsamples it collapsed to 98 rows at 89 deceptive / 9 honest, so those grids run with 10 datasets, not 11.","2,139; 258; 124/134; 200; 98; 89/9; 10 vs 11 datasets",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:342-366,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/pass{A,B,C}/harm-pressure-{knowledge-report,kr-matched}/rows.jsonl ; logs/kd_passAC.log ; logs/passAC11_view.log ; run-crossgen/{,kd11/}pass{A,C}/splits.json ; run-crossgen/{kd11,kd11/passA,kd11/passC,passA,passC}/matrices/*.json",row counts and label Counter per rows.jsonl ; splits['42']['harm-pressure-knowledge-report']['test_row_ids'] intersected with the matched row_ids ; matrix field 'datasets',"passB: HP-KR 2,139 {139/2000}, matched 258 {124/134} - MATCHES. passA/passC TODAY: HP-KR 2,139 and matched 258 {124/134} - the 200-row / 98-row state is gone. kd_passAC.log (2026-09-20 13:35) shows HP-KR n=200 100D/100H and 'harm-pressure-kr-matched: no rows' in both stores.",YES for passB and for the 200-row stratified premise; NO FILE for the 98 and 89/9,"Reconstructed two ways. (a) run-crossgen/passA/splits.json (2026-09-19 14:16, pre-top-up) stores the seed-42 HP-KR test set: 40 row_ids, of which 20 are in the matched slice with labels {deceptive 18, honest 2}; passC and both kd11 copies give the same; the five other seeds give 16-20 matched at 15:1 to 17:3. Scaled to 200 rows that is ~100 matched at ~90:10. (b) Hypergeometric expectation for a 100D/100H draw: 100*124/139 = 89.2 deceptive (sd 1.6) and 100*134/2000 = 6.7 honest (sd 2.4). F-20's 89 / 9 sits on both.","Recount rows.jsonl per store; intersect the surviving pre-top-up split row_ids with the matched slice; check every passA/passC matrix's dataset list (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py, P6_lab_c.py). make_view_ac.py WRITES files, so it was not run - only its read-only half was reimplemented.","Lab only (RF-10). passA/passC HP-KR topped up 2026-09-21 11:29 and 11:52; their kr-matched views rebuilt 2026-09-22 15:47:01 by the boot-trigger wave (RF-13) - which is why the claim's own state no longer exists. passB's view untouched (2026-09-19 20:09). make_view_ac.py exists only as a loose lab file, in no branch (RF-8). No BH q.","Not applicable - a composition fact, as the entry says. What was checked instead is whether the rule was followed downstream: every passA/passC matrix lists 10 datasets and none contains harm-pressure-kr-matched (kd11/passA 160 files, kd11/passC 12, passA 960, passC 72), while the passB grid kd11/matrices (42 files) lists 11 and does contain it. audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv agrees: n_datasets = 10 for every passA/passC row.",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for passB, for the 200-row stratified premise and for the 10-dataset rule; MEDIUM for the literal 98 and 89/9, which have strong indirect corroboration but no surviving direct record",MEDIUM-HIGH - the guard that kept a 9-negative AUROC out of the heatmaps and the reason the passA/passC grids are 10-dataset,"audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py, P6_lab_c.py (outputs audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_a.txt, P6_lab_c.txt)","The entry's table now describes a state no file holds. It should be dated or annotated: passA/passC were topped up on 2026-09-21 and their views rebuilt on 2026-09-22, and all three stores now carry the same 258 rows at 124/134. Any passA/passC result computed before 2026-09-21 used the 200-row HP-KR.",P6-kd-rest
F-59,"A pre-registered gate of denial rate >= 0.70 failed on all three routes for growing the HP-KR matched slice: 5/20 = 0.250 on wrong items with the harmful template, 3/20 = 0.150 with the neutral template, and 5/12 = 0.417 when selecting on the model's own confidence - so stated knowledge tracks confidence, not correctness; the model claims to know 75% of the items it gets wrong.",0.70; 0.250; 0.150; 0.417; 75%; 312 wrong items; 8 of 20 lost to OOM; +-0.10,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1829-1863,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/run/denial/{rollouts,control,margin}.jsonl ; C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/hpkr_denial_{smoke,control,margin}.log ; C:/Users/user4/expLB/kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl (FULL lab copy, 279,757 B)","share of rows with denies==true per jsonl; GATE lines smoke.log:210, control.log:208, margin.log:551; count of correct==0 in scores.jsonl","GATE lines read: 5/20 = 0.250 (GATE FAILED), 3/20 = 0.150 (GATE FAILED), 5/12 = 0.417",YES - all three,"Recomputed from the raw rollouts: 5/20 = 0.250, 3/20 = 0.150, 5/12 = 0.417; 15 of 20 primary rollouts do not deny = 75%; correct==0 in the full scores.jsonl = 312 of 1,459 (accuracy 0.7862; bio 0.8674, cyber 0.7358 - which also reproduces F-08); margin route has 12 rows where the logs say 20 selected, i.e. 8 lost.",Recount the denies field per rollout file; recount correct==0 in the FULL lab scores.jsonl; cross-check each route's selection by joining item_ids back to scores.jsonl (audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py). Exact binomial CIs and Fisher tests in audit/scripts/claims/F-59_power.py.,"Lab copies. RF-5 APPLIES: the committed kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl is truncated to exactly 204,800 B (1,095 of 1,459 records) by the scp 200-KiB bug, so the git copy would select different items and cannot be used; the lab copy (279,757 B) is what the run read. Denial rollouts (2026-09-20 22:53-22:56) and logs untouched by the 09-22 wave. No BH q.","Exact binomial 95% CIs: primary [0.087,0.491], fallback1 [0.032,0.379], fallback2 [0.152,0.723]. So 0.70 is EXCLUDED for the two correct==0 routes (gate solidly failed) but NOT for fallback 2, which matches the entry's own 'MARGINAL'. The two directional readings are not distinguishable at this n: Fisher two-sided 5/20 vs 3/20 p=0.6948, 5/20 vs 5/12 p=0.4382, 3/20 vs 5/12 p=0.1161. Selection was verified: primary and fallback1 items all have correct=0 and margins 0.947-1.000; fallback2 items have margins 0.097-0.345 and include 3 the model got RIGHT.",HOLDS,"HIGH for the three rates, the 312, the 75% and the OOM count (all recomputed from raw rollouts and cross-read in the GATE lines); MEDIUM for the interpretive comparisons between routes, which n=20/12 cannot separate","MEDIUM-HIGH - why route (b) for growing the matched slice was deprioritised, and the mechanism behind F-08's belief/accuracy disagreement at the heart of the HP-KR confound","audit/scripts/claims/P6_lab_a.py, audit/scripts/claims/F-59_power.py (outputs audit/phase2/out/P6/P6_lab_a.txt, F-59_power.txt)","The entry's '+-0.10' is about one standard error, not an interval; the exact intervals are roughly +-0.2. The headline reading (confidence, not accuracy) is better supported by the COMPOSITION of the fallback-2 sample (margins 0.10-0.35, 3 of 12 answered correctly) than by the difference between the rates.",P6-kd-rest
F-73,"On our own 11-dataset store at L40 (mean pooling, paper probe, 110 off-diagonal cells) a length-only rule reaches 0.5555 off-diagonal AUROC vs raw 0.6623, datapca 0.6651 and random 0.5849; the positive class is longer in 9 of 11 datasets, 6 of the 8 in the reviewer's repo, median gap 3.7 tokens; mask is 283.2 vs 176.4, not the previously quoted 245 vs 96.",raw 0.6623; datapca 0.6651; random 0.5849; length 0.5555; 9 of 11 longer; 6 of 8; median gap 3.7; mask 283.2/176.4; sandbagging 529.4/340.4,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2629,run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git=lab=Drive) + C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/passB/<ds>/rows.jsonl (lab-only),"results[feature,probe=paper].auroc off-diagonal mean; rows.jsonl span_len grouped by label","n/a - kd/scripts/check_length_claim.py is print-only, no artifact",n/a,raw 0.6623 / datapca 0.6651 / random 0.5849 / length 0.5555 (n=110); longer 9 of 11; 6 of 8; median |gap| 3.689; mask 283.1831/176.4235; sandbagging 529.396/340.386,own script: off-diagonal means from the matrix; span_len means per label over 11 rows.jsonl on the lab PC,"matrix = git working tree (Phase 1: identical to lab and Drive); rows.jsonl = lab originals, mtimes 2026-09-15..09-19, untouched by the 09-22 wave; no BH q quoted","length reads 0.5555 under all three probes; on block9 (10 ds) length 0.5467 / raw 0.6870, on 9 ds 0.5319 / 0.6841; random@2 only 0.4910; single layer + single seed as stated",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - both halves recomputed from primary data, inputs pre-date the entry",MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-73_F-74.py; audit/scripts/claims/P7_lab.py length,"All primary measurements reproduce exactly. Two statements fail: (1) 'our stated 0.553 vs 0.665 is confirmed to three decimals' - measured 0.5555/0.6623, agreement is to 2 dp, and F-73's own closing line uses the correct 0.556/0.662; (2) 'on harm-pressure-choice the gap is exactly zero' - measured +0.0035 (1.0075 vs 1.0040). SEPARATE DOC BUG: five docs (ONBOARDING:78, NOVELTY_CHECK_PROMPT:110, kd/docs/DESIGN.md:176+202, docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:497+1105) and the memory note still say '9 of 10' - the store gives 8 of 10 on block9 and 9 of 11 with sycophancy_mt; 9 of 10 matches neither.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-74,"corr(raw, random@2 - raw) = -0.7684 at L40 sits inside its own coupling null (analytic -0.7462, permuted -0.7456 [-0.7986,-0.6892], P=0.2135), so the -0.76 is arithmetic; and the uncoupled test (pc:unified@2 - datapca@2 regressed on raw) gives slope -0.100, r -0.067, mean margin +0.0063.","-0.7684; -0.7462; -0.7456 [-0.7986,-0.6892]; -0.7462 [-0.8106,-0.6683]; P=0.2135; sd(raw) 0.2128; sd(random@2) 0.1898; -0.100 / -0.067 / +0.0063; +0.630 / +0.571 / +0.0290",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2706,run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json,"110 off-diagonal cells of results[raw|random@2|pc:unified@2|datapca@2, paper].auroc","n/a - kd/scripts/ceiling_null.py is print-only, no artifact",n/a,"-0.7684; analytic -0.7462; permuted mean -0.7455 [-0.8001,-0.6889]; P=0.2117; sd 0.2128 / 0.1898; slope -0.0998, r -0.0671, margin +0.0063; coupled row +0.6297 / +0.5711 / +0.0290","own implementation (longhand Pearson r and OLS), B=20,000 permutations + 2,000 noise draws, seed 42",git working tree copy = lab = Drive; no BH q quoted,my simulated-noise null gives P=0.3005 vs the permuted 0.2117 - the entry quotes only one P without saying which null; substituting datapca(k=5) for datapca@2 in the coupled row gives +0.398 / +0.460 / -0.0028,HOLDS,"HIGH - single file, independent reimplementation, exact on every deterministic quantity",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-73_F-74.py,"P=0.2117 vs the stated 0.2135 is Monte-Carlo noise (binomial s.e. ~0.003 at B=20,000); conclusion unchanged. Caveat (1) of the entry is correct: this is the paper16 unified bank, and the cap bank's +0.154 margin over the same matched control (F-77) is untouched by it.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-75,"Across all 80 layers the matched-slice axes probe is below chance to L20 (floor L19 0.355), plateaus at L27-L48 (0.61-0.75) and rises late to L77 0.764; it beats raw at 28/80 layers and datapca at 31/80; L40 reads 0.739 (+0.034 vs raw, +0.065 vs datapca) and the longest contiguous positive-margin run is 16 layers.",floor L19 0.355; L0-L20 0.355-0.483; plateau L27-L48 0.61-0.75; 16 contiguous; L20 0.374 (-0.216/-0.226); L22 0.624; L40 0.739 (+0.034/+0.065); L44 0.732; L77 0.764 (+0.055/+0.130); 28/80 raw; 31/80 datapca,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2772,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/passA11/banks/kd_s23/matrices/mean_L{0..79}_s42.json (axes) + .../passA11/matrices/mean_L{0..79}_s42.json (raw, datapca)","row 'harm-pressure-kr-matched' of results[feature, probe=paper].auroc, mean over the other 10 columns",n/a - matched_profile.py and the lab-only margin.py are print-only,n/a,"L19 0.3555; L0-L20 0.3555-0.4834; L27-L48 0.6114-0.7469; 16 contiguous (L29-L44); L20 0.3743 (-0.2161/-0.2257); L22 0.6237 (+0.0823/+0.0843); L40 0.7393 (+0.0336/+0.0655); L44 0.7321 (+0.0273/+0.0304); L77 0.7642 (+0.0553/+0.1296); beats raw 28/80, datapca 31/80","own loader + margin code over the 160 matrices, run read-only on the lab PC","lab originals - root matrices mtime 2026-09-21 12:20-12:52, bank 12:22-13:28; the 09-22 16:05 A-kd-all re-run did NOT rewrite them; passAC11.status WAS rewritten 09-22 16:05 so the quoted gate line is the re-run's; no BH q quoted","same bootstrap with raw as control: L40 +0.0336, 95% [-0.1350,+0.1850], P(<=0) 0.3296 - also fails, so the negative verdict is not datapca-specific; single seed, single pooling (only _s42 exists)",HOLDS,"HIGH - 160 original files, recomputed with my own code, every quoted number exact",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P7_lab.py f7576,"Two clarifications, not errors: the 16 CONTIGUOUS positive-margin layers are L29-L44, while 'L27-L48' is the band where the axes level sits in 0.61-0.75 - the entry uses 'plateau' for both. Against raw the longest run is 19 layers (L26-L44). F-75's own verdict was withdrawn by F-76; only the profile is checked here.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-76,"Resampling the ten transfer datasets (B=10,000, seed 42) over the 80-layer profile, the margin at the pre-specified L40 over datapca is +0.0655 with 95% CI [-0.0693,+0.1887] and P(<=0)=0.161; the argmax has median L31, 95% [L5,L79], never lands on L40 and is inside L27-L48 only 31.1% of the time; the median fraction of positive layers is 0.46 [0.16,0.75].","+0.0655; [-0.0693,+0.1887]; P=0.161; median argmax L31; [L5,L79] width 74; 0.0% on L40; 31.1% in plateau; fraction positive median 0.46 [0.16,0.75]; B=10,000 seed 42",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2846,"same 160 matrices as F-75 (run-crossgen/kd11/passA11/{matrices,banks/kd_s23/matrices}/mean_L*_s42.json)",80 layers x 10 transfer cells: axes(bank) minus datapca(root) on row harm-pressure-kr-matched; bootstrap over the 10 columns,n/a - kd/scripts/layer_significance.py is print-only,n/a,"+0.0655; [-0.0693,+0.1887]; P(<=0)=0.1611; argmax median L31, 95% [L5,L79] width 74, 0.00% on L40, 31.1% inside L27-L48; fraction positive median 0.4625, 95% [0.16,0.75]","own bootstrap (numpy default_rng(42), index resampling of the 10 units), B=10,000, no refitting","lab originals (09-21 12:20-13:28); bootstrap computed in-script, NOT read from significance.json, so RF-13's regenerated BH q-values do not apply","with raw as control: +0.0336, [-0.1350,+0.1850], P 0.3296 - also fails; selection-priced-in best-layer margin +0.1296 [+0.0596,+0.3138]; resampling unit is only 10, which is why the interval is wide",HOLDS,HIGH - independent reimplementation reproduces the interval to 4 dp,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P7_lab.py f7576,"THIS SETTLES THE F-75 vs F-77/F-81 CONFLICT. F-77/F-81 quote the kd slice as '37/80 (46%)' positive layers. The observed counts are 28/80 (vs raw) and 31/80 (vs datapca) - F-75's figures, reproduced here. 0.46 is F-76's bootstrap MEDIAN FRACTION (measured 0.4625) and 0.4625 x 80 = 37.0, so 37/80 is a bootstrap median fraction written as a layer count. F-75 is right. The cluster-permutation test F-76 still owes has not run in this batch; run-premise/cluster_perm_kd_matched.json (09-22 16:07) may be it - flagged, not chased.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-77,"For pc:capitulation@2 against datapca@2 on sycophancy_mt as target, the margin is positive at all 21 stored layers; at the pre-specified L40 it is +0.1542 with 95% dataset-level CI [+0.0913,+0.2113] and P(<=0)=0.0000; argmax median L36, 95% [L28,L60], on L40 in 3.9%; peak L32 +0.175; +0.108 still at L76; vs raw +0.005..+0.139.","21/21 positive; run 21; +0.1542; [+0.0913,+0.2113]; P=0.0000; argmax [L28,L60] median L36, 3.9% on L40; peak ~L32 +0.175; L12 +0.012; L76 +0.108; vs raw +0.005..+0.139; kd slice '37/80 (46%)'",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2923,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_s23/matrices/mean_L{0,4,...,76}_s42.json (21 files)","column sycophancy_mt of results[pc:capitulation@2|datapca@2|raw, paper].auroc, mean over the 10 source rows",n/a - cap/scripts/cap_layer_profile.py is print-only,n/a,"21/21 positive vs datapca@2 and vs raw; L40 +0.1542, 95% [+0.0913,+0.2113], P(<=0) 0.0000; argmax median L36, 95% [L28,L60], on L40 3.85%; peak L32 +0.1747; L12 +0.0116; L76 +0.1081; vs raw +0.0045..+0.1388","own loader + bootstrap (default_rng(42), 10 source datasets resampled, B=10,000)","lab originals (mtimes 2026-09-21 03:48-13:44); cap_layers.status overwritten 09-22 15:50-15:52 and cap_s23/significance.json regenerated 09-22 16:01 - neither is read by the entry or by me, so RF-13 does not bite; bank axes_s23.pt / bank_name=cap_s23","the 21/21 is specific to the sycophancy_mt column: on the full 11-dataset off-diagonal (audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv) cap@2 is NEGATIVE vs raw at L12/L20/L22/L24 and the L40 margin over raw is +0.0983, which matches F-67's +0.098 that F-77 cites as its bound; F-87 confirms the L40 margin at four seeds",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the cap numbers (exact); HIGH for the 37/80 error (arithmetic identity with F-76's 0.4625),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P7_lab.py f77,"Every cap-bank number reproduces exactly. The comparison column's 'kd matched slice 37/80 (46%)' does NOT: the observed counts are 28/80 vs raw and 31/80 vs datapca (F-75), and 37 is F-76's bootstrap median fraction 0.4625 x 80. The error runs against F-77's own argument (31/80 makes the contrast stronger), but it puts a bootstrap statistic and a layer count in the same column. F-81 carries the same figure.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-87,"At L40 on sycophancy_mt the cap bank's pc:capitulation@2 reads 0.7159/0.7132/0.7186/0.7136 at seeds 1/7/13/42, beating raw by +0.111 to +0.120 (spread 0.009) and the matched control by +0.149 to +0.177 on every seed.",cap@2 0.7159/0.7132/0.7186/0.7136; raw 0.6050/0.5962/0.5988/0.6013; datapca@2 0.5545/0.5638/0.5418/0.5594; vs raw +0.111..+0.120 spread 0.009; vs control +0.149..+0.177,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3532,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_s23/matrices/mean_L40_s{1,7,13,42}.json","results[feature, probe=paper].auroc column sycophancy_mt, mean over the 10 source rows","n/a - the table came from a loose lab-only print-only script capseedread.py (not in git, not on Drive)",n/a,0.7159/0.7132/0.7186/0.7136; raw 0.6050/0.5962/0.5988/0.6013; datapca@2 0.5545/0.5638/0.5418/0.5594; vs raw +0.1110..+0.1198 (spread 0.0088); vs control +0.1494..+0.1767,"own loader over the four seed matrices, read-only on the lab PC","lab originals - s1/s7/s13 mtime 2026-09-21 17:28 (before commit 1155730 at 17:30), s42 03:49; cap_seeds.status overwritten 09-22 16:00-16:01 but the matrices were not; no BH q quoted","4 seeds at one layer only; depth covered separately by F-77 (21/21 at seed 42); the seed spread 0.0088 is an order of magnitude below F-66's CI width 0.135, as claimed",HOLDS,HIGH - all twelve cells exact,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P7_lab.py f87,"F-87's postscript about the --extra_* trap (extra-seed matrices written with no paper probe) is not present in the current files: all four contain the paper probe with the full cap feature set. Wording nit: the entry's opening contrasts 'five seeds' with 'one', then gives a table of four seeds.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-88,"Three papers were read in full and their bearing on our work recorded: Kumar (arXiv:2605.27958) rejects the single-direction hypothesis and contradicts the draft title, Kirch et al. (arXiv:2511.17408) give the text-evident/text-ambiguous taxonomy and the clustering argument, and Yoo & Skapars (arXiv:2609.02893) state our near-orthogonality result in their own vocabulary.",k=1 captures 0.61-0.80 AUROC; >=0.998 clean; style-augmented 0.979-0.983; 8 stylistic shifts; peak-layer CIs span nearly the full network; TF-IDF <0.5 at 12B/27B; eight behaviours; Appendix N mixed-effects,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3568,"papers/Pressure-Testing Deception Probes in LLMs Scaling, Robustness, and the.pdf; papers/The Impact of Off-Policy Training Data.pdf; papers/Probe Generalization as Subspace Selection for OOD Deception Detectio.pdf","abstracts, contribution bullets, Table 3 caption (Kumar), Appendix N (Kirch), abstract (Yoo & Skapars)","every quoted sentence located in the PDFs, most of it verbatim","yes, except the two venue labels","n/a - a reading, not a measurement","pdftotext -enc UTF-8 over the three PDFs, then targeted search for each quoted phrase","git working-tree PDFs (first committed 4d0d046 2026-09-22 02:46); Kumar arXiv:2605.27958v1 27 May 2026, Kirch arXiv:2511.17408v4 19 Apr 2026, Yoo & Skapars arXiv:2609.02893v1 1 Jul 2026",n/a,HOLDS,HIGH for the quotations (read during this audit); LOW for the two venue labels (absent from the documents),HIGH,pdftotext + grep (commands recorded in audit/claims/F-88.md),"PHASE-1 DATING FLAG RESOLVED: the PDFs' working-tree mtimes are 2026-09-21 17:20/17:23/17:24, 19-23 min BEFORE F-88's commit d55dd4d at 17:43. The 9-hour gap Phase 1 saw is a delayed git add, not a false claim. NOT VERIFIED: 'GEM @ ACL 2026' (Kumar) and 'Findings of ACL 2026' (Kirch) appear nowhere in the PDFs; Yoo & Skapars' 'ICML 2026 Workshop' IS in the PDF. Minor attribution shift: the abstract attaches 'nearly matches probes trained directly on the test distribution' to PC-subspace projection, while the judge-selected variant closes 78%/25% of the baseline-to-oracle gap. The 0.883 and cosine +0.051 re-quoted here belong to F-86 and are not checked in this card. None of the three PDFs has a notes file under docs/papers/.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-92,"Over 100 ironic-arm rollouts (5 instruction variants x 20 questions), the fraction of responses carrying at least one irony marker falls 0.85/0.15/0.10/0.00/0.00 from v1 to v5, with marker counts exclamation 27, rhetorical_q 13, stock_irony 11, allcaps 4 - so unmarked deadpan is producible at instruction strength v4 or above.",0.85/0.15/0.10/0.00/0.00; exclamation 27; rhetorical_q 13; stock_irony 11; allcaps 4; n=100,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3934,cap/run-sarc-pilot/marker_report_partial.json and responses/pc_ironic_critic.jsonl (lab-only; md5-verified copy in audit/cache/labpc/cap/run-sarc-pilot/),markers.pc_ironic_critic.per_variant; per_marker.pc_ironic_critic,"per_variant [0.85,0.15,0.1,0.0,0.0]; exclamation 27, rhetorical_q 13, stock_irony 11, allcaps 4; n 100","yes, exact","recomputed from the 100 raw responses: 0.85/0.15/0.10/0.00/0.00; exclamation 27, rhetorical_q 13, stock_irony 11, allcaps 4",own script re-using the scorer's MARKERS regexes and strip_question over the raw JSONL,"marker_report_partial.json mtime 2026-09-21 21:31 (before commit 57cfa3a at 21:32) - the ORIGINAL; responses 21:26 originals; lab-only, no Drive backup (RF-10), now cached md5-verified by the audit","the eight-regex detector misfires on non-ironic text: recomputing the other two arms gives allcaps 23 and reveal_aside 13 on the sincere arm, so a marker rate is only interpretable within the ironic arm - which is F-92's own caveat (2); 20 questions, one temperature, one seed",HOLDS,HIGH - original artifact and recompute from raw both exact,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-92_F-93_F-105.py,"F-92's hedge is correct and should survive into any write-up: the marker check cannot distinguish deadpan sarcasm from a praise instruction simply complied with, and the entry says so. Its caveat (1) - the decisive separability check had no result yet - is what F-93 then answered negatively.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-93,"Bag-of-words logistic regression grouped by question id separates ironic from sycophantic responses at 0.953 raw / 0.947 stripped over all variants, 1.000 on v1, and still 0.919/0.921 on the marker-free v4+v5 subset, on ordinary content vocabulary - so a direction fit on these personas would be a register axis; the amendment's polarity check passes at 100%/96%/100% >=2.","0.953/0.947 n=200; 1.000/1.000 n=40; 0.919/0.921 n=80; 0.997/0.996 n=80; marker rates ironic [.85,.15,.10,0,0], sincere [.60,.15,.15,.25,.05], sycophant [.85,1.0,.50,0,.05]; polarity 2.59/100%, 2.44/96%, 2.37/100%",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3992 (+ its 23:05 amendment),cap/run-sarc-pilot/marker_report.json (REGENERATED 2026-09-22 15:55) over original responses/*.jsonl (09-21 21:26-21:40) and scores/*.json (09-21 21:42-21:44),"lexical_subsets[pair,subset].{auroc_raw,auroc_stripped,n}; markers.<arm>.per_variant; polarity.<arm>","0.9525/0.9472 n200; 1.0/1.0 n40; 0.91938/0.92125 n80; 0.99688/0.99625 n80; polarity 2.59/1.00, 2.44/0.96, 2.37/1.00","yes, exact - but the file post-dates the entry, so Level 1 alone proves nothing","A (repo functions) and B (independent sklearn pipeline) both give 0.9527/0.9472, 1.0000/1.0000, 0.9194/0.9213, 0.9969/0.9963; all marker rates and the full polarity table reproduce","two passes over the original 300 responses: the scorer's own strip_question/bow/grouped_auc, and my own echo-stripping + CountVectorizer(min_df=3) + LeaveOneGroupOut logistic regression",marker_report.json is the 09-22 15:55 regeneration (RF-13/RF-14) but the inputs are 09-21 originals; lab-only data (RF-10) now md5-cached by the audit; no layer/bank/BH q involved,"NEW: bootstrapping the 20 question ids (B=2,000, seed 42) on the out-of-fold scores gives the missing CI for the decisive 0.921 - 95% [0.8719, 0.9669], P(<=0.65 pre-registered ceiling) = 0.0000, so F-93's caveat (1) is discharged and the gate fails with room to spare",HOLDS,HIGH - two independent implementations agree to 4 dp on original inputs,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-92_F-93_F-105.py,"The gate-failure story checks out in the preserved status files: sarc_pilot.status.2026-09-21-buggy-verdict has 'VERDICT PRODUCIBLE' one line above 'stripped=0.947'. The 0.947 in the 09-22 02:29 status and the 0.921 in the 15:55 one are the same data under different gate subsets (all-variant vs unmarked v4+v5), both in my recompute. PROVENANCE NUANCE: F-93's ironic feature list is the UNSTRIPPED fit - it quotes 'definitely', which is a MARKER_TOKEN and cannot appear in a stripped model; F-105's corrected list matches the stripped fit. The register reading is the same either way.",P7-register-sarcasm
F-105,F-93's four separability rows and both feature lists re-derive exactly from the raw responses; none of them was persisted by the saved tooling; and F-93's polarity amendment is withdrawn because the sincere arm declines to the same 2.10 over the same range.,"0.953/0.947, 1.000/1.000, 0.919/0.921, 0.997/0.996; marker_report.json holds only auroc_raw 0.9525 / auroc_stripped 0.9472 n=200; ironic 2.85->2.10, sincere 2.85->2.10, sycophant 2.45->2.80",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4934 (commit 6c9a5cf 2026-09-22 03:25),cap/run-sarc-pilot/responses/*.jsonl + scores/*.json (originals); cap/run-sarc-pilot/marker_report.json (09-22 15:55); git history of cap/scripts/score_sarcasm_markers.py,"lexical_subsets; lexical_features.{ironic_side,sycophant_side}[0:12]; polarity.<arm>.per_variant","the current marker_report.json DOES hold all six subset rows, both 15-word feature lists with coefficients and the per-variant polarity table",values yes; the 'not persisted' statement no longer describes the file,"0.9194/0.9213 etc. all four rows exact; ironic top-12 and sycophant top-12 match F-105 word for word and in order; polarity table exact (ironic 2.85/2.85/2.60/2.55/2.10, sincere 2.85/2.25/2.40/2.25/2.10, sycophant 2.45/2.25/2.55/2.15/2.80)","same two-pass recompute as F-93, plus git log/diff on the scorer",inputs are 09-21 originals; artifact is the 09-22 15:55 re-score; the persistence fix landed in commit 6c9a5cf - the SAME commit that added F-105,"F-105's claim that F-93's verdict is unaffected is supported: 0.9213 with a question-level 95% CI [0.872,0.967] and P(<=0.65)=0.0000",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - recompute exact; the persistence question settled from git history and the current file,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-92_F-93_F-105.py,"Parts 1 and 3 hold exactly. Part 2 ('none of them is persisted') was true of the artifact it inspected but is SUPERSEDED by the fix committed alongside it (6c9a5cf adds lexical_subsets + lexical_features to the scorer) plus the 09-22 15:55 re-run, which wrote them into marker_report.json. Minor overstatement: 'all ten words F-93 quoted appear in the top-25' - 11 of 12 ironic words do; 'definitely' is a MARKER_TOKEN and is absent from the stripped model (14 of 14 sycophant words are present).",P7-register-sarcasm
D-081,"On HP-KR at layer 20 the RepE-trained base probe also inverts, AUROC 0.109; so does Liars' Bench's own Mean Probe at 0.12.",0.109; 0.12,draft main (1).pdf p.7 sec 5.1 + Table 2,persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot_operating.csv; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Table 6 p.54,"arm='base probe (RepE-trained)', threshold_source='control', dataset=harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain, col auroc | LB Table 6 AUROC row, Llama 3.3 70B, HP-KR",0.109 (his file); 0.12 (LB PDF),YES both (tol 5e-4),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Recomputed where his own cell-level CSVs allow it.,n/a,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible.",The same base probe at L40 reads 0.9358 and at L44 0.8281 on HP-KR: the inversion is layer-20-only (see D-124).,MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only); the Liars' Bench 0.12 VERIFIED in the PDF,HIGH - exact match in his file and in the published table,HIGH - the 'it is not only the persona contrast' half of the HP-KR story,audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py,"LB Table 6 (Mean Probe), Llama-3.3-70B row, HP-KR AUROC = 0.12. Draft reproduces it exactly.",P8-draft-rest
D-084,"The extended (12v13) contrast keeps nearly all of the HP-KR repair: zero-shot AUROC 0.882 / 0.912 / 0.894 at layers 20 / 40 / 44, response-mean pooling, no seed.",0.882; 0.912; 0.894,draft main (1).pdf p.7 sec 5.1 + Table 2 + Table 6,"persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv","row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain, col auroc_ext_axis",0.881568 / 0.912392 / 0.893637,YES (tol 5e-4),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Recomputed where his own cell-level CSVs allow it.,n/a,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible.","The 4v6 knowledge-denial contrast is slightly higher at all three layers (0.890/0.919/0.908, D-083, P5). The 'mod' bank (more rollouts, persona_ood_mod_L40) gives 0.9066 not 0.9158 off-diagonal - the draft reports the ext bank only.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only),HIGH - three exact matches,"HIGH - Table 2, Figure 3, the repair claim",audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py,,P8-draft-rest
D-085,"The HP-KR repair comes from the new personas, not from re-extracting the old ones: the published 8v7 grouping inverts on the original bank (0.103 at L20) and still inverts on the re-extracted bank (0.148).",0.103; 0.148,draft main (1).pdf p.7 sec 5.1,persona_ood/zero_shot.csv; persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot.csv,"row harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain, col auroc_axis",0.102856 (original bank); 0.148277 (re-extracted),YES (tol 5e-4),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Recomputed where his own cell-level CSVs allow it.,n/a,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible.","This is a two-point comparison at one layer. The stronger version of the same argument (0.103 vs 0.148 at L20 only) is not repeated at L40/L44, where the published contrast is near chance rather than inverted, so the 'still inverts' wording is layer-20-specific.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only),HIGH - both numbers exact,HIGH - it is the causal attribution behind contribution 2,audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py,"The causal reading ('comes from the new personas') is an inference from two banks, not an experiment that varies one factor; the two banks differ in BOTH rollout count and persona membership. See also persona_ood_mod_* which varies rollout count alone.",P8-draft-rest
D-094,At layer 40 the base probe ranks HP-KR well (AUROC 0.936) yet flags nothing at the Alpaca threshold (balanced accuracy 0.500); the published and extended contrasts also flag nothing.,0.936; 0.500,draft main (1).pdf p.8 sec 5.1 + Table 2,persona_ood_ext_L40/zero_shot_operating.csv,"threshold_source='control', dataset=harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain; arms 'base probe (RepE-trained)', 'deception axis (8v7)', 'extended axis (12v13)'",auroc 0.9358; balacc 0.5 / 0.5 / 0.5 with recall 0.0 and specificity 1.0 in all three,YES (0.9358 rounds to 0.936; balacc exact),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Recomputed where his own cell-level CSVs allow it.,n/a,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible.","recall=0 and specificity=1 in all three arms, so the 0.500 is the metric's floor, not a measurement.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only),HIGH,HIGH - the AUROC-vs-threshold gap is a main message,audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py,,P8-draft-rest
