D-107,"Three random directions used as probe features score 0.527, 0.504 and 0.493 mean off-diagonal AUROC at layers 20, 40 and 44, so the persona subspace is not empty of signal.",0.527; 0.504; 0.493,draft main (1).pdf p.9 sec 5.3 + Table 3,"persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","features=random3, off_diagonal_mean",0.526938 / 0.503798 / 0.492709,YES (tol 5e-4),Level 2 on his pipeline NOT POSSIBLE (his activations are gone; owner's rule). Recomputed where his own cell-level CSVs allow it.,n/a,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible.","WEAK AS A NULL: his store keeps a single random draw (persona_ood.py builds it from one QR of a standard-normal matrix). No seed column, no repeats, no spread - so this cannot support a statement about what a random direction typically does. The owner's own work has a many-draw random null (memory note 'significance and random nulls'); the draft does not use it.",MATCHES HIS DATA (Level 1 only); the control itself is UNDERPOWERED (n=1 draw),"HIGH for the number, LOW for it being a null",MED - it is the only control in Table 3,audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py,Flag for the lead: a one-draw random baseline is quoted in Table 3 as if it were a null distribution.,P8-draft-rest
