D-207,"For detection at the 1%-FPR threshold the top-10% token read is best: at layer 40 it reaches 0.737 balanced accuracy and 0.531 recall against 0.694 and 0.413 for the mean (five-dataset average, extended contrast).",0.737; 0.531; 0.694; 0.413,draft main (1).pdf p.18 App D + Table 9,persona_positions_L40/reads_summary.csv,"axis=extended, read in {top10, mean}: balacc, recall",top10 0.7372 / 0.5306; mean 0.6939 / 0.4129,YES (tol 5e-4),"RECOMPUTED ordering: at L40 the single MAXIMUM is actually higher than top-10% on both metrics (0.7497 / 0.548), so 'the top-10% read is best' is not true at layer 40 on these two metrics.",full six-read table printed from his reads_summary.csv,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible.","All six reads at L40 (extended): mean 0.899/0.6939/0.4129, top10 0.9075/0.7372/0.5306, max 0.9095/0.7497/0.548, first 0.8631/0.6059/0.227, last 0.8797/0.6556/0.4221, pre 0.8254/0.6515/0.3829.","PARTLY - all four quoted numbers match his data, but 'the top-10% read is best' is contradicted by the maximum read in the same table at layer 40 (Table 9 shows this too)",HIGH - his own Table 9 carries the contradicting row,MED - it feeds the future-work recommendation 'the top tenth of response tokens is a better read than the mean',audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py,"The draft's own argument for preferring top-10% over max is the RepE instability in D-208, which is a different dataset; on the five-dataset mean at L40 max wins.",P8-draft-rest
