D-234,"Our measurement of the Liars' Bench Follow-Up Probe averages 0.636 AUROC and 0.622 balanced accuracy over the five datasets, against published values of 0.634 and 0.578 (Kretschmar et al. 2025, Table 7).",0.636; 0.622; 0.634; 0.578,draft main (1).pdf p.19 App G,persona_ood_followup_L20/zero_shot_operating.csv; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Table 7 p.55,"arm='base probe (RepE-trained)', control, 'Average (Liars' Bench)'; LB Table 7, Llama 3.3 70B row","his file: auroc 0.636, balacc 0.6223",YES (tol 5e-4),"PUBLISHED VALUES VERIFIED IN THE PDF: Table 7, Llama-3.3-70B, AUROC HP-C 0.50 / HP-KR 0.14 / CG 0.75 / ID 0.93 / IT 0.85 -> five-dataset mean 0.634; balanced accuracy at 1% FPR 0.50 / 0.26 / 0.60 / 0.87 / 0.66 -> mean 0.578. Both reproduce exactly.",re-averaged the five shared datasets from the published table (the paper's own AVERAGE column is over seven datasets and reads 0.57 / 0.54),"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible. Published side: papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf, printed page 55.","The comparison is not like for like on Insider-Trading (his scores exclude the reasoning scratchpad; see D-064, D-160), which the draft states.",HOLDS - his measured side matches his data and the published side is correct in the PDF,HIGH - both sides checked,HIGH - it is the reproduction argument,audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py + PDF read,,P8-draft-rest
