D-236,"Nearly all of the balanced-accuracy gap to Liars' Bench is Insider-Trading, where our scores exclude the reasoning scratchpad: our base probe reaches 0.909 there against the published 0.50.",0.909; 0.50,draft main (1).pdf p.19 App G,persona_ood_ext_L20/zero_shot_operating.csv; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf Table 6 p.54,"base probe, control, insider_trading_cadenza__plain, col balacc; LB Table 6 balanced accuracy at 1% FPR, Llama row, IT","his file 0.9085 (rounds to 0.909 half-up, 0.908 banker's); published 0.50 VERIFIED",YES within rounding,"RECOMPUTED the gap: his per-dataset balanced accuracies at L20 are CG 0.8383, HP-C 0.5, HP-KR 0.5, IT 0.9085, ID 0.8578 (mean 0.7209) against published 0.83 / 0.50 / 0.50 / 0.50 / 0.85 (mean 0.636). Per-dataset differences: CG +0.008, HP-C 0.000, HP-KR 0.000, IT +0.409, ID +0.008. So IT is 0.409 of the 0.085 x 5 = 0.425 total, i.e. 96% of the gap - 'nearly all' is exact.",per-dataset difference decomposition from his file and the published table,"his branch @ tip; his own committed CSVs; NOT touched by the 2026-09-22 re-run wave (RF-13 hit the OWNER's lab stores). Persona bank = the owner's kd bank, byte-identical to lab run-kd/vectors_s3 (RF-1 RESOLVED). Activations gone -> Level 2 on his pipeline impossible. Published side: PDF printed page 54.","LB's own ablation (Table 17, p.70) confirms the mechanism: at layer 20, removing reasoning activations moves the Mean Probe from balacc 0.50 to 0.66 and AUROC 0.93 to 0.97 (see D-064).","HOLDS - both sides checked, and the 'nearly all' decomposition reproduces (96%)",HIGH,HIGH - it is the honesty caveat on the headline reproduction,audit/scripts/claims/P8_draft_rest.py + PDF read,,P8-draft-rest
D-237,"Compute/provenance: persona rollouts, judging and all activation extraction ran on NDIF; every analysis runs on CPU from pooled activations and persona vectors; and paper/make_numbers.py regenerates every number from the released result files.",-,draft main (1).pdf p.19 App G Compute,git ls-tree -r origin/feat/persona-pc-ood; git ls-tree -r HEAD,search for 'make_numbers' and for any path starting 'paper/',"NO SUCH FILE. `paper/make_numbers.py` does not exist on his branch, and there is no `paper/` directory on his branch; it does not exist on asix HEAD either.",NO,Related gap (D-233): the pipeline results tables the reproduction claim compares against are missing for three of the four runs.,git ls-tree on both branches,origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (read with `git show`; never checked out) and asix HEAD,Independently re-checked here; P5 reported the same for the abstract/contribution rows.,SUPERSEDED 2026-09-24 (was: DOES NOT MATCH HIS DATA - the named script is not in the repository),HIGH - a file either exists in the tree or it does not,HIGH - a reproducibility claim in the paper that the repository does not support,git ls-tree (inline),"The NDIF half of the sentence is consistent with the owner's pipeline and was not separately audited here.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] PHASE 4 AMENDMENT (verdict unchanged; the named script is confirmed absent from both branches, every commit reachable by git log --all --diff-filter=A, the working tree, and the lab PC). METHODS NOTE: this is a COMPOUND claim - NDIF and CPU-only hold, the reproducibility limb is falsified. The audit failed the whole claim; an independent blinded reader graded it PARTLY, failing the limb. The verdict vocabulary has no rule for compound claims; this is a gap in the vocabulary, not an error by either reader.  [2026-09-24 SUPERSEDED — IN HIS FAVOUR] `paper/make_numbers.py` NOW EXISTS, on the new branch origin/paper, together with paper/make_figures.py. The DOES-NOT-MATCH verdict rested entirely on the script's absence, which was true when checked (it was on no branch, in no commit reachable by git log --all --diff-filter=A, and not on the lab PC) and is true no longer. See F-119 and audit/COLLAB_PAPER_BRANCH.md §5. The audit's ONLY DOES-NOT-MATCH verdict; this is the second correction running in his favour (after D-107).",P8-draft-rest
D-013,"Every method Liars' Bench evaluates has recall near zero on HP-KR at a 1% false-positive rate, and its probe's AUROC on Llama-3.3-70B is 0.12.",0.12; 'recall near zero',draft main (1).pdf p.1 sec 1 Introduction,"papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf, Tables 6-11, printed pages 54-59","HP-KR column, Llama 3.3 70B row, RECALL block of each table",Mean Probe AUROC on HP-KR = 0.12 (Table 6): CORRECT.,YES for the 0.12,"HP-KR recall at 1% FPR, Llama-3.3-70B, per method: Mean Probe 0.00, Follow-Up Probe 0.37, Self-Evaluation 0.05, LLM-as-a-Judge 0.07, Unrelated-Question Classifier 0.12, Self-Eval (deception prompt) 0.01, Upper-Bound Probe (privileged) 0.97. Across-model averages: 0.00, 0.12, 0.02, 0.08, 0.04, 0.01.",read every per-method table of the published PDF during this audit,"papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf (v2), pages 54-59","Whether 'near zero' covers 0.37 is a judgement call; the Follow-Up Probe buys that recall with an 84% false-positive rate on HP-KR, so its balanced accuracy is 0.26.","PARTLY HOLDS - the 0.12 AUROC is exact, but 'every method ... recall near zero' is false for the Follow-Up Probe on Llama-3.3-70B (0.37); it is true of the cross-model averages",HIGH - read in the published tables,"MED - it is a motivating sentence in the introduction, repeated as D-037 in section 2","PDF read (pypdf, audit/tools/pylib)","Same claim as D-037 (section 2 Related work), which this row also covers. Suggested fix: 'recall at or below 0.12 for every unprivileged method except the Follow-Up Probe, whose 0.37 comes with an 84% false-positive rate'.",P8-draft-rest
D-023,"For Llama-3.3-70B on HP-KR, Liars' Bench reports 0.50 balanced accuracy for its Mean Probe, 0.26 for its Follow-Up Probe, and 0.95 for a probe trained on privileged in-distribution labels.",0.50; 0.26; 0.95,draft main (1).pdf p.1 Abstract (D-007) and p.2 sec 1 Contributions (D-023) + Table 2,"papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf, Tables 6, 7 and 8 (printed pages 54, 55, 56)","BALANCED ACCURACY AT 1% FPR block, Llama 3.3 70B row, HP-KR column (Table 8's block is labelled BALANCED ACCURACY)",Table 6 -> 0.50; Table 7 -> 0.26; Table 8 (Upper Bound Probe) -> 0.95. All three exact.,YES,"Also checked the AUROC side quoted in his Table 2: Mean Probe 0.12, Follow-Up 0.14, Upper-Bound 0.97 - all three exact in the same tables.",direct read of the published tables,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf (v2),"The Upper-Bound Probe is privileged (trained on Liars' Bench labels including HP-KR), which the draft states.",HOLDS - all six published values quoted from Liars' Bench for HP-KR are correct,HIGH,HIGH - the comparison the abstract and contribution 2 rest on,"PDF read (pypdf, audit/tools/pylib)","Covers D-007 (abstract) and D-023 (contributions), which state the same three numbers.",P8-draft-rest
