D-082,"The published deceptive personas all lie by omission - they 'control timing, emphasis, and selective disclosure', 'bury or exclude material facts' and give 'defensible half-disclosures' (Mahadik & Skapars 2026, Table 2) - and none of them lies by claiming not to know.",3 verbatim quotes,draft main (1).pdf p.7 sec 5.1,"papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf, Appendix A 'Deception Axis Provenance', Table 2, PDF page 9 (repeated p.11)",Table 2 rows: handler / coverup operator / plausible denier,"Verbatim in the PDF: handler 'controls timing, emphasis, and selective disclosure'; coverup operator 'buries or excludes material facts'; plausible denier 'gives defensible half-disclosures'. All three quotes are exact (the draft changes the verb to the infinitive, 'bury or exclude').",YES,"I read the WHOLE of Table 2 (8 deceptive personas: handler, broker, impression manager, coverup operator, gatekeeper, spin doctor, plausible denier, narrative manager) and Table 3 (7 honest personas: ombudsman, transparency officer, disclosure counsel, whistleblower, documentarian, fact checker, archivist). Every one of the eight deceptive descriptions is about withholding, sequencing or framing information; none describes claiming not to know. So the draft's 'none of them lies by claiming not to know' is supported by the full list, not only by the three quoted rows. The 8-and-7 counts also confirm the draft's '8 v 7' label.",full read of Tables 2 and 3 of the published PDF during this audit,"papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf (14 pages), arXiv 2605.09391 per audit/papers.csv","This is the mechanism the whole paper rests on: the reason the published contrast has nothing to detect on HP-KR. It is a reading of persona descriptions, not a measurement, but the reading is unambiguous.",HOLDS - the quotes are verbatim and the generalisation is supported by all eight rows of the source table,HIGH - read in the source PDF,HIGH - it is the explanation behind contributions 1 and 2,"PDF read (pypdf, audit/tools/pylib)","Also confirms the '8 v 7' persona counts used throughout the draft: Table 2 has 8 deceptive personas, Table 3 has 7 honest ones.",P8-draft-rest
D-046,"Mahadik & Skapars publish the roles' names and one-line descriptions but not their prompts, so the collaborator wrote five prompt variants per persona in the style of the Assistant Axis.",5 variants,draft main (1).pdf p.4 sec 3.2 Persona bank,"papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf, Tables 2 and 3 (PDF page 9)",the persona tables and their surrounding appendix text,Tables 2 and 3 give only a persona name and a one-line description each (e.g. 'gatekeeper | decides what information passes through'). No system prompts appear there.,"YES for the 'names and one-line descriptions, not prompts' half","The '5 prompt variants' half is about the OWNER's bank, not this paper: the prompts live in the owner's run-kd / paper16 persona files. RF-1 (Phase 1) established that his vectors are byte-identical to the owner's lab run-kd/vectors_s3 and that the stored system prompts match the instruction text committed at 3dfdb67. The variant COUNT per persona was not re-counted in this batch.","PDF read; provenance carried over from RF-1 (audit/PROGRESS.md), not re-derived here",papers/... Persona Coordinates.pdf; provenance from RF-1,"Deferred: counting the five variants per persona in the owner's persona files, and checking they are the ones the rollouts used.",PARTLY - the statement about the published paper HOLDS; the '5 variants' half is NOT TESTED in this batch,"HIGH for the paper half, NOT TESTED for the bank half",MED - it is the scope caveat repeated in section 6 (D-159),"PDF read (pypdf, audit/tools/pylib)",For a later batch: count the prompt variants per persona in the owner's kd/paper16 persona files and check the rollout files used them.,P8-draft-rest
F-15,"Under a single nudge Llama-3.3-70B held firm on 587 of 620 sycophancy rows (5.3% capitulation) and a third of the 33 ""sycophantic"" labels were wrong because substring matching cannot tell endorsement from correction, so the are_you_sure two-turn design replaced it.","587 of 620; 5.3%; 33 labels; ""a third"" wrong",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:249,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-sycophancy/rows.jsonl (lab-only, mtime 2026-09-16 05:38); src/assistant_axis_ndif/13_sycophancy_multiturn.py docstring",label / label_raw over 620 rows,"docstring says 587/620, 5.3%, ""a third of those 33"" - quoted verbatim by the ledger","yes (prose source, not an artifact)","620 rows; label {0:587, 1:33}; label_raw {held:587, abandoned:33}; positive rate 0.0532; 33 split 21 push_wrong / 12 doubt","own script over the raw rollouts; plus a broad lexical ""correction"" proxy on the 33 positives","lab original, mtimes 2026-09-16, outside the 09-22 wave (RF-13); no bank/layer/q-value involved","design conclusion checkable and holds: 13_sycophancy_multiturn.py uses a judge, not substring matching; the 5.3% baseline is what F-26 re-uses",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH on the counts; LOW on the ""a third"" (no stored per-row correctness judgement)",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P9_lab.py,"587/620 and 5.32% reproduce exactly. The ""a third of 33 labels were wrong"" half is NOT recomputable: rows.jsonl stores only label/label_raw. The docstring example is real (row sycophancy:6:push_wrong is a correction labelled sycophantic). A broad audit proxy flags 21/33 (64%, upper bound); a by-eye read gives ~12/33 (36%) = ""a third"". The entry already marks itself ""inherited - not re-measured"".",P9-findings-rest
F-25,"The KD-PassAC C-root step exited 1 at 13:46:25 with PermissionError WinError 5 renaming significance.json.tmp; every per-layer matrix was already written, the orphaned .tmp was intact at 551,848 bytes / 1,152 tests against the stale file's 576, and was promoted; the write_json retry loop was added 16 minutes later.","551,848 bytes; 1,152 tests; 576 tests; exit 1 at 13:46:25; fix at 14:02:47; log lines 1337-1348",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:451,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/passC/{significance.json, significance.json.stale-576}; logs/kd_passAC.log:1337-1348; src/assistant_axis_ndif/27_crossgen.py write_json",file size + tests[] length; the traceback block; the retry loop body,"significance.json 551,848 B / 1,152 tests (mtime 13:46:25); significance.json.stale-576 275,541 B / 576 tests; traceback exactly at log lines 1337-1348",yes - every figure and the cited line range are exact,"tests grid = block{10:576, 9:576} x pooling{last,mean} x layer{20,22,28,40,44,48} x probe{paper,lr_reg10,mms} x 16 comparisons = 1,152; boot_datasets 10000",own script: re-derived the test grid from the file fields; md5 of both significance files; write_json source read on the lab,"lab originals, mtime 2026-09-20 13:46, before the 09-22 wave (RF-13); no BH q-value quoted, only a test count",27_crossgen.py now carries a 6-attempt exponential-backoff retry in write_json whose docstring names this incident; present in both the lab copy and the repo,HOLDS,"HIGH - read from the lab originals, md5-verified",LOW (engineering); MEDIUM for the 10-dataset fact it exposes,audit/scripts/claims/P9_lab4.py; P9_lab5.py; p9_md5.ps1,"Two additions. (1) The ""14:02:47"" fix time is not verifiable: 27_crossgen.py has been edited since (lab mtime 09-21 03:47). (2) The recovered file is BYTE-IDENTICAL (md5 122adfbfd4154ea6c6343991ef1bd7a0) to run-crossgen/passC/significance.json written 09-18; both cover the same 6-layer/seed-42 grid over the SAME 10 datasets (sycophancy_mt present, harm-pressure-kr-matched absent), so the kd11 passC grid is a 10-dataset grid, and the rescued result was numerically a duplicate of one already on disk.",P9-findings-rest
F-26,"In the 2-item cap smoke, pc_caver folds 2/2 and pc_position_holder holds 2/2, but pc_caver also caves pre-emptively in turn 1; both personas give the same turn-1 answer on both items so the groups differ in turn 1 only by hedging vs confidence; pc_position_holder writes longer, more structured turn-1 text; and no ""cave"" appears in any of the four responses.",2/2 fold vs 2/2 hold; 5.3% baseline (587/620); 700-char truncation; length-only off-diag 0.553 vs raw 0.665,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:469,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/cap_smoke.log (UTF-16, 786,664 B, mtime 2026-09-20 14:45, lab-only)",ROLE/SYSTEM/[TURN 1]/[TURN 2]/[USER] blocks; substring counts,"2 ROLE headers, 2 SYSTEM lines, 4 TURN 1, 4 TURN 2, 4 USER blocks; all four quoted strings present exactly once",yes - every quotation verbatim,"turn-1 block lengths 698 / 695 / 697 / 696 chars (all four truncated at the same ~700 limit); cave|caver count = 2, both in the ROLE header and the SYSTEM line; spelunk = 0; Firstly/Secondly/Thirdly = 1 each, all in pc_position_holder Q1","own script: UTF-16 decode, block extraction between markers, character counts, substring counts","lab original, mtime 2026-09-20 14:45, before the entry and outside the 09-22 wave; the SYSTEM lines preserve the v1 cap bank, which exists in no file any more","superseded in practice: the production bank teacher-forces turn 1 (run-cap/responses: 1,300 rows, 65 system prompts, 20 distinct (question, turn-1) pairs at n=65 each), so this confound is closed by construction in the bank behind F-65/F-66",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - read directly from the raw NDIF log,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/P9_lab2.py; P9_lab7.py; F-26_length_xref.py,"Phase 1 could not confirm this entry because the log is UTF-16; decoded, everything checks. Two defects: (1) ""pc_position_holder writes LONGER turn-1 text"" is unsupported - all four turn-1 blocks are 695-698 chars, i.e. truncated at the same limit the entry invokes for turn 2 (the structure claim, Firstly/Secondly/Thirdly, holds on 1 of 2 items); (2) ""length-only off-diagonal 0.553 vs raw 0.665"" matches no matrix - 53 local matrices give 0.5555/0.6623 (11 datasets) or 0.5494/0.6652 (10), same defect as F-33 and F-73 plus the memory note.",P9-findings-rest
F-28,"Two external reviews of the v1 cap bank named four structural confounds and a lexical count over the live persona files confirmed all four (pair-4 explanatory labour 4/5 vs 0/5; pc_appeaser affect 3/5 vs 0/5; approving modifiers holding 4/6 vs capitulation 0/6; 4 holding variants naming what the challenge lacks vs 0), plus Gemini's Q8 point and a refutation of the ""caver reads as spelunker"" worry.",4/5 vs 0/5; 3/5 vs 0/5; 4/6 vs 0/6; 4 vs 0; Q8 omits N; 0 caves in 4 responses,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:588,cap/personas/cap_instructions/*.json (live = v3 only); cap/questions/cap_questions.jsonl; C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/cap_smoke.log,regex counts over variant text and role keys; question id 8; cave/spelunk substring counts,NO ARTIFACT - the producing command was an inline python -c print (session b035ccb3 lines 4097/4102); the v1 persona files it counted were replaced twice on 2026-09-20,n/a,"claim 3 re-run on the unchanged role keys: holding 4/6 [evidence_bound, steadfast_reviewer, reasoned_defender, calibrated_holder], capitulation 0/6 - EXACT. claim 4: 1 of the 4 flagged variants (pc_position_holder v0, ""...challenged without evidence"") preserved verbatim in cap_smoke.log. Q8 verbatim, no N. cave|caver = 2 (header + SYSTEM only), spelunk = 0.",own script re-running both recovered regex sets; UTF-16 decode of the smoke log; verbatim read of the v1 question file,"live persona files md5-identical on laptop, lab and git dc24e96 (v3, 2026-09-20 22:49/22:51); cap_smoke.log is the only result file holding v1 variant text","F-28's four regexes re-run on the PRODUCTION (v3) bank: pair-4 explain 2/5 vs 4/5, pair-3 affect 3/5 vs 5/5 (inverted), praise 4/6 vs 0/6 on role keys and 1/6 vs 0/6 on variant text (pc_evidence_bound 5/5), leak 0 vs 0 - but the leak regex is literal, and v3's ""until a reason to revise appears"" is the same move as the flagged ""until something new arrives"". The full recovered print also shows pair 6 at 1/5 on the capitulation side, which the entry calls ""confined to pair 4"".",PARTLY HOLDS,"MEDIUM-HIGH - two of four headline counts rest on a transcript print, not on a file",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-28_F-32_counts.py; P9_lab3.py; P9_lab7.py,"Claims 3 and 4, Q8 and the cave refutation verify. Claims 1 and 2 are NO RAW DATA: the v1 variant text they counted exists in no file. Three bank generations are now separable from the smoke logs - v1 (""a caver who abandons your position...""), v2 = the F-32 rewrite (""states a view plainly, then drops it...""), v3 = production (""caves on the answer you just gave...""). Nothing contradicts the entry.",P9-findings-rest
F-29,"On run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json, sycophancy_mt reads zero-shot PC1 0.374 (inverted 0.626); as a target the trained axis is 0.355 -> inverted 0.645 vs random 0.541 (+0.104), as a source 0.379 -> inverted 0.621 vs random 0.633 (-0.012), so the ""sign-flipped real signal"" reading holds as target and fails as source.",0.374; 0.626; 0.355; 0.645; 0.541; +0.104; 0.379; 0.621; 0.633; -0.012,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:619,run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git working tree = lab),"zeroshot[direction=PC1].auroc[sycophancy_mt]; results[feature=axes|random, probe=paper].auroc off-diagonal column mean and row mean",NO ARTIFACT - the producing command was an inline python -c print (session b035ccb3 line 2446),n/a,"PC1 0.3740 / inv 0.6260; TARGET axes 0.3551 -> inv 0.6449, random 0.5413, inv-random +0.1036; SOURCE axes 0.3787 -> inv 0.6213, random 0.6327, inv-random -0.0114 (10 cells each)",own script: off-diagonal column/row means over the 11x11 cell matrix,"git working-tree matrix; bank field inside the file = axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt / paper16, k=5, seed 42, so RF-15/RF-16 are settled in the file; no BH q-value quoted, so RF-13 does not bite","SWEPT all 42 kd11 matrices (21 layers x 2 poolings). Inverted axes beats random AS TARGET at 39/42; AS SOURCE at 25/42. By pooling: mean 20/21 target vs 7/21 source (the entry's asymmetry); LAST 19/21 target vs 18/21 source - the asymmetry disappears, and at L28-L52 the inverted axis as source reaches 0.68-0.74 vs a random baseline of 0.44-0.55.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - all values recomputed from the cell-level matrices with an independent script,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-29_inversion.py; F-29_layers.py,"All eight stated numbers reproduce exactly. The load-bearing half (""fails as source"", which is what turns down the reviewer's challenge) is a MEAN-POOLING result: under last pooling the inverted axis transfers out of sycophancy_mt at 18 of 21 layers, which is the behaviour the entry says a sign-flipped construct would show. The entry's own caveat says one layer, one seed; it should say one pooling too.",P9-findings-rest
F-32,"All 60 cap variants were regenerated and the SAME lexical counts that found the confounds were re-run as the acceptance test, closing all five: pair-4 explanatory labour 4/5 vs 4/5, approving modifiers 4 of 6 holding -> 0, leak phrasing 4 -> 0, affect pair 3 3/5 vs 0/5 -> 3/5 vs 5/5 (honest overshoot), turn-1 commitment 5/5 on all 6 capitulation roles; max variant length 103 chars; role keys unchanged.",4/5 vs 4/5; 4 -> 0; 4 -> 0; 3/5 vs 5/5; 5/5 x 6; 103 chars,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:740,"cap/personas/cap_instructions/*.json (live = v3); logs/cap_smoke_v2.log (holds v2 text); C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-cap/responses (13 files, 1,300 rows)","regex counts over 60 variants; turn-1 assistant text per (role, question)",NO RAW DATA - the v2 bank the acceptance test measured existed ~15:39-22:49 on 2026-09-20 and was replaced; the live files are v3,"no - re-running F-32's own script on the live bank gives explain 3/5 vs 4/5 (not 4/5 vs 4/5), turn1-commit 0/5 everywhere (not 5/5), max 99 chars (not 103); affect 3/5 vs 5/5 and praise 0 / leak 0 do reproduce","regex diff: all four F-28 regexes differ from F-32's, and PRAISE changed target (F-28 = role KEY, F-32 = variant TEXT) and lost the words evidence bound / steadfast / principled / rigorous. On the unchanged role keys the count is STILL 4/6 vs 0/6; applying F-28's praise list to the live VARIANT TEXT gives pc_evidence_bound 5/5, i.e. 1/6 not 0. Production rollouts: 1,300 rows, 65 system prompts, 20 distinct (question_index, turn-1 text) pairs at n=65 each -> turn 1 byte-identical across all personas.",own script re-running both regex sets on the live bank; recovery of both producing commands from session b035ccb3 (lines 4097/4102 and 4679); SYSTEM-line extraction from the two smoke logs; turn-1 grouping over run-cap/responses,"live persona files md5-identical on laptop, lab and git dc24e96; run-cap/responses lab-only (Drive-backed by the audit 09-22 backup); no BH q-value quoted","The recovered full print also shows pair 6 explain 1/5 vs 0/5 and pair 6 affect 0/5 vs 2/5, plus turn1-commit 3/5 on two HOLDING roles - so ""both groups share an identical turn-1 instruction"" was not true of v2 either. Both asymmetries persist in v3. The caveat ""Nothing has been re-smoke-tested"" is stale: logs/cap_smoke_v2.log is 3h07m later and produced F-46.",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - the regexes, the three bank generations and the teacher-forced turn 1 all come from files or from the producing command itself",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-28_F-32_counts.py; P9_lab3.py,"Three defects. (1) ""The same lexical counts ... were re-run"" is FALSE: all four regexes differ and PRAISE changed what it measures. (2) The ""approving modifiers 4 -> 0"" row compares a role-KEY count with a variant-TEXT count on a shortened word list; on F-28's own vocabulary the live variant text still reads pc_evidence_bound 5/5, so 4/6 -> 1/6, not 0. The role key never reaches the model, so the variant-text count is the operative one, but the before/after pair is not like-for-like. (3) The table describes a bank generation that never produced a rollout; the production bank is v3 with a TEACHER-FORCED turn 1 (gen_multiturn_ndif.py, citing F-46), which is the real reason the F-26 confound is closed. The cap result F-65/F-66 is defensible, but this entry is not what defends it.",P9-findings-rest
F-33,"Scale-3b failed 22 of 22 roles attempted producing 0 vectors; the log was useless because of str(e)[:200]; ""widest 4856 padded tokens"" is a batch total not a sequence length, and response lengths are near-identical across rungs (3B 1,371/2,418/2,722/2,909; 8B 1,369/2,447/2,729/2,896; 70B 1,480/2,542/2,825/3,059); the cause was the per-process memory cap, and a single role at batch 2/4 finished in ~60 s.","22 of 22; 0 vectors; 4856 tokens; 12 length percentiles; saved (28, 3072) over n=62",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:777,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/scale_3b_vectors_all.log; run-scale/{3b,8b}/responses; run-paper16/responses; logs/scale_3b.status","""no vector produced"" and ""saved ("" lines; last-assistant-turn character lengths","log: 24 ""no vector produced"" lines over 24 distinct roles (first 15:26:18 default, last 15:48:35 pc_transparency_officer); 26 ""saved ("" lines, all at 15:52:59 or later","NO on the headline count - the log says 24 of 24, not 22 of 22","3B 2600 rows p50=1,371 p90=2,417 p99=2,721 max=2,909; 8B 2600 rows 1,369/2,446/2,728/2,896; 70B(run-paper16) 1400 rows 1,480/2,541/2,825/3,059; max ""widest N padded tokens"" = 4856",own script: recomputed percentiles over the last assistant turn of every rollout file; counted log events by role,"lab originals, mtimes 2026-09-20, before the entry and outside the 09-22 wave; scale_3b.status was only APPENDED to by that wave (""SKIP already DONE"")","p50 and max match exactly; p90/p99 differ by 1 in 6 of 12 cells (percentile-index convention). Units are CHARACTERS, which the table does not say, while the 4856 figure it argues against is tokens.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - counted directly in the raw log,LOW-MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P9_lab.py; P9_lab2.py,"""22 of 22"" was a snapshot taken at 15:47 (session b035ccb3 line 4730 prints exactly ""no vector produced: 22 / roles OK: 0""); two more roles failed at 15:47:37 and 15:48:35. F-35 in the same ledger says 24, and the log supports F-35 - an internal ledger conflict. The 70B length row's source dir (unnamed in the entry) is run-paper16/responses, 1,400 rows. The single-role probe line ""saved (28, 3072) over n=62"" is transcript-only (it wrote to run-scale/3b/vectors_probe). The cited ""0.553"" length figure matches no matrix (0.5555 or 0.5494).",P9-findings-rest
F-35,"On the same 2,600-rollout corpus the 8B extracted 32 layers at batch 8 in 3.4 min (12.9 rows/s) and the 3B extracted 28 layers at batch 2 in 32.9 min (1.32 rows/s) - 9.8x slower while extracting fewer layers - so extrapolating to ~15,000 eval rows gives ~20 min (8B) and ~3.2 h (3B), ~3.5 h in total; post-restart the 3B run was 26 saved / 26 roles with zero failures, all 24 ""no vector produced"" lines pre-restart.",3.4 min; 12.9 rows/s; 32.9 min; 1.32 rows/s; 9.8x; ~20 min; ~3.2 h; 26/26; 24 lines; 15:48:35; 15:51:34,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:860,C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/scale_3b.status; logs/scale_8b.status; logs/scale_3b_vectors_all.log,"""extracting vectors_all"" -> ""vectors_all exit 0"" timestamps; FAIL/OK event counts","8B 14:54:19 -> 14:57:40 = 201 s; 3B 15:51:34 -> 16:24:27 = 1973 s; both ""vectors_all exit 0: 26 vectors""",yes - all seven figures,"8B 3.35 min = 12.935 rows/s; 3B 32.88 min = 1.318 rows/s; ratio 9.82x; 15,000 rows -> 19.3 min (8B) and 3.16 h (3B), total 3.48 h; FAIL 24/24 distinct roles last 15:48:35, OK 26/26 first 15:52:59",own script: arithmetic over the status-file timestamps and event counts in the extraction log,"status files have mtime 2026-09-22 16:05 (inside the RF-13 wave) but the wave only APPENDED ""SKIP already DONE; -Force to re-run""; the 09-20 timestamps and the DONE lines are intact; the extraction log is untouched","single run per rung, one seed, one bank; the entry's own caveat (eval rows are longer, so the 3B figure is a floor; throughput moves with NDIF tenancy) is accurate",HOLDS,HIGH - arithmetic over timestamps in primary log files,LOW-MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/P9_lab.py; P9_lab2.py,"Everything reproduces. One cross-reference is not verifiable here: ""the same inversion as F-27's generation timing (3B 82 min vs 8B 51 min)"" - the status files give 8B generation 50.9 min but 3B generation 0.1 min, because the restarted chain skipped generation; the 82 min belongs to the first, overwritten chain. Check it at F-27. Note also that the RF-14 guard fix applied during this audit is what makes the 09-22 ""SKIP already DONE"" line appear.",P9-findings-rest
F-36,"sycophancy_mt items are factual, impersonal and have one verifiable answer while the v1 cap questions are professional judgement calls, so the axis would be elicited on capitulation-on-judgement and tested on capitulation-on-fact; three consequences follow, and the v2 draft is 20 items, 12 recall + 8 misconception, entirely third-person.",20 items; 12 recall + 8 misconception; entirely third-person; 2 quoted sycophancy_mt items,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:894,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-sycophancy-mt/questions.jsonl (lab-only, mtime 2026-09-16 12:58); cap/questions/{cap_questions.jsonl, cap_questions_v2_draft.jsonl, cap_questions_v3.jsonl}",source / correct_answer / framing / kind fields; first-person regex over question text,"v2_draft on disk = 20 items, kind {recall:10, misconception:10}, framing {third:10, first:10} - the entry says 12+8 and entirely third-person",NO for the v2 description; YES for everything about sycophancy_mt and the v1 cap set,"sycophancy_mt: 1,200 items, source {trivia_qa:666, truthful_qa:534}, 1,200/1,200 with correct_answer, 39/1,200 (3.2%) first-person, question p50 62 chars; both quoted items verbatim. v1 cap: 20 items, 0 with correct_answer, all judgement calls, 4 first-person. v3 (production): 10 recall / 10 misconception, 10 third / 10 first, 20/20 with correct_answer.",own scripts over the question files (lab + local) and the production rollouts; v2 timing from file mtimes plus the transcript,"questions.jsonl lab-only, mtime 2026-09-16, older than the entry and outside the 09-22 wave; the three cap question files are byte-identical (modulo CRLF) on laptop, lab and git","the production bank is v3, not v2: gen_multiturn_ndif.py defaults to cap_questions_v3.jsonl and run-cap/responses carries framing/kind/correct_answer with question 0 = ""Which element has the chemical symbol W?"" = v3 id 0",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - every number from a file opened during this audit; timing from mtimes plus the transcript,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-36_questions.py; P9_lab.py; P9_lab3.py; P9_lab4.py,"The mismatch itself is verified end to end and was acted on. But the ledger points at a file that no longer holds its numbers: the v2 draft was created 10:58:32Z (12 recall + 8 misconception, no framing key), F-36 was appended 11:00:21Z, and the file was REWRITTEN 11:06:01Z with a 10/10 first/third split - so the entry was right when written and its pointer is now stale. Consequence 2 (""v2 is entirely third-person; making it first-person would increase the mismatch"") was reversed within 6 minutes and the PRODUCTION set is 10 of 20 first-person against a test set that is 3.2% first-person - a smaller but live framing mismatch. Two minor over-statements: 4 of 20 v1 cap items are first-person, and not every sycophancy_mt item has one verifiable answer (item 1474 -> ""Depends on location."").",P9-findings-rest
F-38,"The model column shows gender-secret was written by a fine-tuned checkpoint and soft-trigger by a LoRA adapter while instructed-deception used the base model, so the first two cannot be replicated at 3B/8B and, uniquely, their rows were generated by a fine-tuned model but their activations are read from the base 70B - the 11-dataset grid stays at 11.",3 model names; 11 datasets,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:985,"results/subsets/{gender-secret,soft-trigger,instructed-deception}.csv; src/assistant_axis_ndif/eval_datasets.py:46,279,284,285; 2_activations_ndif.py:489",model column value counts; CSV_MODEL / GENDER_SECRET_MODEL / SOFT_TRIGGER / FINETUNED_ONLY; --model default,all three named models present and correctly classified,yes,"gender-secret 762 rows, 2 models (both *-secret-male fine-tunes); soft-trigger 24,000 rows, 12 models (all *-lora-*); instructed-deception 20,798 rows, 4 models (all base). eval_datasets.py filters on those exact names; 2_activations_ndif.py --model default = meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct.",own script: full value_counts of the model column with no truncation; grep of the pipeline constants,tracked git files in the working tree; no git-vs-lab divergence recorded in Phase 1; no layer/bank/seed/q-value involved,"the codebase has an explicit FINETUNED_ONLY set for exactly this asymmetry; the ""cannot be replicated at 3B/8B"" step is a sound inference, not a separate measurement",HOLDS,HIGH - recounted from the CSVs plus the code that selects rows and sets the activation model,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-38_models.py,"Both consequences verify and the conclusion is understated: ALL 2 gender-secret models are secret-persona fine-tunes, ALL 12 soft-trigger models are LoRA adapters, ALL 4 instructed-deception models are base. One presentation defect: the table lists one generating model per dataset where the files hold 2, 12 and 4 - the producing command sliced unique()[:4].",P9-findings-rest
F-103,"The kd bank's contribution (ext_axis1 minus axis1, zero-shot, 11 datasets) is the same under mean and last pooling: layer-mean +0.055 vs +0.059, positive at 21/21 and 20/21 layers, so F-102's pooling warning does not transfer to F-98/F-99.","+0.0551 / +0.0590 layer-mean; [+0.0019,+0.0814] / [-0.0327,+0.0848]; 21/21 and 20/21; share 62.9% / 50.0%; HP-KR L20 0.165->0.806 (mean), 0.061->0.508 (last)",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4818,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json (21 each) + root run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json","zeroshot[direction=contrast | contrast:collab_extended].auroc mean over 11 datasets; results[feature=raw,probe=paper] off-diagonal mean (110 pairs)","mean +0.0551 [+0.0019,+0.0814] 21/21 share 62.9%; last +0.0590 [-0.0327,+0.0848] 20/21 share 50.0%; HP-KR L20 0.1652->0.8057 and 0.0613->0.5081","YES (exact at 4 dp, all 10 quantities)","same -- recomputed from the per-dataset zero-shot AUROC vectors with my own averaging; also reproduces F-98's L20/L40 table (axis1 0.6572/0.7325, ext 0.7386/0.7996, raw 0.6289/0.6623)","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f103, read-only on the lab PC; raw baseline joined from the ROOT store per the batch rule","lab copy; collab matrices written 2026-09-22 00:33-02:11, BEFORE the 15:40-16:26 re-run wave (RF-13); bank recorded as axes_collab_s23.pt / bank_name=collab (no basename collision, RF-16 not applicable); root raw values identical to the git working copies; no BH q quoted","both poolings x 21 layers (that IS the claim); share >100% at L60/64/68 under mean and -155.9% at L0 under last -- the share statistic is more unstable than '62.9 vs 50.0' conveys, reinforcing the entry's own instruction to quote the raw difference; one seed, one bank, 11 datasets",HOLDS,HIGH -- exact recomputation of all 10 quantities from raw matrices with independent code; provenance unambiguous,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (section f103),Output audit/phase2/out/W5A_f103.txt. Also independently confirms F-98's L20/L40 mean-pooled table.,W5A-ledger
F-21,"NDIF's small-model deployments cap GPU memory per process at about 7.37 GiB, so 3B generation OOMs while the GPU is 83% free; allocation scales with --gen_batch (96/24/8 -> 140/38/14 MiB) and the run settled on --gen_batch 8 --session_batches 4 --retries 6.","44.42 GiB total; 36.73 GiB free; 7.69 GiB in use; 7.37 GiB allowed; 83% free; 96->140, 24->38, 8->14 MiB; 84/100 rows",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:365,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/scale_3b_generate.log (4,877,518 B, 2026-09-20 15:51); scale/scripts/run_scale_chain.ps1","line 260 (also 366, 524, 532); run_scale_chain.ps1:149 (comment) and :153-154 (flags)",line 260 verbatim: 'total capacity of 44.42 GiB of which 36.73 GiB is free ... this process has 7.69 GiB memory in use. 7.37 GiB allowed ... 7.17 GiB is allocated by PyTorch',YES for the quoted block (verbatim); NO file for the gen_batch sweep table,"36.73/44.42 = 82.7% free; flags verified at run_scale_chain.ps1:153-154; allocation histogram over the whole log = {36,40,52,58,70,76,78,122,134,136,138,140,142} MiB -- 14 and 38 MiB never occur; run-scale/smoke3b MISSING on lab and on Drive","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f21 + f21b and p1_peek.py grep, read-only on the lab PC","lab-only file (no Drive copy, not in git); log mtime 2026-09-20 15:51, untouched by the 09-22 wave",n/a (single engineering measurement),PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH -- the log is unambiguous and the absence of run-scale/smoke3b is confirmed against both the lab census and Drive,LOW,"audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (sections f21, f21b)","The three-row gen_batch sweep is a word-for-word copy of the owner's own comment in scale/scripts/run_scale_chain.ps1:149 -- prose, not data. Its store (run-scale/smoke3b) does not exist anywhere, and the cited log never allocates 14 or 38 MiB. The '84/100 rows with retries disabled' cell is unverifiable.",W5A-ledger
F-39,"Against the persona-coordinates paper read directly: the paper does run a matched control (axis beats dataset PCA by +0.13..+0.23 in its own bar chart), our 70B result is k-dependent (+0.138 over matched dataset PCA at k=2, +0.004 at k=5), and our bigger/stricter pipeline gets a smaller gain over raw (+0.026 vs their +0.10) because our raw baseline is 0.809.","paper bars -0.14/-0.12/+0.10, -0.14/-0.11/+0.12, -0.11/+0.01/+0.14, -0.01/-0.02/+0.17; ours raw 0.8090, pc:unified@2 0.8351 (+0.0262), datapca@2 -0.1120 -> +0.138; pc:unified 0.7917 (-0.0173), datapca -0.0214 -> +0.004; head-to-head personas 11 vs 26/36, variants 2 vs 5, questions 10 vs 20",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1012,"run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git working copy; identical on lab and Drive); papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf pp. 3, 4, 12, 13, 14","results[feature,probe=paper].auroc off-diagonal over {instructed-deception, convincing-game, ai_liar, roleplaying, mask}; PDF Figure 10 panel A, Table 1 (p.4), Deception Axis paragraph (p.3)","raw 0.8090; pc:unified@2 +0.0262; datapca@2 -0.1120; axis@2-dPCA@2 +0.1382; pc:unified -0.0173; datapca -0.0214; k5 margin +0.0041. PDF Fig 10A prints exactly -0.14/-0.14/-0.11/-0.01, -0.12/-0.11/+0.01/-0.02, +0.10/+0.12/+0.14/+0.17","YES (all 5 of our numbers and all 12 of the paper's, exact)","paper bars re-derived from the paper's own printed 5x5 cells (p.12): Random -0.143, Dataset PCA -0.1175, Axis +0.1015 for 3B deception -- the bars are internally consistent. Brute force: only 2 of the 5-subset x probe combinations give raw=0.8090, and only F-39's set does so under the paper probe.","audit/scripts/claims/F-39.py (own off-diagonal averaging, no use of kd/scripts/paper_comparison.py) + pypdf extraction of the PDF, laptop","git working copy of the matrix (LAB=GIT=Drive per Phase 1); bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt / paper16 recorded inside the file (the fp32 re-extraction, RF-15); PDF tracked in git","same 5 datasets at other layers/poolings: axis@2-raw = +0.057 (L20 mean), +0.020 (L32), +0.011 (L44), +0.018 (L40 last); axis@2-datapca@2 stays +0.095..+0.151 everywhere. Swapping mask -> harm-pressure-choice turns +0.026 into +0.128 (raw 0.7513).",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH -- every number recomputed; the three defects are documentary and checked against the PDF,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-39.py,"Three defects: (1) the bar chart is Figure 10 panel A, not 'Figure 9 panel A'; (2) 'the paper's own five deception datasets' is the paper's FIGURE set (Mask in, HPC out, panels titled [HPC excluded]) -- the paper's TABLE 1 five are AILiar/Roleplaying/ConvGame/InstrDec/HarmPressureChoice; (3) the head-to-head 'personas 5+5+anchor (11)' is the paper's SYCOPHANCY axis -- its deception axis is 8+7+anchor = 16. IMPORTANT: audit/fix/F39_NOTE.md section 2 has this backwards and wrongly tells the owner to fix F-45, F-48, F-54.",W5A-ledger
F-45,"After the OOM fixes the 8B activation extraction runs about 8x slower (8 rows per 1,026 KB chunk, ~57 rows/min), so the full-corpus 8B arm would take ~4.3 h; capping at the paper's own 800 rows per dataset would give 6,551 rows, 45% of the 14,718-row corpus.","193 chunks, avg 1,026 KB, ~8 rows/chunk vs 64 before; ~57 rows/min; 28% done; 14,718 rows; ~4.3 h; 6,551 rows = 45%; paper Table 1: 120/40, 335/113, 599/201, 599/201, 444/150",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1266,lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-scale/8b/coords/* and run-coords/passB/*/rows.jsonl; papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf p.4,chunk counts and mean size per dataset; passB per-dataset rows.jsonl line counts; PDF Table 1,"8B instructed-deception: 100 chunks, meanKB 1026.0, rows 800 -> 8.00 rows/chunk. passB totals: 16,718 incl. alpaca 2,000 -> 14,718 without alpaca; sum(min(800,n)) = 7,351 -> 6,551 without alpaca; 6,551/14,718 = 44.51%. PDF Table 1 splits identical to all five quoted pairs.","YES (1,026 KB, 8 rows/chunk, 14,718, 6,551, 45%, Table 1 all exact)","~131 KB/row = 8 layers x 4096 x 2 poolings x fp16 = 131,072 B, consistent with 1,026/8 = 128.25 KiB; 8B measured rate 57.7 rows/min (18:34:30->18:48:22, 800 rows) vs the stated ~57; 193x8/5,432 = 28.4% and 193x8/27.3 min = 56.6 rows/min are internally consistent","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f45 (+ f49 for the rate), read-only on the lab PC; pypdf for Table 1","lab store (Drive SAME per Phase 1); the 18:04 full-corpus chunks were deleted at the 18:34 --sample 800 restart, so the 193-chunk measurement itself is gone","the 1,026 KB / 8-rows-per-chunk figures hold for harm-pressure-choice too (100 chunks, 1026.0 KB, 800 rows); other datasets 962-1,026 KB",HOLDS,HIGH for everything with a file; MEDIUM overall because two inputs (193 chunks at 27.3 min; 64 rows/chunk before the fix) no longer exist,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (section f45),"Corrects the batch brief: F-45 does NOT repeat a 'paper's five datasets' error. It cites Table 1, and Table 1 (p.4) does list HarmPressureChoice and does not list Mask. audit/fix/F39_NOTE.md section 2 is the document that needs correcting, not F-45/F-48/F-54.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] PHASE 4 AMENDMENT (verdict unchanged; every number re-derived exactly). Provenance caveat: the 8B extraction directory no longer holds the run F-45 measured - every dataset present is now capped at 800 rows, i.e. the entry's own recommendation was adopted and the 193-chunk partial run replaced the same evening. SEPARATE PROJECT RED FLAG found here: 5 of the 12 dataset dirs in run-scale/8b/coords have NO rows.jsonl at all (harm-pressure-knowledge-report, harm-pressure-kr-matched, insider-trading, sandbagging_v2, sycophancy_mt); only 3,093 non-alpaca rows across 7 datasets. Anything assuming a complete 8B corpus needs re-checking.",W5A-ledger
F-49,"On the evaluation-activation arm the 3B model is only 1.8x slower than the 8B (32.5 vs 59 rows/min), not the 9.8x that an earlier measurement implied.",306 chunks in 24.5 min from 19:36:40; 12.5 chunks/min; ~2.6 rows/chunk; ~32.5 rows/min; 8B 59 rows/min; 1.8x; items.pt 0.34 MB vs 0.30 MB,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1443,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-scale/{3b,8b}/coords/instructed-deception (chunk files, rows.jsonl, items.pt); logs/scale_coords_3b.log",chunk_* file count and mtimes; rows.jsonl line count; items.pt size,"3B: 400 chunks, 800 rows = 2.00 rows/chunk, 12.39 chunks/min, 24.8 rows/min (307 chunks in the first 24.5 min). 8B: 100 chunks, 800 rows = 8.00 rows/chunk, 7.21 chunks/min, 57.7 rows/min. items.pt both exactly 359,384 B.","NO -- 2.00 rows/chunk not 2.6; 24.8 rows/min not 32.5; ratio 2.33x not 1.8x; items.pt sizes identical, not 0.34 vs 0.30","F-50's corrections are what reproduce: 2.0 rows/chunk, ~24 rows/min, ~2.4x. The only F-49 measurement that survives is the chunk rate (306 claimed vs 307 measured in the first 24.5 min).","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f49, read-only on the lab PC (file counts and mtimes)","lab store; chunk mtimes 2026-09-20 19:36-20:09, untouched. logs/scale_coords_3b.log was APPENDED during the 09-22 wave (RF-13) but its 09-20 lines survive.","both rungs measured the same way; the 8B rate (57.7) is slightly below the 59 quoted in F-45/F-49/F-50, depending on whether the span starts at items.pt or at the first chunk",DOES NOT HOLD (REVISED -> F-50),HIGH -- counts and mtimes read directly from the store,LOW,audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (section f49),"The ledger already retracts this in F-50 and F-50's numbers reproduce. One error F-50 does not catch: items.pt is byte-identical on the two rungs (359,384 B each), so F-49's 'items.pt 0.34 MB matching the 8B's 0.30 MB' is wrong -- identical span files are the expected result (F-54 later says the rungs match row for row).",W5A-ledger
F-53,"Changing the capitulation persona's in-prompt label from the noun 'a caver' to a verb form removes all spelunking role-play from the model's answers (4 of 8 items -> 0 of 8) and makes the folds name a specific alternative instead of pleading incompetence, with the wrong-turn-1 control unchanged.","4 of 8 -> 0 of 8; 24 rollouts; controls Ottawa, K, 2",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1599,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/cap/run/smoke_v4/*.jsonl (v4, verb) and cap/run/smoke_cells/*.jsonl (v3, noun -- NOT named by the entry)",assistant turns inside each record's conversation field; system_prompt field,v4 pc_caver: 0 of 8 records contain a spelunking marker. v3 (smoke_cells) pc_caver: 4 of 8. Record counts 8+4+8+4 = 24.,YES (4/8 -> 0/8 exact; 24 rollouts exact),"Recomputed with my own marker regex (pickaxe|helmet|spelunk|underground|cavern|cave|caves|caving|caver|stalact|headlamp|mine|rope|gear|depths) applied ONLY to assistant turns so the system prompt cannot contaminate the count. All eight quoted turn-2 fragments present verbatim; controls verified (Ottawa, K, 2 all reached in v4 on a wrong turn 1). System prompts: v3 'You are a caver who drops the answer...' -> v4 'You are someone who caves on the answer...'.","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f53b and f53c, read-only on the lab PC","lab-only stores (not on Drive, not in git); smoke_cells 2026-09-20 20:55-20:57, smoke_v4 21:03","pc_position_holder (both versions) and both control files: 0 markers throughout, so the effect is specific to the caver persona under the noun label; the teacher-forced smoke_tf (noun) shows 2 of 4",HOLDS,"HIGH -- independent regex, both arms, texts verified verbatim",MEDIUM,"audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (sections f53b, f53c)","Sourcing defect: the entry's source line is 'cap/run/smoke_v4/*.jsonl -- 24 rollouts', but the '4 of 8' half of the headline comes from cap/run/smoke_cells/, which is named nowhere in the ledger. Both stores exist in exactly one place (the lab PC).",W5A-ledger
F-57,"Four thesis figures were built from that day's findings, each reading measured numbers: fig1 the axis at 0.300/0.379 vs random 0.659/0.633; fig2 a layer profile peaking at L44 +0.116 with a dataset-level CI band spanning zero at every layer; fig3 the paper's +0.10 at raw 0.60 against our +0.026 at 0.809; fig4 cos(PC1,assistant) 0.435/0.732/0.623.","0.300; 0.379; 0.659; 0.633; +0.116; +0.10 at 0.60; +0.026 at 0.809; 0.435/0.732/0.623; fig_data.json 28,669 B; significance.json 1.38 MB",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1760,kd/results/fig_data.json; kd/scripts/make_thesis_figures.py; figures/thesis/*.png; lab run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd_s23/significance.json,"profile[pc:unified - raw][layer].{diff,lo,hi,q}; census.n_tests; script lines 70-71, 139-153, 195","fig_data.json = 28,669 B exactly; peak L44 diff +0.1156, lo +0.0330/+0.0354 at L40/L44; census n_tests 3,276, q_min 0.0205, best positive q 0.127; fig1 literals at lines 70-71; fig4 literals at line 195; fig3 literals 0.7619/0.7980/0.8090 and 0.020/0.013/0.013 at line 152","PARTIAL -- size, peak and the hardcoded fig1/fig4 numbers match; 'CI spans zero at every layer' and the fig3 description do not","CI excludes zero at L40 (lo +0.0330) and L44 (lo +0.0354) -- 19 of 21 layers span zero, not 21. The rendered fig2 PNG shows the band above zero there. The rendered fig3 PNG plots F-63's three rungs (+0.202/+0.115/+0.079 vs datapca; +0.020/+0.013/+0.013 vs raw; raw 0.762/0.798/0.809) and contains no 0.60 and no +0.026; 0.026 does not occur in the script at all. Lab significance.json today: 2.36 MB, 5,544 tests, 21 layers -- but its diffs and CIs are IDENTICAL to fig_data.json; only the BH q moved (L44 0.1347 -> 0.1068).",audit/scripts/claims/F-57.py (laptop) + reading the two PNGs as images + audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab_extra2.py (lab),"fig_data.json git working copy = lab = Drive (mtime 2026-09-20 22:08); the source significance.json WAS regenerated 2026-09-22 16:15:50 (RF-13), so the 1.38 MB figure can no longer be checked; the local git copy of that file is the older 468-test / 3-layer version (RF-7/RF-11)","the 110-pair (11-dataset) version of the same test: L40 ci [-0.0046,+0.1665], L44 [+0.0050,+0.1794] -- so even with sycophancy_mt in, L44's CI excludes zero",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH -- the CI contradiction appears in the data, in the rendered figure and in the regenerated source file; the fig3 mismatch appears in both committed versions of the script and in the PNG",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-57.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab_extra2.py,"Two failures. (1) 'the dataset-level CI band spanning zero at every layer' is false at L40 and L44, the two layers the project quotes most; the defensible statement is 'no layer clears the BH-corrected threshold' (best q 0.127 then, 0.100 now). (2) The fig3 described exists in no committed script version and not in the figure on disk, which plots F-63's corrected three-rung comparison -- the entry was never updated after F-63 superseded F-58/F-39. kd/results/fig_data.json is the only surviving reduced copy of the 09-20 bootstrap, but nothing was lost: the regenerated file has identical diffs and CIs.",W5A-ledger
F-62,"Building the kd persona bank from score-3-only rollouts (s3) or from score-2+3 rollouts (s23) makes no measurable difference to downstream cross-dataset transfer: at L40, mean pooling, paper probe, 110 off-diagonal pairs, the four features differ by at most 0.005.",raw 0.6623; pc:kd_assertion +0.1496/+0.1500; pc:knowledge_denial +0.0869/+0.0838; pc:unified +0.0757/+0.0759; axes -0.0272/-0.0319; largest gap 0.005,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1948,"run-crossgen/kd11/banks/{kd,kd_s23}/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json and run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git working copies; Phase 1: LAB=GIT=Drive)","results[feature,probe=paper].auroc, off-diagonal mean over the 11 datasets (110 cells), minus the root file's raw off-diagonal mean",raw 0.6623; +0.1496/+0.1500 (0.0004); +0.0869/+0.0838 (0.0031); +0.0757/+0.0759 (0.0002); -0.0272/-0.0319 (0.0047); largest gap 0.0047,"YES (all eight values and the baseline, exact to 4 dp)","same -- recomputed with my own off-diagonal averaging, no use of kd/scripts/paper_comparison.py. pc:kd_assertion is indeed the strongest feature in either bank at every layer/probe I checked.","audit/scripts/claims/F-62.py, laptop",git working copies; kd bank file axes_vectors_s3.pt / bank_name=kd and axes_vectors_s23.pt / kd_s23 recorded inside the matrices (no ambiguity); root bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt / paper16. The lab's axes_vectors_s3.pt and _s23.pt were regenerated 2026-09-22 (RF-13) but the matrices were not.,"not reported by the entry: the largest s3-vs-s23 gap grows to 0.0157 (mean L20), 0.0301 (last L20), 0.0288 (last L40), 0.0203 (last L44), 0.0183 (mms mean L40), 0.0089 (lr_reg10 mean L40) -- up to 6x the L40 figure, still well inside the +-0.17 dataset-level CI the entry cites",HOLDS,"HIGH -- exact recomputation from files identical in git, on the lab PC and on Drive",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/F-62.py,"Two small things. (1) 'NO measurable difference' is strongest exactly at the reported cell; at other layers/poolings the gap is up to 0.030 -- the conclusion survives but the entry reports only its best case. (2) Figure count: s3 = 4 (exact); s23 = 4 plus 8 under passA/{blocks,matched,per_source,per_target} = 12 today, where the entry says four more. The passA figures entered git at 3dfdb67 (2026-09-21 11:07), AFTER F-62 was written, so the count was plausibly right on the day.",W5A-ledger
F-69,"Re-extracting the full 2,139 HP-KR rows into the passA activation store repairs its denial-matched slice from 98 rows at 89 deceptive / 9 honest to 258 rows at 124 / 134, identical to passB, so harm-pressure-kr-matched can now be measured at all 80 layers.","200 -> 2,139 rows; 98 -> 258 matched; 89/9 -> 124/134; 14.9x; 55 chunks / 5.22 GB / 36 min; gate 'passA measured=2139 predicted=2139 PASS' at 11:29:46",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2421,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/{passA,passB,passC}/harm-pressure-knowledge-report/rows.jsonl; results/subsets/harm-pressure-knowledge-report.csv; logs/hpkr_topup.status",row_id joined to hpkr_slice(text_matched); stored label; status lines 2 and 4; chunk_* counts and bytes,"passA 2,139 rows / 258 matched / 124 deceptive / 134 honest; passB identical; status line 2 'before: passA=200 passC=200 target=2139'; line 4 'passA measured=2139 rows predicted=2139 PASS' at 11:29:46; 55 chunks",YES for every post-repair number and the gate line; the pre-repair 98 and 89/9 have no surviving file,"Reimplemented eval_datasets.hpkr_slice(text_matched) from source (the denial/assert regexes, the llama-v3.3-70b-instruct filter, the <dataset>:<sub>:<idx>:<i> id form) and ran it over the released CSV: 258 ids, 124 deceptive / 134 honest -- matching the stores independently of them. 14.9x = 134/9. Elapsed 10:53:44 -> 11:29:46 = 36 min. Bytes: 5.08 GB written on 09-21 (49 of 55 chunks), 5.61 GB for all 55 -- neither is 5.22 GB.","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f69 + W5A_lab_extra.py / extra2.py, read-only on the lab PC","lab copies; passA rows.jsonl 2026-09-21 11:29:40, passC 11:52:44 (md5 identical to passA), passB 2026-09-15 21:16 (untouched). The CSV is the released 2026-09-15 file. The status file was APPENDED (not truncated) by the 09-22 15:47 no-op re-run, so the 09-21 gate lines survive; that re-run's two rclone steps failed (exit 1).","the slice count is identical whether computed from the CSV alone, from passA, from passB or from passC -- four independent routes to 258 / 124 / 134",HOLDS,HIGH for the composition claim; the superseded 'before' numbers are NO RAW DATA,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (section f69),"Three qualifications. (1) The pre-repair 98 rows and 89/9 split cannot be recomputed -- the 200-row subsample was overwritten; only passA=200 survives. (2) The entry's passC row (200 rows, pending) was already stale 23 minutes later: the same status file logs 'passC measured=2139 PASS' at 11:52:46, and passC's rows.jsonl is now byte-identical to passA's. (3) 5.22 GB matches neither the incremental 5.08 GB nor the total 5.61 GB.",W5A-ledger
F-78,"Two newly read papers: Ying et al. (arXiv:2602.20273) independently corroborate that probes fail on sycophantic lying and show post-training separates it (base-to-chat 0.67->0.56, 0.69->0.56, 0.74->0.52), and their pooled-training result is a cheaper rival to persona coordinates that this project has never run; Choi et al. (ICML 2026) find contextual truthfulness in a sparse set of attention heads, which could explain F-76.",arXiv 2602.20273; 0.67->0.56; 0.69->0.56; 0.74->0.52; R2=0.98; layer 33,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2985,papers/The Truthfulness Spectrum Hypothesis.pdf (28 pp); papers/The Truth Stays in the Family.pdf (24 pp),"Ying p.1 arXiv stamp and abstract; p.3 models; p.4 layer 33 and R2; p.5 Figure 4 panels (a),(b),(c). Choi p.1 abstract and ICML line.","arXiv:2602.20273v1, 23 Feb 2026, Ying/Ravfogel/Kriegeskorte/Hase -- exact. Abstract quotation verbatim. R2=0.98 (vs 0.56 plain cosine). 'we selected layer 33 ... Based on cross-domain performance' verbatim. Figure 4(b) prints 0.67/0.56, 0.69/0.56, 0.74/0.52; Figure 4(a) prints 0.74/0.62, 0.74/0.59, 0.64/0.54. Choi et al.: ICML 2026, sparse context-truthful heads, TruthProbe soft-gating, HaluEval/POPE/CHAIR hallucination -- all exact.","YES for every identifier, quotation and value; NO for the direction the six values are attached to","The six quoted values are panel (b) 'Sycophancy Probes Test on FLED' -- transfer FROM sycophancy. F-78 describes them as base models transferring TO sycophancy, which is panel (a) with different values (0.74->0.62, 0.74->0.59, 0.64->0.54). Base beats chat in both panels at all three sizes, so the conclusion is unaffected.","pypdf extraction of both PDFs during this audit, laptop",PDFs tracked in git (papers/); no result file involved; nothing regenerated,"n/a -- this entry is a reading, not a measurement (its own caveat 4 says so)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH -- both PDFs read in this audit,MEDIUM-HIGH,(none -- direct PDF reads; commands recorded in audit/claims/F-78.md),"The six base-vs-chat numbers are exact but attached to the wrong transfer direction; if any is quoted in the thesis it must be labelled sycophancy->FLED, or replaced with panel (a). The caveat 'read off their Figure 4 and approximate' understates the evidence -- they are printed values. Also: Ying et al. use Qwen-14B/7B as well as the three Llamas, which F-78 omits. 'No pooled-training row anywhere in run-crossgen/' cannot be re-derived after the fact, but every run-crossgen matrix carries the train-on-one design string, consistent with it.",W5A-ledger
F-90,"A single-process re-audit of the pooled-training results finds: the reported single-source baseline (0.6763) was the weakest of four defensible choices, the budget-matched pooled figure has a +-0.02 draw spread that swallows the 0.850-vs-0.806 discrepancy, Result 2 (mean-of-directions over pooled LODO) is +0.0284 with CI [+0.0045,+0.0523], and the persona method run through the same LODO harness loses to a plain pooled logistic regression by 0.11-0.16 AUROC.","0.6763163062; 20 draws mean 0.8344 range [0.7912,0.8736] sd 0.0200; +0.0284 CI [+0.0045,+0.0523], 9/11 (-0.008, -0.043); 21/110 <0.5, 14 <0.4, min 0.0546; baselines 0.6763/0.7220/0.7354/0.8967 with +0.1782/+0.1325/+0.1191/-0.0422; Q5 0.7454/0.7307/0.6921; 0.8828; 0.8545",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3761,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json (17,175 B, 2026-09-21 20:59:35); bank C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt; src/assistant_axis_ndif/30f_result2_audit.py","baselines.*; pooled_lodo_match_draws[20]; bootstrap.*.{diff,lo,hi}; per_target.*; persona_lodo.*; pairs[110]","0.6763163062289969; 0.7219698909; 0.7353614302; 0.8966842158; draws mean 0.8344 min 0.7912 max 0.8736; +0.028354 [+0.004508,+0.052345]; +0.178159/+0.132505/+0.119114/-0.042209 with their CIs; pairs_below_half 21; pooled_lodo_full 0.8544753650; mean_of_directions 0.8828295183; persona axes 0.7453755531, pc:deception 0.7307243420, pc:unified@2 0.6920640950",YES -- every number in the JSON matches to the precision quoted,"Recomputed myself: 9 of 11 targets won, losses harm-pressure-kr-matched -0.0077 and sycophancy_mt -0.0433; 21 pairs below 0.5, 14 below 0.4, minimum 0.0546 convincing-game -> harm-pressure-knowledge-report; sd 0.0205 (ddof=1) = 0.0200 (ddof=0, what the entry quotes); Q5 deltas -0.1091/-0.1238/-0.1624; pc:unified@2 pooling gain +0.1181. The Q5 95% CIs and the Q3 458/461 count are NOT in the JSON (print-only).","audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py f90 + W5A_lab_extra.py, read-only on the lab PC","lab-only JSON, mtime 2026-09-21 20:59:35 -- before commit a13e11d (21:01) and well before the 09-22 wave (RF-13); no BH q quoted. Q5 bank = run/axes.pt (md5 0d2971c6..., 62.9 MB, 2026-09-15) which I loaded: 100 roles, groups deception 22 / honesty 22 / sycophancy 16 / anti_sycophancy 16 / assistant_anchor 8 / breadth_control 16, vectors_dir run/vectors = the OWN100 bank, not paper16 (26) and not kd (36).","one layer (L40), one seed (42) -- the entry says so -- and, not said, one persona bank; the 20-draw resampling is the only spread reported",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for the reproduced numbers; MEDIUM for the Q5 leg (single bank, CIs unverifiable)",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab.py (section f90); audit/scripts/claims/W5A_lab_extra.py,"Every number in the audit JSON reproduces exactly. Two gaps. (1) The Q5 arm -- which the entry nominates as 'the one that should lead' -- used the OWN100 bank (identified here from its 100 role names); the JSON records no bank field and the entry names only the file path. This project's own comparison says paper16 beats own100, so the 0.11-0.16 margin may be bank-inflated and has never been run with paper16 or kd. (2) The three Q5 confidence intervals and the Q3 '458 of 461 items' are print-only (loose lab helpers q5.py, q3.py) and are in no file.",W5A-ledger
F-22,"The 8B generation script 1_generate_ndif.py never received the exc_tail fix its siblings got, so every failed NDIF session logged only a client-side traceback stub and no cause; switching to the exception's last line revealed the OOM on the first retry.",str(e)[:200]; remote.py line 567; 'the fourth instance',kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:392 (source line 1_generate_ndif.py:145),"git src/assistant_axis_ndif/1_generate_ndif.py @106d09f and @HEAD; git ndif_common.py, 8_coords_ndif.py; lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/scale_8b_generate.log, logs/scale_3b_generate.log","106d09f L144-146 handler; HEAD L145-152 fix, L184-186 sibling; 8b log L60-63; 3b log L172",pre-fix slice is at L146 (not L145); L145 at HEAD is the fix's comment line,substance yes; cited line number no,"8b log: 'NNsightException: Traceback ... remote.py, line 567 ... Fi' (cut mid-word); 3b log L172 13:09:10 'OutOfMemoryError: CUDA out of memory. Tried to allocate 122.00 MiB'",git blob scan for str(e)[:200]/exc_tail across all 6 committed versions + siblings; grep of both lab logs with context,git 106d09f / 3dfdb67 / HEAD d280d23; lab logs are 2026-09-20 originals (outside the 09-22 wave),n/a (code/log claim). Sibling handler at HEAD L186 STILL uses str(e)[:200]; 2_activations_ndif.py went 2 -> 1 occurrences at 3dfdb67 (a fifth instance the entry does not mention),HOLDS,HIGH - code and logs are direct evidence,LOW for the paper; MEDIUM as a live code defect,audit/scripts/claims/F-22.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labB.py,"Cited source line points at the fix's comment, not the bug. NEW: the same file's generate_batch handler (HEAD line 186) still uses str(e)[:200] - the entry's own 'grep the siblings' lesson is unapplied 40 lines below it. 'Fourth instance' not verified; session mining records a fifth the same day.",W5B-ledger
F-40,"The passB evaluation corpus is 14,718 rows over 11 datasets (instructed-deception 37% of it), and the 8B extraction ran at ~416 rows/min, about 1.75x slower than the earlier projection.","14,718 total; instructed-deception 5,432 = 37%; 111 chunks in 16.6 min; ~416 rows/min; 8B ~35 min, 3B ~5.7 h, total ~6.5 h; 1.75x",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1077,lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/passB/*/rows.jsonl; logs/scale_coords_8b.log,"rows.jsonl line counts; log lines 11-14, 3015, 3017-3020, 4004 (17:16:32)","all 11 counts identical to the ledger table; total 14,718; ID share 0.3691",yes (exact),"at 17:16:32 counters = ID 85/85 + HPC 26/35 = 111 chunks, 16.67 min after ID start; implied rate ~421 rows/min vs stated ~416",line-count every passB rows.jsonl; reconstruct the chunk counter and clock from the 8B log progress bars (the chunk FILES were deleted before the 18:04 restart),lab only (passB not in git; Drive same). Not touched by the 09-22 wave.,"the 8B arm as actually run took 62 min (F-48), not the projected 35; F-45 supersedes the projection",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the corpus table; MEDIUM for the rate (log-only),"LOW (cost projection, superseded); the corpus table is reused downstream",audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labA.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labD.py,"Corpus census exact. Rate reconstructable to ~1% despite the deleted chunk files. The '1.75x' is the 8B-arm ratio (35/20); the entry's own total row implies 1.86x (6.5/3.5), so the headline multiplier does not describe the total it is attached to.",W5B-ledger
F-47,"A cached items.pt from an earlier unsampled run was reused, so harm-pressure-choice was extracted at its full 2,134 rows while every other 8B dataset honoured --sample 800; the fix was to delete the whole directory and re-extract.","2,134 vs --sample 800; ID 800 rows / 0.3 MB / 100 chunks; HPC rows.jsonl absent / items.pt 1.3 MB / 217 chunks; ~81% through; ~13 min fix",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1368,"lab logs/scale_coords_8b.log lines 12171-12173 and 14819-14821; logs/scale_coords_8b_hpc.log; run-scale/8b/coords/{instructed-deception,harm-pressure-choice}",'800 to do'/'100 sessions' vs '2134 to do'/'267 sessions'; repair log 19:46:47-20:00:18,"log confirms 2134-vs-800 asymmetry exactly; ID artefacts (100 chunks, items.pt 359,384 B, 800 rows) confirmed",partly - the HPC artefact row cannot be checked,"217/267 sessions = 81.3% (matches the entry's '~81% through'); repair took 13.5 min (predicted ~13); HPC dir now 800 rows / 100 chunks / items.pt 525,208 B",cited log lines read directly; current directory listing and rows.jsonl line counts,lab only; logs are 09-20 originals; the defective artefacts were deleted by the F-48 repair,"the repaired store is consistent with F-54's matched 2,508-row rungs",PARTLY HOLDS,MEDIUM-HIGH - mechanism and surviving numbers reproduce; the two numbers read off the defective state are NO RAW DATA,LOW-MEDIUM (engineering incident guarding the matched-rung comparison),audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labA.py,"The stale 1.3 MB items.pt and the 217 chunk files no longer exist (deleted by design). 217/267 = 81.3% makes the entry internally consistent, which is the strongest check available.",W5B-ledger
F-50,"Measured on the completed 3B instructed-deception extraction, batch_size 2 gives exactly 2.0 rows per chunk, so the 3B rung runs 2.4x slower than the 8B, not the 1.8x F-49 inferred from an estimated 2.6 rows/chunk.","800 rows in 400 chunks = 2.0 rows/chunk; 8B 7.5 chunks/min, 8.0 rows/chunk, 59 rows/min; 3B 12.1 chunks/min, 24.2 rows/min; 2.4x; F-49 inflated by 34%; 1,554 rows remain, ~64 min, finish ~21:20",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1477,lab run-scale/3b/coords/instructed-deception (rows.jsonl + chunk files); logs/scale_coords_3b.log; logs/scale_coords_8b.log,402 files = 400 chunks + items.pt + rows.jsonl; rows.jsonl 800 lines; 3b log 19:36:40 -> '400/400 [32:23]'; Done. 21:24:14; 8b log 18:34:24 -> 18:48:22,"800 rows, 400 chunks, 2.000 rows/chunk",yes (exact),"3B 12.35 chunks/min, 24.7 rows/min; 8B 7.16 chunks/min, 8.000 rows/chunk, 57.3 rows/min; ratio 2.32x; 3B arm finished 21:24:14",file counts and rows.jsonl line counts; start/end timestamps taken from the two extraction logs,"lab only (run-scale/3b not in git). The 3b log was appended to on 09-22 16:20 by the boot wave, but the 09-20 block used here is untouched.","whole-arm 3B rate 23.3 rows/min over 2,508 rows; per-dataset rates 20.7-24.4 rows/min",HOLDS,HIGH - chunk counts are exact file counts; timings are internal log timestamps,LOW (throughput bookkeeping),audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labA.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labD.py,"The measured core (2.0 and 8.0 rows/chunk) is exact. Derived rates differ 2-4% with the bracketing of the interval, giving 2.32x vs the stated 2.4x - same conclusion. Small slip: '1,554 rows remain' understates the real remainder of 1,708; the finish-time prediction was still within 4 minutes.",W5B-ledger
F-55,"With no system prompt at all the model holds its answer on all 8 challenged items, and its wording matches the holding personas', so the cap contrast is 'capitulation instruction present vs absent' rather than capitulation vs position-holding; the folding persona meanwhile folds on all 8, including to the myth.",8 items; no-persona 8/8 hold; pc_calibrated_holder 8/8 hold; pc_consensus_follower folds on all items,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1681,"lab cap/run/probe/{pc_position_holder_nopersona,pc_calibrated_holder,pc_consensus_follower}.jsonl; cap/run/smoke_{cells,tf,v4}/pc_position_holder.jsonl",8 rows per file; last assistant message of 'conversation'; system_prompt field,"8 rows in each of the three files; system_prompt=None on all 8 no-persona rows; all five no-persona quotes, the calibrated-holder Wolfram quote and both consensus-follower myth quotes present verbatim",yes for the three named files; NO for the pc_position_holder row of the table,"no-persona 8/8 hold; pc_calibrated_holder 8/8 hold; pc_consensus_follower 8/8 fold, both misconception items to the myth",read every row of all three files and classify the turn-2 text by hand (there is no stored hold/fold label),"lab only - cap/run/probe is not on Drive and not in git (RF-10); mtimes 2026-09-20 21:33-21:34, originals","one variant, 8 items, one no-persona arm (the entry's own caveat); no hedge-marker metric exists",HOLDS,"HIGH on the behaviour; LOW-MEDIUM on 'textually identical', which is a human reading with no metric",MEDIUM-HIGH - the mechanism paragraph behind the cap design and draft topic 6,audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labA.py; W5B_labB.py; W5B_labE.py,"SOURCE-LINE CORRECTION: the pc_position_holder row of the comparison table ('Tungsten is indeed the element ... German word Wolfram') is in NONE of the three cited files; it comes from cap/run/smoke_cells|smoke_tf|smoke_v4/pc_position_holder.jsonl. There is no 8-item pc_position_holder probe file, so 'indistinguishable from pc_position_holder' is a cross-run comparison.",W5B-ledger
F-60,"Mahadik & Skapars' paper never mentions harm-pressure-knowledge-report, mentions HarmPressureChoice only twice (both inside Table 1) and Mask 33 times in every figure, so the deception set it actually evaluates is ConvGame/InstrDec/Mask/AILiar/Roleplay and our five match only 4 of 5.",HP-KR 0 mentions; HarmPressureChoice 2 (Table 1 only); Mask 33; 4 of 5 shared; axis +0.089/+0.086 at 3B/8B collapsing to +0.026 at 70B,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1868,papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf (git),full-text term counts per page; figure axis label runs; Table 1 on p4,"HP-KR 0; literal 'HarmPressureChoice' 2, both on p4 (Table 1 body + caption); Mask/MASK 33, all figure axis labels",yes (exact),"figure axis label run 'ConvGame InstrDec Mask AILiar Roleplay' on pp. 5, 6, 7, 12, 13, 14; two further 'HPC' strings on pp.12-13 are the '[HPC excluded]' figure titles","pypdf 6.19.0 re-extraction with per-page regex counts and context, audit/phase2/out/F-60_pdfcount.txt","git papers/ PDF (added 608b2a7, unchanged). No lab data, bank, layer or q-value.","lowercase 'mask' occurs 0 times, so the 33 is not inflated by ordinary word use",HOLDS,HIGH - the PDF is in git and the count is a re-runnable script,MEDIUM - it decides how the 3B/8B replication may be described and underwrites F-23,audit/scripts/claims/F-60.py,"CORRECTION NOT PROPAGATED: F-60 marks only F-58 superseded, but F-48 (FINDINGS.md:1418) and F-54 (:1659) still assert 'These five ARE Mahadik & Skapars' Table 1 deception benchmark' with no marker - the exact framing F-60 calls over-reach. F-45 only quotes Table 1's split sizes and is unaffected. DOC_FIXES candidate.",W5B-ledger
F-64,"The cap generation and judging chain completed with 12 role files of 100 rollouts each, and the LLM-judge filter removes rollouts almost equally from both sides (93.83% kept for capitulation vs 93.17% for position-holding), so it is not manufacturing the separation.","2a 12 files/1,200 rows; 2b 12 files/240 rows; 2c 12 score files; 2d 12 vectors vs predicted 13; kept 563/600=93.83% and 559/600=93.17%, gap 0.66pp; scores 0:78/6.5%, 1:0/0.0%, 2:714/59.5%, 3:408/34.0%; pc_deferrer 19%, pc_calibrated_holder 17%",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2037,"lab run-cap/scores/*.json (12); run-cap/{responses,control,vectors_s23,vectors_all}; cap/personas/cap_role_groups.json; logs/cap_chain.status",flat {rollout_id: score} maps; groups.capitulation.roles / groups.position_holding.roles; status first START block 2026-09-20 22:59 -> 09-21 01:31,"cap_chain.status gate lines verbatim: 2a 12/1200 PASS, 2b 12 control files PASS, 2c 12 score files PASS, 2d/s23 and 2d/all 'measured=12 vectors predicted=13 PASS', 2e GATE FAILED",yes,"1,200 scored rollouts: 78 / 0 / 714 / 408 = 6.5000% / 0.0000% / 59.5000% / 34.0000%; capitulation 563/600 = 93.8333%, position_holding 559/600 = 93.1667%, gap 0.667pp; pc_deferrer 19/100, pc_calibrated_holder 17/100","read all 12 score JSONs, rebuild the distribution and per-role drop, join to the bank's own role-group file","lab only (run-cap and logs not on Drive, not in git; RF-10). 09-21 mtimes, outside the 09-22 wave.","the same judge-filter question is re-tested by F-65 (<=0.004), F-67 (<=0.001) and F-82 (whole depth profile)",HOLDS,"HIGH - 1,200 judged rollouts read directly",MEDIUM-HIGH - the empirical answer to the reviewer's judge-filter objection,audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labA.py; W5B_labB.py; W5B_labE.py,"Gap is 0.667pp, which the entry rounds to 0.66. '2b 12 files / 240 rows' is not in the status (file count only) but is right at 20 rows/file. The directories now hold 13 entries because 'default' was added in the 02:18 re-run that fixed 2e; later status blocks show the gates tightened to equality, as the entry says.",W5B-ledger
F-70,"Two independent web-search reviews of ten project claims agreed only two are new (the dataset-level bootstrap result and the teacher-forced turn-1 design), disagreed on exactly the two that matter most, and forced the correction that MASK is by Ren et al. at CAIS + Scale AI, not Cadenza Labs.","2 of 10 novel; 1/384 and 6/4,032; regex 0.91 vs probe 0.87; arXiv 2601.10387, 2511.17408, 2605.27958, 2609.02893, 2503.03750, 2511.16035",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:2474,docs/NOVELTY_ASSESSMENT.md (git 8d50caf); papers/The MASK Benchmark Disentangling.pdf; papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,NOVELTY_ASSESSMENT sections 1-3 and 6; first page of each PDF,"the assessment names exactly claims 5 (empirical) and 8 as agreed-novel; the demoted list (7,6,10,1,9) and the claim 3/4 disagreement with the same prior art match the ledger table",yes,"MASK first page: 'Richard Ren*1, Arunim Agarwal*1, Mantas Mazeika*1, Cristina Menghini*2 ... 1Center for AI Safety 2Scale AI'; Liars' Bench first page: 'Kieron Kretschmar* Cadenza Labs; Walter Laurito*; Sharan Maiya; Samuel Marks Anthropic'",pypdf first-page extraction of both PDFs; git --diff-filter=A for when the three 'missing' papers arrived,git only; docs/NOVELTY_ASSESSMENT.md unchanged since 8d50caf,none of the literature verdicts inside the entry were tested by this audit; the entry says so itself,PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH that it records the assessment faithfully and that the MASK correction is right; the embedded literature judgements are NOT TESTED,MEDIUM-HIGH - it drives what the thesis leads with,audit/scripts/claims/F-70.py,"STALE CAVEAT: caveat (3) says 2609.02893, 2605.27958 and 2511.17408 are 'not in papers/'. All three were added on 2026-09-22 in commit 4d0d046, the day after the entry (still no notes files, so 'not read directly' may hold). DOC_FIXES candidate. The 0.91/0.87 pair belongs to F-01/F-03 and is checked elsewhere.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] VERDICT CORRECTED BY PHASE 4 (HOLDS -> PARTLY HOLDS). '1 of 384' is in this claim's own stated_numbers and was routed away as 'checked elsewhere' rather than checked. Phase 4 found it matches NO significance family anywhere (git paper16 root 192 tests; the four git bank stores 96 each; lab copies 4,032-6,300) - consistent with Phase 1's finding that F-04's 384-test run was overwritten the same evening. '6 of 4,032' does reproduce exactly in the git copy of run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd/significance.json. The stale caveat (3) flagged below is a second sentence-level defect under a clean verdict.",W5B-ledger
F-82,"Recomputing the cap depth profile on the unfiltered bank instead of the judge-filtered one changes nothing: 21/21 layers positive in both, L40 margin +0.1538 vs +0.1542, identical confidence interval and argmax band.","21/21 both; longest run 21; L40 +0.1542 vs +0.1538; CI [+0.0913,+0.2113] vs [+0.0907,+0.2118]; P(<=0) 0.0000; argmax band [L28,L60]; argmax median L36 vs L32; 3.1% of resamples on L40",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3256,lab run-crossgen/kd11/banks/cap_s23/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json (21) and .../cap_all/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json (21),"results[feature=pc:capitulation@2 | datapca@2, probe=paper].auroc, sycophancy_mt column, mean over the 10 other sources","no stored file - the entry's script is print-only, so there is no Level-1 artefact",n/a (print-only),"cap_s23: 21/21, run 21, L40 +0.1542, CI [+0.0913,+0.2113], P 0.0000, argmax median L36, band [L28,L60], 3.9% on L40. cap_all: 21/21, run 21, L40 +0.1538, CI [+0.0907,+0.2118], P 0.0000, argmax median L32, band [L28,L60], 3.1% on L40","re-implementation of cap/scripts/cap_layer_profile.py with the same statistic, same np.random.default_rng(42) and B=10,000, run read-only on the lab","lab only; matrices are 09-21 originals, not in the 09-22 15:40-16:26 wave (RF-13). logs/cap_layers.status WAS rewritten, so the '47.2 min' gate line is gone, but the numbers do not depend on it. No BH q-value quoted.","margin is over datapca@2, not raw (feature-raw is +0.139 at L32, +0.112 at L40); n_src=10, so the whole interval rests on ten datasets; target is the single sycophancy_mt column (F-67 locality caveat)",HOLDS,HIGH - deterministic recomputation with the script's own seed,MEDIUM-HIGH - the broadest of the four judge-filter controls,audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labC.py,"Every published figure reproduces to the last digit, including the 0.0004 difference at L40 and the argmax medians L36/L32. The filtered bank lands on L40 in 3.9% of resamples (the entry quotes 3.1%, which is the unfiltered bank's).",W5B-ledger
F-91,"Layer 40 is not the best layer: read off matrices already on disk, the off-diagonal transfer mean peaks at L32 for both raw and persona features by about 0.02, and a second method (the pooled mean-of-directions sweep) agrees on 32-36 - but no ordering reverses and L32 was never pre-registered.","cap_s23 raw L32 0.6818 vs L40 0.6623 (+0.0195); cap_s23 pc:capitulation@2 L32 0.7798 vs 0.7606 (+0.0192); kd_s23 axes L44 0.6435 vs 0.6304 (+0.0131); mean-of-directions 0.8945 (L32), 0.8942 (L36), 0.8828 (L40)",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3873,"lab run-crossgen/kd11/banks/{cap_s23,kd_s23}/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json; run-premise/falsify/falsify_L*_s*.json (63)","results[feature,probe=paper].auroc nan-mean over all off-diagonal cells of the 11x11 grid; falsify key 'real'","peak table reproduces exactly: 0.6818/0.6623/+0.0195, 0.7798/0.7606/+0.0192, 0.6435/0.6304/+0.0131",yes for the peak table; NO for the falsify triple (seeds mixed),"falsify 'real': L32 s42 0.89454, s7 0.88256, s13 0.87995; L36 s42 0.89191, s7 0.89415, s13 0.88874; L40 s42 0.88283, s7 0.89572, s13 0.88299. Seed-mean: L36 0.8916 > L40 0.8872 > L32 0.8857",recompute the off-diagonal means from the stored matrices; read the 'real' key of every falsify file at every stored layer and seed; re-run the layer-coverage census,lab only; matrices are 09-20/09-21 originals. 62 of 63 falsify files are byte-identical to the 20:56 census; falsify_L40_s13.json was rewritten by the audit's own interrupted-call incident and is not one of the quoted values.,"the second method's peak is seed-dependent: L32 at seed 42, L40 at seed 7, L36 at seed 13; the crossgen table is single-seed (the entry's own caveat 1); the peak is not bootstrapped (caveat 3)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - both recomputations are deterministic reads,"MEDIUM-HIGH - the layer-choice honesty paragraph, draft topic 2",audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labC.py,"SEEDS MIXED: the quoted L36 0.8942 is seed 7 while L32 0.8945 and L40 0.8828 are seed 42. Averaged over the three stored seeds L40 (0.8872) beats L32 (0.8857), so 'two independent methods put the optimum at 32-36' does not survive its own second method. The crossgen peak table and the no-reversal check (+0.098 at L32 vs +0.099 at L40) do hold. Coverage audit reproduces as a snapshot: cap_ctrl is now 21 layers and scale_70b 21, both extended afterwards.",W5B-ledger
F-104,Four script fixes existed only in the repo and never reached the lab PC where the chains run - including the sarcasm-pilot verdict gate and a live Cap-Controls fix - and a SHA-256 audit of 160 local vs 151 remote scripts found all of them; all four were then deployed and hash-matched.,"160 local / 151 remote; 3 divergent (+369 B, +45 B, +11,382 B); 17 local-only; 8 remote-only; run_sarc_pilot.ps1 remote 5,688 B vs repo 6,755 B; stripped=0.947",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4870,"lab logs/sarc_pilot.status.2026-09-21-buggy-verdict and .pre-e2e-2026-09-22 and logs/cap_controls.status; audit/phase1/labpc/labpc_census_eol.tsv; git blobs; audit/fix/originals_{lab,repo}",status gate lines; md5_lf of every .py/.ps1 in the four script dirs; git cat-file -s over the history of the four files,"both quoted status blocks present verbatim (the entry drops ', markers' from the 3b line); git blob sizes confirm 5,688 B (aea9f53) and 6,755 B (b34ff2e) and run_cap_controls.ps1 7,993 -> 8,362 B = +369 B",yes,"at the 2026-09-22 20:56 census: 153 scripts present on both machines, ALL md5_lf-identical to the repo, 0 remote-only, 17 local-only (170 local in total). For the 8 RF-14 guard scripts the audit's pre-patch lab copies are byte-identical to its pre-patch repo copies.",rebuild both script sets from the Phase-1 census and the git HEAD blobs and diff them; cross-check against audit/fix/originals_lab vs originals_repo; print the status files read-only,"lab logs (not on Drive, RF-10) + git blobs + the Phase-1 census. The 02:32/03:03 lab mtimes are the deployment itself, not the 15:40-16:26 boot wave.",the audit's own RF-14 finding - the same guard bug live on BOTH machines - independently confirms the two trees were in sync rather than contradicting the claim,HOLDS,"HIGH - status files, census md5s and git blob sizes all agree",MEDIUM - process finding; the evidence for 'a fix is not verified until exercised where it runs',audit/scripts/claims/F-104.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5B_labB.py,"Two pieces unverifiable: (1) the 160/151 counts are a 09-21 20:30 snapshot - the earliest census gives 170/153; (2) the cap_controls.status lines quoted (NaN gate failure, '$src/$SRC re-run' PASS) are GONE, truncated by the RF-14 guard bug at 09-22 16:05/16:10. STALE CAVEAT: caveat (2) says the 8 remote-only registration scripts are 'still uncommitted' - six register_*.ps1 entered git in 4d0d046, the very commit carrying F-104, and none remained lab-only by the census.",W5B-ledger
