F-48,"The 8B evaluation arm finished in 62 minutes with zero OOMs, producing five dataset stores, and those five ARE Mahadik & Skapars' Table 1 deception benchmark (AILiar, Roleplaying, ConvGame, InstrDec, HarmPressureChoice).","exit 0 19:36:28; 62 min; chunks/rows 100/800, 267/2134, 47/371, 34/270, 34/267; '11 dataset dirs written, expect 5'",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1406,"lab logs/scale_coords.status; run-scale/8b/coords/*; papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf (Table 1, p.4, and all figures)",status lines; chunk counts and rows.jsonl line counts; pdftotext of Table 1; mention counts of HarmPressureChoice vs Mask,"status '19:36:28 8b: coords exit 0 (11 dataset dirs written, expect 5)'; 18:34:09 -> 19:36:28 = 62 min; ai_liar 34/270, convincing-game 34/267, roleplaying 47/371, instructed-deception 100/800 - all exact; harm-pressure-choice now 100/800 (re-extracted 20:00:18) consistent with 'being redone'",yes,"no OOM line in the log after 18:03:50, i.e. zero OOMs in the 18:34:09-19:36:28 run - VERIFIED. PDF: Table 1 does list HarmPressureChoice as the 5th deception dataset, but 'HarmPressureChoice' occurs exactly twice in the whole paper (both inside Table 1 and its caption) and in no figure; every figure and result matrix uses Mask (33 hits).",chunk/row recount on the lab; OOM census by hour; pdftotext -layout of pages 4-5 and a whole-PDF grep,lab-only store; RF-13 wave only appended a SKIP on 2026-09-22 16:20,"the 'six empty directories' hold an items.pt and 0 chunks; alpaca and mask got rows later (22:01, 23:15), so at 19:36 there were 5 filled + 6 unfilled dirs = 11, as the status says",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - chunk counts, log timestamps and the PDF text are all primary",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W5C_labA.py,"F-48 is right about Table 1 but wrong that these are the paper's benchmark: the paper evaluates Mask, not HarmPressureChoice, in every figure. F-60 records exactly this correction against F-58 but F-48 was never back-annotated. SEP