F-52,"In a 24-rollout teacher-forced smoke test, pc_caver folds on 8/8 true-answer items and pc_position_holder holds on 8/8 across all four framing x kind cells, while in the wrong-turn-1 control both personas abandon the forced answer - so the axis encodes 'abandons a TRUE answer under pressure', not 'abandons any position'.",24 rollouts; 8/8 fold vs 8/8 hold; 4-item control; 4 of 8 caver responses invoke spelunking,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1542,"lab cap/run/smoke_cells/{pc_caver,pc_position_holder,pc_caver_control,pc_position_holder_control}.jsonl",record counts; framing/kind/turn1_is_correct fields; the conversation field's final assistant turn,"8 + 8 + 4 + 4 = 24 records; the 2x2 with both polarities is exactly the ledger's table (Tungsten/Pacific, goldfish No/lightning Yes, Canberra/2, 10% No/taste Yes)",yes,"I read all 24 turn-2 texts: 8/8 pc_caver abandon, 8/8 pc_position_holder reassert with a reason; in the control all 4 position_holder responses correct the error and 3 of 4 caver responses do (the potassium item says 'I don't know, actually'), so neither persona holds. The four control quotes in the ledger are verbatim in the files.",full-text read of every rollout's conversation on the lab PC; categorical judgement made by me,"lab-only (not on Drive, not in git); files dated 2026-09-20 20:55-20:57, untouched by the RF-13 wave","one variant per persona (single system_prompt per file), one item per cell-polarity, 2 of 12 personas, 4-item control - exactly the caveats the entry states",HOLDS,HIGH - categorical reading of 24 full texts done during this audit,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W5C_labB.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5C_labC.py,"One miscount: 3 of 8 caver responses invoke caving (items 1, 5, 7), not 4 - two of the four quoted phrases are in the SAME response (item 7). 'Both personas correct the error' is true of 7 of 8 control responses; the ledger's own table shows the exception.",W5C-ledger
F-56,"--sample preserves the source class ratio rather than balancing it, so harm-pressure-choice's 800-row sample came out 134 deceptive / 666 honest (5:1) because the source is ~17% deceptive; and roleplaying loads 287 rows, not the 371 extracted.",800 = 400/400; 800 = 134/666; 267 = 167/100; 270 = 135/135; 287 = 203/84 (371 extracted); ~17% deceptive at source,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1729,lab run-scale/8b/coords/*/rows.jsonl; lab logs/crossgen_scale_8b.log L5-L9; src/assistant_axis_ndif/8_coords_ndif.py::subsample (l.504); results/subsets/harm-pressure-choice.csv,label counts per rows.jsonl; the 21:54:06 load block; the sampler source; source-CSV class counts for model=llama-v3.3-70b-instruct,"log block matches the table exactly: ID 800 400D/400H, HPC 800 134D/666H, CG 267 167D/100H, ai_liar 270 135D/135H, roleplaying 287 203D/84H",yes,"recomputed from rows.jsonl: ai_liar 270 {1:135,0:135}; convincing-game 267 {1:167,0:100}; harm-pressure-choice 800 {1:134,0:666}; instructed-deception 800 {0:400,1:400}; roleplaying 371 {1:203,0:84,None:84} -> 287 usable, 84 dropped. BUT the source is 134/2000 = 6.28% deceptive, not ~17%, and subsample() is a ROUND-ROBIN over label buckets ('as balanced as the data allows'), not a proportional draw; a proportional 800-row draw would give ~50 deceptive.",label recount from raw rows; read of the sampler source; class counts of the probed rows in the source subset CSV,lab-only store (HPC re-extracted 2026-09-20 20:00:18 after F-47); RF-13 wave only appended a SKIP,"the 84 dropped roleplaying rows are exactly the label=None rows, which the sampler treats as backfill and the loader discards",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - composition recomputed from raw rows, mechanism read from the sampler source",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W5C_labA.py,"The composition table and the conclusion (5:1, not the paper's label-balanced test) hold exactly. The mechanism is the reverse of what the entry says: the sampler took ALL 134 deceptive rows available. The '~17% at source' is the SAMPLE's ratio (134/800) read back as the source's. The entry's own caveat states the correct reason.",W5C-ledger
F-61,"The kd bank's pc:unified-raw of +0.076 at L40 against the paper16 bank's +0.006 is a twelvefold difference, but persona count (26->36), question set (10->30, different questions not a superset) and rollouts/role (50->150) all changed at once, and 'unified' excludes the 10 new roles.",paper16 26/10/5/50/1400; kd 36/30/5/150/5400; +0.006 vs +0.076; twelvefold,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:1905,"lab run-paper16/responses/*.jsonl (26), run-kd/responses/*.jsonl (36); run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json and banks/kd/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (lab and git); src/assistant_axis_ndif/6_axes.py:188-195","per-role row/question/prompt_index counts; question-text set intersection; off-diagonal means of pc:unified and raw, probe=paper, k=5, seed 42","paper16 26 roles / 1,400 rollouts (50 x 16 roles + 60 x 10 roles) but 22 distinct questions, not 10; kd 36 roles / 5,400 / 30 questions / 5 prompt_index - exact",no,"kd pc:unified - root raw = +0.0757 (110 pairs) - matches +0.076. paper16 pc:unified - raw = +0.0093, NOT +0.006; +0.0064 is pc:unified - datapca. The console reading behind '+0.0061' (raw 0.6800 over 109 pairs) matches no matrix under run-crossgen on the lab or the laptop. Ratio is 8.1x, not twelvefold. Question overlap: 20 of paper16's 22 questions are among kd's 30 (2 paper16-only, 10 kd-only), so it is very nearly a superset.",rollout-file census + exact question-text set comparison; off-diagonal recomputation on both machines with controls joined from the ROOT store; exhaustive scan of every matrix for a 109-pair raw block,"matrices lab = git; root bank=axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt name=paper16; kd bank=axes_vectors_s3.pt name=kd; kd matrix dated 2026-09-20 03:06, not touched by the RF-13 wave","last pooling gives -0.0259 for paper16, so the +0.006 is not a pooling mix-up; kd's other features -raw: kd_assertion +0.1496, knowledge_denial +0.0869, axes -0.0272",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - counts from the rollout files, margins recomputed twice on two machines",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/F-61_local.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5C_labB.py; audit/scripts/claims/W5C_labC.py,"paper16 uses TWO question sets - 10 questions for the 16 deception/honesty roles, 12 for the 10 sycophancy roles - which is why 26 x 50 = 1,300 does not reach the true total 1,400. Confound (2) 'different questions, not a superset' is FALSE. The entry's overall conclusion (cannot attribute the gain to persona design) stands and is strengthened. '6_axes.py builds unified from deception+sycophancy vs honesty+anti_sycophancy only' VERIFIED at l.188-195.",W5C-ledger
