F-84,"A Maris-Oostenveld cluster permutation test on the kd matched-slice layer profile (passA, 20 layers, mean pooling, k=5, B=200, matched random control) gives an observed largest cluster mass of 0.9155 against a null mean of 0.8871 and 95th percentile of 2.5787, hence p = 0.38 - the band is indistinguishable from label noise.","0.9155; [0.916, 0.059]; 0.8871; 2.5787; p=0.38; B=200; 20 layers",kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:3357,lab run-premise/cluster_perm_kd_matched.json; logs/premise_extras.log L535-547 (09-21) and L992-1004 (09-22); src/assistant_axis_ndif/30c_cluster_perm.py,observed_max_mass; observed_clusters; null_max_mass[200]; p; B; layers; observed_margins,"observed_max_mass=0.9155195683; observed_clusters=[0.9155195683, 0.0588123939]; p=0.38; B=200; layers=[0,4,...,76] (20)",yes,"recomputed from the stored null: mean 0.887128, np.percentile(null,95)=2.5787, 76 of 200 draws >= observed -> p = 0.3800 (plain) / 0.3831 (+1). Re-derived the statistic from observed_margins alone: 7 of 20 layers positive (idx 7-12 and 19); the contiguous run 7-12 sums to 0.91552 = observed_max_mass exactly; idx 19 = 0.05881 = the second cluster.","recomputation of the p-value, null mean and percentile from the stored null; independent re-derivation of the cluster statistic from the per-layer margins","JSON regenerated 2026-09-22 16:07:02 in the RF-13 boot wave AND the original is gone - BUT logs/premise_extras.log retains the 2026-09-21 16:09 run, which printed identical values (0.9155, p=0.3800, null mean 0.8871, 95th 2.5787), so a pre-wave comparison does exist and the regeneration reproduced the original exactly. run-premise/ is lab-only (not on Drive, not in git).","control is a matched RANDOM projection at the same k (30c_cluster_perm.py:101-120), as the caveat says, not dataset-PCA; the same permutation is applied at every layer (l.134); no BH q-value is quoted so the RF-13 test-family problem does not apply",HOLDS,HIGH - p-value recomputed from the stored null and the statistic 