M-082,"Using response length alone as the classifier, roleplaying gives AUROC 0.441 with median 31 tokens for the positive class against 38 for the negative, and it is the only dataset in the note's ten-row table whose direction inverts.","0.441; 31 vs 38; ""the only inversion""",C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/response-length-transfers-on-its-own.md:35 (table row; inventory cites line 28 of an earlier revision),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/confounds_L44_last.json (LAB-ONLY, 10,004 B, 2026-09-16 19:36, md5 11bc6e6567a3ce77f398b63572ec5cbc); C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-coords/passB/<dataset>/rows.jsonl","confounds.length_only_auroc[dataset='roleplaying'] -> auroc_from_length, median_pos, median_neg; raw: span_len grouped by label","roleplaying auroc_from_length = 0.4415, median_pos 31, median_neg 38; all ten table rows match the note exactly","yes (0.4415 vs ""0.441"" - truncated rather than rounded; every other row is rounded correctly)","independent recompute from passB/roleplaying/rows.jsonl (287 labelled rows, 203 pos / 84 neg) with a tie-corrected Mann-Whitney AUROC: 0.4415, medians 31 vs 38, means 39.38 vs 43.49 (gap -4.10). Of the ten table rows, roleplaying is the ONLY AUROC below 0.5.","own AUROC implementation over the raw per-row span_len/label data, read-only on the lab PC","lab originals (confounds 2026-09-16 19:36, three minutes before the note, whose timestamp is UTC; passB rows 09-15..09-19), all outside the 09-22 wave; length is layer/pooling/bank invariant by construction, so RF-12/15/16 do not apply",direction counts depend entirely on metric and dataset set: mean gap over 11 passB datasets 9 of 11; mean gap over block9 (10) 8 of 10; AUROC>0.5 over the note's 10 table datasets 9 of 10; AUROC>0.5 over all 11 passB datasets 10 of 11; median_pos>median_neg over the 10 8 of 10,HOLDS,HIGH - two independent derivations agreeing to 4 decimals,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W5D_lab.py (section G),"C