/out/W5E/W5E_local2.txt); regex half from audit/scripts/claims/F-01_F-02_F-16.py,"REACHES THE PAPER. 0.91 is verified (0.9125 on the Llama-3.3-70B rows). 'probes report ~0.87' has no source: the only 0.87 attached to HP-KR anywhere in this project is the project's OWN superseded regex AUROC over all 7,068 rows (0.8699), which F-01 replaced with 0.9125 and which kd/docs/DESIGN.md:71, kd/docs/REPORT.md:18 and the 2026-09-18 session transcript all call 'HP-KR is 87% a lexical task'. If that is the origin, claim 9 compares the regex against ITSELF on two row sets while calling one of them 'probes'. This sentence is the only part of claim 9 the novelty review left as the project's own contribution, and it is repeated verbatim in a PRE-REGISTRATION document (docs/LAYER_PREREGISTRATION.md:93). Needs the owner's call.",W5E-ownerdoc
O-065,"The own100 persona bank is 100 AA roles x AA's 240 shared questions x 5 prompt variants, about 1,200 rollouts per role of which a median 1,163 are kept, judged by Llama-3.1-70B.","100 roles; 240 questions; 5 prompts; ~1,200 per role; kept median 1,163; judge Llama-3.1-70B",docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:377 (unchanged by the audit's edits to this file),"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/responses (100 .jsonl), C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/scores (99 .json), C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/vectors.log, logs/shard{0,1,2}.log; assistant_axis/data/extraction_questions.jsonl (local, 240 lines)",rollout line counts; distinct question_index / prompt_index; count of judge score == 3 per role; 'Role X: N kept' log lines; 'judge=' log field,no intermediate result file - the table is stated against the raw stores,n/a,"100 response files (one is `default`) x exactly 1,200 rows = 120,000; question_index 0-239 (240 distinct), prompt_index 0-4; score-3 per role min 548, MEDIAN 1163, max 1200, mean 1119; logs/vectors.log independently prints 'kept min=548 median=1163 max=1200'; logs/shard0-2 record model=meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct judge=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct; assistant_axis/data/extraction_questions.jsonl = 240 lines and is 1_generate_ndif.py's default --questions_file with --question_count 240.","own counters over the rollout and score stores + the extraction log's own kept lines; 'kept' definition read from 2_activations_ndif.py:449,459,469 (judge score in --keep_scores, default '3')",lab only. None of these paths is in RF-13's rewrite list. No bank ambiguity (this IS the bank's raw material). No BH q.,"kept counts are uneven - 548 (proofreader) to 1,200 - a 2.2x spread that the median hides; score distribution over the 99 judged roles is {3: 110,780, 2: 4,154, 1: 3,271, 0: 595}.",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - rollouts, scores and the extraction log agree exactly",MEDIUM - a methods data table; no result moves,audit/scripts/claims/W5E_lab3.py (output audit/phase2/out/W5E/W5E_lab3.txt); W5E_lab.py O-065 block,"Every number is exact, including the median 1,163 which reproduces twice independently. ONE error: '100 AA roles' counts `default`, the no-persona anchor, as a role - there are 99 AA roles + default. The same table's paper16 row writes '25 paper personas + default', so the inconsistency is inside one table. A reader also meets a third count, the 45 labelled roles in own100_role_groups_strict.json, with no note reconciling them. Also confirms the thesis's 'AA's 240 shared questions' really is the Assistant-Axis repo's extraction_questions.jsonl.",W5E-ownerdoc
O-075,"At L20 with mean pooling and the mms probe, erasing the paper16 assistant direction costs 0.006 transfer AUROC (0.652 -> 0.646), random erasures cost ~0, the erased probe's dataset-level 95% CI is [0.513, 0.796], and the cost is not significant across datasets (BH q 0.52).","0.652; 0.646; 0.006; ~0.000; [0.513, 0.796]; q 0.52",docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:656 (inventory :655),"run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (git working tree; lab copy md5-identical 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e, mtime 2026-09-17)","q4_table[layer=20,pooling='mean',probe='mms']; comparisons[name='cost of erasing Assistant Axis, L20 mean mms']","raw 0.6523819821789706; erase_assistant 0.646230375193732; cost_assistant 0.0061516069852385336; cost_random 5 values mean +5.23e-05; erased_dataset_ci95 [0.5127429605373054, 0.7956263084897787]; dataset_q_bh 0.5151058823529412 (dataset_p 0.3284, row_p 0.001)","YES - all six cells, and all five sibling rows of the same table (q 0.54, 0.003, 0.16, 0.003, 0.04)",not recomputed from activations (needs the run-coords passB/passC tensor store); internal consistency checked instead,own reader over the stored bootstrap file; BH family size counted (26 tests: Q3 14 + Q4 12),"lab and laptop copies md5-identical (2f616b3e...), mtime 2026-09-17, BEFORE the 09-22 15:40-16:26 wave and not in its rewrite set. THE DOC DOES NOT SAY WHICH BH FAMILY: it is this file's own 26 comparisons, not the 4,788-test crossgen family RF-13 shifted. erase_test.json (the 4-dataset pilot, not this row's source) records bank axes_vectors_s3.pt = the OLD paper16 axes (RF-15); RF-15's measurement bounds any old-vs-fp32 effect at ~1% of norm, well under the 0.006 cost.","the table is itself the sweep: cost 0.005-0.018 across 3 layer/pooling settings x 2 probes, always positive, always small against a 0.28-wide dataset CI. Only FIVE random erasures back the '~0.000'.",HOLDS,HIGH for Level 1 (6/6 cells plus 5 sibling rows exact); MEDIUM overall (no recompute from activations),MEDIUM - the non-significant row of Q4,audit/scripts/claims/W5E_local.py (output audit/phase2/out/W5E/W5E_local.txt),"The one Level-2 gap in this batch: re-fitting the erased probes needs the ~30 GB passB/passC activation store (CPU-feasible, no model calls).",W5E-ownerdoc
O-082,"Dataset identity is 99.3% decodable from the L40 mean-pooled eval activations while the deception label is decodable at only +0.032 over its majority baseline, so a high within-construct transfer mean is expected whether transfer clusters by construct or by provenance.",99.3%; +0.032 (and 7.12 as the cross-reference),"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:702-703, cross-referencing 7.12 (:879-891)","run-coords/validate_L40.json (lab md5 d17705873619231f6be457c450f58269 = laptop, mtime 2026-09-16 18:45:12); C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/validate.log (UTF-16)",dataset_acc; label_acc; the log's 'label : 0.646 (majority baseline 0.614) lift +0.032' and 'dataset : 0.993 (majority baseline 0.110) lift +0.883 over 10 datasets',dataset_acc = 0.9933774834437085; label_acc = 0.6462472406181016; lift +0.032 is LOG-ONLY (17_validate.py:126-131 never writes it),"YES - 99.3% in the JSON, +0.032 in the run's own log, mutually consistent (0.6462 - 0.614)","not recomputed (needs the passB activation store); 7.12's PC label AUROCs 0.704/0.503/0.507 confirmed to be max(a,1-a) of the stored 0.2959/0.4973/0.4927",own reader over the result JSON + decoded run log; 'lift' definition read from 17_validate.py:126-131,"lab and laptop copies md5-identical, mtime 2026-09-16, not in the 09-22 rewrite set. No bank ambiguity (bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt is the script default, used only for the axis-vs-PC cosines). No BH q.","one layer (L40), one pooling, one subsample seed (default_rng(0)), 3-fold CV; no validate_L20/L44 exists, so the decodability gap is not depth-checked.",HOLDS,HIGH for both numbers (result file + producing run's log); MEDIUM that the probe fit itself is right,"MEDIUM-HIGH - the load-bearing step of the Q5 verdict, reused at line 1101","audit/scripts/claims/W5E_local.py and W5E_lab2.py (outputs W5E_local.txt, W5E_lab2.txt)","Two precision points for DOC_FIXES. (1) 7.12 says '400 rows per dataset'; 400 is the --cap, and the realised run was 3,624 rows over 10 datasets (avg 362), with the dataset accuracy computed over the 10 sets with >=100 rows. (2) 7.5 borrows a 10-dataset pooled measurement into a 9/11-dataset pair-matrix argument without saying so; the inference survives, the row sets differ. Bonus cross-check from the same log: cos(deception, assistant) = -0.371, matching the -0.37 contamination figure quoted elsewhere.",W5E-ownerdoc
O-086,"Trained cross-dataset transfer with the pc:deception feature, mms probe, mean pooling reads 0.524 at L20, 0.517 at L22 and 0.661 at L40, and its own best layer is L40 at 0.661.",0.524; 0.517; 0.661; L40 0.661,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:725 (inventory :724),"run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, lab = laptop) and run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_mms.json (md5 3506b84d16e7b686c094de79c468f708, lab = laptop)","rows[source='trained transfer, full corpus', method='pc:deception / mms / mean'].at{20,22,40}, .best_layer, .best; sweep[layer].['pc:deception']","0.5237417568658953 / 0.5174643904798112 / 0.6607664342269597; best_layer 40, best 0.6607664342269597","YES, all four to 3 dp","layer_sweep_passB_mms.json gives the identical three values; argmax over its full 21-layer sweep = L40, 0.6607664342269597",own reader; argmax recomputed over all 21 stored layers rather than taken from the compiled row,"lab and laptop md5-identical for both files; mtimes 2026-09-16/17, not in the 09-22 rewrite set. Bank read from INSIDE the sweep file: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5 (the re-extracted fp32 axes, RF-15's good side). No BH q.","one seed, one probe, one pooling per row - the table's purpose is the within-row layer comparison, which is what was checked. pc:deception loses to raw (0.652/0.646/0.669) at all three layers, as the verdict text says.",HOLDS,"HIGH - Level 1 and Level 2 exact, argmax independently recomputed",MEDIUM - one row of the layer-choice table,audit/scripts/claims/W5E_local.py (output audit/phase2/out/W5E/W5E_local.txt),"The compilation step is faithful. Caveat for the table as a whole, not this row: rows come from different protocols and corpora (trained off-diagonal transfer here, pooled-corpus zero-shot two rows down, LODO Pass C at the bottom) and the thesis names the provenance only in aggregate ('compiled from every result file'); per-row provenance is in q6_layers.json's source/file fields. Cross-row comparisons are not like-for-like.",W5E-ownerdoc
O-088,"The zero-shot projection onto PC1 of the paper16 DECEPTION axis, mean pooling, reads 0.673 at L20, 0.699 at L22 and 0.877 at L40, and its own best layer is L40 at 0.877.",0.673; 0.699; 0.877; L40 0.877,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:727 (inventory :726),"run-coords/q6_layers.json and run-coords/dotproducts_mean.json (md5 a12563f5c24afc0a6b001ed26236c6d9, lab = laptop, mtime 2026-09-16 11:09)","rows[source='zero-shot, full corpus', method='PC1 / mean']; dotproducts_mean.json matched[layer].pc1",0.672741905827186 / 0.6985357918446898 / 0.8768949185173067; best_layer 40,"YES, all four to 3 dp","dotproducts_mean.json gives the identical values; argmax pc1 over all 21 layers = L40 0.8768949185173067 (argmax contrast = L40 0.8630105619589489, matching the row above at 0.608/0.630/0.863)","own reader; axis identity settled from the producing code, 12_dotproduct_layers.py:79 takes bank['pca']['deception']['components'][L,0]","lab and laptop md5-identical; mtime 2026-09-16, not in the 09-22 rewrite set. Bank = run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (script default, fp32 re-extraction). RF-15: old-vs-fp32 PCA sign pinning differs at a few layers but NOT at L20/L40/L44. No BH q.","mean pooling only, one seed. Reconciles with 8.2's 0.881 for the 'pooled corpus L40 mean (incl. alpaca)' - this file EXCLUDES single-class sets, hence 0.877 vs 0.881 on different row sets, which neither section says. 8.2 also records that zero-shot deception-axis readings sit inside the random-direction null in several tests.",HOLDS,"HIGH - Level 1 and Level 2 exact; the axis label verified against the producing code, not the column name","MEDIUM - a layer-choice row, but the one behind 'moving to L40 is worth ~+0.113 for persona methods'",audit/scripts/claims/W5E_local.py (output audit/phase2/out/W5E/W5E_local.txt),"Checked specifically against DF-31: here the 'deception PC1' label is CORRECT - the script names the deception axis explicitly, so this is not another bare-PC1 mis-attribution. Caveat: this row is a POOLED-CORPUS zero-shot AUROC while the trained rows above it are means over 90-110 off-diagonal transfer cells; within-row layer comparison is fine, across-row is not.",W5E-ownerdoc
O-057,"The paper's persona set largely removes the Assistant-Axis contamination of the deception axis: cos(deception contrast, assistant direction) at layer 40 falls from -0.66 (own100) to -0.37 (paper16) against each bank's own assistant direction, and to -0.23 against the published Assistant Axis.",-0.66; -0.37; -0.23 (L40); table at L20/22/40/60,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:46 (summary) and :522-541 (7.1 table + verdict),"run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3.pt; run-paper16/vectors_s3/*.pt; run-hf275/vectors_100; run-hf275/vectors_275; run-hf275/published_assistant_axis.pt. own100 = C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt (LAB ONLY, not reachable this session)",axes['deception'][L] vs axes['assistant'][L]; published axis tensor [L],paper16_s3 -0.3641/-0.3376/-0.3705/-0.3742 (L20/22/40/60); paper16 vs published -0.1677/-0.1407/-0.2263/-0.1800; hf275 -0.6856/-0.6621/-0.6097/-0.5161; own100 NOT MEASURED,YES for all 12 paper16 and hf275 cells (tol 5e-4). own100 row unchecked.,"Rebuilt the axes from the 26 per-persona vectors with 6_axes.py's construction: cos(dec,asst) L40 = -0.370490, identical to the stored bank. cos^2 at L40 = 0.1373 (doc: ~14%) and 0.0512 (doc: ~5%).",full axis rebuild from per-persona .pt files (not a read of a stored cosine); all four axes reconstructed and compared,"laptop/git copies. paper16 = OLD axes_vectors_s3.pt (RF-15 'old'); O-064 measures old-vs-fp32 at <=0.00065, so RF-15 cannot move these cells. run-coords not in the RF-13 rewrite set. No BH q.",holds at all four stored layers; paper16 cleaner than hf275 by 0.18-0.32 everywhere; not layer-specific,PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for the paper16 halves (rebuilt from raw vectors, exact); MEDIUM overall - the -0.66 own100 cell is DEFERRED (lab unreachable)",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_geom.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_geom.txt),"FINDING: the hf275 column is measured against the PUBLISHED Assistant Axis, not against 'each bank's own assistant direction' as 2.8 and 7.1's verdict say. Against the 100-role bank's own direction it reads -0.669/-0.651/-0.577/-0.479. The published axis has cos 0.99995 with an assistant direction built over all 275 roles, so the substantive conclusion is untouched (<=0.04), but the wording is wrong. Would need C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt to close the own100 cell.",W6A-thesis1
O-058,"Erasing the paper16 assistant direction from the activations costs only 0.005-0.018 mean off-diagonal transfer AUROC across six layer/pooling/probe settings, so deception signal survives beyond assistant-ness.",0.005; 0.018,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:49 (summary), backed by :658-665","run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (md5 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e, 24187 B)","q4_table[*].cost_assistant; comparisons[name='cost of erasing Assistant Axis, ...']",costs 0.0062 / 0.0054 / 0.0177 / 0.0141 / 0.0081 / 0.0053 -> range 0.0053..0.0177,"YES (rounds to exactly 0.005 and 0.018, tol 5e-4); all 6 rows positive","cost_assistant = raw - erase_assistant in all 6 rows; the parallel 'vs random erasures' comparisons give the same diffs to <=4e-4, confirming the ~0.000 random baseline. Cost as a share of raw: 0.80%-2.64%.","own reader over the bootstrap file; internal-consistency checks. NOT re-fit from activations (needs the ~30 GB Pass B store, lab/Drive only).",mtime 2026-09-17; NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab copy md5-identical (per claim O-075). Claim quotes no q. Bank = paper16; RF-15 old-vs-fp32 bounded at 0.2% of norm.,"the table IS the sweep: 3 layer/pooling settings x 2 probes, all positive. Only FIVE random erasure directions back the '~0.000'.",HOLDS,HIGH for Level 1 (6/6 exact); MEDIUM overall (no recompute from activations),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"Two qualifications the 1.2 one-liner drops: (1) 3 of the 6 costs ARE BH-significant across datasets (q 0.0035, 0.0035, 0.0399), so 'only' is about size, not significance; (2) 7.4's verdict says the erasure costs '1-3%' of transfer AUROC, measured 0.80-2.64%, two rows below 1%. The erased direction is bank-local (cos 0.30-0.37 with the published axis), so 'the Assistant Axis' has not been erased - the doc flags this.",W6A-thesis1
O-059,"Moving from layer 20/22 to layer 40 gains a median +0.025 AUROC for raw probes (10 methods) and +0.113 for persona methods (13 methods); layers 20 and 22 are equivalent (median gap 0.012, max 0.037 over 17 methods).","+0.025; +0.113; (also 0.012, 0.037, +0.234)","docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:51 (summary), backed by :717-747",run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6); run-coords/significance.json (md5 b52ff6166e2849258cf0e34a8715eecf),rows[*].gap_40_minus_best_of_20_22 and rows[*].gap_20_22; comparisons[kind='equiv'],"raw n=10 median +0.0251 (range -0.0157..+0.0681); persona n=13 median +0.1135 (range -0.0283..+0.2335); 20-vs-22 n=17 median |gap| 0.0115, max 0.0370; ratio 4.5x",YES on all five quantities; my raw/persona split reproduces the doc's own 10/13 counts,medians re-derived from the 23 per-row gaps rather than read; 4 rows cross-checked against their source sweeps (layer_sweep_passB_mms/last.json),own classifier over method names + recomputed medians; sanity check against source sweeps,"run-coords, mtime 2026-09-16/17, md5 lab=laptop (per O-086/O-088), NOT in the RF-13 rewrite set. Source sweeps record bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt. No BH q quoted by this claim. Seed 42 only.",the direction is the same in every sub-population; dropping the 5 zero-shot persona rows leaves median +0.113 unchanged,HOLDS,HIGH - four independent quantities matched and the 10/13 split reconstructed independently,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"Caveat: '20 vs 22 is immaterial' is a median of |gaps|, not a test. All four actual dataset-bootstrap equivalence tests return equivalent_within_margin=False at the pre-registered +/-0.02 margin; they are equivalent only under the ROW bootstrap, and 7.6 widens the margin to +/-0.04 to call them equivalent. Also the two medians pool different protocols (raw group = 4 P1 + 6 Pass C LODO; persona group = 8 P1 + 5 zero-shot).",W6A-thesis1
O-060,Q8: zero-shot per-token top-10% scoring beats mean pooling at every Pass C layer; trained pooled probes beat per-token probes at every layer; the trained advantage is significant across datasets only at layers 20 and 28.,"10%; (also +0.0023..+0.1027, gaps 0.027-0.060, q<=0.024, folds 8-9/9)","docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:53 (summary), backed by :764-825",run-coords/pertoken_q8.json (md5 ee4f78d17623e37098e18ac2933b96fa); run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json (md5 907b05ce36f8accf1a21bae09e305ce2); run-coords/significance.json,"aggregations[*].{mean,top10pct}; results[*].{probe,aggregation,auroc_mean}; comparisons[question='Q8']","zero-shot: top10pct-mean = +0.1027/+0.0642/+0.0529/+0.0046/+0.0144/+0.0023 at L20/22/28/40/44/48, positive 6/6. trained: best pooled - best token = +0.0604/+0.0497/+0.0485/+0.0300/+0.0276/+0.0445, positive 6/6 (doc says 0.027-0.060). significance: BH-significant at L20 (q 0.00127, 0.00095) and L28 (q 0.02375, 0.00095); not at L40/L44.",YES on all three parts,"stronger form also true: pool_mean_mms beats EVERY one of the 8-12 token-probe rows at every layer, worst-case gap +0.0276",re-derived 'best pooled' and 'best token' from the 106 raw results records instead of reading the summary block,"run-coords, mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in the RF-13 rewrite set; q's come from this file's own 23-test family, not the crossgen family RF-13 enlarged. Bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt.","6 Pass C layers, 9 LODO folds, one seed; self-checks in the file (0 of 12,000 row-layers outside tolerance; shuffled-label token probe 0.476-0.553)",HOLDS,HIGH - every quoted number matched and the 'every layer' claim strengthened by checking all token-probe rows,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"Two scope limits the 1.2 one-liner hides: (1) only 4 of the 6 layers were ever entered into a significance test (22 and 48 never were), so 'significant at 20 and 28 only' is 'only among 20/28/40/44'; (2) the significance tests compare pooled-mean-mms against tok_lr ONLY, but the best token probe at L20/22/28 is tok_mms, which was never tested. 7.8's own wording is precise; the summary line is looser.",W6A-thesis1
O-061,"Trained raw probes detect sleeper-agent lies at ~0.96 AUROC including across trigger types, but what they detect is answer falsity, not deception; the zero-shot persona deception axis on the sleeper corpora does not beat a random-direction null.",0.96 (cross-trigger 0.964),"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:56 (summary), backed by :850-881",run-coords/q11_sleeper_L44_last.json (md5 dd99eba1294d3e733bee88884f95905a); run-coords/zeroshot_nulls.json (md5 0c241a653587a570ed37a9bffe578dcd),"tests.cross_trigger['raw|*']; tests.within_organism; tests.token_stratified; sleeper_L44_last[*].deception_axis.{auroc,p_vs_random,beats_random_p95}","cross-trigger raw 0.9653/0.9630/0.9634 (mean 0.9639); within-organism raw 0.9589/0.9633/0.9653 (mean 0.9625); answer token alone 0.6165/0.6275/0.6190; probe within one answer token 0.9461-0.9608; zero-shot axis 0.9128/0.8738/0.8769 with p 0.0909/0.1828/0.1968 and beats_random_p95 FALSE on all three (gender-secret 0.3512, p 0.3457, FALSE)","YES on all eight cells of 7.11 that I checked, to 3 dp",derived means recomputed: axes cross-trigger 0.8490 (doc 0.849); raw corpus->sleeper over 10 sources 0.8534 (doc 0.853); excluding belief sources 0.9315 (doc 0.932); gender-secret transfer 0.2551-0.6599 (doc 0.255-0.660),own reader + recomputed means over the stored per-source cells. NOT recomputed from rollouts (the sleeper activation store is lab/Drive only).,"run-coords, mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in the RF-13 rewrite set. Bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, layer 44, last pooling, mms. No BH q.","layer-specific: 7.11 records raw cross-trigger falling to 0.768 at L20 (q11_sleeper_L20_last.json exists locally). Zero-shot null = 1,000 random directions per corpus.",HOLDS,"HIGH for the numbers; MEDIUM for the interpretation ('falsity') - that rests on two eliminations (cue, answer token), not a positive measurement",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"One of the cleanest negative results in the project and already self-withdrawn by the doc ('the zero-shot axis claim is withdrawn'). The natural control holds too: gender-secret, whose lie is not context-checkable, transfers at chance (mean 0.4720) while its within-organism number is 0.997.",W6A-thesis1
O-062,"'Top-10%' aggregation means the mean of the highest tenth of the per-token scores s_t = <h_t, w>, not the 90th percentile and not the max.",10%,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:141 (2.4),"src/assistant_axis_ndif/14_pertoken.py (aggregate(), lines ~43-60, and the scoring at :105-106); src/assistant_axis_ndif/21_q8_trained_pertoken.py (aggregate(), :87-92)","k = max(1, int(round(0.1*n))); srt = np.sort(scores); top10pct = srt[-k:].mean()","both producing scripts implement top10pct as mean(sorted(scores)[-k:]) with k = max(1, round(0.1*n)); scoring is s = seg @ unit(axis), a dot product","YES - the document's definition is the code's definition, in both scripts","k = 1 for n = 1..14, 2 for n = 15..24, 3 at n = 29 (checked); so for responses of <=14 tokens top10pct collapses to the single maximum token, and for 1-token responses it equals mean/max/last/first",read the producing code and evaluated the k formula over response lengths,"repo code, branch asix working tree; not a result file, so RF-13/15/16 do not apply; 21_q8_trained_pertoken.py is not one of RF-14's seven affected scripts","the zero-shot and trained halves of Q8 use the SAME definition, so their numbers are comparable",HOLDS,HIGH - read from the code that wrote the numbers,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"Undocumented edge case worth a sentence in the methods: the floor at k=1 makes top10pct identical to max on short responses, and identical to mean/max/last/first on harm-pressure-choice's 1-token rows - which is precisely the dataset token probes lose on hardest in 7.8.",W6A-thesis1
O-063,"In protocol P1 the diagonal (train and test on the same dataset) is scored on the held-out 25% split, and the reported off-diagonal mean is the unweighted average of every i != j cell.","25%; (72 pairs for 9 datasets, 90 for 10)",docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:222 (2.9),"src/assistant_axis_ndif/9_persona_probes.py (group_split at :248-259, P1 loop at :316-355); run-coords/p1_L44_last_withsyc.json (md5 45270a3c1fe942bd2820481d2e99c30e); run-coords/splits.json","group_split(meta, 0.75, seed); te = np.arange(len(yt)) when t != s; off = [v for (s,t),v in mat.items() if s != t]","code: diagonal uses the 25% held-out item split, off-diagonal uses the target's full balanced pool, off_diagonal = mean over all i!=j non-NaN cells",YES,"recomputed from the stored matrix in all 8 feature/probe rows: off_diagonal matches to 6 dp over exactly 90 cells (10 labelled datasets) and diagonal over 10 cells - e.g. raw/mms off 0.664576 = 0.664576, diag 0.901282 = 0.901282","own arithmetic over the per-cell matrix, not a read of the summary field","repo code + run-coords files, mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in the RF-13 rewrite set; protocol is feature-agnostic so no bank ambiguity; no BH q","verified on all 8 stored feature x probe rows of one file; the sibling claim '9 datasets give 72 pairs, adding sycophancy_mt gives 90' also checks out (10 labelled datasets x 9 = 90)",HOLDS,HIGH - Level 2 is an exact arithmetic reproduction,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"Two precisions: (1) the 75/25 split is over item_ids, not rows, so 'the held-out 25%' is 25% of ITEMS and the realised row share differs (ai_liar: 54 items x 5 samples -> 70 test items but only 20 balanced on-diagonal rows). 2.9 says '75% of items' one line earlier, so the section is right; the sentence alone is not. (2) after balancing, diagonal pools can be tiny (ai_liar 20 rows, alpaca 0), so diagonal AUROCs are much noisier than off-diagonal ones and no table says so.",W6A-thesis1
O-064,"The bf16 response-mask count bug changed persona-bank cosines by at most 0.001, because a wrong pooling denominator rescales a vector without rotating it.",0.001,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:357 (3.3),"run-paper16/vectors_s3/*.pt (26 buggy vectors, laptop = Drive per RF-12) vs audit/cache/labpc/run-paper16/vectors_s3_fp32/*.pt (26 re-extracted, copied from the lab)","rebuilt axes: cos(deception[L], assistant[L]) for both stores, all 80 layers",no result file states this; it is prose in 3.3 and in the memory note 'bf16 mask reductions' -> Level 1 unavailable,n/a,"max |delta cos(deception, assistant)| over all 80 layers = 0.000654 (at L20 0.00028, L40 0.00021, L44 0.00022). Old-vs-new axis cosines: deception >=0.999986, sycophancy >=0.999988, assistant >=0.999959. Relative norm change 0.04%-0.20%.",rebuilt both banks from their per-persona .pt files with 6_axes.py's construction and compared; sanity: the old rebuild reproduces the stored bank's cos to 6 dp (-0.370490),"directly on RF-12/RF-15: old = laptop run-paper16/vectors_s3 (= Drive, md5-identical), new = lab vectors_s3_fp32 (mtimes 2026-09-15/16, cached during this audit). The lab no longer holds the old copy, so this comparison is only possible on the laptop.","all 80 layers checked, not just 20/40/44; effect is <=0.00065 everywhere",HOLDS,"MEDIUM-HIGH - a clean recompute, but it bounds the count bug TOGETHER WITH the fp32 change rather than isolating it (an upper bound, which is the right direction for a '<=' claim)",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_geom.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_geom.txt),"Independently corroborates RF-15's 'old-vs-fp32 cosine 1.0000 at every layer'. My norm-change measurement on the AXES (0.04-0.20%) is smaller than RF-15's reported 0.5-0.9%, which was presumably over the per-persona vectors. The second half of the doc's sentence (the argmax bug) concerns last-token pooling of the EVALUATION corpus and was handled by restarting Pass B; it is not testable from the persona store and I did not test it.",W6A-thesis1
O-066,"Length alone predicts the deception label above chance on 9 of the 10 datasets the control was run on, with per-dataset AUROCs sandbagging_v2 0.854 down to roleplaying 0.441.",0.854; 0.776; 0.664; 0.625; 0.613; 0.595; 0.560; 0.507; 0.502; 0.441,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:503-507 (was :498; edited by the audit 2026-09-23, DF-49)","audit/cache/labpc/run-coords/confounds_L44_last.json (10,004 B, md5 11bc6e6567a3ce77f398b63572ec5cbc, lab mtime 2026-09-16 19:36). NOT present in the git working tree.",confounds.length_only_auroc[*].auroc_from_length (and .median_pos/.median_neg),0.854402 / 0.775612 / 0.663967 / 0.624940 / 0.613032 / 0.594546 / 0.560396 / 0.506766 / 0.501731 / 0.441473,"YES - all ten match to 5e-4; 10 datasets, 9 above 0.5, roleplaying the sole inversion","the file's own dataset list has 11 entries incl. alpaca (single-class, no length AUROC) and does NOT contain harm-pressure-kr-matched, confirming the doc's set description. Median token gap in the same file: deceptive longer in 8 of 10, tied in 1 (harm-pressure-choice), shorter in 1 (roleplaying).",own reader over the cached lab result file + recomputed counts and median gaps,"LAB-ONLY file, copied into audit/cache/labpc during this audit. run-coords is NOT in RF-13's 09-22 rewrite list. Bank recorded inside: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (irrelevant - length uses no persona direction). No BH q.","one layer/pooling label (L44 last), but the feature is token count, which is layer-invariant; 7.8's Pass C per-fold length control (0.617 LODO) points the same way",HOLDS,HIGH - ten-for-ten exact against the producing result file,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"THREE DEFECTS IN THE AUDIT'S OWN 2026-09-23 EDIT, all documentation-level: (1) the cited path run-coords/confounds_L44_last.json DOES NOT EXIST in the git working tree - the file is lab-only, so the citation does not resolve for a reader of the repo; (2) the key is nested at confounds.length_only_auroc and the value field is auroc_from_length, not a top-level mapping called length_only_auroc; (3) the edit leaves the sentence two lines below intact - 'Only the sycophancy value (0.664) is also in a result file' - which now directly contradicts the path the edit added. One of the two must go.",W6A-thesis1
O-067,"PC1 of a PCA over a broad role library is the Assistant Axis, not a behaviour axis (|cos| 0.73-0.82 on own100, 0.75-0.80 on hf275, layers 20-60); running PCA per behaviour fixes it, raising cos(PC1, deception contrast) from -0.63 to +0.947 at layer 40 on the HF vectors.",0.73; 0.82; 0.75; 0.80; -0.63; +0.947,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:544-546 (7.1),"run-hf275/axes_hf100.pt (pca['all'], pca['deception'], axes); run-hf275/vectors_100; run-hf275/vectors_275; run-hf275/published_assistant_axis.pt. own100 = lab-only.","|cos(pca['all'].components[L,0], reference[L])|; cos(pca['deception'].components[40,0], axes['deception'][40])",hf275 PC1 vs PUBLISHED axis: 0.8025/0.7938/0.7814/0.7544 at L20/22/40/60 -> range 0.754-0.803 (doc 0.75-0.80). PC1_all vs deception contrast at L40 = -0.6331 (doc -0.63). PC1_deception vs deception contrast at L40 = +0.9470 (doc +0.947). own100 NOT MEASURED.,YES for the three hf275/HF quantities; own100 unchecked,recomputed the 100-role and 275-role PCAs from the raw vector files; the stored pca['all'] PC1 is identical to my recompute (|cos| = 1.00000 at all four layers) and equals the legacy top-level pca_components. Whole band L20-L60 (41 layers): PC1(100) vs published 0.7517-0.8109; vs the bank's own assistant 0.7707-0.8190; PC1(275) vs published 0.6350-0.7702.,"own SVD per layer over the role vectors, then cosines against three candidate assistant references","run-hf275 laptop files; not the paper16 bank, so RF-12/RF-15/RF-16 do not apply; not in RF-13's rewrite set; no BH q","PC1 is assistant-like under every variant tested (|cos| >= 0.71 across the whole 20-60 band and all three references), so the qualitative claim is robust to the reference-direction choice",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the three recomputed quantities; the own100 range is DEFERRED and corroborated only by a memory note (DOC-ONLY),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_geom.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_geom.txt),"Same reference-direction slippage as O-057: the printed 0.75-0.80 reproduces only against the PUBLISHED Assistant Axis. Against the hf bank's OWN assistant direction the range is 0.779-0.812. Also '0.75-0.80' is a four-layer sample, not the band min/max - the matching variant's band is 0.752-0.811. Would need C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt for the own100 range.",W6A-thesis1
O-068,"Regrouping the cached HF roles by disclosure stance (8 concealment vs 14 disclosure) moves mean |cos(deception, assistant)| only from 0.655 to 0.585, about 11%, so relabelling the library does not fix the contamination.",0.655; 0.585; ~11%; 8 vs 14,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:547-549 (7.1),"run-coords/regroup_hf.json (1,770 B)","results[*].ours, results[*].disclosure, results[*].n_disclosure","ours -0.7067/-0.6792/-0.6544/-0.5783 -> mean |cos| 0.6547; disclosure -0.6493/-0.6162/-0.5764/-0.4990 -> mean |cos| 0.5852; reduction 10.60%; n_disclosure = [8, 14] in every row",YES on all four quantities,"the two means and the percentage re-derived from the per-layer cosines rather than read; role lists confirmed (conceal 8, disclose 14, ours 12 vs 12)",own arithmetic over the stored per-layer values,"run-coords laptop copy, produced by 16_regroup_hf.py; run-coords is not in RF-13's rewrite list; HF vectors so RF-12/RF-15 do not apply; no BH q","same sign and similar size at all four stored layers (disclosure cleaner by 0.057-0.079 everywhere), so the conclusion is not layer-dependent; but 'about 11%' is a 4-point mean with no bootstrap",HOLDS,HIGH - exact and re-derived,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_geom.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_geom.txt),"Reader trap: this bullet's 0.655 baseline is a 12-vs-12 contrast, NOT the 22-vs-22 contrast that gives 7.1's hf275 column (-0.610 at L40). Three different groupings of the same HF library appear within eight lines of 7.1 (22v22, 12v12, 8v14) and the text does not distinguish them. The comparison inside the bullet is internally consistent, so the claim stands.",W6A-thesis1
O-069,Building the deception axis from trait vectors instead of role personas makes the assistant-axis contamination worse: -0.725 against -0.610 for the role contrast at layer 40.,-0.725; -0.610,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:550 (7.1),"-0.610: run-hf275/vectors_275 + published_assistant_axis.pt. -0.725: NO FILE - no trait vector store and no producing script exists in the repo, in any branch, or in the lab census.","cos(22v22 deception contrast[40], assistant reference[40]); trait-vector axis: absent",role contrast at L40 = -0.6097 vs the published axis (-0.6088 vs an assistant direction over all 275 roles; -0.5771 vs the 100-role bank's own). Trait-vector value: NOT FOUND.,YES for -0.610; the -0.725 has no file to match against,"searches: repo tree has no *trait*.pt and no trait vector directory (assistant_axis/data/traits holds only prompt instructions + trait_list.json); audit/phase1/labpc/joined_labpc.tsv.gz returns 0 rows for *trait*.pt, hf_axis_check*, vectors_trait*, traits/vectors*; run-hf275/vectors_275 contains no trait names (transparent, factual, enigmatic, cryptic, subversive all absent)",filesystem + lab-census search for the artefacts and the producing script,"run-hf275 laptop files for the verified half. The -0.725 exists only in the memory note 'persona-axis-diagnostics' ('Fix routes tested 2026-09-15 (layer 40, HF vectors, laptop only)'), which is prose.",n/a for the unverifiable half,PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH that -0.610 is right; HIGH that -0.725 is unverifiable from stored data,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_geom.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_geom.txt),"NO RAW DATA, not DEFERRED: the lab census confirms the trait vectors and hf_axis_check.py are absent on the lab PC too, so this is not a lab-unreachable problem. The memory note is at least self-consistent with the doc (it carries both -0.610 and -0.725 in one table) and names the traits used, but no file holds them. For a reframed paper: either re-run it (the HF trait vectors are downloadable, CPU-only) or drop the sentence; do not print a 3-dp number no file supports.",W6A-thesis1
O-070,"Each method at its own best layer, the persona axes beat the raw probe: axes@44 - raw@32 = +0.014 with mean pooling and axes@44 - raw@28 = +0.026 with last-token pooling (9 datasets, 72 pairs, mms, Pass B).",+0.014; +0.026,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:587-588 (7.2),run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_mms.json (md5 3506b84d16e7b686c094de79c468f708); run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_last.json (md5 67cf30ed464d53b14526d0545dc53308); run-coords/significance.json,"sweep[L].{raw,axes}; comparisons[name contains 'each at its best']",significance.json: +0.014161 (mean) and +0.025898 (last),YES (to 3 dp),"recomputed the argmax over all 21 stored layers: mean raw peaks L32 0.7167, axes L44 0.7309 -> +0.014161; last raw peaks L28 0.7399, axes L44 0.7658 -> +0.025898. Peak layers also confirm 7.2's 'the axes peak at 44 under both poolings'.","own argmax + subtraction over the raw sweeps, independent of the stored comparison","run-coords, mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; the q's are from this file's own 23-test family; bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt; seed 42 only (no seed sweep exists for the 9-dataset set)","does NOT generalise: over audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv (crossgen family, dataset_set='all', layers>=20, 126 store x bank x pooling x seed x probe configurations) the best-vs-best axes-raw gap has median -0.0314 and is positive in only 28/126. Those stores use 10-11 datasets, so this is a robustness signal, not a contradiction of the quoted value.",HOLDS,HIGH for the arithmetic (Level 1 and Level 2 both exact),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6A_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_robust.txt),"The numbers are right; the framing is the risk. Both gaps are non-significant across datasets in the very file that stores them (dataset_p 0.8612 and 0.598, BH q 0.86 and 0.67), yet the bullet sits under the heading 'What HOLDS on these nine datasets'. A best-vs-best difference is also a maximum over 21 layers on both sides, on one seed, with no selection correction. Honest form for the reframed thesis: '+0.014/+0.026 at each method's own best layer, one seed, one 9-dataset set, q 0.86 and 0.67; negative in 98 of 126 other configurations'.",W6A-thesis1
O-071,"On the 2,000-row Pass A with the mms probe and mean pooling, the persona axes peak at layer 44 (0.687) and the raw probe at layer 32 (0.725), so raw wins the best-vs-best comparison on Pass A even though the peak layers agree with Pass B.",0.687; 0.725,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:602-603 (7.2),run-coords/layer_sweep_mms.json (md5 6a6788e6c726569f8e709760dc5209a2),"sweep[L].{raw,axes}, argmax over all 20 stored layers",axes peak L44 0.6870; raw peak L32 0.7245; axes@44 - raw@32 = -0.0375,"YES (0.687 and 0.725 to 3 dp), and the direction 'raw wins' is confirmed","argmax recomputed over the full 20-layer sweep rather than read; peak layers match Pass B's (raw L32 mean, axes L44), confirming 'Pass A agrees on peak layers'",own argmax over the stored sweep,"run-coords laptop copy, mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42","on Pass A the axes beat raw at only ONE of the 15 stored layers >= 20 (L44, +0.0140); everywhere else raw wins by up to 0.19. The 36-48 'window' of 7.2 is one layer wide on Pass A.",HOLDS,HIGH - argmax recomputed over the whole sweep,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"This is the document's own strongest internal counter-evidence to O-070. Same probe, same bank, deeper 80-layer pass, 2,000 rows instead of ~15,000: the persona axes lose best-vs-best by 0.038. In a controls-first reframing this belongs beside O-070, not three bullets below it.",W6A-thesis1
O-072,"With the lr_reg10 probe on Pass A (mean pooling), the persona axes never beat the raw probe at any layer from 20 up; the closest they come is layer 40 (0.674 vs 0.675) and layer 44 (0.665 vs 0.665).",0.674; 0.675; 0.665; 0.665,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:603-604 (7.2),run-coords/layer_sweep_mean.json (md5 430e636c0652c333720c60a60619d323),"sweep[L].{raw,axes} for every L >= 20",L40 axes 0.6740 vs raw 0.6751; L44 axes 0.6646 vs raw 0.6647,YES to 3 dp on all four numbers,"the universal form checked at all 15 stored layers >= 20: axes - raw is negative everywhere, largest value -0.0001 (L44), next -0.0010 (L40), worst -0.1837. axes peak L40 0.6740 vs raw peak L32 0.7176 -> best-vs-best -0.0436.","full stored sweep printed and checked, not a two-cell read","run-coords laptop copy, mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42","broad sweep over layer_sensitivity.csv (layers >= 20, 5,848 cells with both features): axes beat raw in 24.3% of cells, median axes-raw = -0.0447; by layer, median +0.0003 at L20, -0.0101 at L40, -0.0125 at L44, -0.0683 at L60",HOLDS,HIGH - full-sweep check,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6A_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_robust.txt),"With O-071 this shows the headline persona advantage is not probe-robust: it exists for mms on Pass B and for no probe on Pass A. Single seed for this file; the Pass A crossgen store has seeds 0-4 but under P3-D those seeds carry a reduced feature/probe list, so I did not build a 6-seed mean from them.",W6A-thesis1
O-073,The paper reports a mean off-diagonal AUROC gain of +0.10 for its persona-PC projection over a raw probe; in our replication pc:deception is never better than raw at any layer >= 20.,+0.10,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:618 (7.2, comparison table)","ours: run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_{mms,last}.json, layer_sweep_{mms,mean}.json; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv. paper: docs/papers/persona-coordinates-notes.md section 5.5 (audit's own Phase-1 figure-read; the PDF was not opened this session).","sweep[L].['pc:deception'] - sweep[L].raw for every L; notes table 'Mean off-diagonal AUROC improvement over the raw probe (Figure 10, panel A)'","ours: 0 of 66 layer x sweep cells at L >= 20 have pc:deception > raw; max(pc - raw) at L>=20 is -0.0085 / -0.0203 / -0.0397 / -0.0395 in the four sweeps. paper: the notes say '~ +0.10' for 3B Deception, and '13/20' pairs won.",YES for our column; the paper column matches the audit's own notes but is an approximate figure-read,"7.2's companion sentence also holds: the only pc-over-raw wins are at layers 0, 8, 16 (PassB last) and 0 (PassA lr_reg10), max +0.0223, i.e. 'near-chance layers 0-16, by at most 0.023'. Wider census (layer_sensitivity.csv, 5,848 cells at L>=20): pc beats raw in 326 cells (5.6%), median pc-raw = -0.1002.","exhaustive scan of every stored layer in every sweep, plus the crossgen census","run-coords sweeps mtime 2026-09-16/17, NOT in the RF-13 rewrite set, bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. layer_sensitivity.csv derives from crossgen stores that RF-13 DID rewrite, so it is used only for direction-of-effect. The largest pc-over-raw cells are scale_70b rows, which RF-16 shows mix two banks - context only.","our column is robust: 94.4% of 5,848 census cells agree, across banks, poolings, seeds, probes and dataset sets",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for our column (exhaustive); LOW-MEDIUM for the paper column (DOC-ONLY, read off a figure, not re-checked against the PDF this session)",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6A_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_robust.txt),"THE TWO COLUMNS ARE NOT THE SAME ESTIMATOR. The paper's deception PC projection is k=1 (the doc itself says so at 2.7); our pc:deception is k=5 in every run-coords sweep and in 12,128 of 12,812 census cells. The table compares k=1 against k=5 without saying so. Also: the paper's +0.10 is at layer 14 of a 3B model (mid-depth), whereas our quoted band starts at a quarter depth of 80 layers - and our sweeps DO show pc-over-raw gains below layer 20 (up to +0.0223). The only census cells where pc beats raw by >0.06 are the 5-dataset, paper-question, k=3 cells of the 70B scale rung, i.e. the closest setting we have to the paper's. The thesis also prints '+0.10' where the audit's notes say '~ +0.10'.",W6A-thesis1
O-074,"The Q4 table: for six layer/pooling/probe settings it reports raw transfer AUROC, the AUROC after erasing the paper16 assistant direction, the cost, the random-erasure control, the erased dataset-level 95% CI, and whether the cost is significant across datasets.",36 cells: raw 0.652/0.660/0.669/0.686/0.720/0.661; erased 0.646/0.655/0.652/0.672/0.712/0.656; cost 0.006/0.005/0.018/0.014/0.008/0.005; ~0.000; six CIs; q 0.52/0.54/0.003/0.16/0.003/0.04,docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:658-665 (7.4 table),run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (md5 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e),"q4_table[*].{raw,erase_assistant,cost_assistant,cost_random,erased_dataset_ci95}; comparisons[name='cost of erasing Assistant Axis, L<n> <pool> <probe>'].dataset_q_bh","raw 0.6524/0.6599/0.6693/0.6862/0.7200/0.6611; erased 0.6462/0.6545/0.6516/0.6721/0.7119/0.6558; cost 0.0062/0.0054/0.0177/0.0141/0.0081/0.0053; random-erasure means 5.2e-5/3.7e-4/-1.9e-5/2.0e-4/-1.9e-5/3.8e-4; CIs [0.513,0.796] [0.558,0.741] [0.510,0.786] [0.586,0.760] [0.608,0.824] [0.570,0.752]; q 0.5151/0.5425/0.0035/0.1618/0.0035/0.0399","YES - 36 of 36 cells at the document's own precision, including the yes/no significance column","cost_assistant = raw - erase_assistant in all six rows; the 'vs random erasures' comparisons give the same diffs to <=4e-4, so the ~0.000 baseline is consistent. Cost as a share of raw: 0.80%-2.64%.","own reader over the bootstrap file, matching each q to its exact comparison name; NOT re-fit from activations (needs the lab/Drive Pass B store)","mtime 2026-09-17, NOT in RF-13's rewrite set, lab copy md5-identical. THE BH FAMILY IS THIS FILE'S OWN 26 COMPARISONS (Q3's 14 + Q4's 12) and the doc does not say so. RF-13 changed q's in the crossgen family (192 -> 4,788 tests), not this one. Bank: paper16 assistant direction; O-064 bounds any old-vs-fp32 difference at 0.2% of norm.","the table is itself a 3 x 2 sweep; every cost positive; but only FIVE random directions back the '~0.000' column and the file stores their mean, not a distribution",HOLDS,HIGH for Level 1 (36/36 cells); MEDIUM overall (no recompute from activations),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6A_transfer.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6A/W6A_transfer.txt),"Three things to carry into the thesis: (1) the q column's family is local to this file and undeclared - a reader assuming a project-wide correction would be wrong, and the q's would be larger; (2) 7.4's verdict says the erasure costs '1-3%' of transfer AUROC, measured 0.80-2.64%, with two rows below 1%; (3) the erased direction is bank-local (cos 0.30-0.37 with the published Assistant Axis, confirmed in O-057), so 'the Assistant Axis' has not been erased - the doc flags this in 10 but the table's caption does not.",W6A-thesis1
O-076,"Q4 table row L20/mean/lr_reg10: raw transfer 0.660, 0.655 after erasing the paper16 assistant direction, cost 0.005, random erasures ~0.000, erased dataset 95% CI [0.558, 0.741], cost not significant across datasets (q 0.54).","0.660; 0.655; 0.005; ~0.000; [0.558, 0.741]; q 0.54",docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:662 (7.4 table; inventory says :656 - the audit's 2026-09-23 edit shifted every 7.4-7.7 line by +6),"run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (md5 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e, mtime 2026-09-17)","q4_table[layer=20,pooling=mean,probe=lr_reg10].{raw,erase_assistant,cost_assistant,cost_random,erased_dataset_ci95}; comparisons[name='cost of erasing Assistant Axis, L20 mean lr_reg10'].dataset_q_bh","raw 0.659862; erased 0.654512; cost 0.005351; random mean 3.68e-04; CI [0.5584, 0.7411]; q_BH 0.54245 (dataset_p 0.4358)",YES - 6 of 6 cells at the document's precision (tol 5e-4),cost = raw - erased = 0.005350625 exactly (delta 0.00e+00); cost as share of raw = 0.811%,"own reader over the producing bootstrap file; cost re-derived rather than read; each q matched to its named comparison and the family size printed. NOT re-fit from activations (needs the ~30 GB Pass B store, lab/Drive only).","laptop/git copy; mtime 2026-09-17; run-coords NOT in RF-13's 09-22 rewrite set; lab copy md5-identical per sibling O-075. BH FAMILY = this file's own 26 comparisons (Q3 14 + Q4 12), not stated in the doc. Bank: NO bank field is stored (RF-16), 26_q3_q4_bootstrap.py:139 defaults to run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt and its usage line passes no args -> fp32 paper16 (INFERRED); O-064 bounds old-vs-fp32 at <=0.00065 cosine / 0.2% norm.",the Q4 table is itself a 3 layer/pooling x 2 probe sweep; cost positive in 6/6. This is the joint-smallest cost in the table. The '~0.000' control rests on FIVE random directions and only their mean is stored.,HOLDS,"HIGH for Level 1 (6/6 exact, cost exact to machine precision); MEDIUM overall (no re-fit from activations)",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q4.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q4.txt),"The q column's BH family is local to this file (26 tests) and the thesis does not say so; a reader assuming a project-wide correction would get larger q's. q3_q4_bootstrap.json stores no bank field at all, so the bank rests on the script default (RF-16).",W6B-thesis2
O-077,"Q4 table row L40/mean/mms: raw 0.669, erased 0.652, cost 0.018, random ~0.000, erased dataset 95% CI [0.510, 0.786], cost IS significant across datasets (q 0.003).","0.669; 0.652; 0.018; ~0.000; [0.510, 0.786]; q 0.003","docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:663 (7.4 table; inventory :657, +6 offset)","run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (md5 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e, mtime 2026-09-17)","q4_table[40,mean,mms]; comparisons[name='cost of erasing Assistant Axis, L40 mean mms']","raw 0.669278; erased 0.651595; cost 0.017684; random mean -1.89e-05; CI [0.5098, 0.7861]; q_BH 0.003467 (dataset_p 0.0004)",YES - 6 of 6 cells (tol 5e-4),"cost = raw - erased = 0.017683543 exactly; cost as share of raw = 2.642% (the largest in the table); the 'vs random erasures' twin gives 0.017702, q 0.0052","same script/reader as O-076; cost re-derived, q matched by comparison name, family size printed","laptop/git copy; mtime 2026-09-17; run-coords NOT in RF-13's 09-22 rewrite set; lab copy md5-identical per sibling O-075. BH FAMILY = this file's own 26 comparisons (Q3 14 + Q4 12), not stated in the doc. Bank: NO bank field is stored (RF-16), 26_q3_q4_bootstrap.py:139 defaults to run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt and its usage line passes no args -> fp32 paper16 (INFERRED); O-064 bounds old-vs-fp32 at <=0.00065 cosine / 0.2% norm.","largest cost of the six settings; its lr_reg10 partner at the same layer/pooling costs 0.0141 but does NOT clear BH (q 0.16), so the significance verdict is probe-dependent at L40 while the estimate is not.",HOLDS,HIGH for Level 1; MEDIUM overall (no re-fit from activations),HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q4.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q4.txt),"This is the row 7.4's 'small but real' verdict leans on. dataset_p = 0.0004 on 10,000 dataset-bootstrap draws, so it is not a marginal call.",W6B-thesis2
O-078,"Q4 table row L40/mean/lr_reg10: raw 0.686, erased 0.672, cost 0.014, random ~0.000, erased dataset 95% CI [0.586, 0.760], cost not significant across datasets (q 0.16).","0.686; 0.672; 0.014; ~0.000; [0.586, 0.760]; q 0.16","docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:664 (7.4 table; inventory :658, +6 offset)","run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (md5 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e, mtime 2026-09-17)","q4_table[40,mean,lr_reg10]; comparisons[name='cost of erasing Assistant Axis, L40 mean lr_reg10']","raw 0.686207; erased 0.672102; cost 0.014105; random mean 2.02e-04; CI [0.5855, 0.7595]; q_BH 0.16185 (dataset_p 0.0492)",YES - 6 of 6 cells (tol 5e-4),"cost = raw - erased = 0.014104915 exactly; share of raw 2.055%; raw dataset_p is 0.0492, i.e. nominally < 0.05 before BH",same script/reader as O-076,"laptop/git copy; mtime 2026-09-17; run-coords NOT in RF-13's 09-22 rewrite set; lab copy md5-identical per sibling O-075. BH FAMILY = this file's own 26 comparisons (Q3 14 + Q4 12), not stated in the doc. Bank: NO bank field is stored (RF-16), 26_q3_q4_bootstrap.py:139 defaults to run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt and its usage line passes no args -> fp32 paper16 (INFERRED); O-064 bounds old-vs-fp32 at <=0.00065 cosine / 0.2% norm.","highest raw transfer in the table (0.686) and second-largest cost, yet the only one of the three largest costs that fails BH. The 'no' here is correction-dependent: RF-13 showed q's moving by up to 0.39 when a family grew.",HOLDS,HIGH for Level 1; MEDIUM overall,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q4.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q4.txt),"If 7.4's q column survives into the thesis, the family size (26 tests, local to q3_q4_bootstrap.json) must be printed with it - this cell is where the label, not the estimate, is fragile.",W6B-thesis2
O-079,The paper16 assistant direction carries a small but real 1-3% of transfer AUROC (i.e. erasing it costs 1-3% of the raw transfer AUROC).,1-3%,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:670 (7.4 verdict bullet 2; inventory :664, +6 offset)","run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json (md5 2f616b3ed18c3d74863635bb0ba4053e, mtime 2026-09-17)","q4_table[*].{raw,cost_assistant}; comparisons[name startswith 'cost of erasing'].dataset_q_bh",no result file states a percentage - this is prose; Level 1 unavailable,n/a,"cost/raw per setting: 0.943%, 0.811%, 2.642%, 2.055%, 1.127%, 0.798% -> RANGE 0.798%-2.642%, median 0.943%. 3 of 6 rows are BELOW 1%; 0 of 6 reach 3%. Absolute cost 0.0053-0.0177 AUROC.",computed 100*cost_assistant/raw for all six rows of the producing file; also counted BH-significant rows,"laptop/git copy; mtime 2026-09-17; run-coords NOT in RF-13's 09-22 rewrite set; lab copy md5-identical per sibling O-075. BH FAMILY = this file's own 26 comparisons (Q3 14 + Q4 12), not stated in the doc. Bank: NO bank field is stored (RF-16), 26_q3_q4_bootstrap.py:139 defaults to run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt and its usage line passes no args -> fp32 paper16 (INFERRED); O-064 bounds old-vs-fp32 at <=0.00065 cosine / 0.2% norm. UNDERSPECIFIED: '1-3% of transfer AUROC' could mean a share of raw (tested, most favourable) or 0.01-0.03 AUROC points (fails outright: 4 of 6 are below 0.01).","sign is positive in 6/6; BH-significant across datasets in 3/6 (q 0.0035, 0.0035, 0.0399), not in 3/6 (q 0.52, 0.54, 0.16). The erased direction is bank-local (cos 0.30-0.37 with the published axis, O-080), so this is not a statement about *the* Assistant Axis.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - exact arithmetic over all six rows of the producing file,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q4.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q4.txt),"The stated interval does not bracket the data: measured 0.80%-2.64%, with HALF the settings below the 1% floor and none above 3%. Correct form: '0.8-2.6% of transfer AUROC (0.005-0.018 AUROC), positive in 6/6, BH-significant in 3/6'. NOTE FOR THE LEAD: W6A's notes on O-058 and O-074 both say 'two rows below 1%'; the correct count is THREE (0.798, 0.811, 0.943%).",W6B-thesis2
O-080,"The direction Q4 erases is paper16's OWN assistant direction, which has only cos 0.30-0.37 with Lu et al.'s published Assistant Axis, so 'signal survives removal of THE Assistant Axis' has not been tested.",0.30; 0.37,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:677-679 (the audit's caveat box under 7.4; inventory :672, +6 offset)","run-hf275/published_assistant_axis.pt (md5 2807d7caa7f5f0126be9ba4c4b6ea906, 80x8192); run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3.pt (md5 5d05a42542ae13fc7ac5d893a4ae4f8c, RF-15 'old'); audit/cache/labpc/run-paper16/vectors_s3_fp32/*.pt (26 files, the fp32 re-extraction, rebuilt into an assistant axis here)","cos(axes['assistant'][L], published[L]) for all 80 layers, for both bank versions","no result file holds this cosine (prose only, also in memory note paper16-assistant-direction-not-lu-axis) - Level 2 only",n/a,"OLD bank: L20 0.3662, L22 0.3059, L40 0.3719, L44 0.3566, L60 0.2997 -> range over the five thesis layers 0.2997-0.3719. fp32 rebuild: 0.3664/0.3062/0.3718/0.3565/0.2998. Q4 erasure layers only (20,40,44): 0.3565-0.3719. Whole L20-L60 band: 0.2601-0.4212. All 80 layers: 0.2601-0.6590.",rebuilt the fp32 assistant direction from the 26 cached per-persona vectors with 6_axes.py's construction (assistant = default - mean(role personas)); SANITY CHECK: the same rebuild over the OLD per-persona vectors reproduces the stored old assistant axis at min cos 1.000000 over 80 layers,"laptop copies + the audit's own cache of the lab fp32 vectors. RF-15 immaterial here: max |old-fp32| difference in this cosine is 0.000796 and cos(old assistant, fp32 assistant) >= 0.999959 at every layer. No BH q.","the substantive point is stronger than the bracket: across the whole L20-L60 band the cosine never exceeds 0.42, i.e. the two directions share at most ~18% of variance anywhere the thesis works.",HOLDS,HIGH - computed from raw per-persona vectors with a construction sanity check that returns cos 1.000000 against the stored bank,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_geom.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_geom.txt),"'0.30-0.37' is a five-layer sample, not a band range: over L20-L60 it is 0.26-0.42 and over all 80 layers 0.26-0.66 (early layers). Name the layers or quote the band. The caveat itself is correct and load-bearing: 7.4 is not a result about the published Assistant Axis.",W6B-thesis2
O-081,"In P1 at layer 44, last-token pooling, mms probe on RAW activations over 10 labelled datasets, transfer cells that share a label construct average 0.748 and cells that cross constructs 0.585, permutation p 0.043.",0.748; 0.585; p 0.043,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:704 (7.5 verdict bullet 1; inventory :698, +6 offset)","run-coords/q5_semantics_L44_last.json (44,835 B, md5 5b7c206abfadaac325a60d68f2d5a4f3, mtime 2026-09-16 19:22), built from run-coords/p1_L44_last_withsyc.json","results[features='raw', probe='mms'].{within_semantics, across_semantics, permutation_p, n_within, n_across, blocks}","within 0.748208 (n=44), across 0.584580 (n=46), permutation_p 0.043348 -> 0.748 / 0.585 / 0.043",YES on all three (tol 5e-4),"difference re-derived 0.748208-0.584580 = 0.163628 = stored. Block means confirm the companion sentence: instructed_intent->instructed_intent n=42 mean 0.761032, belief->belief n=2 mean 0.478891, so 42 of the 44 within-cells ARE intent->intent.","own reader + arithmetic over the stored per-block means; the 44/46 split reconstructed from the construct map (8 intent / 1 judge / 2 belief mapped, 10 of the 11 present in the matrix -> 7*6+2 = 44 within, 46 across)","laptop copy, mtime 2026-09-16; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set. DATASET SET = 10 labelled datasets INCLUDING sycophancy_mt (90 ordered off-diagonal cells); ai_audit is mapped but absent from the matrix. Raw-activation feature, so no persona bank enters this row; no BH q (raw permutation p).","the gap has the same sign for every feature, but crosses p<0.05 only for raw/mms (0.043), pc:deception/mms (0.027) and pc:deception/lr_reg10 (0.042); axes/mms gives 0.103 and raw/lr_reg10 0.286. The random-feature control gives a gap of 0.044-0.047 at p~0.21.",HOLDS,"HIGH - read and re-derived from the producing file, including the block counts",MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q5q7.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q5q7.txt),"The bullet exists to be refuted by the next three bullets (42 of 44 within-cells are one construct from two related pipelines; mask<->sycophancy_mt does not transfer). For a negative-results framing that is the finding, and this number is its set-up.",W6B-thesis2
O-083,"Q6 table row: trained P1 transfer on raw activations, mms probe, mean pooling, Pass B full corpus reads 0.652 at L20, 0.646 at L22, 0.669 at L40, own best L32 at 0.717.",0.652; 0.646; 0.669; L32 0.717,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:726 (7.6 table; inventory :720, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); source sweep run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_mms.json (md5 3506b84d16e7b686c094de79c468f708)","rows[method='raw / mms / mean', source='trained transfer, full corpus'].{at['20'],at['22'],at['40'],best_layer,best}",0.652382 / 0.646258 / 0.669278 / L32 0.716728,YES - 5 of 5 cells,"re-read from layer_sweep_passB_mms.json: L20 0.652382, L40 0.669278, argmax over all 21 stored layers = L32 0.716728 - identical to the compiled row",independent argmax over the full source sweep rather than a read of the compiled 'best' field,"laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row.","cross-check: the same two values are the 'raw' column of the 7.4 Q4 table (L20 mean mms 0.652382, L40 mean mms 0.669278), so 7.4 and 7.6 are internally consistent. This is the only raw row whose L40 beats both L20 and L22 (+0.0169); its last-token partner goes the other way (-0.0157).",HOLDS,HIGH - Level 2 is an independent argmax over the whole sweep,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt),"Neither 20, 22 nor 40 is this method's best layer (L32 is), which is the table's own point.",W6B-thesis2
O-084,"Q6 table row: trained P1 transfer on raw activations, lr_reg10 probe, mean pooling, Pass A (no layer 22) reads 0.676 at L20, nothing at L22, 0.675 at L40, own best L32 at 0.718.",0.676; -; 0.675; L32 0.718,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:727 (7.6 table; inventory :721, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); source sweep run-coords/layer_sweep_mean.json (md5 430e636c0652c333720c60a60619d323)","rows[method='raw / lr_reg10 / mean', source='trained transfer, Pass A (no layer 22)']",0.676238 / null / 0.675064 / L32 0.717615,"YES - 5 of 5, and the em-dash correctly renders a stored null","re-read from layer_sweep_mean.json: L20 0.676238, L40 0.675064, argmax over all 20 stored layers = L32 0.717615","independent argmax over the source sweep; the row is disambiguated from the Pass B raw/mms/mean row by its source field, not its method string","laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. Pass A = the 2,000-row / 80-layer pass, a different corpus from the Pass B rows in the same column.",flattest raw row in the table: L20 is very slightly HIGHER than L40 (by 0.0012) while L32 is 0.042 above either. One of the two negative entries behind O-092's +0.025 median.,HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt),"Because L22 is null, this row feeds the 10-method L40 median (O-092) but not the 17-method 20-vs-22 median (O-091). It is the clearest single piece of evidence that layer 40 is not a raw-probe optimum.",W6B-thesis2
O-085,"Q6 table row: trained P1 transfer on the 'axes' feature (four paper16 persona-axis projections), mms probe, mean pooling, Pass B full corpus reads 0.570 at L20, 0.566 at L22, 0.721 at L40, own best L44 at 0.731.",0.570; 0.566; 0.721; L44 0.731,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:729 (7.6 table; inventory :723, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); source sweep run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_mms.json (md5 3506b84d16e7b686c094de79c468f708)","rows[method='axes / mms / mean', source='trained transfer, full corpus']",0.569769 / 0.566187 / 0.720791 / L44 0.730889,YES - 5 of 5 cells,"re-read from layer_sweep_passB_mms.json: L20 0.569769, L40 0.720791, argmax over all 21 stored layers = L44 0.730889",independent argmax over the full source sweep; row disambiguated from the Pass A axes row by its source field,"laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. Bank settled by a FIELD, not a filename: bank=axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5 (RF-16 satisfied). k=5 is our default, not the paper's (paper: deception k=1, sycophancy k=3); the 'axes' feature does not use k, so k only matters for this file's pc:deception rows.","largest layer effect of any trained method in the table: +0.151 from the better of L20/22 to L40, and +0.161 from L20 to its L44 peak. Its peak is one half of 7.2's headline +0.014 (axes@44 0.7309 vs raw@32 0.7167), a gap significance.json records as non-significant across datasets (dataset_p 0.8612, q 0.8612).",HOLDS,HIGH,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt),This row carries the whole 'layer 40/44 window' narrative and half of the headline persona-vs-raw margin.,W6B-thesis2
O-087,"Q6 table row: zero-shot projection onto the paper16 deception CONTRAST axis with mean pooling reads 0.608 at L20, 0.630 at L22, 0.863 at L40, and L40 is its best layer.",0.608; 0.630; 0.863; L40 0.863,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:731 (7.6 table; inventory :725, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); source file run-coords/dotproducts_mean.json (md5 a12563f5c24afc0a6b001ed26236c6d9); null test run-coords/zeroshot_nulls.json (md5 0c241a653587a570ed37a9bffe578dcd)",rows[method='deception contrast axis / mean']; dotproducts_mean.matched[*].contrast; zeroshot_nulls.corpus_L40_mean,0.608052 / 0.629506 / 0.863011 / L40 0.863011,YES - 5 of 5 cells,"re-read dotproducts_mean.json: same three values, argmax over all 21 layers = L40 0.863011. BUT zeroshot_nulls.json gives 0.880950 for nominally the same quantity, because 12_dotproduct_layers.py DROPS single-class datasets (alpaca) and 25_zeroshot_nulls.py KEEPS them in the pooled set.","independent argmax over the full stored depth + a cross-read of the second producing script's pooled number and its 1,000-random-direction null","laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. dotproducts_mean.json stores no bank field; 12_dotproduct_layers.py:47 defaults to axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (RF-16: script default, not the filename). RF-15's sign-pinning differences do not touch L20/L40/L44 and the contrast axis is not sign-pinned by PCA.","pooled, the axis beats the 1,000-random-direction null (p 0.0010, random p95 0.7636). PER DATASET at L40 mean it beats the p95 null on only 5 of 9: ai_liar 0.937 Y, convincing-game 0.788 N, harm-pressure-choice 0.544 N, harm-pressure-knowledge-report 0.644 N, insider-trading 0.980 Y, instructed-deception 0.971 Y, mask 0.467 N, roleplaying 0.784 Y, sandbagging_v2 0.845 Y.",HOLDS,HIGH for the numbers,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6B_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_robust.txt),TWO THINGS FOR THE THESIS. (1) The project prints two pooled values for the same quantity - 0.863 (alpaca dropped) and 0.881 (alpaca kept); neither document says which corpus. (2) The pooled 0.863 is substantially a between-dataset effect: it is at or below chance on mask (0.467) and harm-pressure-choice (0.544). Print the per-dataset null result next to it.,W6B-thesis2
O-089,"Q6 table row: leave-one-dataset-out on Pass C, mass-mean probe on pooled MEAN activations, fold-mean AUROC 0.857 at L20, 0.854 at L22, 0.883 at L40, own best L40.",0.857; 0.854; 0.883; L40 0.883,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:734 (7.6 table; inventory :728, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); source file run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json (md5 907b05ce36f8accf1a21bae09e305ce2, 188,408 B)","rows[method='pool_mean_mms / pooled']; q8_trained_pertoken.results[probe='pool_mean_mms', aggregation='pooled'].auroc_mean and .per_fold",0.857024 / 0.854373 / 0.882577 / L40 0.882577,YES - 5 of 5 cells,"re-read from the 106 raw records: same values; argmax over the file's six layers [20,22,28,40,44,48] = L40 0.882577. Per-fold spread behind the means: L20 min 0.6593 (mask) max 0.9993 sd 0.1248; L40 min 0.6515 (mask) max 1.0000 sd 0.0944.",own reader over the per-record results and per_fold arrays; argmax and fold statistics recomputed,"laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. Raw-activation feature, so no persona bank applies. Only SIX layers exist in this file, so 'own best' here is an argmax over 6, not over the 21-layer grid other rows of the same table use. Single seed.","the 0.883 is a mean over nine held-out datasets running 0.65-1.00, sd 0.094; the worst fold is mask at every layer except L22.",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6B_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_robust.txt),Strongest trained number in 7.6 and the one a reader will read as 'the detector works'. The 0.094 fold sd and the 0.65 mask fold belong beside it. Also: 'own best layer' is not comparable across rows of this table (6-layer vs 21-layer argmaxes) and nothing says so.,W6B-thesis2
O-090,"Q6 table row: leave-one-dataset-out on Pass C, logistic probe on individual TOKEN activations scored by the mean of token scores, fold-mean AUROC 0.785 at L20, 0.779 at L22, 0.839 at L40, own best L44 at 0.851.",0.785; 0.779; 0.839; L44 0.851,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:736 (7.6 table; inventory :730, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); source file run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json (md5 907b05ce36f8accf1a21bae09e305ce2)","rows[method='tok_lr / mean']; q8_trained_pertoken.results[probe='tok_lr', aggregation='mean']",0.785067 / 0.779317 / 0.839061 / L44 0.850734,YES - 5 of 5 cells,re-read from the raw records: same values; argmax over the six stored layers = L44 0.850734. Per-fold: L20 min 0.4120 (harm-pressure-knowledge-report) max 0.9971 sd 0.1880; L44 min 0.6826 (harm-pressure-choice) sd 0.1003.,own reader over the per-record results and per_fold arrays; argmax and fold statistics recomputed,"laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. Raw-activation feature; six layers only; single seed; no BH q (the Q8 tests in significance.json are pooled-vs-token, not layer tests).","the L20 fold mean of 0.785 contains a BELOW-CHANCE fold: harm-pressure-knowledge-report at 0.412, sd 0.188 across folds. That is the HP-KR inversion the kd/ experiment was built for, sitting inside a 7.6 table row that reports only the mean.",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM for the row; HIGH for the fold detail,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6B_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_robust.txt),"At the layer the replication target uses (L20), a trained token probe is below chance on one of nine datasets. The table's mean hides it.",W6B-thesis2
O-091,"Layers 20 and 22 are equivalent: over the 17 method rows that have both, the median absolute gap is 0.012 and the maximum 0.037; the four dataset-level equivalence tests have 90% CIs from -0.038 to +0.033.",0.012; 0.037; -0.038 to +0.033,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:739-741 (7.6 verdict bullet 1; inventory :733, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); run-coords/significance.json (md5 b52ff6166e2849258cf0e34a8715eecf, mtime 2026-09-17 01:03)",rows[*].gap_20_22 (17 non-null); comparisons[kind='equiv'].dataset_ci90 and .equivalent_within_margin,"median |gap| 0.011547 -> 0.012; max 0.037019 -> 0.037; union of the four CI90s [-0.03830, +0.03345] -> -0.038 to +0.033",YES on all three quantities and on the count of 17,"medians recomputed from the 17 per-row gaps (all stored as absolute values, verified); the four equivalence tests all return equivalent_within_margin = FALSE at the file's own pre-registered margin of 0.02",own arithmetic over the stored gaps + a read of every kind='equiv' comparison with its margin,"laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. significance.json mtime 2026-09-17, NOT in RF-13's rewrite set, so these CIs are not the ones RF-13 shifted (that was the run-crossgen family). 1,000 row-bootstrap / 10,000 dataset-bootstrap draws, 9 datasets, seed 42. The bullet quotes no BH q.","the 17 rows pool four protocols (Pass B and Pass A trained transfer, zero-shot dot products, Pass C LODO) whose AUROCs are not on a common scale; the median is across methods, not a per-method statement.",HOLDS,HIGH - recomputed from the 17 per-row gaps rather than read,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt),"'Immaterial' is a median of absolute gaps, not a test. ALL FOUR formal equivalence tests fail at the pre-registered +/-0.02 margin; 7.6 reaches equivalence only by widening the margin to +/-0.04 after seeing the CIs. A methods paper should declare that step. (W6A recorded the same under O-059; I confirm it independently.)",W6B-thesis2
O-092,"For raw probes, moving to layer 40 from the better of layers 20/22 gains a median +0.025 AUROC, range -0.016 to +0.068, over 10 method rows.",+0.025; -0.016; +0.068; 10 methods,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:742-743 (7.6 verdict bullet 2; inventory :736, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22)",rows[*].gap_40_minus_best_of_20_22 for the 10 raw-feature rows,median +0.025100 -> +0.025; min -0.015704 -> -0.016; max +0.068146 -> +0.068; n = 10,"YES on all four, and my independently rebuilt raw/persona split returns the document's own 10/13 counts","raw group split by protocol: the 4 trained-transfer rows have median +0.0051 (two of them negative), the 6 Pass C LODO rows +0.0333. All six rows above +0.024 are Pass C LODO.","raw/persona classification rebuilt from the method strings, medians recomputed from the 23 per-row gaps, then re-split by protocol","laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. Layer grids differ between rows (21 layers for Pass A/B sweeps, 6 for the Pass C LODO file); the L40-vs-better-of-20/22 gap is well defined in both, but 'own best layer' in the same table is not comparable across rows. Single seed.",see level2_value: the median is carried by one protocol.,HOLDS,HIGH - recomputed from the 23 per-row gaps with an independently rebuilt split,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6B_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_robust.txt),"Honest form: '+0.005 median over the four trained-transfer raw rows, +0.033 over the six Pass C LODO rows, +0.025 pooled'. Pooling two protocols into one median is what makes the raw baseline look layer-sensitive, and the raw/persona contrast in bullet 3 pools DIFFERENT protocols on each side.",W6B-thesis2
O-093,"For persona methods, moving to layer 40 from the better of 20/22 gains a median +0.113 over 13 method rows, up to +0.234 on a zero-shot method - about 4x the raw-probe handicap.",+0.113; +0.234; 13 methods; about 4x,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:744-746 (7.6 verdict bullet 3; inventory :738, +6 offset)","run-coords/q6_layers.json (md5 01e35cf0b472cb13e05ec871d7ab27c6, mtime 2026-09-16 21:22); run-coords/significance.json for the matching formal tests",rows[*].gap_40_minus_best_of_20_22 for the 13 persona rows; comparisons[name='axes: layer 40 vs 22 (mean|last)'],"median +0.113456 -> +0.113; max +0.233504 -> +0.234, and it IS a zero-shot row (the deception contrast axis); n = 13; persona-median/raw-median = 4.52x",YES on all four,"median unchanged (+0.1135) if the five zero-shot rows are dropped, so unlike O-092 it is not a pooling artefact; but the zero-shot subgroup alone gives only +0.0665 and one zero-shot row is NEGATIVE (per-token top-10%, -0.028). The two formal tests of the same thing in significance.json are NON-significant: axes L40 vs L22 mean diff +0.1546 (dataset_p 0.0256, q 0.0973, significant=false), last diff +0.0852 (dataset_p 0.2158, q 0.4556, significant=false).","split rebuilt from method strings; medians, maximum and the 4x ratio recomputed from the 23 per-row gaps; cross-read of the matching dataset-bootstrap tests","laptop/git copies; q6_layers.json mtime 2026-09-16 21:22, source sweeps 2026-09-16 19:21; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set; lab md5-identical per sibling O-086. Bank recorded INSIDE the sweep files: axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt, k=5, seed 42. No BH q in this row. Every pc:deception row here is k=5, our default - the paper uses k=1 for deception and k=3 for sycophancy, and k=5 appears nowhere in it. Single seed.","see level2_value: robust to dropping zero-shot rows, weaker within the zero-shot subgroup, and not significant across datasets in the project's own bootstrap.",HOLDS,HIGH - recomputed from the per-row gaps with an independently rebuilt split,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6B_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_robust.txt),"This is the mechanism the thesis uses to justify reading persona coordinates at layer 40 rather than at the paper's layer, so it underwrites the headline persona-vs-raw comparisons. A large median over 13 hand-grouped method rows AND a non-significant dataset bootstrap (q 0.097, 0.456) are the same finding seen two ways - print both.",W6B-thesis2
O-094,"Zero-shot persona scores collapse in late layers: the deception-axis AUROC is 0.491 at layer 60 and 0.445 at layer 68, i.e. below chance.",0.491; 0.445,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:747-748 (7.6 verdict bullet 4; inventory :741, +6 offset)","run-coords/dotproducts_mean.json (md5 a12563f5c24afc0a6b001ed26236c6d9, 26,923 B, mtime 2026-09-16 19:21)",matched[layer=60].contrast and matched[layer=68].contrast,L60 0.491368 -> 0.491; L68 0.444665 -> 0.445; both < 0.5,YES on both,"full depth profile from the L40 peak: 0.863 (40), 0.806 (44), 0.741 (48), 0.658 (52), 0.556 (56), 0.491 (60), 0.450 (64), 0.445 (68), 0.435 (72), 0.613 (76). Layers below 0.5: [0,4,8,12,16,60,64,68,72].",read every stored layer of the matched-layer series rather than the two quoted points,"laptop copy; run-coords NOT in RF-13's rewrite set. No bank field stored; 12_dotproduct_layers.py:47 defaults to axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (RF-16). RF-15 note: old-vs-fp32 PC SIGN pinning differs at a few layers (e.g. L65 for pca.all/unified) - the quoted numbers are the CONTRAST axis, which is not sign-pinned, so they are unaffected, but the neighbouring PC1 column at L64-72 is the kind of reading where a sign difference could matter. Pooled corpus = 9 labelled datasets (alpaca dropped), no sycophancy_mt. Single seed.","the low point is L72 (0.435), not L68, and the curve RECOVERS to 0.613 at the last stored layer L76 - a deep trough, not a monotone collapse. The whole early network L0-L16 is also below 0.5, so 'below chance' is not unique to late layers.",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q6.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q6.txt),"A clean negative result the reframed paper can use directly: a fixed persona direction is not a detector outside roughly L36-L52. Better stated as a band than as two points - 'above chance only ~L20-L56, peak 0.863 at L40, below chance at L0-L16 and L60-L72, recovering to 0.613 at L76'.",W6B-thesis2
O-095,"Judging the same paper16 rollouts, the 70B judge gives the top score (3) to 80.7% and the 405B judge to 79.9% - a gap of 0.8 percentage points - and score 3 is the filter that selects which rollouts build the persona vectors.","80.7%; 79.9%; 0.8 pp (and, in the same section, 91.2% agreement, 1,231 of 1,350)","docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:757-758 (7.7; inventory :751, +6 offset)","run-paper16/scores/*.json (25 files, 70B judge) and run-paper16/scores_405b/*.json (25 files, 405B judge); run-paper16/responses/*.jsonl (26 files, 1,400 records)","every (persona, item) score in both stores; judge identity from run_judge_405b.ps1:47-48 and 3_judge_ndif.py:262-263","NO RESULT FILE EXISTS for Q7 - no script in the repo aggregates the two stores, so the section's numbers are print-only. Level 1 unavailable.",n/a,"1,350 paired items. Exact agreement 1231/1350 = 91.185%. 70B distribution {0:12, 2:249, 3:1089}; 405B {0:19, 1:2, 2:250, 3:1079}. Score-3 rate 80.667% vs 79.926%, exact gap 0.74 pp. Lowest per-persona agreement: handler 0.740, plausible_denier 0.760, fact_checker 0.780. Score-3 KEEP SETS: 1089 vs 1079, intersection 1029, symmetric difference 110 = 8.15% of items.","own reader pairing the two raw judge stores on (persona, item key) and recomputing every quantity; independent of the sibling batch W5D and agreeing with it to the digit","run-paper16/scores is md5-identical to the lab copy (per M-014); run-paper16/scores_405b exists ONLY in git and on the laptop (a lab scan found no *405* folder under C:/Users/user4). Upstream of the vectors, so RF-12/15/16 do not apply; no aggregate file and no BH q, so RF-13 does not apply.","all 1,350 paired items used; the rates and both full distributions reproduce exactly; the second half ('score 3 is the filter') is verified in code by sibling M-015 (2_activations_ndif.py:20-21, --keep_scores default '3').",HOLDS,"HIGH - 1,350 paired items recomputed from the raw judge output",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q5q7.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q5q7.txt),"THREE THINGS FOR THE THESIS. (1) The exact gap is 0.74 pp; '0.8' is the difference of the ROUNDED rates. (2) 7.7's evidence line says 'all 1,400 paper16 rollouts re-judged' - only 1,350 were; default.jsonl (50 rollouts, the anchor persona) has no score file in either store, and line 390 of the same document already says so. (3) NEW: the two judges keep near-identical NUMBERS of rollouts but disagree about WHICH on 110 of 1,350 items (8.15%). For a sentence about the filter that builds the vectors, 8.15% of the training set changing is the relevant number, not 0.74 pp.",W6B-thesis2
O-096,"Verdict 7a: the judges are interchangeable here, and the earlier ~7-9% own100-vs-hf275 contamination gap confounded the judge with a different generation run.",~7-9%,"docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:762-763 (7.7 verdict; inventory :756, +6 offset)","run-paper16/scores + scores_405b (part a); run-hf275/axes_hf100.pt + run-hf275/published_assistant_axis.pt (hf275 column of part b); memory/persona-axis-diagnostics.md:50,91-96 (the only source of the own100 column); own100 bank = C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt - LAB ONLY, unreachable this session","part a: paired judge scores. part b: cos(axes['deception'][L], published_assistant_axis[L]) at L20/22/40/60, vs the memory note's own100 column","part a: 91.185% agreement, 0.74 pp score-3 gap (see O-095). part b: no result file holds an own100-vs-hf275 contamination comparison - the ~7-9% is prose only (DOC-ONLY).",part a YES; part b has no file to match against,"hf275 measured locally: -0.6856 / -0.6621 / -0.6097 / -0.5161 at L20/22/40/60, vs the memory note's -0.686 / -0.662 / -0.610 / -0.516 - max |diff| 0.0004. Taking the note's own100 column (-0.729/-0.710/-0.660/-0.573) as given, the RELATIVE gap is 5.9% / 6.8% / 7.6% / 9.9%, i.e. 5.9-9.9%, not 7-9%. The confound itself is verified from the thesis's own pipeline table: own100 = our roles, AA's 240 questions, ~1,200 rollouts/role, Llama-3.1-70B judge (:267); hf275 = Lu et al.'s PUBLISHED vectors, gpt-4.1-mini judge (:268) - different judge AND different generation run.",Q7 recomputation from the raw judge stores + a cosine re-measurement of the hf275 column from the local vectors; the own100 term is taken from prose and flagged,laptop copies throughout; run-hf275 is not a paper16 bank so RF-12/15/16 do not apply and it is not in RF-13's rewrite set. The own100 bank is lab-only and the lab PC is unreachable (see the INCIDENT section of audit/PROGRESS.md).,"part a's 'interchangeable' holds at the level of RATES; the two judges keep 8.15% different SETS of rollouts (110 of 1,350). Inherited slip: the hf275 column is measured against the PUBLISHED Assistant Axis; against the hf bank's own assistant direction it reads -0.6687/-0.6507/-0.5771/-0.4787, which would move the implied gap (same slippage W6A found in O-057/O-067).",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for part (a) and for the confound argument; LOW-MEDIUM for the '~7-9%' (DOC-ONLY, own100 term DEFERRED - lab unreachable, file C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt)",MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6B_q5q7.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_q5q7.txt) ; audit/scripts/claims/W6B_robust.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6B/W6B_robust.txt),"The verdict and its reasoning are sound; only the quoted magnitude is unsupported locally. Either drop '~7-9%' (the sentence works without it) or state it as '5.9-9.9% across layers 20-60, own100 vs hf275, both against the published Assistant Axis' and note that the own100 vectors exist only on the lab machine. DEFERRED (lab unreachable) applies to the own100 column only.",W6B-thesis2
