O-021,"Of four single-source baselines computed on the same 110 pairs, the mean over sources - the estimator the abstract compares against - is 0.676 (median 0.722, sign-oriented mean 0.735, best-source oracle 0.897).","0.676 (and 0.722, 0.735, 0.897)",docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:352 (table 350-355),audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json,"baselines.{mean_over_sources, median_over_sources, oriented_mean, best_source_oracle}; per_target.* for the recomputation",0.6763163062 / 0.7219698909 / 0.7353614302 / 0.8966842158,YES - all four round to the briefing's values,"mean over sources recomputed from the 110 pairs = 0.6763163062 (exact). The other three are per-TARGET statistics averaged over the 11 targets, not statistics of the flat 110: mean of per-target medians 0.7219698909, of per-target oriented means 0.7353614302, of per-target maxima 0.8966842158 - all reproduce exactly. The plain median of the 110 pairs is 0.6844, which is NOT the quoted 0.722.",own reader; each estimator rebuilt from the per-pair list and compared with the stored per_target arrays,"audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. L40, mean pooling, paper probe, seed 42.",The estimator definition matters: 'median over sources' means per-target median then average. Anyone recomputing it as the median of all 110 pairs gets 0.684 and will think the table is wrong.,HOLDS,HIGH - all four values reproduced from the per-pair list,MEDIUM-HIGH - these four numbers are what section 7 then mis-attaches to HIS baseline (see O-036),audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"Values exact. The row label '(what the abstract compares against)' is true of the ESTIMATOR but not of the VALUE - the abstract compares against his 0.732 on his six, not our 0.676 on our eleven. Harmless here; it becomes an error in section 7 (O-036).",W6C-briefing
O-023,"The principal components are not doing the work: at L20 ext_pc1 trails ext_axis1 by 0.243, and the 1-d contrast beats the 3-d subspace at every depth the collaborator ran.",0.243; 'every depth',docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:373-374,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (head 45b16d9) and f386a72, read with `git show`: src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv,matrix_baseline.csv} (L20, L40, L44 summary.csv)","summary.csv off_diagonal_mean for features ext_pc1, ext_axis1, pc1, axis1, pc3, ext_pc3",L20 ext_pc1 0.6612748487 vs ext_axis1 0.9041173922 -> -0.2428,YES for the 0.243,"0.24284 at L20 (also -0.1479 at L40 and -0.1232 at L44). 1-d vs 3-d, EXTENDED bank: ext_axis1 - ext_pc3 = +0.2204 (L20), +0.0503 (L40), +0.0235 (L44) - positive at all three. PAPER bank: axis1 - pc3 = -0.0281 (L20), +0.1925 (L40), +0.2095 (L44) - NEGATIVE at L20, i.e. the 3-d subspace (0.6792) beats the 1-d contrast (0.6511) there.",own reader over his summary.csv at all three layers,his branch at head 45b16d9 and f386a72 - identical,"On the off_diagonal_excl_hpkr column the paper bank's L20 case flips to positive (+0.0315), so the exception is driven by harm-pressure-knowledge-report - the same dataset that drives everything else in this file.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - every value read verbatim from his committed CSV,MEDIUM - it is the resolution of the withdrawn 'PC1 contradiction',audit/scripts/claims/W6C_collab.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_collab.txt),"The 0.243 is exact. 'The 1-d contrast beats the 3-d subspace at every depth you ran' is true of the EXTENDED bank (all three depths) but FALSE of the paper bank at L20, where axis1 0.6511 < pc3 0.6792. Suggested fix: say 'the extended 1-d contrast beats the extended 3-d subspace at all three depths', or add 'except axis1 vs pc3 at L20'.",W6C-briefing
O-024,"An earlier version of this briefing asserted that the collaborator scored per token while our pipeline mean-pools, and concluded that 'token aggregation alone is worth up to +0.103'; that premise is withdrawn because his pipeline mean-pools too.",+0.103,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:355-356,"git: docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md at 1a482b7 (line 227) and aea9f53 (line 247); origin/feat/persona-pc-ood at f386a72: src/probes/deception-detection/deception_detection/scripts/pool_activations.py; docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:770,1048",the quoted sentence; pool_activations.py line 84; the Q8 pooling table,"aea9f53:247 reads verbatim '**Token aggregation alone is worth up to +0.103.** Add the six-dataset subset effect (+0.079, section 5a) and 0.811 -> 0.916 is fully accounted for without anyone being wrong.'","YES - the self-quotation is verbatim, including the second sentence","The +0.103 traces to the project's own Q8 measurement (top-decile vs mean pooling, zero-shot): docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:770 gives +0.103 at L20, and :1048 records '+0.103 (L20), +0.064 (L22), +0.053 (L28), <= +0.014 at 40-48'. The retraction's own evidence also checks out: at f386a72, pool_activations.py LINE 84 is exactly `pooled.append(acts[row_mask].float().mean(0).squeeze(0).numpy())`, and the module docstring says 'the mean over the assistant response tokens'.",git history of the briefing; line-exact read of his script at the commit the briefing cites; grep of the project's own Q8 tables,git only (both branches); no lab file needed,"The line number is version-specific: at branch head 45b16d9 the same statement has moved to line 123 and reads `example.acts[example.mask]`. The briefing cites head f386a72 in section 5, so ':84' is right for the commit it names.",HOLDS,"HIGH - quotation, code line and source of +0.103 all verified",MEDIUM - a self-correction; getting it wrong would re-open a settled dispute,git show (see evidence_file); audit/scripts/claims/W6C_collab.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_collab.txt) for the branch reads,"Path nit, same family as the one the 09-23 audit already fixed for persona_ood.py: the file is `deception_detection/scripts/pool_activations.py`, not `scripts/pool_activations.py`. The docstring is paraphrased as 'the model's response tokens'; it actually says 'the assistant response tokens'.",W6C-briefing
O-025,"Kumar's abstract says the single-direction hypothesis is decisively rejected, k=1 capturing only 0.61-0.80 AUROC of the signal, with cross-domain transfer failure confirmed as geometric rather than layer-mismatch-driven.",0.61; 0.80,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:418-420 (block quote),"papers/Pressure-Testing Deception Probes in LLMs Scaling, Robustness, and the.pdf (18 pages, Sachin Kumar, LexisNexis)","page 1 abstract, clause (b); Table 6 on page 5; Figure 2 caption on page 15","abstract, verbatim: '(b) the single-direction hypothesis is decisively rejected (k=1 captures only 0.61-0.80 AUROC of the signal, with cross-domain transfer failure confirmed as geometric rather than layer-mismatch-driven;'",YES - word for word,"Table 6 (page 5) gives the k=1 row 0.609 / 0.661 / 0.804 / 0.672 for 1B / 4B / 12B / 27B, min 0.609 max 0.804 - so 0.61-0.80 is the rounded min-max of the k=1 row. Body text: 'all four models capture only 0.609-0.804 of the deception signal'.","pypdf text extraction of the PDF present in the repo, searched for the quoted strings and for the underlying table",the repo's tracked PDF; read during this audit,"Also checked the two other Kumar figures the same section quotes: style-augmented 0.979-0.983 (abstract) and 'CIs ... spanning nearly the full network, indicating weak localization' (page 5) - both present verbatim.",HOLDS,HIGH - quotation checked against the PDF opened in this audit,MEDIUM - it is the concurrent-paper threat the briefing tells the collaborator to answer,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_misc.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_misc.txt),"The briefing silently repairs an unbalanced parenthesis in the original ('of the signal), with' vs the paper's 'of the signal, with'). Substantively identical; if it is reproduced as a block quote in the paper, use [sic] or re-punctuate openly.",W6C-briefing
O-026,"Run like-for-like under leave-one-dataset-out at L40, all three persona feature sets lose to raw 8192-d logistic regression: axes 0.679->0.745 (-0.109, CI [-0.187,-0.039]), pc:deception 0.621->0.731 (-0.124, [-0.203,-0.055]), pc:unified@2 0.574->0.692 (-0.162, [-0.288,-0.059]), against raw 0.676->0.854.",0.676; 0.854; 0.679; 0.745; -0.109; 0.621; 0.731; -0.124; 0.574; 0.692; -0.162; the three CIs,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:475-480 (5d table),audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json (md5 712bca920f38b6c321fd0eeeed50bc4b); cross-check audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L40_mean_s42.json (md5 e5ddaaa13ea6aa5a4b97bbafa38592ba),"persona_lodo[feature].{single,lodo,lodo_per_target}; pooled_lodo_full; baselines.mean_over_sources; per_target.pooled_lodo_full",axes 0.6794089978 / 0.7453755531; pc:deception 0.6213570249 / 0.7307243420; pc:unified@2 0.5739826680 / 0.6920640950; raw 0.6763163062 / 0.8544753650,YES - all eight values round to the table,"vs raw pooled: axes -0.1091, pc:deception -0.1238, pc:unified@2 -0.1624. My own paired dataset-level bootstrap over the 11 targets (B=10,000, default_rng(42)) gives CI95 [-0.187,-0.039] P(>=0) 0.0006 ; [-0.203,-0.055] P 0.0001 ; [-0.288,-0.059] P 0.0002 - the three stated intervals reproduce to 3 dp, and none of them is in the file, so this is a genuine re-derivation rather than a read-back.",own loader + own paired dataset bootstrap over the 11 per-target values (the CIs are not stored in the artifact),audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. The audit file was written by the 5d review run; run-premise has no Drive copy (RF-10). No BH q involved.,"One layer (40), one pooling (mean), one seed, one probe ('paper'). The raw pooled figure 0.8545 also appears independently in premise_L40_mean_s42.json's summary, and the two agree exactly.",HOLDS,"HIGH - the three confidence intervals were independently re-derived, not copied",HIGH - it is the briefing's single strongest claim against the method,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"All eleven quantities exact. Worth telling the collaborator that this is a single-layer, single-seed result, which the briefing does not say.",W6C-briefing
O-027,Pooling helps the persona features too - pc:unified@2 gains +0.118 from leave-one-dataset-out pooling - so diversity is not something personas provide.,+0.118,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:484,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json,persona_lodo['pc:unified@2'].lodo - .single,0.6920640950 - 0.5739826680 = +0.1181,YES,+0.11808. The other two features gain +0.0660 (axes) and +0.1094 (pc:deception); raw gains +0.1782. So pc:unified@2 is the LARGEST persona gain and the briefing quotes the most favourable of the three.,own reader; all four gains computed so the quoted one can be placed,audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch.,"The argument ('diversity is not something personas provide') holds for all three features, so picking the largest does not change the conclusion - but raw still gains more (+0.178) than any persona feature.",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),Exact. The sentence would be stronger with 'between +0.066 and +0.118' than with the single best figure.,W6C-briefing
O-028,"The secondary mean-of-directions result is +0.028 over pooled leave-one-dataset-out, 95% CI [+0.005, +0.052].",+0.028; +0.005; +0.052,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:496,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json; also audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/why/why_L40_s42.json (md5 db563a7ccb9ceb98cd1dc2ab799a69da),"bootstrap['mean_of_directions-pooled_lodo_full'].{diff,lo,hi}; per_target.mean_of_directions vs per_target.pooled_lodo_full","file: diff 0.0283541533, lo 0.0045082540, hi 0.0523446105",YES,"recomputed from the 11 per-target values: +0.028354, own CI95 [+0.004610, +0.052037], P(<=0) 0.0088 (B=10,000, default_rng(42)). Scalars: mean_of_directions 0.8828295183 (the same value appears in why_L40_s42.json), pooled_lodo_full 0.8544753650.","own paired dataset bootstrap over the 11 targets, independent of the stored interval","audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. L40, mean pooling, seed 42.","The interval is narrow and its lower bound sits at +0.0045; a different bootstrap implementation (mine) moves it to +0.0046, i.e. the conclusion 'it clears, barely' is implementation-stable.",HOLDS,HIGH - stored interval and an independent re-derivation agree,MEDIUM - the briefing deliberately demotes it,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"Exact. This is the +0.028 that F-86's 0.883 'mean of ten single-source directions' sits behind, and the briefing's demotion of it is warranted.",W6C-briefing
O-029,"The mean-of-directions result clears, but its lower bound is +0.005, so it is not a headline.",+0.005,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:497,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json,bootstrap['mean_of_directions-pooled_lodo_full'].lo,lo = 0.0045082540,YES to the stated precision (0.0045 -> +0.005),"my own bootstrap gives +0.004610. Both are above zero, so 'it clears' is correct; the exact bound is +0.0045, which the briefing rounds UP to +0.005.",own paired dataset bootstrap over the 11 targets,audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch.,"P(<=0) = 0.0088 in my bootstrap, i.e. it clears a one-sided 1% threshold as well. The claim is a self-deflation, so rounding the bound up is the conservative direction only if you are trying to sound confident - here it makes the result look very slightly better than it is.",HOLDS,HIGH,LOW-MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"Exact to the quoted precision. If a reviewer recomputes, they get +0.0045; writing '+0.0045' would be unimpeachable.",W6C-briefing
O-030,"In the sarcasm pilot, deadpan is producible: the marker rate falls to 0.00 at variants v4 and v5.","0.00 (v4, v5)",docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:575 (and the table label at :573),"audit/cache/labpc/cap/run-sarc-pilot/marker_report.json (md5 bcc633166d53e73a565d76318e977c75, 4,938 B, n=300)","markers[arm].per_variant (five entries, v1..v5) for the three arms","pc_ironic_critic [0.85, 0.15, 0.10, 0.00, 0.00]; pc_sycophant [0.85, 1.00, 0.50, 0.00, 0.05]; pc_sincere_critic [0.60, 0.15, 0.15, 0.25, 0.05]",PARTIAL - exactly 0.00/0.00 for the ironic arm only,"ironic v4 = 0.00, v5 = 0.00 (both exact). Sycophant v4 = 0.00 but v5 = 0.05. Sincere-critic v4 = 0.25, v5 = 0.05. The lexical table the same section prints does reproduce exactly: ironic vs sycophant, all v1-v5 raw 0.9525 / stripped 0.9472; v4+v5 raw 0.9194 / stripped 0.9213.","own reader over the cached marker report; all three arms printed, not just the one the sentence is about","audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. cap/run-sarc-pilot is lab-only with no Drive copy (RF-10). A marker_report_partial.json (n=100, ironic arm only) carries the same per-variant vector.","PROGRESS.md records that the sarcasm-pilot status file logged a stripped AUROC of 0.947 at 02:29 and 0.921 at 15:55 for different subsets - the 0.921 here is the v4+v5 subset, so the briefing's table uses the later, narrower one and labels it correctly.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - read directly from the artifact,MEDIUM - it is the 'encouraging half' of a negative result,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_misc.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_misc.txt),"True of the IRONIC arm, which is the arm 'deadpan' refers to. The table header 'v4+v5 (marker rate 0.00)' labels the ironic-vs-sycophant comparison, and the sycophant arm reads 0.05 at v5. Safe wording: 'the ironic arm's marker rate falls to 0.00 at v4 and v5 (the sycophant arm to 0.00 and 0.05)'.",W6C-briefing
O-031,"Running both of the collaborator's arms through our crossgen on our eleven datasets is done: the kd bank supplies 49-74% of the margin, and both arms lose to a pooled probe.",49%; 74%,"docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:614 (section 7 table), backed by the 5a table at :269-275","raw baseline recomputed from run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L{20,40}_s42.json (local, md5 414a8f1adc1bd55534e9cc2145397249 and d7616aa50814267e38bd38931e25a6a0 - the latter byte-identical to the cached lab copy); pooled from audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L{20,40}_mean_s42.json; the two arms from run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/mean_L{20,40}_s42.json (LAB ONLY)","share = (ext_axis1 - axis1) / (ext_axis1 - raw); raw = off-diagonal mean of results[feature='raw',probe='paper'] over the 110 pairs; pooled = summary.pooled_lodo",briefing 5a table: 74% (L20) and 49% (L40),YES,"raw recomputed here: 0.6289 (L20) and 0.6623 (L40), 110 pairs - matching the 5a table exactly. pooled recomputed here: 0.8027 and 0.8545 - matching exactly. With P12's lab-side arms (axis1 0.6572/0.7325, ext_axis1 0.7386/0.7996) the share is 74.2% and 48.9%, and both arms lose to pooled: axis1 by +0.1455 / +0.1220 and ext_axis1 by +0.0641 / +0.0549.",three of the five rows of the 5a table re-derived this session from local and cached files; the two collab arms DEFERRED (lab unreachable) and taken from batch P12,audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. Would need run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json for a full re-derivation.,"'49-74%' is the range over TWO layers. Over all 21 layers, mean-pooled, the same share runs 2%-114% (median 63%) and under last-token -156% to +145% - which the same document says two sections earlier. The section-7 one-liner does not carry that caveat.",HOLDS,MEDIUM-HIGH - the arithmetic and three of five inputs re-derived here; the two arms rest on P12's re-derivation,HIGH - it is the headline of the whole revision,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_eleven.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_eleven.txt),"LEVEL-2 PARTLY DEFERRED. The raw and pooled rows of the 5a table reproduce exactly. The 09-23 audit addition 'and axis1 by 0.146 and 0.122' is CORRECT (+0.1455, +0.1220). Suggest 'roughly half at L40, three quarters at L20 - but see the 2%-114% range across depth' so the section-7 line does not travel alone.",W6C-briefing
O-032,"Run through the same leave-one-dataset-out harness, the persona method loses to raw pooled logistic regression by 0.11-0.16 AUROC.",0.11; 0.16,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:616 (section 7 table),audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json,persona_lodo[feature].lodo minus pooled_lodo_full,"the 5d table it points at: -0.109, -0.124, -0.162",YES,"-0.1091 (axes), -0.1238 (pc:deception), -0.1624 (pc:unified@2). Rounded, the range is 0.11 to 0.16.",own reader; all three differences recomputed from the stored scalars and cross-checked against the per-target arrays,"audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. Single layer (40), single seed, mean pooling.","All three losses clear a paired dataset-level bootstrap over the 11 targets (P(>=0) 0.0006 / 0.0001 / 0.0002), so the range is not an artefact of picking the ends.",HOLDS,HIGH,HIGH - the briefing proposes this as the paper's revised contribution,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"Exact. Same measurement as O-034, which states it in prose.",W6C-briefing
O-033,"In the format-matched control, swapping what the six negative-side personas say costs only about +0.03, clears no significance test at any layer, and removing the six entirely costs two to four times as much.",~+0.03; 'no significance test at any layer'; 'two to four times',docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:630-631,"C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/{cap_s23,cap_ctrl}/matrices/{mean,last}_L*_s42.json (90 files) - LAB ONLY, in no branch and not in audit/cache/","sycophancy_mt COLUMN of each feature's 11x11 matrix, mean over the 10 sources; content = pc:capitulation@2 - pc:cap_vs_neutral@2, presence = pc:capitulation@2 - pc:cap_only_ctrl@2; per-layer paired dataset bootstrap over the 10 sources","F-94 (kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4107-4180): content mean +0.0356, clears at 3 of 21 layers (L0, L12, L36); presence mean +0.0730, clears at 15 of 21; ratio about 2:1 mean-pooled and about 1:1 last-token; 'No ratio should be quoted at all'",NO for two of the three parts - see notes,"DEFERRED. Using the audit's own earlier re-derivation of those raw matrices (audit/claims/F-94.md, batch P2-pooled, script audit/scripts/claims/p2p_F94_lab.py): content mean +0.0356 and it CLEARS at L0 (+0.0524), L12 (+0.0171) and L36 (+0.0290); presence mean +0.0730, clearing at 15 of 21; presence/content = 2.05x on the means, with per-layer ratios spanning 0.42x (L8) to 4.86x (L40).",DEFERRED (lab unreachable). Ratios computed here from the F-94.md table; the underlying matrices were read read-only on the lab PC by batch P2-pooled.,"audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. Would need run-crossgen/kd11/banks/{cap_s23,cap_ctrl}/matrices/. The cap_ctrl completeness gate is separately broken by RF-6, but all 42 matrices exist.","Under LAST-token pooling F-94 records content +0.0346 and presence +0.0373, i.e. about 1:1, and content CLEARS at L28, L32 and L36 there too. So the 'clears nothing' claim fails under both poolings.",PARTLY HOLDS,"MEDIUM-HIGH - the magnitude and the counter-examples come from an audit re-derivation of the raw matrices, but not one re-run this session",MEDIUM-HIGH - it is the qualification the briefing attaches to Claim 2,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_misc.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_misc.txt),"The '~+0.03' is right (+0.0356). The other two clauses are not. (1) 'clears no significance test at any layer' is FALSE: the content effect clears at L0, L12 and L36 mean-pooled, and at L28/L32/L36 last-token. (2) 'two to four times that' is a ratio F-94 explicitly says should not be quoted at all: it is 2.05x on the 21-layer means, ~1:1 under last-token pooling, and ranges 0.42x-4.86x by layer. Safe wording, from F-94's own bottom line: 'swapping what the negative-side personas say costs ~+0.035 and rarely clears; removing them costs ~+0.073 and usually does.' THIS ONE WOULD TRAVEL INTO THE PAPER.",W6C-briefing
O-034,In a like-for-like leave-one-dataset-out comparison the trained persona-coordinates method loses to ordinary logistic regression on raw activations by 0.11-0.16 AUROC.,0.11; 0.16,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:644-645,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json,"persona_lodo[feature].lodo minus pooled_lodo_full, all three features",5d table: -0.109 / -0.124 / -0.162,YES,"-0.1091, -0.1238, -0.1624 - range 0.109 to 0.162, i.e. 0.11-0.16 rounded. All three clear a paired dataset bootstrap over 11 targets.",own reader plus own bootstrap (see O-026),"audit's cached lab copies under audit/cache/labpc/ (lab PC UNREACHABLE this session: Tailscale down). No BH q-value quoted by any claim in this batch. One layer, one seed, one pooling, one probe.","The claim is stated in the paragraph that proposes it as the paper's contribution, so its single-layer basis matters: no layer sweep of the persona LODO harness exists in run-premise (only L20/L32/L40 for the clustered variant, and those do not carry persona features).",HOLDS,HIGH for the number; the SCOPE is single-layer and the sentence does not say so,HIGH - proposed as the paper's revised headline,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"Exact. Recommend adding 'at layer 40, mean-pooled' - four of this project's headline margins have already failed a layer sweep (memory note 'No margin from one layer').",W6C-briefing
O-035,"The 0.732 the abstract compares against is a single-source trained baseline - one dataset trained on, another tested on - averaged over the collaborator's six datasets at layer 40.",0.732,"docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:653-654 (also :248, :317)","origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (head 45b16d9) and f386a72, read with `git show`: src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv,matrix_baseline.csv}",summary.csv row features='baseline' col off_diagonal_mean; matrix_baseline.csv,summary.csv L40 baseline off_diagonal_mean = 0.7320325942,YES,"recomputed as the off-diagonal mean of his 6x6 matrix_baseline.csv = 0.732027 over n=30 pairs (the 6e-6 gap is his own rounding in the CSV). It is a per-target mean over the five other sources, averaged over the six targets - i.e. a single-source mean, exactly as described. L20 reads 0.6478 and L44 0.7156.",own reader; the summary value recomputed from the raw transfer matrix,his branch at head 45b16d9 and f386a72 - identical,"The per-target spread is wide: 0.571 (harm_refusal_choice) to 0.827 (instruct_dishonesty) at L40, and the worst single pair is 0.060.",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM-HIGH - it is the baseline the whole abstract rests on,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_collab.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_collab.txt); audit/scripts/claims/W6C_collab2.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_collab2.txt),"Exact, and the characterisation 'single-source mean' is right.",W6C-briefing
O-036,A reviewer may not accept 0.732 as 'the trained probe' when the median over the same pairs is 0.722 and the sign-oriented mean is 0.735.,0.722; 0.735,docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md:653-655,"origin/feat/persona-pc-ood (head 45b16d9) and f386a72, read with `git show`: src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/{summary.csv,zero_shot.csv,matrix_baseline.csv} (matrix_baseline.csv at L20/L40/L44) vs audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json","per-target median over sources and per-target sign-oriented mean, averaged over targets - the same two estimators as our audit file's baselines block","the briefing's 0.722 and 0.735 are, verbatim, OUR values in the 5b table (audit_L40_s42.json baselines.median_over_sources 0.7219698909 and oriented_mean 0.7353614302), computed over our 110 pairs on our eleven datasets",NO for the stated scope: 'the same pairs' as 0.732 means HIS 30 pairs,"Applying the identical estimators to HIS 6x6 matrix_baseline.csv: L40 median over sources 0.7608, sign-oriented mean 0.7850 (mean over sources 0.7320, oracle 0.9186). L20: 0.6581 / 0.7448 against a mean of 0.6478. L44: 0.7435 / 0.7659 against 0.7157. So on HIS pairs the two alternatives are 0.761 and 0.785, not 0.722 and 0.735.","own script applying the audit file's own estimator definitions (per-target statistic, then averaged over targets) to his committed transfer matrix",his branch read out of git; our side from the cached lab audit file. Both verified during this session.,"The direction of the argument is unaffected and in fact strengthened: on his own pairs the median (0.761) and the sign-oriented mean (0.785) both exceed 0.732 by MORE than our figures do, so the abstract's margin shrinks further under either alternative.",DOES NOT HOLD,HIGH - both sides measured this session with the same estimator definitions,HIGH - it is the closing sentence of the document and the one the collaborator is most likely to paste into a rebuttal,audit/scripts/claims/W6C_collab2.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_collab2.txt); audit/scripts/claims/W6C_premise.py (out audit/phase2/out/W6C/W6C_premise.txt),"ERROR THAT WOULD REACH THE COLLABORATOR. 0.722 and 0.735 are our eleven-dataset numbers; 'the same pairs' as 0.732 are his six-dataset ones, where the same estimators read 0.7608 and 0.7850. Fix: either quote his numbers ('the median over the same pairs is 0.761 and the sign-oriented mean 0.785') or keep ours and say so ('on our own eleven datasets the same three estimators read 0.676 / 0.722 / 0.735'). The section-5b table's row label '(what the abstract compares against)' is what seeds the confusion. SPREAD: the same conflation is already in audit/phase3/DRAFT_GAPS.md:424-428 (A-13), which advises the collaborator that 'the draft compares against the lowest of these' using our 0.676/0.722/0.735; his own three are 0.732/0.761/0.785. The lead should fix A-13 too. Claim O-022 (the table on OUR pairs) is unaffected.",W6C-briefing
