O-039,"Every kd headline is quoted at L40 while L44 is the peak, by +0.007 (vs raw) and +0.009 (vs datapca).",+0.007; +0.009,"docs/ROADMAP_TO_DEFENCE.md:115 (Tier 2), via docs/OPEN_DECISIONS.md:102-103 and kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:840 (F-34)","audit/cache/labpc/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd_s23/significance.json (md5 c6dd8f7bdb9205f5f0f8225766fda614, 5544 tests) AND run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd_s23/significance.json (committed, md5 186431f0f45a598551dd6d0b3f029bef, 468 tests)","tests[] comparison in {pc:unified - raw, pc:unified - datapca}, block '9' (=10 datasets, 90 pairs), pooling='mean', probe='paper' -> diff, dataset_ci95, dataset_q_bh, significant_datasets","pc:unified - raw: L40 +0.1082, L44 +0.1156 -> L44-L40 = +0.0074; pc:unified - datapca: L40 +0.1199, L44 +0.1291 -> +0.0092. Identical in both copies.",YES - +0.0074 and +0.0092 round to +0.007 and +0.009,"Full 21-layer profiles recomputed: vs raw positive at 16/21, argmax L44; vs datapca positive at 17/21, argmax L44. Neither L40 nor L44 is significant: significant_datasets=false at both; q 0.100/0.107 (5,544 family) and 0.074/0.075 (468 family); F-34's quoted q=0.130 is the superseded 3,276 family.","own reader (audit/scripts/claims/W6D_misc.py) filtering the tests[] array by key, both copies","cache copy is the extended 21-layer lab file; committed copy is the pre-extension 3-layer one. Both give the same diffs, so the RF-13 regeneration did not move them. BH q DOES depend on the family (3,276 -> 5,544).","Scope: this is the kd_s23 pc:unified - raw margin only. F-75 (80 layers, matched slice axes) puts the argmax at L77 with L40 0.7393 > L44 0.7321; F-76's bootstrap argmax is median L31, 95% [L5,L79], 0.0% on L40; F-91 puts the crossgen peak at L32. 'L44 is the peak' is not a project-wide fact.",HOLDS,HIGH - two independent copies read by key,LOW-MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6D_misc.py -> audit/phase2/out/W6D/W6D_misc.txt,The re-quote is cosmetic: +0.007 on a margin whose 95% CI is ~0.17 wide and which clears neither BH nor the dataset bootstrap at either layer. Doing it would NOT move the headlines to any layer the other three sweeps call optimal.,W6D-ownerdocs
O-041,"On Claim 4 (the matched-control margin is a scale-dependent ceiling artifact) Reviewer A said APPARENTLY NOVEL ('your best card') and Reviewer B said ADJACENT, citing Kantamneni et al. (ICML 2025) and Kumar (2605.27958).",none measurable (the inventory's '5.2795' is a parse artifact of the arXiv id 2605.27958); the related figure in the same document is 'corr -0.76' at :103,"docs/NOVELTY_ASSESSMENT.md:49 (and :103, :97-100)","audit/phase1/sessions/findings_printed_numbers.csv (session b035ccb3, 2026-09-21T05:38:46Z, line 9620); audit/phase1/sessions/findings_targets.csv:41; audit/papers.csv; audit/claims.csv rows F-74 and F-63",printed_snippet of the pasted reviewer TL;DR; papers.csv arxiv_id/pdf_present; F-74 level2_value; F-63 verdict,"Reviewer A corroborated: the pasted TL;DR reads 'Only three claims are defensible as genuine contributions and should carry the paper: Claim 4 (the matched-control margin is a scale-dependent ceiling artifact...), Claim 5 ..., and Claim 8 ...'. Reviewer B: NOT FOUND in any file; 'Kantamneni' appears nowhere outside NOVELTY_ASSESSMENT.md.",PARTIAL - 1 of 2 reviewer reports recoverable,"F-74 (verdict HOLDS): corr(raw, random@2 - raw) = -0.7684 vs analytic null -0.7462 and permuted null -0.7456 [-0.7986,-0.6892], P=0.2135 -> INSIDE the null; the uncoupled replacement test gives slope -0.100, r -0.067, mean margin +0.0063. F-74's status line says it supersedes the -0.76 as evidence for Claim 4. F-63 (the scaling half) is PARTLY HOLDS: 3B cell is that rung's best layer and the decline is mean-pooling-only (F-100/F-102).","session-transcript mining table (read, not re-run) + reuse of the already-checked F-74/F-63 rows of audit/claims.csv",git HEAD docs; session table from audit/phase1/sessions (2026-09-21 sessions); no compute,"audit/papers.csv: Kumar 2605.27958, Kirch 2511.17408, Yoo&Skapars 2609.02893 and Lu 2601.10387 all have PDFs; Kantamneni et al. has NO row at all (no arXiv id in the doc, no PDF, no notes); Vennemeyer 2509.21305 is CITED, NO PDF and its title was not identified.",PARTLY HOLDS,MEDIUM on the review-verdict half (one of two reports recoverable); HIGH on the F-74 half,HIGH,no new script; reads audit/phase1/sessions/findings_printed_numbers.csv and audit/claims.csv,"LIVE RISK FOR THE REFRAME. The document nominates Claim 4 as a lead contribution and still states its mechanism as 'ceiling artifact, corr -0.76' (:103), but F-74 - written the same day, verdict HOLDS - shows that -0.76 is mathematical coupling inside its own null (P=0.21) and explicitly withdraws it as evidence for Claim 4, and the clean uncoupled test does not support Claim 4 either. Reviewer B's decisive counter-citation has never been opened here.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] PHASE 4 AMENDMENT (verdict unchanged). METHODS NOTE: this claim is about an EVENT (what two reviewers said), not a measurement, so 'raw data' would mean the review outputs themselves - which are not in the repo (no reviews folder). An independent blinded re-derivation correctly returned NO RAW DATA. Such claims cannot be scored either way by a raw-data check; they are attested, not reproduced. Phase 4 adds that the two papers attributed to Reviewer B are not in papers/, so the citation is itself unverifiable.",W6D-ownerdocs
O-042,"Setting of the pooled-training result: Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct, residual stream layer 40, mean-pooled over response tokens, eleven datasets, logistic regression on 8192-d activations, class-balanced training, 80/20 splits BY ITEM ID.",layer 40; 11 datasets; 8192-d; 80/20,docs/REVIEW_REQUEST_POOLING.md:15-18,audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/premise_L40_mean_s42.json (md5 e5ddaaa13ea6aa5a4b97bbafa38592ba); src/assistant_axis_ndif/30_premise.py; src/assistant_axis_ndif/9_persona_probes.py; src/assistant_axis_ndif/2_activations_ndif.py,"layer, pooling, probe, seed, datasets, n_train, pairs; 30_premise.py:79,102-108,114","layer=40; pooling=mean; probe=paper; seed=42; 11 datasets; 110 pairs; n_train {single_mean 666, pooled_full 7336, pooled_match 414}",6 of 7 sub-claims YES; the split description NO,"30_premise.py:106 splits with rng.permutation(n) over ROWS; 'group_split' occurs 0 times in the file although 9_persona_probes.py defines group_split(meta, frac, seed). --frac default 0.8 confirmed (:79). P.balance() is called on every training index set (:114). 8192-d confirmed at 25_zeroshot_nulls.py:90 and 30_premise.py:97,185. 2_activations_ndif.py:185-204 pools the LAST ASSISTANT SPAN only.",read the producing source line by line; audit/scripts/claims/W6D_premise.py prints the lines and the grep count,"lab copy 2026-09-21, pre-RF-13; no bank, no BH family, no k","F-90 independently found the same split issue and drew the right consequence: it does not touch any transfer number (LODO/off-diagonal probes never train on the target's rows) but it inflates the in-domain ceiling 0.9506, which is row 4 of the document's own table.",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - read from the producing source, not prose",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6D_premise.py -> audit/phase2/out/W6D/W6D_premise.txt,"'80/20 splits by item id' is FALSE for every number in this document: the split is a plain row permutation. ai_liar is 54 scenarios x 5 samples, so samples of one item straddle train and test. This is the header paragraph of a document being sent for external adversarial review, and it describes a grouping the code does not do while displaying the one number that grouping would change.",W6D-ownerdocs
