O-097,"Two abandon-gates were registered in the design document, with thresholds, before generation - G1 lowest ironic marker rate <= 0.20 and G2 bag-of-words AUROC <= 0.65 grouped by item - with G2's rationale given as 'the design's own words'.",0.65; 0.20,docs/thesis/sarcasm-pilot-negative-result.md:70-75,"git history of cap/docs/SARCASM_DESIGN.md, cap/scripts/run_sarc_pilot.ps1, cap/scripts/score_sarcasm_markers.py at 3d80071 / 5ced550 / aea9f53 / b34ff2e (git show, no checkout); audit/phase2/out/P7_status_files.txt (lab status dump)","occurrence counts of '0.65', '0.20', '0.75' per file per commit; chain START/generate/verdict timestamps",'0.65' occurs 0 times in cap/docs/SARCASM_DESIGN.md at EVERY commit and in the working tree. It first appears in run_sarc_pilot.ps1 at b34ff2e (2026-09-21 21:48:54). '0.20' is in run_sarc_pilot.ps1 from aea9f53 (21:25:55) but never in the design document. '0.75' occurs once in the design document at every commit.,NO,"Generation window from the preserved chain status: START 21:21:17, '1 generate ... PASS' 21:40:53, 'VERDICT PRODUCIBLE' + 'stripped=0.947' printed 21:44:27. The 0.65 enters the repository 21:48:54 - after the data AND after the number. v1 of the design (3d80071, 17:48, before anything was generated) registered 'If it separates sarcastic from sincere above ~0.75 ... the bank is dead'; v2 (5ced550, 19:03, still before generation) REMOVED the number: 'report selectivity ... rather than a bare number against an arbitrary 0.75'. The quoted 'design's own words' are the print statements at score_sarcasm_markers.py:198-199.","own git-history sweep in audit/scripts/claims/W6D_misc.py (git show only, read-only), timestamps from batch P7's lab status dump","git HEAD + four historical commits; no lab write; the sarc-pilot status files are P7's read-only dump (RF-14 means each chain trigger truncates and rewrites that file, so only three snapshots survive)",The gate failure is robust to the correction: measured 0.947 (all variants) and 0.921 (unmarked v4+v5) both exceed 0.65 AND v1's pre-registered ~0.75.,DOES NOT HOLD,"HIGH - commit timestamps and byte counts, not prose",HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6D_misc.py -> audit/phase2/out/W6D/W6D_misc.txt,"THE PRE-REGISTRATION CLAIM OF THE PROJECT'S FLAGSHIP NEGATIVE RESULT DOES NOT SURVIVE ITS OWN GIT HISTORY. The 0.65 is in no version of the design document and was written into the chain 8 minutes after the number it judges was first printed. Section 5 already concedes the gate RULE was absent on 09-21; this shows the THRESHOLD was too. Honest restatement: the design registered a separability abandon-condition before generation (v1, ~0.75), v2 replaced it with a selectivity criterion, the 0.65 operationalisation came after the first number - and the measured 0.921-0.947 fails every version of the bar.",W6D-ownerdocs
O-098,"Grouped-by-item bag-of-words AUROC separating the ironic from the sycophantic arm over all five variants is 0.953 raw / 0.947 with marker tokens stripped, n = 200.",0.953; 0.947; 200,docs/thesis/sarcasm-pilot-negative-result.md:116,"audit/cache/labpc/cap/run-sarc-pilot/responses/{pc_ironic_critic,pc_sycophant}.jsonl (md5 bdb597f5..., 2f7e6de7...); marker_report.json (md5 bcc63316...)","marker_report.json['lexical'] = {auroc_raw, auroc_stripped, marker_effect, n}","stored: auroc_raw 0.9525, auroc_stripped 0.9472, n 200",YES to 3 dp,"Two implementations from the raw rollouts: repo functions 0.9527 / 0.9472; independent sklearn CountVectorizer(min_df=3) + leave-one-question-out LogisticRegression 0.9527 / 0.9472. n = 200 confirmed (100 ironic + 100 sycophantic, 5 variants x 20 questions).",audit/scripts/claims/W6D_sarcasm.py - implementation A (cap/scripts/score_sarcasm_markers.py functions) and implementation B (own pipeline),"marker_report.json was REGENERATED in the RF-13 wave (2026-09-22 15:55) over the ORIGINAL 09-21 21:26-21:40 responses; the responses did not change, so the recompute is the load-bearing check",all four table rows recomputed; see O-099/O-100/O-101,HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6D_sarcasm.py -> audit/phase2/out/W6D/W6D_sarcasm.txt,"The only row of section 3.2 that exists in a file. The stored 0.9525 differs from a fresh run by 2e-4 (fold ordering), inside the quoted precision.",W6D-ownerdocs
