O-102,The reading that the ironic arm becomes less legibly ironic as the deadpan instruction strengthens (2.85 -> 2.10) does not survive its control: the sincere arm declines over the same range to exactly the same value.,2.85; 2.10; full 3x5 table plus means 2.59 / 2.37 / 2.44,docs/thesis/sarcasm-pilot-negative-result.md:140-152,"audit/cache/labpc/cap/run-sarc-pilot/scores/{pc_ironic_critic,pc_sincere_critic,pc_sycophant}.json (md5 aeaa2c78..., 9f5a1f10..., 34e97b05...)","per-response judge role score 0-3, keyed pos_p<variant>_q<question>, averaged per variant",no per-variant table is stored anywhere; marker_report.json carries only the arm means,"arm means YES (2.59 / 2.37 / 2.44, already verified as F-93's amendment); the per-variant table has no stored counterpart",ironic 2.85/2.85/2.60/2.55/2.10 (mean 2.59); sincere 2.85/2.25/2.40/2.25/2.10 (mean 2.37); sycophant 2.45/2.25/2.55/2.15/2.80 (mean 2.44); n = 100 per arm. All 18 cells and all three means exact.,"own reader over the raw judge output (audit/scripts/claims/W6D_sarcasm.py), variant parsed from the score key","md5-verified cached lab scores (09-21 21:42-21:44), unchanged by the RF-13 wave","the self-correction is arithmetically right: sincere starts at 2.85 and ends at 2.10, identically to ironic, and its instruction says nothing about markers; the sycophantic sequence is non-monotone and its rise rests on one cell",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6D_sarcasm.py -> audit/phase2/out/W6D/W6D_sarcasm.txt,"No spread, no per-item variance and no test accompanies these means - 20 items per cell, one judge, one pass. The document's own caveat stands and should be kept: this used the standard role-adherence judge, not the blind five-rating protocol the design specifies, so it cannot separate literal from intended valence.",W6D-ownerdocs
O-103,"The pilot's own chain reports 3a markers PASS and 3b separability measured=bag-of-words AUROC stripped=0.947 predicted=<=0.65 GATE FAILED, with VERDICT TEACHER-FORCED (0.947).",0.947; 0.65; 0.00; 0.20,docs/thesis/sarcasm-pilot-negative-result.md:199-204 (section 5),audit/phase2/out/P7_status_files.txt (md5 e6f6a80ecaac9b9bdd66952fa2de3115) - batch P7's read-only dump of the lab logs/sarc_pilot.status and its two preserved predecessors,"the three sarc_pilot.status snapshots: 2026-09-21 21:45 (buggy), 2026-09-22 02:29 (pre-e2e), 2026-09-22 15:55 (current)","The quoted block matches the 2026-09-22 02:29 file verbatim ('measured=bag-of-words AUROC, markers stripped=0.947 ... GATE FAILED', 'separable (0.947)'). The CURRENT file (15:55) reads 'measured=bag-of-words AUROC on unmarked(v4,v5), markers stripped=0.921 ... GATE FAILED' and 'separable (0.921)'.","matches a SUPERSEDED snapshot, not the current chain","Both numbers are correct measurements of different subsets and both were recomputed here (O-098: 0.9472 all variants; O-100: 0.9213 unmarked v4+v5). Both fail the 0.65 bar, so the verdict is identical either way. The 09-21 21:45 file does log 'VERDICT PRODUCIBLE' with 'stripped=0.947' on the next line and no 3b gate at all, exactly as section 5 describes.",text comparison against P7's preserved status dump plus my own recompute of both subsets,"status text from P7's read-only lab dump; RF-14 (the DONE guard can never fire) means every chain trigger truncates and rewrites this .status file, which is why only three snapshots survive",F-104's account (the fix was written 09-21 but never copied to the machine until 09-22) is consistent: the 02:29 file is the first to carry a 3b gate line at all,PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6D_sarcasm.py -> audit/phase2/out/W6D/W6D_sarcasm.txt,Internal inconsistency to fix: section 3.2 quotes 0.921 as 'the measured value' against the 0.65 threshold (:121) while section 5 presents 0.947 as what 'the chain reports'