M-049,"On the sycophancy_mt corpus, random unit directions reach |AUROC-0.5| of about 0.13-0.17 at the 95th percentile, so a bare zero-shot AUROC means little without the null.",0.13; 0.17,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q10-sycophancy-axis-inverted.md:31,run-coords/zeroshot_nulls.json; run-coords/q10_sycophancy_axis.json,"sycophancy_mt.{L40_mean,L40_last,L44_mean,L44_last}.random_p95_auroc_dev ; random.{mean,last}.per_layer_abs_dev_p95","zeroshot_nulls (1,000 directions): L40 mean 0.1304, L40 last 0.1700, L44 mean 0.1131, L44 last 0.1636. q10 file (50 directions x 21 layers): mean 0.1431, last 0.1400","partly - the stated 0.13-0.17 is exactly the L40-mean/L40-last pair and covers 3 of the 4 stored settings, but L44 mean is 0.1131, below the stated floor",same numbers recomputed as abs(value-0.5) from the stored p95 AUROCs,read random_p95_auroc_dev in both files and converted to a deviation,"both files local, git-tracked, clean, 2026-09-17; n_random = 1000 in zeroshot_nulls.json","the best-of-21-layers null is much wider: q10 file best_of_layers_p95 0.1935 (mean) / 0.1833 (last), max 0.2232 / 0.1893. Quoting 0.13-0.17 for a best-layer claim would understate the null by ~0.05",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - the numbers are unambiguous; only the stated range is,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q10.py,"The measured range over the four stored sycophancy_mt settings is 0.113-0.170, not 0.13-0.17; the floor comes from L44 mean. This does not change the conclusion (it makes the null slightly WIDER to beat at one setting, not narrower). But a future session quoting ""0.13"" as the smallest null would be quoting a number the file does not have. Also: there are two different nulls in play (50 dirs in the q10 file, 1,000 in zeroshot_nulls.json) and a best-of-layers null nearly 0.05 wider - state which one is meant.",W6E-memory-q
