M-051,"On the soft-trigger corpora, deceptive rows answer ""True"" 37% of the time against 61% for honest rows, so the answer token alone gives AUROC ~0.62; scored within one answer token the raw probe still reaches 0.946-0.961 and the zero-shot axis 0.83-0.92 (layer 44, last token).",37%; 61%; 0.62; 0.946; 0.961; 0.83; 0.92,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q11-sleeper-detection-is-falsity.md:27,run-coords/q11_sleeper_L44_last.json,"tests.token_stratified[raw|soft-trigger-*|{True,False}].{n,n_pos,probe_from_instructed-deception,zeroshot} ; token_only|soft-trigger-*","pooled over the 3 organisms: deceptive say ""True"" 1116/3000 = 37.20%; honest 1842/3000 = 61.40%; token-only AUROC = 0.6210 (stored per-organism token_only: 0.6165 / 0.6275 / 0.6190). Within-token raw probe 0.9461-0.9608; within-token zero-shot 0.8288-0.9181","yes - 37%, 61%, ~0.62, 0.946-0.961 and 0.83-0.92 all reproduce","the 37/61 split was RECOMPUTED from the stored per-cell row counts (n, n_pos) rather than read: sum over the three organisms of n_pos for the ""True"" cell / total deceptive rows",counts summed from the stored token_stratified cells; token-only AUROC recomputed as (TPR+TNR)/2 for the binary predictor,"local git-tracked, clean, 2026-09-16 20:44","per organism the ""True"" share is 39.2 / 35.9 / 36.5 % for deceptive and 62.5 / 61.4 / 60.3 % for honest, so the pooled 37/61 is representative. At layer 20 the within-token raw probe falls to 0.6907-0.8611 and the AXES within-token to 0.4998-0.5981",HOLDS,HIGH - recomputed from counts,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q11.py,"37% / 61% are POOLED over the three soft-trigger organisms (1,000 deceptive and 1,000 honest rows each); no single organism gives exactly those numbers. Worth saying so in the note.",W6E-memory-q
M-052,"The correct phrasing of Q11 is ""a base-model probe detects that a sleeper agent's answer is false with AUROC 0.96, transferring across trigger types"" - not ""detects deception"".",0.96,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q11-sleeper-detection-is-falsity.md:39,run-coords/q11_sleeper_L44_last.json,tests.cross_trigger[raw|soft-trigger-*],"0.9653 / 0.9630 / 0.9634, mean 0.9639 - a probe trained on two organisms and tested on the third",yes,"cross-trigger (0.9639) is not lower than within-organism (0.9625), which is the file-level evidence that the trigger cue is not what is read; within one answer token the raw probe still gets 0.9461-0.9608",means recomputed from the per-organism cells; the within-token control read from token_stratified,"local git-tracked, clean, 2026-09-16 20:44","the interpretive half (""answer is false for the passage"") is NOT directly measured anywhere in these files - it is an inference from (a) cross-trigger = within-organism, (b) within-token AUROC stays ~0.95, (c) gender-secret, where falsity is uncheckable, is at chance/inverted. All three supporting facts verify; the causal claim does not",HOLDS,"MEDIUM - the number holds; the ""falsity, not deception"" reading is an inference from three controls, not a measurement",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q11.py,"The phrasing advice is sound and the 0.96 is exact. Flagging only that ""answer is false for the passage"" is an interpretation supported by three negative controls, not a measured quantity - there is no third condition in these files that varies falsity while holding the rest fixed.",W6E-memory-q
