M-054,"On the five-dataset subset at layer 20 the pc:deception feature reached off-diagonal transfer AUROC 0.815 against the raw probe's 0.768, the opposite ordering to the full 10-dataset corpus where the same comparison is 0.583 (pc:deception) vs 0.660 (raw).",0.815; 0.768; 0.583; 0.660,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q2-answer-is-layer-dependent.md:34,run-coords/probes_L20.json; run-coords/FULL_L20.json,"p1[features,probe].off_diagonal","SUBSET (5 datasets, L20, mean, k=5): pc:deception/paper 0.8146, raw/paper 0.7678. FULL (10 datasets, same layer/pooling/k): pc:deception/lr_reg10 0.5833, raw/lr_reg10 0.6599",yes - all four figures within 0.0005,"the ordering reversal is robust to probe choice: on the subset pc:deception beats raw under paper (0.8146 vs 0.7678), lr_reg10 (0.7871 vs 0.7634) and mms only in within-semantics; on the full corpus raw beats pc:deception under all three probes (0.6473/0.5801 paper, 0.6599/0.5833 lr_reg10, 0.6524/0.5236 mms)","read every (feature, probe) row of both files and compared the orderings","both files local, git-tracked, clean; bank field in both = axes_vectors_s3.pt (the OLD paper16 bank, RF-15; RF-15 measured old-vs-fp32 cosine 1.0000 and <=1% norm difference, so this cannot move the comparison); mtimes 2026-09-16 19:21/19:22, before the 09-22 wave","the 5-dataset subset includes alpaca and 12 ordered pairs; the full corpus has 72. On the subset raw/mms actually gives 0.7363, BELOW pc:deception/paper - the reversal is not an artefact of one probe",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q2.py,"PROBE MISMATCH inside the sentence: 0.815 vs 0.768 is the ""paper"" probe, 0.583 vs 0.660 is ""lr_reg10"". Every number is exact, and the reversal survives holding the probe fixed (lr_reg10 subset: 0.787 vs 0.763), so the claim stands - but as written it compares two different estimators and should name them.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] VERDICT CORRECTED BY PHASE 4 (HOLDS -> PARTLY HOLDS). The probe mismatch is stated in this note ('as written it compares two different estimators and should name them') and the verdict cell did not follow it. The conclusion survives with either probe held fixed; the printed sentence still compares two estimators.",W6E-memory-q
M-055,"On the full 10-dataset corpus at layer 20, across-semantics transfer is slightly EASIER than within-semantics for the raw probe: 0.691 across vs 0.637 within.",0.691; 0.637,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q2-answer-is-layer-dependent.md:36,run-coords/FULL_L20.json,"p1[features=raw, probe=lr_reg10].{across_semantics, within_semantics}","raw/lr_reg10: across_semantics 0.6913 (n=30 pairs), within_semantics 0.6374 (n=42 pairs)",yes - both exact to 0.0001,the same direction under the other probes: raw/paper 0.6750 across vs 0.6276 within; raw/mms 0.6626 vs 0.6451. So it is not probe-specific,read all three raw rows of the same file,"local git-tracked, clean, 2026-09-16 19:21; old paper16 bank (axes_vectors_s3.pt), which does not enter a raw-probe number at all",on the 5-dataset subset the same raw/lr_reg10 numbers are 0.7660 across vs 0.7503 within - i.e. ALSO across > within,HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q2.py,"CAVEAT on the surrounding sentence (not on these two numbers): the note says the subset made ""within-semantics transfer look much easier"". For the RAW probe the subset does not show that (0.750 within vs 0.766 across under lr_reg10); the within>across reversal on the subset is a property of the PERSONA features (pc:deception/paper 0.9455 within vs 0.7885 across). The note should say which feature it means.",W6E-memory-q
M-056,"Erasing the Assistant Axis from the 8,192-d activations costs 0.006-0.014 AUROC of transfer, while a rank-matched random erasure costs 0.000.",0.006; 0.014; 0.000,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q2-answer-is-layer-dependent.md:41,run-coords/FULL_L20.json; FULL_L22.json; FULL_L40.json,"p1[features=raw].off_diagonal minus p1[features=erase:assistant].off_diagonal, per probe; erase:random likewise","lr_reg10, mean pooling: L20 +0.0056, L22 +0.0086, L40 +0.0139 -> range 0.006-0.014, exactly as stated. With mms: L20 +0.0062, L22 +0.0074, L40 +0.0177. With paper (L20 only): +0.0053. Random erasure (stored only at L20): lr_reg10 -0.0000, mms +0.0002, paper -0.0014",yes for lr_reg10; no if the probe is left free (the mms L40 cost is 0.0177),"the later full bootstrap (run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json, 2026-09-17) gives cost_assistant 0.0053-0.0177 over six settings with five random erasures each, all |cost_random| <= 0.00093","costs recomputed as raw minus erased off-diagonal from the stored per-feature rows, then cross-checked against the independent bootstrap file","FULL_L* are the OLD-bank (axes_vectors_s3.pt) 2026-09-16 files; q3_q4_bootstrap.json is the fp32-bank 2026-09-17 re-run. All local, git-tracked, clean","the claim ""Q4 holds at every layer"" rests on three layers only (20, 22, 40) at the time of writing; the 2026-09-17 bootstrap adds L44 last and finds the cost significant across datasets (BH) only at L40 mms and both L44 probes",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - the range is exact for one probe and wrong for the other,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q2.py; audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q3q4.py,"UNDERSPECIFIED (no probe named). Exact for lr_reg10 at L20/22/40 (0.0056/0.0086/0.0139); with the mms probe the L40 cost is 0.0177, outside the stated range. The q4 note itself later states 0.005-0.018, i.e. this line in the Q2 note is SUPERSEDED by q4-signal-survives-assistant-erasure.md. Recommend the Q2 note point at the Q4 note instead of carrying its own range.",W6E-memory-q
M-057,"In the Pass B full-corpus layer sweep (mean pooling, mms probe, paper16 fp32 bank) the persona contrast axes peak at layer 44 with off-diagonal AUROC 0.731, beat the raw probe only in the band of layers 36-48, and at layer 20 read 0.570 against raw's 0.652.",0.731; 0.570; 0.652; 0.717,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q2-answer-is-layer-dependent.md:64,run-coords/layer_sweep_passB_mms.json,"sweep[layer].{raw, pc:deception, axes}","axes peak = 0.7309 at L44 (the maximum over all 21 stored layers). raw peak = 0.7167 at L32. L20: axes 0.5698, raw 0.6524, pc:deception 0.5237. Layers where axes > raw: 0, 36, 40, 44, 48. pc:deception > raw at 0 of 21 layers",yes - every figure of the note's RESOLVED table reproduces to 0.001,recomputed the peaks and the axes>raw layer set directly from the stored sweep rather than reading the note's table,argmax and per-layer comparison over the 21 stored layers,"local git-tracked, clean, mtime 2026-09-16 19:21; bank field = axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (the re-extracted fp32 bank, so NOT affected by RF-15's old-vs-new question); outside the 09-22 wave","INDEPENDENT PROTOCOL: in the run-crossgen 80/20 store (audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv, store=passA, 10 datasets, mean/mms, seed 42, 80 layers) raw beats axes at EVERY layer from 0 to 77 and axes win only at L78-79. At L40 raw 0.6593 vs axes 0.6257; at L44 raw 0.6514 vs axes 0.6342. raw peaks at L31 (0.7170), which does corroborate the L32 raw peak",HOLDS,HIGH for the stated file; the layer-band conclusion is protocol-specific,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q2.py; audit/scripts/claims/W6E_robust_layers.py,"Two things to carry with this number. (1) axes also edge raw at L0 (0.5560 vs 0.5554) - a near-chance tie, so ""beat raw in a band of 36-48 and lose everywhere else"" is true only if L0 is ignored. (2) The 36-48 band does NOT replicate under the 80/20 cross-generalisation protocol, where axes never beat raw below L78. The raw peak at L31/L32 DOES replicate. For a methods-and-negative-results framing this is the sharper statement: the persona advantage is confined to one layer band AND one transfer protocol.",W6E-memory-q
M-058,"With the mean-difference (mms) probe the raw 8,192-d probe IMPROVES with more in-domain training rows (+0.021 from n=16 to n=1024) and the persona axes equal raw at n=1024 (+0.001), so the ""raw degrades / axes improve"" pattern is specific to the regularised logistic probe.",+0.021; +0.001,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q3-advantage-grows-with-n.md:28,run-coords/q3_q4_bootstrap.json,"q3_curves[""raw|mms""|""axes|mms""][n].auroc ; comparisons[name=""raw (mms): n=1024 minus n=16""], [name=""axes minus raw at n=1024 (mms)""]","raw|mms: 0.7025 at n=16 -> 0.7238 at n=1024, difference +0.0213 (stored comparison: +0.0213, row CI [+0.0184,+0.0244], dataset CI [-0.0151,+0.0549], dataset p 0.187, q_BH 0.324, significant False). axes minus raw at n=1024 (mms) = +0.0009 (row CI [-0.0063,+0.0082], p 0.810)",yes - +0.021 and +0.001 both exact,"recomputed n1024 - n16 from the stored curves: raw|mms +0.0213, axes|mms +0.0317, raw|lr_reg10 -0.0323, axes|lr_reg10 +0.0263 - matching the note's lr_reg10 figures (-0.032 / +0.026) too","differences recomputed from the seven stored curve points per (feature, probe)","local git-tracked, clean, mtime 2026-09-17 02:23; bank = run-paper16/axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt (26_q3_q4_bootstrap.py:139 default); 3 seeds (--p2_seeds default 3); sycophancy_mt EXCLUDED by default, so ""full corpus"" = 9 labelled datasets + alpaca; boot_rows 1000, boot_datasets 10000","NONE of the 14 Q3 comparisons is significant at the dataset level after BH (smallest q = 0.205, the lr_reg10 difference-in-differences). q3_reproduction_worst = 2.15e-09, i.e. the recomputed curve matched the stored sweep before testing",HOLDS,HIGH,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q3q4.py,"The BH q-values here come from this file's own 26-test family and are not affected by RF-13 (which concerns run-crossgen significance.json). Protocol is layer 44, last-token, 3 seeds - a single layer/pooling, so the probe-dependence conclusion is not