M-066,"Response length alone gives AUROC 0.664 on sycophancy_mt (against its 0.845 diagonal) and 0.625 on mask (against 0.727); since the positive class is the longer one in both, length predicts POSITIVE transfer between them, yet they still land at 0.397 / 0.560.",0.664; 0.845; 0.625; 0.727; 0.397; 0.560,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q5-semantics-does-not-predict-transfer.md:42,audit/cache/labpc/run-coords/confounds_L44_last.json; run-coords/q5_layers/p1_L44.json,"confounds.length_only_auroc[sycophancy_mt|mask] ; p1[raw,mms].matrix[""mask->sycophancy_mt""],[""sycophancy_mt->mask""] and the diagonals","length-only AUROC: sycophancy_mt 0.66397 (median_pos 174.5 vs median_neg 97.0), mask 0.62494 (median_pos 245.0 vs 96.5). L44 raw/mms diagonals: sycophancy_mt 0.8453, mask 0.7269. Cross cells: mask->sycophancy_mt 0.3973, sycophancy_mt->mask 0.5604",yes - all six figures exact at the stated precision,"the cross cells were recomputed from the stored 110-cell matrix; the positive class is longer in both datasets (174.5>97.0 and 245.0>96.5), confirming the direction of the length confound",cell reads from the transfer matrix plus the stored per-dataset length medians,"confounds file = the audit's cached lab copy (L44, last, bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt); p1_L44.json = local git-tracked, clean",across all 8 layers mask->sycophancy_mt ranges 0.3789-0.4843 and sycophancy_mt->mask 0.5582-0.5970 for raw/mms; the failure is not layer-specific,HOLDS,HIGH,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q5.py; audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q10.py,"All six numbers are layer-44 last-token, raw/mms. Note that sandbagging_v2 has an even larger length confound (length-only AUROC 0.854) and HP-KR 0.776 - the note picks the two belief datasets, which is the right comparison, but a reader should know those are not the worst cases.",W6E-memory-q
