M-069,"Peak layer depends on protocol: full-corpus pairwise transfer peaks at L28 with last-token pooling (0.740) and L32 with mean pooling (0.717), while Pass C leave-one-dataset-out peaks at L40 (pooled-mean mms 0.883) with L28 within 0.007; Pass C stores no layer 32 or 36.",0.740; 0.717; 0.883; 0.007,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q6-layer-choice-depends-on-method.md:18,run-coords/q6_layers.json; run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json,"rows[method=""raw / mms / last""|""raw / mms / mean""].{best_layer,best} ; results[probe=pool_mean_mms].auroc_mean by layer","raw/mms/last best_layer 28, best 0.7399 (-> 0.740). raw/mms/mean best_layer 32, best 0.7167 (-> 0.717). pool_mean_mms: L20 0.857, L22 0.854, L28 0.876, L40 0.883, L44 0.878, L48 0.874 -> peak L40 = 0.882577; L40 - L28 = 0.006144 (within 0.007; the W5D M-070 note reports the same as +0.0061). Stored layers = [20, 22, 28, 40, 44, 48], so no 32 or 36","yes - all four figures reproduce, and the ""no 32/36"" statement is confirmed by the layers field",the peak and the L40-L28 difference recomputed directly from the six stored per-layer values,argmax and subtraction over the stored q8_trained_pertoken results,"both files local, git-tracked, clean, 2026-09-16 21:22; Pass C protocol: 2,000 label-stratified rows, alpaca as the TPR@1%FPR control, 16 tokens per row","the LODO peak is flat: L28 0.8764, L40 0.8826, L44 0.8783, L48 0.8739 - a spread of only 0.0087 over layers 28-48, so ""peaks at L40"" is a very shallow peak (over all six stored layers, including L20 and L22, the spread is 0.028)",HOLDS,HIGH,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q6.py; audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q8.py,"Passes are not comparable: Pass B uses balanced k=5 pairwise splits on the full corpus, Pass C is 200 rows per dataset with leave-one-dataset-out. The note says so elsewhere (""Do not compare across passes"") but this line puts the two peaks side by side.",W6E-memory-q
