M-072,"Q8 has two halves that point opposite ways: zero-shot, top-decile token scoring beats mean pooling by +0.053; trained, pooled-mean probes beat token-trained probes at every layer by 0.03-0.06 AUROC.",+0.053; -0.03; -0.06,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q8-per-token-beats-pooling.md:3,run-coords/pertoken_q8.json; run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json,"aggregations[layer].{top10pct, mean} ; results[probe,aggregation,layer].auroc_mean","zero-shot top10pct minus mean, by layer: L20 +0.1027, L22 +0.0642, L28 +0.0529, L40 +0.0046, L44 +0.0144, L48 +0.0023. Trained: best pooled minus best token-trained = +0.0604 (L20), +0.0497 (L22), +0.0485 (L28), +0.0300 (L40), +0.0276 (L44), +0.0445 (L48)","half yes - the trained range 0.028-0.060 is exact; the +0.053 is the gain at layer 28 only, and is NOT the largest gain (that is +0.103 at layer 20)",both halves recomputed from the per-cell AUROCs rather than read from the note's tables,per-layer differences over the stored aggregation table and over all probe x aggregation cells,"both files local, git-tracked, clean (2026-09-16 19:21 / 21:22); bank axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt; Pass C, 2,000 rows, 16 tokens/row, alpaca control","top10pct beats mean at all six layers, so the qualitative half-1 claim is robust; the size of the gain is not - it falls to +0.005 at L40 and +0.002 at L48",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - the arithmetic is unambiguous,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q8.py,"""+0.053"" is the top-decile-over-mean gain AT LAYER 28 (where top10pct attains its best absolute value 0.8067). Read as ""the best gain is +0.053"" - the natural reading of the note - it is wrong: the largest gain is +0.1027 at layer 20, and the gain is nearly zero (+0.005) at layer 40. A future session quoting +0.053 as the size of the pooling effect will understate it by a factor of two at the literature layers and overstate it at layer 40. The trained half (-0.03 to -0.06) is exact.",W6E-memory-q
M-073,"Zero-shot on Pass C, top-decile token scoring beats mean pooling at every layer, best +0.053 at layer 28; the deceptive-honest gap is present throughout a response (0.35 at the start, 0.43 at the end), so top10pct exploits a few discriminative tokens within a response rather than a fixed position.",+0.053; 0.35; 0.43,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/q8-per-token-beats-pooling.md:28,run-coords/pertoken_q8.json,"aggregations[layer].{top10pct, mean}; localisation","top10pct - mean: +0.1027, +0.0642, +0.0529, +0.0046, +0.0144, +0.0023 at layers 20/22/28/40/44/48. All six positive. The +0.053 is layer 28","partly - ""beats mean at every layer"" is exact; ""best +0.053 at 28"" is the layer-28 value, not the maximum",same differences recomputed from the six stored aggregation rows,per-layer subtraction,"local git-tracked, clean, 2026-09-16 19:21; Pass C, 2,000 label-stratified rows, 304,706 response tokens per the note, projection on the paper16 fp32 deception axis","the ""first"" aggregation (0.617-0.763) is always the weakest and ""max"" is close to top10pct, consistent with the localisation reading. The 0.35 / 0.43 start-vs-end gap numbers are in the file's `localisation` block as raw dot-product sums per decile, not as a stored 0.35/0.43 pair - they were not reproduced here",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the AUROC half; the 0.35/0.43 pair NOT re-derived,HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6E_q8.py,"Same wording problem as M-072: ""best +0.053 at 28"" reads as the maximum gain but the maximum is +0.1027 at layer 20. The localisation figures 0.35 / 0.43 would need the per-decile means normalised by token count from the `localisation` block; I did not re-derive them and mark that part UNVERIFIED rather than guess a normalisation.",W6E-memory-q
