M-096,"A random 2-d projection gains +0.056 where the raw off-diagonal AUROC is below 0.6 and loses -0.44 where it is at or above 0.85, with corr(raw, delta) = -0.76 - so 'gains where raw is weak' is partly a ceiling/regression effect.",+0.056; -0.44; 0.85; -0.76,C:/Users/SURAIYA/.claude/projects/C--Users-SURAIYA-Documents-STUDY-thesis-expLB/memory/unified-pc1-is-question-family.md:29,"run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (md5 d7616aa5..., == lab) - the 2026-09-17 matrix that produced the note no longer exists","results[feature,probe='paper'].auroc, 110 off-diagonal cells binned on the raw value",print-only; no stored derived file,n/a,"all 11 datasets: random@2 low-bin +0.0691, high-bin -0.4437, corr -0.7684. block9 (10 datasets): +0.0574, -0.4503, -0.7742.","binned the off-diagonal cells on raw and took mean deltas plus Pearson corr, for every feature and for both dataset blocks",closest surviving matrix; F-74 independently recomputed the same corr -0.7684 and showed it sits inside its analytic coupling null (-0.7462),"EVERY feature shows the pattern, including the matched controls: corr -0.46 to -0.79 (datapca@2 -0.5711, axes -0.4994)",PARTLY HOLDS,"MEDIUM - two of three numbers exact on the closest surviving matrix, the third only under a different dataset block",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/M-094_M-097_unified_pc1.py,"-0.44 and -0.76 reproduce on the 11-dataset reading; +0.056 reproduces only on the 10-dataset block9 reading, where the other two move. No single surviving reading gives all three. The conclusion is if anything stronger than stated.",W6F2-memory
