S-05,"Before any Q8 per-token number was trusted, the streaming per-token probe was validated against scikit-learn: cos(sklearn mms, streamed mms)=1.0, max |w.x+b - sklearn decision_function| = 3.66e-06, and 0 of 3,072 row-layer means outside tolerance; the smoke ran 512 rows, 6,028 sampled tokens, layers [20,22,28,40,44,48], 9 LODO folds.","3.66e-06; 0 of 3072; rows 512; sampled tokens 6028; layers [20,22,28,40,44,48]; folds 9",6d4b2181:7726,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/logs/q8_smoke.log (15,270 B, 2026-09-16 21:12:35); lab logs/q8_full.log (15,292 B, 21:21:06); run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json (git working tree); src/assistant_axis_ndif/21_q8_trained_pertoken.py:238,264,338,436-438",q8_smoke.log lines 21:11:49 / 21:11:49 / 21:12:33; q8_trained_pertoken.json .self_checks,"q8_smoke.log: 'rows 512, sampled tokens 6028, layers [20, 22, 28, 40, 44, 48], folds 9'; 'cos(sklearn mms, streamed mms) = 1.000000'; 'max |w.x+b - sklearn| = 3.66e-06'; '0 of 3072 row-layer means outside tolerance, worst relative deviation 9.66e-02'",yes - all four values reproduce exactly from the surviving lab log,"the FULL run (q8_full.log, and its saved artefact) gives the same checks at production scale: max |w.x+b - sklearn| = 1.02e-05, 0 of 12,000 row-layer means outside tolerance; the artefact stores self_checks = {offset_worst_rel_dev 0.17864677788199257, offset_rows_bad 0, offset_rows 12000}","read the lab log excerpts (W6G_lab_logs.ps1 / W6G_lab_logs2.ps1, read-only) and the saved JSON (W6G_local.py S-05); the checks themselves are internal assertions in 21_q8_trained_pertoken.py, which raises SystemExit if the moments check fails","lab logs (never regenerated: mtimes 2026-09-16, outside the RF-13 09-22 wave); artefact = git working tree run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json","the same three checks were re-run at 4x the sample (2,000 rows, 12,000 row-layers) and still passed; tolerance is relative deviation, worst 9.66e-02 in the smoke and 0.179 in the full run - the PASS criterion is a count, not that worst value",HOLDS,"HIGH - all four printed values recovered verbatim from the lab log, and the saved artefact carries the full-run analogues",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_logs.ps1; W6G_lab_logs2.ps1; W6G_local.py,"ABSENT FROM EVERY OWNER DOCUMENT: '3.66e-06' has zero hits across kd/, docs/, cap/, scale/, src/ and the memory notes (278 files scanned). Only the offset check survives in a file (self_checks in the JSON); the sklearn cross-check and the moments check are log-only. This is the only evidence anywhere that the per-token pipeline behind Q8/F-39 was numerically validated, so it belongs in a methods appendix.",W6G-session
S-06,"The Q8 smoke printed a full layer-44 leave-one-dataset-out table (AUROC and TPR@1%FPR for every probe x aggregation), of which only the headline entered a document; its four token-level random-label null rows sat at 0.392-0.462.",pool_mean_mms 0.898 / TPR 0.482; tok_lr top10pct 0.893 / 0.574; zeroshot_axis top10pct 0.856 / 0.717; tok_lr_null 0.392-0.462; '14-row' table,6d4b2181:7726,lab logs/q8_smoke.log lines 120-141 (layer 44 block); run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json results[] layer=44,"q8_smoke.log 'layer 44 -- leave-one-dataset-out, mean over 9 held-out datasets'; JSON results filtered to layer 44 (21 rows)","smoke log L44: pool_mean_mms 0.898/0.482, tok_lr top10pct 0.893/0.574, zeroshot_axis top10pct 0.856/0.717 - ALL THREE EXACT. But the log's four tok_lr_null rows read 0.705/0.559/0.525/0.516, NOT 0.392-0.462, and the log has a length_only row (0.424) the transcript table lacks. The table is 21 rows, not 14.",partial - the 16 real rows match exactly; the null rows and the row count do not,"the FULL run that superseded the smoke (run-coords/q8_trained_pertoken.json, 2,000 rows) gives L44: pool_mean_mms 0.878/0.425, tok_lr top10pct 0.844/0.154, zeroshot_axis top10pct 0.805/0.494, tok_lr_null 0.476-0.553, length_only 0.617/0.086",W6G_lab_logs2.ps1 printed the log's layer-44 block; W6G_local.py S-05 tabulated the saved full-run artefact,"log = lab, 2026-09-16 21:12:35, not in the RF-13 wave; artefact = git working tree","the smoke used 512 rows, the saved run 2,000 - the headline falls 0.898 -> 0.878 and the top TPR falls 0.482 -> 0.425, so the smoke figures are optimistic by ~0.02 AUROC and ~0.06 TPR",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the three headline cells (verbatim in the log and recomputed in the artefact); HIGH that the quoted null range does not reproduce anywhere,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_logs2.ps1; W6G_local.py,"TWO CORRECTIONS. (1) The table has 21 rows (16 real + 4 nulls + length_only), not 14. (2) The null range 0.392-0.462 appears in NO surviving file: the log written 3 minutes after the transcript's print gives 0.516-0.705, and the full run gives 0.476-0.553. So the transcript captured an earlier smoke whose log was overwritten; the 16 real rows are byte-identical between the two, so only the random-label draw changed. A null at 0.705 is itself worth noticing - a random-label control should sit at 0.5 - and it is the surviving version. The smoke numbers should NOT go in the thesis: the full 2,000-row run exists as an artefact and is lower.",W6G-session
S-07,"The Pass-B activation smoke test's integrity checks - mean and last poolings are genuinely different vectors (cos 0.388-0.603), n_tok matches the client-side span on every row, no all-zero row - were printed once and never recorded; the +1.74/-2.73 separation was fitted on the same 16 rows and so is not evidence of generalisation.","cos(mean,last) 0.388-0.603; n_tok [129,127,123,119,115,146]; separation deceptive +1.74 honest -2.73",6d4b2181:3089,"git commit c0349ff77a48c998ca299f201059701e28b52b2b (2026-09-15, '8_coords_ndif: per-sample pooled activations for the evaluation corpus'), commit-message lines 30-31","commit message body: '...returns (16,1,8192,2) fp16, all finite, no all-zero rows, n_tok matching every span, and cos(mean,last) of 0.39-0.60 -- below 1.0, so the last-token index is a real second pooling rather than a copy of the mean.'","the commit message records: 16 ai_liar rows, layer 40, shape (16,1,8192,2) fp16, all finite, no all-zero rows, n_tok matching every span, cos(mean,last) 0.39-0.60. The separation +1.74 / -2.73 and the exact n_tok list are NOT in the commit message and are in no document.",partial - the premise 'never recorded' is wrong for most of it,"NOT RECOMPUTABLE: the smoke store was deleted in the same command that made the commit ('rm -rf run-coords-smoke'), so the 16 pooled vectors no longer exist on the laptop, the lab or in Drive.","git log/show on c0349ff (read-only); grep of every owner .md for '1.74', '2.73', '0.388', '0.603'","git history, branch asix; the commit is reachable from HEAD",n/a - a one-off 16-row smoke; the production Pass B run is a separate artefact,PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for the doc check (the commit message is in git); LOW-MEDIUM for the numbers, which cannot be recomputed because the smoke store was deleted",LOW,git log -1 --format=%B c0349ff (run during this audit),"PREMISE WRONG for the main integrity checks: they are preserved in the commit message of c0349ff, which is a durable record, just not a findings document. What IS unrecorded anywhere: the per-row n_tok list and the separation numbers +1.74 / -2.73 - and, more usefully, the caveat attached to them ('I fit the direction on the same 16 rows, so it only shows the vectors aren't garbage - it is not evidence of generalization'). That caveat is the part worth keeping, and it is transcript-only.",W6G-session
S-08,NDIF's out-of-memory limit was pinned by exact arithmetic on the eager attention matrix - 6 rows x 64 heads x 1869^2 x 4 bytes = 4.997 GiB against NDIF's 'Tried to allocate 5.00 GiB' - and that figure disagrees with the 5.36 GiB the memory note records for the same B and T.,"4.997 GiB vs 'Tried to allocate 5.00 GiB'; memory note records 5.36 GiB for B=6, T=1869",6d4b2181:4928,~/.claude/projects/.../memory/ndif-attention-memory-limit.md (the 4-row table); arithmetic recomputed in audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"memory note row 'B=6  T=1869   product 11,214  attn 5.36 GiB  FAIL  ""Tried to allocate 5.00 GiB""'","memory note says 5.36 GiB; the session says 4.997 GiB. Both describe B=6, T=1869, 64 heads, fp32.",no - the two documents of the same quantity differ,"6 x 64 x 1869^2 x 4 = 5,365,495,296 bytes = 4.9970 GiB (base 2^30) = 5.3655 GB (base 1e9). The session's 4.997 GiB is correct; the note's '5.36 GiB' is the same byte count mislabelled - it is GB, not GiB. The note's other three rows ARE in GiB: B=1/T=3000 -> 2.1458 (note 2.15), B=16/T=400 -> 0.6104 (note 0.61), B=2/T=3000 -> 4.2915 (note 4.30).","exact integer arithmetic, audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-08",memory note as of 2026-09-16T19:05Z; arithmetic is version-free,"all four rows of the note recomputed; exactly one (B=6, T=1869) is in decimal GB while labelled GiB",HOLDS,"HIGH - pure arithmetic, and the mixed-unit row is isolated","LOW for the science, MEDIUM for the methods section (it is the evidence that the limit is the attention matrix)",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"The discrepancy is a UNIT ERROR, not a measurement disagreement: 5.365e9 bytes = 4.997 GiB. It matters because the note's own row undercuts its tightest piece of evidence - 4.997 GiB matches NDIF's 'Tried to allocate 5.00 GiB' to two decimals, whereas 5.36 does not. Recommended doc fix: make the B=6/T=1869 row read 5.00 GiB (or state the units as GB for the whole column). '4.997' appears in no owner document.",W6G-session
S-10,"An external review of the project plan was checked number by number: its Spearman -0.94 re-derived to -0.943, four of its claims were refuted, cos(sycophancy, assistant) is 0.04-0.14, and the deception axis is contaminated but not collapsed (cos^2 = 0.44 at layer 40, so 56% orthogonal).","Spearman -0.943 (review said -0.94); cos(syc,asst) 0.04-0.14; cos^2(deception,assistant) = 0.44 at L40 i.e. 56% orthogonal",6d4b2181:619,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run/axes.pt (own100 bank, 100 roles, 2026-09-15 12:51); memory note persona-axis-diagnostics.md",axes['deception'|'sycophancy'|'assistant'] at layers 20/22/40/60/79; pca['all'] components/variance_ratio; the six group means quoted by the review,"memory note persona-axis-diagnostics.md already tabulates cos(dec,asst) -0.729/-0.710/-0.660/-0.573, cos(syc,asst) 0.125/0.112/0.144/0.102, cos(dec,syc) -0.071/-0.057/-0.061/-0.038, cos(PC1,asst) 0.816/0.804/0.774/0.731 and states 'cos^2 = 0.44 at layer 40, so 56% of it is orthogonal'. The Spearman -0.943 is in NO document.",partial - the cosines are documented; the Spearman re-derivation is not,"recomputed from run/axes.pt: L20 -0.7288/+0.1246/-0.0706, L22 -0.7097/+0.1123/-0.0572, L40 -0.6599/+0.1440/-0.0608, L60 -0.5726/+0.1022/-0.0377, L79 -0.5638/+0.0446/+0.0656; cos(PC1,asst) 0.8156/0.8036/0.7741/0.7309 with PC1 var 31.2/28.6/24.5/26.4%. cos(dec,asst)^2 at L40 = 0.4354 -> 56.5% orthogonal. Spearman over the six group means = 1 - 6*68/(6*35) = -0.942857.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom2.py, run read-only on the lab against run/axes.pt","lab run/axes.pt mtime 2026-09-15 12:51 - the bank was REBUILT on 09-15 (per-behaviour PCA + sign pinning) after the 09-14 diagnostics, so the PC1 figures are from the rebuilt file and still match the 09-14 table","cos(syc,asst) over all 80 layers is +0.0201 to +0.1647; the '0.04-0.14' range is the five reported layers only",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH - every number recomputed from the bank during this audit, and the Spearman derived independently",MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom2.py,"PREMISE LARGELY WRONG: the memory note persona-axis-diagnostics.md (and, for '56%', docs/COLLABORATOR_BRIEFING.md) already record the cosine table, the cos^2=0.44 / 56% reading, the judge-health numbers and the sycophancy-is-clean conclusion. What is genuinely unrecorded is (a) the Spearman re-derivation -0.943 and (b) the four refuted review claims, one of which is a real process lesson: the review read roleplaying__plain__llama-70b.json, a file the plan never used, and concluded the rollouts came from a different model. Note also that the memory note itself later SUPERSEDES the 'sycophancy is clean under every construction' conclusion (Correction 2: under paper16 cos(syc,asst) = -0.269 and cos(dec,syc) = +0.302).",W6G-session
S-15,"Every zero-shot AUROC in q10_sycophancy_axis.json carries two length controls (within length quintiles, length regressed out) for 4 directions x 2 banks x 2 poolings x 21 layers, and the thesis document quotes only the uncontrolled figure.",paper16|mean assistant L40 0.710 -> 0.660 / 0.645; paper16|mean deception best L16 0.487 -> 0.600 / 0.553; own100|mean sycophancy best L0 0.549 -> 0.501 / 0.517,dc605d01:231,run-coords/q10_sycophancy_axis.json (git working tree),"results['<bank>|<pooling>']['<direction>'].by_layer and .key_layers[L].{auroc, within_length_quintiles, length_regressed_out}","paper16|mean assistant L40 auroc 0.7102, within_length_quintiles 0.6601, length_regressed_out 0.6453; paper16|mean deception best L16 0.4875 -> 0.6004 / 0.5527; own100|mean sycophancy best L0 0.5492 -> 0.5014 / 0.5174. All three quoted triples EXACT.",yes for the numbers; no for the coverage statement,"the file holds 5 directions (sycophancy, deception, unified, assistant, syc_PC1) x 2 banks x 2 poolings x 21 layers = 420 by_layer AUROCs, of which only 60 (3 key layers per combination: the best layer plus 40 and 44) carry the two length controls. Not 4 directions, and not every AUROC.",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-15 - counted every by_layer entry and every key_layers entry,git working tree run-coords/q10_sycophancy_axis.json; not touched by the RF-13 wave (it is a laptop-side coords result),"both controls move the assistant reading DOWN (0.710 -> 0.660 / 0.645) and the near-chance deception reading UP toward 0.5-0.6; length_only alone scores 0.664 on this dataset, and the random-direction p95 for best-of-layers is 0.694 (mean) / 0.683 (last)",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - every quoted value reproduced from the file; the coverage count is a direct count,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"IMPORTANT CONTEXT the claim does not carry: on this dataset length ALONE scores 0.664 and the random-direction best-of-layers p95 is 0.694. The assistant axis's headline 0.710 (L40) is barely above the random null and only 0.046 above length-only; after either length control it is 0.660/0.645, i.e. BELOW the random p95. That materially weakens the 'only the Assistant Axis detects capitulation' reading in the Q10 memory note. The note quotes 0.660 too (memory persona-set-decides-detection.md etc.), so the controls are partly documented - the untested part is the comparison against the random null.",W6G-session
S-16,"The 2026-09-22 re-run wave had a mechanical cause: the lab PC rebooted at 15:34:30 and the project's Scheduled Tasks carry MSFT_TaskBootTrigger with staggered delays, so roughly two dozen compute chains fired over about fifty minutes with no person and no schedule involved.",boot 15:34:30; KD-Bank-Crossgen PT20M fired 15:54:30; KD-S23 PT25M fired 15:59:30; Scale-3b/8b PT30M fired 16:04:30; ~24 chains over ~50 minutes,1ac8bb19:2344,lab Win32_OperatingSystem.LastBootUpTime; lab Get-ScheduledTask + Get-ScheduledTaskInfo (35 tasks with MSFT_TaskBootTrigger); audit/phase2/out/W6G_forensics.txt,LastBootUpTime; per-task Triggers[].Delay and LastRunTime,"LastBootUpTime = 2026-09-22 15:34:30 EXACT. Delays confirmed: KD-Bank-Crossgen PT20M, KD-S23 PT25M, Scale-3b PT30M, Scale-8b PT30M.","yes for the boot time and the delays; the firing times are predictions, not observations","observed LastRunTime: KD-Bank-Crossgen 15:55:01 (predicted 15:54:30), KD-S23 16:00:01 (predicted 15:59:30), Scale-3b/8b 16:05:00 (predicted 16:04:30) - Windows fires ~30 s after boot+delay. 25 project tasks have a LastRunTime inside 2026-09-22 15:40:01-16:25:01, a 45-minute span: Cap-Chain, Cap-Controls, Cap-Ctrl-Layers, Cap-Ctrl-XG, Cap-Layers, Cap-Seeds, Crossgen-Chain, Crossgen-Final-Report, Falsify-MeanDir, HPKR-Topup, KD-Bank-Crossgen, KD-Chain, KD-Crossgen, KD-Extract, KD-Knowledge, KD-PassAC, KD-S23, KD-S23-AllLayers, PassAC-11, Premise-Extras, Premise-Layers, Sarc-Pilot, Scale-3b, Scale-8b, Scale-Coords.",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1 (read-only Get-ScheduledTask / Get-ScheduledTaskInfo / Win32_OperatingSystem),"lab PC live state, read 2026-09-23 15:29:41; LastRunTime values are unchanged since the wave because the tasks were disabled at 17:31 on 09-22",35 non-Microsoft tasks carry a boot trigger in total; 25 of them are project chains that ran in the wave; boot+delay matches LastRunTime to within 31 s for every one checked,HOLDS,"HIGH - boot time, trigger type, delay and last-run time all read from the live task store during this audit","HIGH (it is the explanation for RF-13, which changes how every 09-22 file mtime must be read)",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1,"Two refinements. (1) The quoted firing times are boot+delay PREDICTIONS; the observed runs are ~30 s later (15:55:01, 16:00:01, 16:05:00), which is what audit/PROGRESS.md's RF-13 entry already records. (2) '~24 chains over ~50 minutes' measures as 25 tasks over 45 minutes. NOTE A DISCREPANCY WITH THE AUDIT'S OWN RF-13 ENTRY: PROGRESS.md says '~17 tasks fired' (counted from logs); the task store says 25 project tasks have a LastRunTime in the window. Eight therefore ran without leaving a log line - which matters because the audit uses log presence to decide what was regenerated.",W6G-session
S-17,"A standing misreading was corrected: 'Next=none' on a Windows scheduled task does not mean the task cannot fire, only that no time-based run is scheduled; a boot trigger does not populate NextRunTime. Roughly twenty status readings had asserted the wrong thing.",~20 identical status readings asserted the wrong thing,1ac8bb19:2351,"lab task store (audit/phase2/out/W6G_forensics.txt); transcript 1ac8bb19 (counted, not quoted)","tasks with MSFT_TaskBootTrigger, empty NextRunTime and a non-null LastRunTime",counted in the transcript: 23 records contain the literal string 'Next=none'; 21 assistant messages contain an assertion of the form trigger-less / cannot fire / never fire / Next=none. 'Roughly twenty' is right.,yes,"the underlying fact is directly demonstrated in the live task store: 25 project tasks have a boot trigger, an EMPTY NextRunTime, and a LastRunTime of 2026-09-22 15:40:01-16:25:01 with lastResult 0 - i.e. they fired while showing no next run. Conversely Thesis_Train has no delay and no next run and has not fired since 08/04.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1 (task store); a streaming count over the transcript with a regex, printing only counts",lab live state 2026-09-23; transcript 1ac8bb19 (775 records carrying text),"the demonstration is structural, not a single case: every one of the 25 tasks shows the same empty-next / non-null-last pattern",HOLDS,"HIGH for the mechanism (demonstrated on 25 tasks); MEDIUM for the exact count of misreadings, which depends on how an 'assertion' is matched (21 by my regex, 23 records mention the string)","MEDIUM - it is the reason RF-13's cause was missed for a day, and it is a reusable operational lesson",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1; an inline streaming count over the transcript,"In no owner document: 'Next=none' has zero hits across the 278 owner .md/.txt files scanned. This belongs in the repo's operational notes (CLAUDE.md already warns that long jobs must be Scheduled Tasks; it does not warn that a boot-triggered task shows no NextRunTime). The claim's own framing is a self-correction, which is the kind of thing the thesis's methods section can quote directly.",W6G-session
S-18,"24 boot-triggered compute chains were disabled on the lab PC at 17:31 local on 2026-09-22, about 73 minutes before the audit's baseline; three sync tasks were deliberately kept enabled.","24 named tasks disabled; kept: KD-Sync-Periodic, Crossgen-Sync-Periodic, Coords-Supervisor",1ac8bb19:2763,lab task store (audit/phase2/out/W6G_forensics.txt); audit/START_STATE.md (baseline 2026-09-22T18:44:50+06:00),Settings.Enabled / State per task,"all 24 named tasks are Disabled / Enabled=False today. The 17:31 timestamp corresponds to the session message at 2026-09-22T11:31:32Z = 17:31:32 lab (UTC+6); the audit baseline is 18:44:50, so the gap is 73.3 minutes - EXACT.",yes for the 24; no for the 'kept' list as of today,"of the three said to be kept, only KD-Sync-Periodic (boot trigger PT8M) and Crossgen-Sync-Periodic (time trigger) are still Ready/Enabled. Coords-Supervisor is now Disabled (lastRun 2026-09-23 00:28:46, lastResult 267014). PassAC-11, Night-Chain and PassC-PerToken - which audit/PROGRESS.md RF-13 recorded as 'still armed' on 09-22 - are also Disabled now, with last runs on 2026-09-23 00:20-00:28.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1, read-only enumeration of every non-Microsoft task",lab live state 2026-09-23 15:29,35 non-Microsoft tasks carry a boot trigger; 29 of them are Disabled today,HOLDS,HIGH for the 24 and the timing; HIGH that the 'kept' list has since changed,"MEDIUM - it is the reason no compute has run on the box since, which underwrites the audit's assumption that the files are stable",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1,"FOR THE LEAD: four more tasks (Coords-Supervisor, PassAC-11, Night-Chain, PassC-PerToken) were disabled between the Phase-1 census and now, after last running 2026-09-23 00:20-00:28. audit/scripts/fix_disable_done_tasks.ps1 exists in this audit's own toolbox, so this is most likely the audit's own fix round rather than the owner; audit/LABPC_WRITES.md should carry it. Worth confirming, because RF-13's 'still armed' line in PROGRESS.md is now stale.",W6G-session
S-19,Drive sync from the lab PC failed for about five hours on 2026-09-22 (12:18 to 17:26 local) because the rclone OAuth token for the tamara: remote expired; after the token was replaced the backlog uploaded cleanly.,"first exit 0 since 12:18; run-kd 184 files exit 0 at 17:27:11; crossgen11 68,666 files exit 0 at 17:27:53; manual whole-tree exit 0 at 17:28:20",1ac8bb19:2735,"lab logs/coords_rclone.log, logs/kd_rclone.log, logs/kd_sync.status, logs/crossgen_sync.status, logs/scale_rclone.log",CRITICAL 'couldn't find root directory ID' lines; the exit 0 / EXIT 1 lines in the .status files,"kd_sync.status: '2026-09-22 17:27:11  periodic run-kd exit 0 (184 files)' and '17:27:53  periodic crossgen11 exit 0 (68666 files)' and '17:27:53  periodic DONE exit 0' - all three EXACT. crossgen_sync.status: '17:28:20  manual EXIT 0' - EXACT, and '17:26:43 periodic SKIP (another sync holds the lock)' is present as described.",yes,the failure window is bracketed independently: coords_rclone.log's FIRST CRITICAL on 09-22 is 12:18:23 and its LAST is 17:13:47 (21 CRITICAL lines in all); kd_rclone.log's last CRITICAL is 17:25:11 and its first clean transfer is 17:27:04. crossgen_sync.status runs EXIT 1 from 12:16:11 through 17:2x; kd_sync.status's last exit 0 before the outage is 11:11:25 and the first after is 17:27:11. scale_rclone.log carries the same CRITICAL at 16:20:15 (the failed run-scale sync behind part of RF-10).,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics2.ps1 and W6G_lab_forensics4.ps1 (read-only log reads),lab logs as they stand 2026-09-23; these are append-only .status/.log files,four independent log families agree on the window; the error text is the same in all of them,HOLDS,"HIGH for the window and the recovery; MEDIUM for the CAUSE - the logged symptom is 'couldn't find root directory ID', not an explicit token error; the token-expiry diagnosis rests on the fact that replacing the token line fixed it (see S-20)",MEDIUM-HIGH - it explains RF-10 (result folders with no Drive backup) and the failed scale/coords syncs in RF-13,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics2.ps1; W6G_lab_forensics4.ps1,"This is the mechanism behind two existing red flags. RF-13 notes an rclone CRITICAL at 15:47 and 16:20 without explaining it; RF-10 lists folders with no Drive copy. Both are the same five-hour outage: every sync attempted between 12:18 and 17:25 exited non-zero, including the 15:40-16:25 boot-wave chains' own final syncs. Anything written on 09-22 before 17:27 that was not re-synced afterwards is still box-only. In no owner document: 'rclone.conf.bak' and 'invalid_grant' have zero hits; docs/ONBOARDING.md mentions OAuth but not this outage.",W6G-session
S-20,"A previous Claude session wrote to the lab PC shortly before the audit's baseline: it replaced exactly one line - the OAuth token - in the lab's rclone.conf, leaving a backup alongside.",1 token line replaced; backup at rclone.conf.bak-2026-09-22; '78 minutes before the audit's baseline',1ac8bb19:2727,lab C:/Users/user4/AppData/Roaming/rclone/rclone.conf and rclone.conf.bak-2026-09-22; audit/START_STATE.md,per-line structural comparison (keys and lengths only - no secret values read out),"the backup exists: rclone.conf.bak-2026-09-22, 690 B, mtime 2026-09-22 17:19:52. Both files have 8 lines. Exactly ONE line differs: line 6, key 'token', same length in both (488 chars). Lines 1-5 and 7-8 ([tamara], type, client_secret, scope, client_id, team_drive, blank) are identical.",yes - exactly one token line replaced,"the write is confirmed independently by its effect: the last failing sync is at 17:25:11 and the first success at 17:27:04-17:27:11 (S-19), i.e. minutes after the backup was written. Timing: backup mtime 17:19:52 vs audit baseline 2026-09-22T18:44:50 = 84.97 minutes, not 78.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics2.ps1 - structural diff that prints only the key name, a SAME/DIFF flag and the line lengths; no credential value was read into the audit","lab live state 2026-09-23; the current rclone.conf has since been rewritten by rclone's own token refresh (mtime 2026-09-23 15:25:10), so line 6 differs from the backup for that reason too",the structural comparison is exact and independent of the token's value; the file has not grown or shrunk,PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for '1 token line replaced' and the backup; HIGH that the '78 minutes' figure is 85 minutes against audit/START_STATE.md,"MEDIUM - it establishes that the lab PC was written to before the audit began, which the audit's own safety rules need to account for",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics2.ps1,"A DELIBERATE, SCOPED WRITE by a pre-audit session, outside the audit's write rules but before they existed. It is not logged in audit/LABPC_WRITES.md (which starts at the audit) and is in no owner document: 'rclone.conf.bak' has zero hits across the 278 owner .md/.txt files. Two things follow for the lead: (1) the backup still holds a real OAuth refresh token and should be deleted by the owner once she is satisfied; (2) the pre-audit lab state was not pristine, so 'nothing was written before the baseline' is not true.",W6G-session
S-21,"The lab PC is shared, and four run_benchmark_* jobs belonging to another account drove free RAM to a fraction of a gigabyte while the F-99 and F-100 layer sweeps were running, forcing the sweeps to complete through a resume loop rather than a single pass.",free RAM 0.2 GB then 0.6 GB; three foreign jobs launched 00:39:59 and a fourth at 00:43:26; the sweep resumed past each failure and landed 21/21,1ac8bb19:893,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-crossgen/kd11/banks/collab/matrices/*.json (21 layers, mtimes); run-crossgen/scale_70b/matrices (42 files); kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-99 caveat (2), line 4589; lab C:/Users listing",per-file LastWriteTime; F-99 caveat text,"THE PREMISE IS WRONG - this IS in the ledger. kd/docs/FINDINGS.md:4589 (F-99, caveat 2) says: 'the run OOMed repeatedly - four foreign run_benchmark_*.py jobs on the shared lab PC took free RAM to 0.1 GB and a 23 MiB numpy allocation failed at L28. Completed by a resume loop, not by reducing --boot_rows'. The ledger says 0.1 GB; the claim says 0.2 then 0.6 GB.",no - the ledger records the same event with a different RAM figure,"the resume pattern is visible in the file mtimes. The collab-bank sweep wrote mean_L20 and mean_L40 at 00:33:41/00:33:52, then L0,L4,L8,L12,L16 at 00:42:33-00:43:18, then L22,L24 at 00:43:29/00:43:45, then a 2-minute gap, then L28 at 00:45:44 and L32..L76 through 00:49:31 - 21 layers in all, written out of order, exactly as a skip-completed-layers resume produces, with the gap at the layer F-99 names (L28). The 70B sweep that followed (run-crossgen/scale_70b/matrices) wrote its 21 mean layers cleanly 00:52:06-01:02:44 and its 21 last layers 01:29:04-01:33:59: 42 files, 21/21 per pooling. The box is shared: C:/Users holds Administrator, bracu, user1-user7 and others; 61.58 GB total RAM.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics3.ps1 - directory listings with mtimes, read-only; profile folder NAMES only, nothing read inside another user's folder",lab live state 2026-09-23; these matrices were not rewritten in the RF-13 wave (mtimes are 09-22 00:33-01:34),the out-of-order write pattern and the L28 gap are independent of any log; 21/21 holds for both poolings of the 70B sweep and for the collab sweep,PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH for the resume pattern, the 21/21 and the shared box; the RAM figures and the process launch times cannot be verified (no process record survives) and the ledger disagrees (0.1 vs 0.2/0.6 GB)","MEDIUM - it is a caveat on F-99/F-100, already partly carried",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics3.ps1,"PREMISE WRONG: F-99's caveat (2) already records the foreign jobs, the OOM and the resume loop. The claim's value is the operational detail the ledger omits - that the sweep landed 21/21 and that every cell kept the same bootstrap settings, which is what makes the layers comparable. The RAM number differs between the two sources (0.1 GB in the ledger, 0.2/0.6 GB in the session) and neither can be re-measured, so quote it as 'under a gigabyte' or drop it.",W6G-session
S-22,A stale 0-byte .git/index.lock created at 16:54:01 blocked the owner's GitHub Desktop commit on 2026-09-22; it was diagnosed as stale (no git.exe running) and deleted at about 17:37.,"index.lock 0 bytes, created 16:54:01, deleted 17:37",1ac8bb19:2788,laptop .git/logs/HEAD (git reflog); .git/index,reflog entries for 2026-09-22,"the lock file itself is gone (deleted by design), so its size and creation time cannot be re-measured.",not checkable - the artefact was intentionally removed,"the reflog corroborates the window exactly: commit cf11749 'finfdings' at 2026-09-22 16:51:52 +0600, then NO commit for 46 minutes, then 43ee6d3 'collaborator breifing' at 2026-09-22 17:37:48 +0600. A lock created at 16:54:01 (2m09s after the 16:51:52 commit) and cleared at ~17:37 fits the gap to the minute, and 17:37:48 is the first successful commit after it.",git reflog --date=iso (read-only) run during this audit,"laptop repo, branch asix",single event; no other evidence survives,PARTLY HOLDS,"MEDIUM - the lock file is gone, but the 46-minute commit gap ending at 17:37:48 is strong circumstantial corroboration","LOW - housekeeping, no bearing on any result",git reflog --date=iso -n 12,"NO RAW DATA for the lock itself; the reflog gap is the only surviving trace and it fits. Note the lock was on the LAPTOP repo (GitHub Desktop), not the lab PC, which per the memory note is not a git repo at all. 'index.lock' has zero hits in any owner document.",W6G-session
S-23,"An early self-assessment of the replication - 'the signal is positive but about half the size the paper claims, and it isn't robust yet' - rested on a 3-probe x 4-feature off-diagonal table at layer 20 over 5 datasets and 12 transfer pairs, using the paper16 score-3 bank with k=5 and mean pooling.","pc:deception 0.815 / 0.787 / 0.681; axes 0.781 / 0.785 / 0.804; raw 0.768 / 0.763 / 0.736 (probes: paper, lr_reg10, mms)",6d4b2181:5089,"run-coords/probes_L20.json (git working tree; layer 20, pooling mean, k=5, bank axes_vectors_s3.pt)","p1[].{features, probe, off_diagonal, diagonal, n_pairs}","pc:deception 0.8146 / 0.7871 / 0.6809; axes 0.7811 / 0.7853 / 0.8044; raw 0.7678 / 0.7634 / 0.7363; random 0.4619 / 0.5013 / 0.4834; axes_resid 0.7703 / 0.7764 / 0.7839. Every quoted value EXACT to 3 dp, n_pairs = 12 for all.",yes,"the deltas the session quoted also reproduce exactly: pc:deception - raw = +0.0469 (paper), +0.0238 (lr_reg10), -0.0554 (mms); axes - raw = +0.0681 (mms). raw's diagonal is 0.9547 ('0.955'). axes_resid vs axes under lr_reg10 = 0.7764 vs 0.7853 ('0.776 vs 0.785').","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-23, reading the stored matrix and recomputing every delta","git working tree; datasets ai_liar 270, alpaca 2000, convincing-game 267, mask 585, roleplaying 287 - 1,641 non-alpaca rows, ~11% of the eventual corpus, as the session said",this is 12 transfer pairs of an eventual ~90-110; the 5 datasets over-weight mask and roleplaying; the advantage reverses under the mms probe (-0.055),PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - all twelve table cells and all four deltas recomputed exactly,"MEDIUM-HIGH - it is the project's first honest self-assessment, and the '+0.10 in the paper vs +0.02 to +0.05 here' framing is what the thesis needs",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"PREMISE PARTLY WRONG: docs/thesis/persona-coordinates-70b-results.md:556 already records two cells of this table (paper16 pc:deception 0.815 and axes_resid 0.770 against own100 0.706/0.553) and flags it 'provisional, 5 datasets, layer 20 only'. What is NOT in any document is the full 3x4 grid - in particular the raw row (0.768/0.763/0.736) and the mms column, which is where the persona advantage REVERSES (-0.055). Also unrecorded: the sentence 'the advantage has already halved once: going from 3 datasets sharing one label semantics to 5 with mixed semantics, it fell from +0.084 to +0.026' - the single most informative early observation, and the one that foreshadows F-61/F-80. Worth putting in the thesis as the honest progression.",W6G-session
S-24,Two of the cap bank's three declared axis variants are the same contrast: cap_vs_default and cap_only both score cosine +0.9313 against the capitulation contrast and have the identical norm 4.411 at layer 40.,"cos(capitulation, cap_vs_default) = +0.9313 norm 4.411; cos(capitulation, cap_only) = +0.9313 norm 4.411; cos(capitulation, capitulation) = +1.0000 norm 3.954",b035ccb3:7881,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-cap/axes_s23.pt (62,934,010 B, 2026-09-21 03:22)",axes['capitulation'|'cap_vs_default'|'cap_only'][40]; counts,"cos(capitulation, capitulation) = +1.0000 norm 3.954; cos(capitulation, cap_vs_default) = +0.9313 norm 4.411; cos(capitulation, cap_only) = +0.9313 norm 4.411 - all three EXACT (recomputed 3.9536 / 4.4115 / 4.4115).",yes,"stronger than the claim: cap_vs_default and cap_only are the SAME VECTOR, not merely collinear. cos(cap_vs_default, cap_only) = +1.000000 at L40 and max |cap_vs_default - cap_only| over ALL 80 layers = 0.0. The bank's own counts explain it: capitulation is (6 vs 6) roles, while cap_vs_default and cap_only are both (6 vs 1) - both are 'the six capitulating roles minus default'.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py and W6G_lab_geom2.py, run read-only on the lab against run-cap/axes_s23.pt","lab run-cap/axes_s23.pt, mtime 2026-09-21 03:22; not touched by the RF-13 wave","the identity holds at every one of the 80 layers, exactly (max abs difference 0.0)",HOLDS,"HIGH - recomputed from the bank, and the identity is exact rather than approximate",MEDIUM-HIGH - the cap bank's 'three axis variants' are really two,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py; W6G_lab_geom2.py,"ABSENT FROM EVERY OWNER DOCUMENT: '0.9313' and '4.411' have zero hits across the 278 owner .md/.txt files. The related insight IS documented twice - memory pc-features-use-basis-not-contrast.md and docs/OPEN_DECISIONS.md line 'cap variants A and B agreeing ... a tautology' - but both are about the PCA BASES; neither records that the cap_vs_default and cap_only CONTRAST directions are the identical vector. That is a separate and stronger fact: the cap bank declares three axis variants and holds two distinct contrasts. Anywhere the design says three variants were compared, it should say two.",W6G-session
S-25,"Two PCA bases built over an identical role set differ by up to 1.347 in a single component, while a basis built over a different role set differs by only 0.663 - so comparing components instead of AUROCs makes a tautology look like a finding.",A roles == B roles : True; max|A-B| over all layers/PCs = 1.347235918045044; max|A-C| = 0.6633388996124268,b035ccb3:7881,"lab run-cap/axes_s23.pt, pca['capitulation'|'cap_vs_default'|'cap_only'].components (80, 5, 8192) fp32",role sets and componentwise max absolute differences,A roles == B roles : True; max|A-B| = 1.347235918045044; max|A-C| = 0.6633388996124268 - all three EXACT to every printed digit.,yes,"the 1.347 is ENTIRELY sign: after aligning each (layer, PC) pair's sign, max|A-B| = 0.0 exactly, i.e. A and B are the identical subspace with the identical components up to per-component sign. The 0.663 for A vs C does NOT shrink under sign alignment (still 0.6633388996124268), because C is a genuinely different 7-role basis.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py, run read-only on the lab; added a per-(layer, PC) sign alignment the original check did not do","lab run-cap/axes_s23.pt, mtime 2026-09-21 03:22",the sign-aligned identity holds over all 80 layers and all 5 PCs,PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - exact digit-for-digit reproduction plus an added control that explains the number,MEDIUM-HIGH - it is a general trap for any component-level comparison in this project,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py,"PREMISE WRONG: this IS documented. memory/pc-features-use-basis-not-contrast.md says in as many words 'max|A-B| is nonzero (1.35) purely from sign flips, which makes it look like a real difference if you check components instead of AUROCs', and docs/OPEN_DECISIONS.md line ~178 records the same as a self-correction ('a tautology - pc:<name> projects onto the PCA basis, never the contrast'). What this audit ADDS is the proof rather than the assertion: after sign alignment max|A-B| is exactly 0.0, while max|A-C| is unchanged at 0.663. That is the number to quote if the thesis explains the trap.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] VERDICT CORRECTED BY PHASE 4 (HOLDS -> PARTLY HOLDS). The claim's PREMISE is wrong: the two PCA bases over an identical role set do not 'differ by up to 1.347' - they are identical up to a per-component SIGN FLIP, cos = -1.0000 exactly at the argmax (L77, PC4, dim 5114). Element-wise max-abs-difference between PCA bases is not a distance and is quoted as one. The conclusion (compare AUROCs, not components) is better supported than the claim states. Consistent with RF-15 on PC sign pinning.",W6G-session
S-26,"The 36-persona kd score-3 bank's all-roles PCA concentration was printed and is in no document: PC1 explains 25.6% of role variance and the top five components 69.2%, with cos(PC1, assistant axis) at +0.583 at layer 40, minimum +0.539 and median +0.598 across layers.","PC1 25.6%; top-5 69.2%; cos(PC1,assistant) L40 +0.583, min +0.539, median +0.598",b035ccb3:2436,"lab C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt (94,402,222 B, mtime 2026-09-22 15:41); lab logs/kd_axes.log (16,164 B, 2026-09-22 15:41:57)","pca['all'].variance_ratio[40], .components[:,0]; axes['assistant']","kd_axes.log holds both blocks: the axes_vectors_all build (PC1 26.5%, top-5 70.7%, cos +0.607, min +0.573, median +0.626) and the axes_vectors_s3 build (PC1 25.6%, top-5 69.2%, cos +0.583, min +0.539, median +0.598). The claim's numbers are the s3 block, exactly.",yes,"recomputed from the bank itself: 36 roles, variance_ratio shape (80,5); L40 PC1 = 25.6449%, top-5 = 69.2412%; cos(PC1,assistant) L40 = +0.5833; across 80 layers min +0.5387, median +0.5989, max +0.7077. Per-behaviour PCA at L40: deception n=16 cos(PC1,contrast)=+0.961 var 44.6%; sycophancy n=11 +0.993 var 46.0%; unified n=26 +0.887 var 35.1%; knowledge_denial n=8 +0.894 var 40.5%; kd_assertion n=8 +0.966 var 39.2%.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py, run read-only on the lab","run-kd/axes_vectors_s3.pt has mtime 2026-09-22 15:41, i.e. it WAS rewritten in the RF-13 boot wave - but the rebuilt file reproduces the 2026-09-20 printed values exactly, so the rebuild is deterministic","the max over layers is +0.7077, so the Assistant-Axis paper's '>0.60 all layers' threshold fails on this bank (min 0.539) while its '>0.71 mid-layer' threshold fails at L40 (0.583)",HOLDS,HIGH - recomputed from the bank and independently confirmed by the build log,MEDIUM,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py; W6G_lab_logs.ps1,"PREMISE MOSTLY WRONG: kd/docs/FINDINGS.md already carries cos(PC1,assistant) = +0.583, min +0.539 and median +0.598 (F-11, which also records the default-anchor 0.882 and the group-projection table). The genuinely unrecorded pieces are the VARIANCE numbers - PC1 25.6% and top-5 69.2% - which have zero hits in any owner document, and the fact that the axes_vectors_all build of the same bank reads 26.5% / 70.7% / +0.607. Useful because F-37 compares PC1 variance across model sizes (33.4% / 39.6% / 37.2%) and the kd bank's 25.6% is well below all three - a 36-role library concentrates less than a 26-role one.",W6G-session
S-27,"The WMDP self-scoring smoke test scored 5 of 8 items correct on items kn00000-kn00007, with one item at margin 0.097 and the rest near 1.0.","5/8 correct; margin range 0.097 to 1.000; pred spread {0:2,1:4,2:2}; gold spread {0:2,1:2,2:2,3:2}",b035ccb3:1480,"kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl (git working tree; the TRUNCATED committed copy, RF-5)","records item_id kn00000..kn00007, fields gold/pred/correct/margin/probs","the full-run file reproduces the smoke exactly for all 8 items: kn00000 gold3 pred1 wrong m1.000; kn00001 gold3 pred0 wrong m1.000; kn00002 gold1 pred1 ok m0.09663 probs[0.4517,0.5483,0,0]; kn00003 gold2 pred2 ok m1.000; kn00004 gold0 pred1 wrong m1.000; kn00005 gold0 pred0 ok m0.9853; kn00006 gold2 pred2 ok m0.99999; kn00007 gold1 pred1 ok m0.99999. correct = 5/8; pred spread {0:2,1:4,2:2}; gold spread {0:2,1:2,2:2,3:2}.",yes - every field matches,"the smoke is therefore not a separate measurement: the production run over 1,459 items scored the same first 8 items identically, so the smoke's 5/8 is a prefix of the real scores file rather than a throwaway.",parsed kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl during this audit and printed the first eight records,"git working-tree copy, which is the scp-truncated one (exactly 204,800 B, 1,095 parseable records + 1 cut record, versus 1,459 items) - the truncation is at the END, so kn00000-kn00007 are intact","the one low-margin item (kn00002, margin 0.0966, probs 0.452 vs 0.548) is a genuine near-tie; the three wrong items all have margin 1.000, i.e. the model was confidently wrong, which is the more interesting fact",HOLDS,HIGH - every field of all eight records reproduced from the surviving scores file,MEDIUM - it is the validation of the WMDP knowledge labels the whole kd/HP-KR attribution rests on,inline python over kd/run/knowledge/scores.jsonl (pasted in the note),"This RESOLVES a Phase-1 INFERRED note about which 8 records the smoke used: it is the first eight by item_id, kn00000-kn00007, and they survive in the (truncated) committed scores file. Nothing about the smoke is in an owner document ('5/8' in kd/docs/FINDINGS.md is an unrelated table cell). The substantive point worth recording: the model is CONFIDENTLY wrong on 3 of 8 WMDP items (margin 1.000 each), which bears directly on how the 'knows' label in the HP-KR confound is constructed.",W6G-session
S-28,"The accidental 70B download was 56.64 GB, not the 40.22 GB the ledger records; the 40.22 was measured mid-download and retracted in the same session, and F-24 was never corrected.",40.22 GB (mid-download) vs 56.64 GB (final),b035ccb3:4319,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-24 (line ~428); docs/OPEN_DECISIONS.md line 175; lab ~/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--meta-llama--Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct; audit/claims/F-24.md (batch W5C),F-24 body text; OPEN_DECISIONS section C 'Corrections I made to my own earlier statements',F-24 still reads 'writing 40.22 GB into ~/.cache/huggingface' and its caveat still reads 'the 40 GB of weight blobs are still on disk pending an approved delete'. Neither has been corrected.,no - the ledger keeps the retracted figure,"neither figure is re-measurable: the lab's Llama-3.3-70B cache is now blobs 7 files / 0.02 GB, snapshots 15 files / 0 GB, refs 1 file. C: has 17.06 GB free of 930 GB. The blobs were deleted. BUT the correction IS recorded in a document the claim does not mention: docs/OPEN_DECISIONS.md line 175, 'the stale blobs were 40 GB | 56.6 GB - I quoted a figure measured mid-download, three times'.",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1 (cache walk on the lab); grep of every owner document for '56.64' and '56.6 GB',lab live state 2026-09-23; ledger as committed at d280d23,"this claim duplicates an already-checked ledger claim - audit/phase2/claims_batch_W5C-ledger.csv row F-24 - which reached the same conclusion (PARTLY HOLDS, both figures NO RAW DATA today)",PARTLY HOLDS,"HIGH that F-24 keeps the retracted number and that the correction exists in OPEN_DECISIONS; MEDIUM on which figure is physically right, since neither can be re-measured","LOW - engineering, no scientific result depends on it",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_forensics.ps1,"DUPLICATE of the already-checked F-24 (batch W5C-ledger, audit/claims/F-24.md), which additionally found that (a) the buggy version of smoke_multiturn.py is preserved nowhere, (b) '~45 GB free' appears in no transcript line, and (c) F-24's line reference 2_activations_ndif.py:330 is stale. The one thing S-28 adds and gets wrong: 'never corrected' is true of F-24 itself but not of the project's documents - docs/OPEN_DECISIONS.md section C records the 40 -> 56.6 GB correction, alongside two further corrections about the same incident (the delete silently did nothing; the >1MB filter deleted tokenizer.json).",W6G-session
S-30,The F-86 mean-of-directions margin over its matched comparator is smaller than the comparator's own subsampling spread; the audit script printed that verdict in one line and the ledger did not carry it.,margin over pooled_lodo_full +0.0284; spread of the matched draw alone 0.0824; verdict 'the margin is INSIDE the subsampling spread of its own comparator',b035ccb3:12414,"audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json (lab copy, in audit cache); kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-86","mean_of_directions, pooled_lodo_full, pooled_lodo_match_draws (20 values)","mean_of_directions = 0.8828295183, pooled_lodo_full = 0.8544753650, margin = +0.0284 (EXACT). pooled_lodo_match over 20 draws: mean 0.8344, min 0.7912, max 0.8736, range 0.0824 (EXACT), sd 0.0205.",yes,"margin / range = 0.344; margin / sd = 1.381. Other quoted context also reproduces: mean_over_sources 0.6763, median 0.7220, oriented_mean 0.7354, best_source_oracle 0.8967, pairs below 0.5 = 21 of 110, margin vs mean_over_sources = +0.2065.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-30, recomputing every statistic from the stored draws","run-premise is lab-only (RF-10); the copy used is audit/cache/labpc/run-premise/audit/audit_L40_s42.json, copied 2026-09-22/23 and not part of the RF-13 rewrite (run-premise had 7 files rewritten, all in falsify/)","one layer (40), one seed (42), one probe (paper), budget 666, 20 draws - exactly the caveats F-86 itself lists",HOLDS,HIGH - every statistic recomputed from the stored 20 draws,HIGH - F-86 is one of the project's headline positive results ('mean of directions beats joint training'),audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"THE LEDGER GAP IS REAL. F-86 states the +0.028 margin over pooled_lodo_full and its caveat (1) explicitly defends that comparison ('the fair comparison is against pooled_full (0.8545), which it still beats by +0.028'), while caveat (3) says 'no dataset-level bootstrap on the mean-of-directions number yet'. Neither mentions that the row-budget-matched pooled probe ranges over 0.0824 across 20 subsampling draws, i.e. about 2.9x the margin. The comparison is not exact - the 0.0824 is the spread of a DIFFERENT quantity (the budget-matched probe) while the margin is against the deterministic full-data probe - so the script's one-line verdict is a warning rather than a refutation. But the ledger should carry it: F-86's margin is 1.38 sd of the nearest available spread estimate, on a single layer and a single seed. Recommended: add the 0.0824 range to F-86's caveats.",W6G-session
S-31,"The 8B axes build printed a second geometry block for the s23 (score-2-or-3) bank; F-37 quotes only the first block, so the s23 geometry is in no document.","8B s23: cos(PC1,assistant) +0.739 at L16, min +0.524, median +0.688; PC1 40.4% of role variance, top-5 76.7%; deception basis 0.955 / 38.5%; unified 0.925 / 40.4%",b035ccb3:4339,"lab logs/scale_8b_axes.log (3,663 B, 2026-09-20 15:01:26); lab run-scale/8b/axes_8b.pt (12,594,790 B, 2026-09-20 15:01); kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-37","the two '=== report at layer 16 ===' blocks in the log; pca['all'].variance_ratio[16] and components[16,0] in the bank","the log holds TWO blocks. Block 1 (all bank): cos +0.732, min +0.514, median +0.701, PC1 39.6%, top-5 77.4%, deception 0.921/36.0%, sycophancy 0.983/47.8%, unified 0.908/39.6%, anchor 0.949. Block 2 (s23 bank): cos +0.739, min +0.524, median +0.688, PC1 40.4%, top-5 76.7%, deception 0.955/38.5%, sycophancy 0.983/47.6%, unified 0.925/40.4%, anchor 0.931. F-37's 8B column is block 1 throughout (0.732 / 0.514 / 0.701 / 39.6% / 77.4% / 0.949 / 0.921 / 0.983 / 0.908).",yes - F-37 quotes only block 1,"recomputed from run-scale/8b/axes_8b.pt: 26 roles, L16 PC1 = 40.4092%, top-5 = 76.7206%, cos(PC1,assistant) L16 = +0.7395, across 32 layers min +0.5244 median +0.6917; deception n=16 cos 0.955 var 38.5%; sycophancy n=11 0.983 var 47.6%; unified n=26 0.925 var 40.4%; assistant norm 0.998, deception 1.016, sycophancy 1.920, unified 1.201; vectors_dir = run-scale/8b/vectors_s23. So the FILE ON DISK IS THE s23 BUILD.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py, run read-only on the lab",log and bank both 2026-09-20 15:01; not touched by RF-13,"the s23 bank is the cleaner one on the contrast alignment (deception 0.955 vs 0.921) and the more concentrated one (PC1 40.4% vs 39.6%), so the choice of block changes the sign of the 'is the 8B cleaner?' comparison in two rows of F-37",HOLDS,HIGH - both blocks read from the log and the surviving block recomputed from the bank,MEDIUM-HIGH - it bears on F-37's cross-scale geometry table,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_lab_geom.py; W6G_lab_logs2.ps1,"A PROVENANCE PROBLEM THE CLAIM DOES NOT STATE. Both blocks end 'wrote C:/Users/user4/expLB/run-scale/8b/axes_8b.pt' - the same path. The s23 build therefore OVERWROTE the all build, and the surviving file is the s23 one (vectors_dir = vectors_s23). So F-37's entire 8B column describes a bank that no longer exists as a file and can only be reproduced from the log. Anything downstream that loaded axes_8b.pt (the 8B crossgen matrices, and hence F-63's 8B rung) used the s23 bank, not the bank F-37 describes. Worth a look by whoever owns the scale rungs; it is the same class of problem as RF-16.",W6G-session
S-32,"The kd bank's largest dataset-level effect at layer 40 mean pooling - paper probe, pc:unified@2 minus random@2, +0.2861 with 79 of 90 pairs won and a dataset 95% CI of [+0.147, +0.427] - fell just short of significance at q_BH 0.067 and is recorded nowhere.","+0.2861, 79/90 pairs, CI [+0.147,+0.427], q_BH 0.067, not significant; lr_reg10 +0.2837; mms +0.2647",b035ccb3:4614,"run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd/significance.json - git working tree (4,032 tests, mtime 2026-09-20 03:39:51) AND audit/cache/labpc/... (6,300 tests, mtime 2026-09-22 16:01:20)","tests filtered to layer 40, pooling mean; fields diff, pairs_won, dataset_ci95, dataset_q_bh, significant_datasets, block","git copy (4,032 tests, 96 at L40/mean): paper pc:unified@2 - random@2 diff +0.2861, pairs_won 79, CI [+0.147,+0.427], q_BH 0.067, sig=False, block=9; lr_reg10 +0.2837 (76 won) q 0.067; mms +0.2647 (74 won) q 0.088. Every quoted value EXACT. Total clearing the dataset bootstrap: 6 of 4,032.","yes, against the version the session read","THE VERDICT HAS SINCE FLIPPED. The lab copy (rewritten in the RF-13 boot wave, 2026-09-22 16:01:20) has 6,300 tests and 150 at L40/mean; the SAME test now reads diff +0.2861, pairs_won 79, CI [+0.147,+0.427] - identical raw statistics - but q_BH = 0.050 and significant_datasets = True. lr_reg10 likewise +0.2837 q 0.050 sig=True; mms +0.2647 q 0.052 sig=False. Tests clearing the bootstrap: 65 of 6,300, up from 6 of 4,032.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-32, reading both copies and filtering on (layer, pooling)","BOTH - the 09-20 git copy (4,032-test BH family) and the 09-22 lab copy (6,300-test family). This is RF-13/RF-14 in action: the guard bug re-ran the chain, the BH family grew, and the q-values moved.","block=9 means the 10-dataset block (90 pairs) in the kd11 era, NOT 9 datasets; the same comparison in block=10 (110 pairs) reads +0.2038 with q 0.372 in the old family - a third of the effect, nowhere near significance. So the headline is specific to the 10-dataset block.",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH - both file versions read directly; the raw statistics are identical and only the BH q differs,"HIGH - it is a worked example of the RF-13/RF-14 q-value instability, on the project's largest measured effect",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"THE MOST CONSEQUENTIAL FINDING IN THIS BATCH. The claim's numbers are exact for the version the session read, but 'not significant, q 0.067' is now 'significant, q 0.050' in the regenerated file, purely because the BH family grew from 4,032 to 6,300 tests. Nothing about the data changed - diff, pairs won and the dataset CI are byte-identical. Anyone quoting this effect must say which family the q was corrected over. The count of tests clearing the dataset bootstrap went 6/4,032 -> 65/6,300, so this is not an isolated cell. Also note the TRAP: block='9' here is the TEN-dataset block (90 pairs); the eleven-dataset block reads +0.2038, q 0.372.",W6G-session
S-33,F-61's paper16-vs-kd bank comparison is not like-for-like because the paper16 side is 109 transfer pairs against a raw baseline of 0.6800 while the kd side is 110 pairs against 0.6623.,paper16: raw 0.6800 over 109 pairs; axes -0.0312; random -0.0633; length -0.1140. kd: raw 0.6623 over 110 pairs,b035ccb3:5219,"run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json (git working tree AND lab, md5 d7616aa50814267e38bd38931e25a6a0 - identical); run-crossgen/kd11/banks/kd/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json; kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-61","results[].auroc off-diagonal means, probe=paper, over the 11 datasets","THE NUMBERS DO NOT REPRODUCE. Today the kd11 ROOT matrix (which IS the paper16 side: bank_name=paper16, bank=axes_vectors_s3_fp32.pt) gives raw off-diagonal 0.6623 over 110 pairs, with 0 NaN and 0 null cells. Not 0.6800 over 109. The other quoted deltas also differ: axes -0.0215 (not -0.0312), random -0.0773 (not -0.0633), length -0.1068 (not -0.1140).",no,"the current paper16 side is raw 0.6623 / 110 pairs and pc:unified 0.6715, so pc:unified - raw = +0.0093. The kd bank store holds no raw block at all (only pc:*/axes features), so its delta must borrow the ROOT baseline: kd pc:unified 0.7380 - 0.6623 = +0.0757. BOTH SIDES THEREFORE USE THE SAME BASELINE, 0.6623 over 110 pairs, and the like-for-like objection does not apply to the current data.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-33 - off-diagonal means recomputed cell by cell from the stored matrices, for git, lab-cache and the commit blob; plus a run of the owner's own kd/scripts/paper_comparison.py logic","git working tree == lab (md5 identical, lab mtime 2026-09-19 20:12) == the blob committed at 3dfdb67 (numerically identical, md5 differs only in encoding). The 109-pair/0.6800 version exists in NO copy I can find - git, lab or audit cache.","all 110 off-diagonal cells are populated in every surviving copy, so a 109-pair reading requires a matrix with one cell missing - i.e. an incomplete build that has since been overwritten",DOES NOT HOLD,HIGH that the current files give 0.6623/110 on both sides; HIGH that the 0.6800/109 version is not recoverable,HIGH - it changes F-61's headline,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"THIS OVERTURNS THE CLAIM AND EXPOSES A LEDGER PROBLEM INSTEAD. F-61 states 'paper16 +0.006 vs kd +0.076 - a twelvefold difference'. The +0.006 reproduces ONLY from the superseded 109-pair matrix (0.6861 - 0.6800 = +0.0061); the +0.076 reproduces from the CURRENT files (0.7380 - 0.6623 = +0.0757). So F-61's twelvefold comparison mixes two versions of the same store. On the current files the comparison is +0.0093 vs +0.0757, about eightfold. The likely cause of the version change is the HP-KR top-up committed at e9969af (2026-09-21 10:55, 'HP-KR top-up into passA and passC'), which changed the harm-pressure rows the matrix is built from. RECOMMENDED: recompute F-61's headline from the current matrices and state the date of the store.  [PHASE 4 2026-09-23] PHASE 4 AMENDMENT - RESOLVES AUDIT SELF-CORRECTION #6. That correction said two candidate explanations for F-61's '+0.006' both fit and 'the audit cannot separate them', because the 'raw 0.6800 over 109 pairs' reading survives 'in no copy'. It survives in no copy because NO FILE EVER HELD IT: it was manufactured at read time by a script bug. kd/scripts/paper_comparison.py originally took its axis labels from d['rows'] / d['columns'], which are human captions ('trained on (80% split)', 22 chars), not label lists - so zip iterated CHARACTERS and the diagonal test compared single letters, leaving most in-distribution cells in the 'off-diagonal' mean. Lead reproduced both code paths on run-crossgen/kd11/matrices/mean_L40_s42.json: fixed = 110 pairs / raw 0.6623 / pc:unified +0.0093; buggy = 109 pairs / raw 0.6800 / +0.0061. F-61's headline '+0.006' is the bug artifact; like-for-like is +0.0093 and the ratio is 8.1x, not twelvefold. The bug is already fixed in the committed script.",W6G-session
S-34,"A pre-patch run of response_lengths.py printed p50 = p90 = p99 = max = 0 for every rung because it read the wrong record field; it was fixed minutes before F-33's table was produced, and the units are characters, not tokens.","all percentiles 0 for 3B, 8B and 70B before the patch; after the patch 70B run-paper16/responses 1,400 rows, chars p50=1,480 p90=2,542 p99=2,825 max=3,059",b035ccb3:4746,"run-paper16/responses/*.jsonl (26 files, git working tree) and the identical lab copies in audit/cache/labpc/; scale/scripts/response_lengths.py; kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-33",record keys; len() of the last assistant turn in record['conversation'],"F-33's 70B row reads p50 1,480 / p90 2,542 / p99 2,825 / max 3,059. Recomputed from the 26 rollout files: 1,400 rows, p50=1,480 p90=2,542 p99=2,825 max=3,059 - EXACT, and 0 rows over 12,000 chars.",yes,"the bug is reproduced exactly. The records carry keys ['conversation','label','prompt_index','question','question_index','system_prompt'] - there is NO 'response' field. Reading d.get('response','') gives p50=0 p90=0 p99=0 max=0 for every file, which is precisely what the pre-patch run printed for all three rungs. The current script reads d['conversation'] and takes the last assistant turn, which gives the F-33 numbers.",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-34 plus an inline reimplementation of both the fixed and the buggy field access,"git working tree and the audit's lab cache give identical results; scale/scripts/response_lengths.py has ONE commit (3dfdb67), so the buggy version was never committed",the same computation on the lab cache copy of the same 26 files gives the identical percentiles,HOLDS,HIGH - the fixed numbers reproduce to the digit and the bug reproduces exactly by changing one field name,"MEDIUM - F-33's conclusion ('rollout length is not a rung-dependent confound') depends on this table being right, and it is",audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"UNITS CONFIRMED: characters. scale/scripts/response_lengths.py prints 'chars' and computes len(text); its 12,000-char threshold is annotated '~3k tokens of English'. F-33's table has no unit header, so a reader could take 1,480 for tokens - worth a one-word doc fix, especially as F-33's whole argument is about a 4,000-TOKEN NDIF ceiling and the rows are 1,480 CHARACTERS (roughly 370 tokens). The bug itself is in no document; the buggy version was never committed (the file has a single commit), so this transcript is the only record that the first reading was all zeros.",W6G-session
S-35,"Every per-layer scale table printed for the 3B, 8B and 70B rungs carries a random-feature column - a per-layer random-direction baseline - that no F-entry quotes.",70B k=3 mean L0: raw 0.5661 axes 0.4908 pc:dec 0.5045 datapca 0.5159; scale_3b L12: raw 0.7985 axes 0.8106 pc:dec 0.8175 datapca 0.8039 random 0.4821,1ac8bb19:1016,"audit/cache/labpc/run-crossgen/scale_3b/matrices/mean_L*_s42.json and scale_8b/...; audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv (store scale_70b, 2,772 rows)","results[].{feature, probe, auroc} off-diagonal means, probe=paper, seed 42, mean pooling","scale_3b L12: raw 0.7985 axes 0.8106 pc:deception 0.8175 datapca 0.8039 random 0.4821 - EXACT. 70B k=3 mean L0: raw 0.5661 axes 0.4908 pc:deception 0.5045 datapca 0.5159 - EXACT, and its random reads 0.4718 (L40 random = 0.5043).",yes for the values; no for 'every table',"the random column exists in the MATRIX FILES for all three rungs and is recomputable everywhere. But the transcript table the claim cites (the 70B k=3 sweep) has NO random column - it prints raw/axes/pc:dec/datapca only. An earlier table in the same session does print random for all three rungs (3B, 8B and the 70B L40 row at 0.5043). So 'every printed table carries it' is false; 'every matrix file carries it' is true.","audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py S-35 (3B and 8B, recomputed cell by cell from the cached matrices) and a query over audit/phase2/layer_sensitivity.csv for the 70B","3B/8B matrices from the audit's lab cache, bank_name paper16_3b / paper16_8b, k=3, 5 datasets, seed 42; the 70B rows come from layer_sensitivity.csv, store scale_70b, bank field 'axes_vectors_s3.pt', k=3, 5 datasets","the random baseline sits at 0.445-0.557 for the 3B, 0.462-0.680 for the 8B and 0.451-0.541 for the 70B; the 8B's 0.680 at L16 and 0.629 at L24 are the outliers and are NOT near 0.5",PARTLY HOLDS,HIGH for the values (recomputed from the matrices); HIGH that the cited 70B table has no random column,MEDIUM-HIGH,audit/scripts/claims/W6G_local.py,"RF-16 CAVEAT, which the claim does not carry: the scale_70b store is labelled bank_name=paper16_70b but its non-L40 layers were computed with the 36-persona KD bank, per RF-16. So the 70B random column above is a kd-bank sweep except at L40. The substantive point stands and is worth reporting: the random-direction baseline is NOT flat at 0.5. On the 8B it reaches 0.680 at L16 and 0.629 at L24 - layers where the real features read 0.80 and 0.76 - so a persona-coordinate margin measured at those layers is against a null that is itself 0.13-0.18 above chance. No F-entry quotes any of this; '0.4821', '0.4718' and '0.5043' have zero hits in any owner document.",W6G-session
D-001,Linear probes for lie detection often fail to transfer across datasets.,,draft p1 Abstract,"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","features=baseline, columns diagonal_mean / off_diagonal_mean, L20/L40/L44",see level2_value,yes,Re-derived: baseline (8192-d raw) diagonal_mean 0.9833 vs off_diagonal_mean 0.7320 at L40 -- a 0.251 in-distribution-to-transfer drop. L20 0.9787/0.6478; L44 0.9826/0.7159.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Supported by his own Table 3 source file. The gap is largest at L20 (0.331). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B23
D-002,Mahadik and Skapars (2026) ... They report better cross-dataset generalization at 3B and 8B.,,draft p1 Abstract,papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf,pp.1-5 contribution bullets and Section 5; cross-check kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-121,see level2_value,yes,"Checked against the cited paper itself: main model Llama-3.2-3B, 'additional replications on Llama 3-8B' (p.4), with the 8B evaluations in Appendices E and F. Contribution bullets on p.2 claim persona-PC projections 'generalize better across datasets than probes trained on the raw activations'.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Faithful to the source. TWO caveats a reader needs: (1) the paper's own words for 8B are 'auxiliary comparisons ... broadly supportive' (p.5), not a full replication; (2) this project's own three-rung ladder (F-121) finds the persona gain DECLINES with scale on both banks (+0.038 -> +0.015 -> -0.012 for 26 personas; +0.036 -> +0.019 -> +0.005 for 36), so 'better at 3B and 8B' does not extend to 70B. That is the paper's contribution and should be said here. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B23
D-005,"We extend the persona bank with ten roles that feign ignorance, are sincerely ignorant, or plainly assert what they know.",10,draft p1 Abstract,kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json,"groups.{knowledge_denial,sincere_ignorance,plain_assertion}.roles",see level2_value,yes,"Re-derived exactly from the persona bank: knowledge_denial 4 (pc_amnesiac_witness, pc_deniable_expert, pc_stonewaller, pc_feigned_novice) + sincere_ignorance 3 + plain_assertion 3 = 10. Consistent with the 12v13 contrast: 8+4=12 deceptive, 7+3+3=13 honest.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Exact, and the three-way split matches the abstract's three-way wording. Note DF-25: his KNOWLEDGE_CANDOUR_PERSONAS merges sincere_ignorance and plain_assertion into one arm, which is the split the owner kept apart to remove a wording confound. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B23
D-007,"The benchmark's own probes score 0.50 and 0.26 there, and its upper bound, trained on privileged labels, 0.95.",0.50; 0.26; 0.95,draft p1 Abstract,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,"Table 6 p.54 / Table 7 p.55 / Table 8 p.56, row 'Llama 3.3 70B', column HP-KR",see level2_value,yes,"All three re-derived from the Liars' Bench paper, Llama-3.3-70B / HP-KR: Mean Probe BA@1%FPR 0.50 (Table 6 p.54), Follow-Up Probe BA@1%FPR 0.26 (Table 7 p.55), Upper-Bound Probe BA 0.95 (Table 8 p.56). Exact.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Two scope conditions the sentence omits. (1) These are the Llama-3.3-70B rows; the cross-model averages are 0.50 / 0.42 / 0.72, so 0.26 in particular is model-specific. (2) The 0.95 upper bound is NOT a 1%-FPR operating point -- Table 8's FPR row gives 0.08 on HP-KR for Llama-70B, and the Follow-Up Probe's 0.26 carries a realised FPR of 0.84. Both thresholds are calibrated on alpaca, not on the evaluation set. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B23
D-011,"A threshold calibrated on benign chat still does not transfer to every dataset, which leaves calibration as the open problem.",,draft p1 Abstract,"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","threshold_source=control, specificity column; FPR = 1 - specificity",see level2_value,yes,"Re-derived and strengthened. With the threshold calibrated to 1% FPR on alpaca, 23 of the 90 (arm x dataset x layer) cells exceed 1% realised FPR on the evaluation set; 67 sit at or below it. The failures are concentrated, not diffuse: knowledge-denial axis 88.3% on HP-KR and 35.6% on RepE at L20 (6.5% at L40, 4.7% at L44), and instruct_dishonesty runs 5-15% for every arm at every layer.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"The claim holds and is understated. This is the same defect the draft levels at Liars' Bench (Follow-Up Probe 0.37 recall at 84% FPR) and it is present in the draft's own headline arm at L20. Quote the realised FPRs. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B23
D-086,"Published contrast (8 v 7), zero-shot: AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.148 0.593 0.589; BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.500 0.500 0.500",0.148 0.593 0.589 | 0.500 0.500 0.500,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","arm='deception axis (8v7)', dataset=harm_refusal_knowledge_report__plain, threshold_source=control",see level2_value,yes,AUROC 0.1483 / 0.5926 / 0.5895 -> 0.148 / 0.593 / 0.589. BA 0.5000 at all three. Exact.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"BA is exactly 0.500 because the arm never fires: recall 0.0000, specificity 1.0 at all three layers. A 0.500 that means 'no detections' is worth distinguishing from a 0.500 that means 'chance'. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-087,"Knowledge-denial contrast (4 v 6), zero-shot: AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.890 0.919 0.908; BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.533 0.910 0.757",0.890 0.919 0.908 | 0.533 0.910 0.757,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","arm='knowledge-denial axis (4v6)', dataset=HP-KR, threshold_source=control, cols balacc/specificity/recall",see level2_value,yes,AUROC 0.8899 / 0.9185 / 0.9077 -> 0.890 / 0.919 / 0.908 EXACT. BA 0.5331 / 0.9102 / 0.7571 -> 0.533 / 0.910 / 0.757 EXACT.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"All six values exact. Re-derived operating point: the threshold is fitted on Alpaca, so the realised FPR on HP-KR is 88.35% at L20 (specificity 0.1165, recall 0.9496), 6.45% at L40, 4.70% at L44. REVISED 2026-09-24 after Level 1 -- an earlier reading of mine reduced this to PARTLY for an undisclosed operating point. **The draft discloses it**: the Figure 3 caption says 'At layer 20 its threshold falls inside HP-KR and flags most honest answers too', which is the 88% FPR in words. The L40 headline 0.910 stands, at 6.5% realised FPR. Worth quantifying in the text, but it is not a hidden defect. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-088,"Extended contrast (12 v 13), zero-shot: AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.882 0.912 0.894; BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.500 0.500 0.500",0.882 0.912 0.894 | 0.500 0.500 0.500,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","arm='extended axis (12v13)', dataset=HP-KR, threshold_source=control",see level2_value,yes,AUROC 0.8816 / 0.9124 / 0.8936 -> 0.882 / 0.912 / 0.894. BA 0.5000 at all three. Exact.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Same never-fires pattern as D-086: recall 0.0000, specificity 1.0. An arm with AUROC 0.912 and BA 0.500 is a ranking success and a calibration failure; that contrast is the paper's own point (D-011) and should be drawn here explicitly. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-089,"Base probe (trained on RepE, same pipeline): AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.109 0.936 0.828; BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.500 0.500 0.500",0.109 0.936 0.828 | 0.500 0.500 0.500,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv and origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/matrix_baseline.csv","arm='base probe (RepE-trained)', dataset=HP-KR, control; vs matrix_baseline row repe_honesty col HP-KR",see level2_value,yes,AUROC 0.1090 / 0.9358 / 0.8283 -> 0.109 / 0.936 / 0.828. BA 0.5000 at all three. Exact.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Reproduces from zero_shot_operating.csv. NOTE a second, different base-probe number exists in the same result directory: matrix_baseline.csv[repe_honesty -> HP-KR] reads 0.3808 / 0.9281 / 0.8803. At L20 the two disagree sharply (0.109 vs 0.381). Table 2 uses the operating file, so the claim matches -- but the draft should say which base probe it means, because the matrix version does not show the L20 inversion nearly as starkly. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-090,"LB Mean Probe (reported, LB Tables 6-8): AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.12 (one layer); BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.50",0.12 (one layer) | 0.50,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,"Table 6 p.54, AUROC and BALANCED ACCURACY AT 1% FPR blocks, row 'Llama 3.3 70B', col HP-KR",see level2_value,yes,"Liars' Bench Table 6 p.54, Llama-3.3-70B, HP-KR: AUROC 0.12, BA@1%FPR 0.50. Exact.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Correctly attributed and correctly transcribed. Recall is 0.00 -- the probe never fires on HP-KR, so 0.50 is the no-detection floor, not chance-level discrimination. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-091,LB Follow-Up Probe (reported): AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.14 (one layer); BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.26,0.14 (one layer) | 0.26,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,"Table 7 p.55, AUROC / BA@1%FPR / FPR AT 1% FPR blocks, row 'Llama 3.3 70B', col HP-KR",see level2_value,yes,"Liars' Bench Table 7 p.55, Llama-3.3-70B, HP-KR: AUROC 0.14, BA@1%FPR 0.26. Exact.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Exact. The FPR block on the same page gives 0.84 for this cell -- the 0.26 balanced accuracy is produced at an 84% false-positive rate, which independently confirms DF-13. Quote the FPR whenever this number is used. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-092,"LB Upper-Bound Probe (reported; privileged, trained incl. HP-KR): AUROC L20/L40/L44 = 0.97 (one layer); BA@1%FPR L20/L40/L44 = 0.95",0.97 (one layer) | 0.95,draft p8 Table 2 (Detection on HP-KR),papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,"Table 8 p.56, BALANCED ACCURACY / AUROC / FPR blocks, row 'Llama 3.3 70B', col HP-KR",see level2_value,yes,"Liars' Bench Table 8 p.56, Llama-3.3-70B, HP-KR: AUROC 0.97, BA 0.95. Both exact.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"The transcription is exact and correctly attributed; the reduction is for a caveat the draft does not carry. Liars' Bench Table 8's first block is headed 'BALANCED ACCURACY' with no 'AT 1% FPR' qualifier (Tables 6 and 7 have it), and its own FPR block gives 0.08 for this cell. So the privileged upper bound operates at 8% FPR while the arms compared against it are held to 1% -- the comparison is not like-for-like, and that is a property of the benchmark's table rather than of this transcription. Any 'within 0.03 of the upper bound' statement (DF-26) inherits it. One line noting the upper bound's operating point would settle it. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B41
D-109,Probe on raw activations (8192-d): all six L20/L40/L44 = 0.648 0.732 0.716; excl. HP-KR L20/L40/L44 = 0.728 0.758 0.730,0.648 0.732 0.716 | 0.728 0.758 0.730,draft p9 Table 3 (mean off-diagonal AUROC),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","features=baseline, off_diagonal_mean and off_diagonal_excl_hpkr",see level2_value,yes,summary.csv features=baseline (dim 8192): all-six | excl-HP-KR at L20/L40/L44 = 0.648 0.732 0.716 | 0.728 0.758 0.730 -- EXACT,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"All six values reproduce exactly. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B42
D-110,"Published contrast, 8 v 7 (1-d): all six L20/L40/L44 = 0.651 0.832 0.826; excl. HP-KR L20/L40/L44 = 0.919 0.880 0.873",0.651 0.832 0.826 | 0.919 0.880 0.873,draft p9 Table 3 (mean off-diagonal AUROC),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","features=axis1, off_diagonal_mean and off_diagonal_excl_hpkr",see level2_value,yes,summary.csv features=axis1 (dim 1): all-six | excl-HP-KR at L20/L40/L44 = 0.651 0.832 0.826 | 0.919 0.880 0.873 -- EXACT,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"All six values reproduce exactly. A dim=1 arm: its trained off-diagonal EQUALS the zero-shot AUROC up to sign (verified here -- every cell in a test column is identical across training rows). REVISED 2026-09-24 after Level 1: this is NOT an undisclosed framing problem. The draft states the identity explicitly in section 3.4 -- 'A probe on a single feature can learn only a sign and a scale. Whenever every training set agrees on the sign, its AUROC on a test set therefore equals the zero-shot AUROC, and it has no training set to overfit' -- Table 3's own caption says 'The 1-d rows are persona contrasts, a probe on one feature', and the Contributions call the arm 'the zero-shot extended contrast'. DF-93's second half does not bite either: intervals are '95% stratified bootstrap intervals over examples (1,000 resamples)', never over the 30 matrix cells. The L20 value is depressed by a sign flip: the HP-KR TRAINING row of matrix_axis1.csv is exactly 1-x of every other row (verified cell by cell, diff 0.00000), row mean 0.0806 against 0.750-0.806 for the other five. Sign-corrected, the L20 off-diagonal is 0.7909 -- precisely the 0.791 the draft prints in Table 6's Mean row for the SAME arm at the SAME layer. REVISED after Level 1: the draft DISCLOSES this mechanism in section 4 with the matching worked example -- 'the inverted ranking on HP-KR carries into every test set (for instance CG falls from 0.940 to 0.060)' -- and 0.940/0.060 is exactly the cell pair verified here. The only thing left is presentational: Table 3 does not cross-reference that explanation, so a reader comparing Table 3 with Table 6 must find it in the prose. At L40/L44 no row inverts and the two tables agree to 4 dp. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B42
