D-188,Mean: L20 = 0.791 0.866 0.904; L40 = 0.832 0.912 0.916; L44 = 0.826 0.900 0.903,0.791 0.866 0.904 | 0.832 0.912 0.916 | 0.826 0.900 0.903,"draft p17 Table 6 (zero-shot AUROC, 8v7 / 4v6 / 12v13)","origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv and origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","mean of auroc_{axis,denial_axis,ext_axis} over 6 datasets vs summary.csv off_diagonal_mean",see level2_value,yes,Mean row reproduces exactly as the unweighted mean of the six zero-shot cells: L20 0.7909/0.8660/0.9041 -> 0.791 0.866 0.904; L40 0.8319/0.9115/0.9158 -> 0.832 0.912 0.916; L44 0.8260/0.9001/0.9034 -> 0.826 0.900 0.903.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"All nine values exact. Worth knowing when reading it beside Table 3: for the 8v7 arm at L20 this Mean reads 0.791 while Table 3 reads 0.651 for the same arm at the same layer. Both reproduce; they are different quantities -- Table 6's is the zero-shot mean, Table 3's the trained off-diagonal -- and the 0.140 gap is entirely one sign-flipped HP-KR training row (row mean 0.0806, exactly 1-x of the others). REVISED after Level 1: the draft explains this mechanism in section 4 with the matching example (CG 0.940 -> 0.060), so it is disclosed; an earlier reading of mine reduced this claim on the assumption it was not. What remains is presentational -- neither table cross-references the explanation. At L40/L44 the two agree to 4 dp. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B45
D-189,CG: raw/12v13 L20 = 0.663 0.969; L40 = 0.788 0.912; L44 = 0.757 0.859,0.663 0.969 | 0.788 0.912 | 0.757 0.859,"draft p17 Table 7 (per test set: raw vs 12v13, mean over 5 training sets)","origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/matrix_baseline.csv and origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv",matrix_baseline.csv column CG mean over 5 off-diagonal rows; zero_shot.csv auroc_ext_axis,see level2_value,yes,CG: raw / 12v13 at L20 | L40 | L44 = 0.663 0.969 | 0.7875->0.788 0.912 | 0.757 0.859 -- EXACT,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Both columns reproduce exactly. The two columns are different protocols -- 'raw' is a TRAINED 8192-d probe averaged over the 5 off-diagonal training rows, while '12v13' is a label-free 1-d direction whose trained column mean equals its zero-shot AUROC exactly at every dataset and every layer (verified: all 18 pairs identical). REVISED 2026-09-24 after Level 1: an earlier reading of mine reduced this to PARTLY on the ground that the table does not say so. It does -- section 3.4 states the dim=1 identity outright, Table 3's caption flags the 1-d rows, and the Contributions call the arm 'the zero-shot extended contrast'. Trained-vs-zero-shot is the stronger claim and the draft makes it. The L40 raw cell is an exact half-way value 0.7875; the draft's 0.788 is correct round-half-up. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B46
