D-232,Off-diagonal mean (as probe feature): L20/L40/L44 = 0.615 0.663 0.708,0.615 0.663 0.708,draft p19 Table 11 (sycophancy contrast 5v5),"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/matrix_syc_axis1.csv and origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv",features=syc_axis1 off_diagonal_mean; matrix_syc_axis1.csv per-row off-diagonal means,see level2_value,yes,Off-diagonal mean reproduces exactly as printed: syc_axis1 = 0.6153 / 0.6626 / 0.7078 -> 0.615 0.663 0.708.,"re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Values exact, verdict reduced because all three are sign artifacts. matrix_syc_axis1.csv has an inverted HP-KR training row at EVERY layer (row mean 0.1171 / 0.0638 / 0.0779). Sign-corrected the row means become 0.7429 / 0.8080 / 0.8485, each equal to the mean of the six zero-shot cells to 4 dp. So this row understates the arm by 0.128 / 0.145 / 0.141. **This falsifies DF-46's scope claim** that the inversion occurs 'only at L20, only in axis1, only in the HP-KR training row': a full sweep of the seven dim=1 arms finds inverted rows in axis1, syc_axis1, syc_pc1 and pc1 at L20; syc_axis1 and syc_pc1 at L40; and syc_axis1 at L44 -- 7 (arm, layer) cells, not 1. In every case the inverted row is HP-KR's. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B40
D-223,"It detects the instructed lies well, and it inverts on HP-KR at every layer (Table 11).",,draft p19 App F Sycophancy contrast,"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv","column auroc_syc_axis across all six datasets, L20/L40/L44",see level2_value,yes,"Both halves re-derived. 'Detects the instructed lies well': ID 0.923 / 0.948 / 0.949 and RepE 0.977 / 0.999 / 1.000. 'Inverts on HP-KR at every layer': 0.0429 / 0.1671 / 0.4804, all below 0.5.","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"Holds. Two refinements: the inversion weakens sharply with depth (0.457 below chance at L20, 0.020 at L44), and CG/IT are also near ceiling (0.983-0.999), so 'instructed lies' understates how broad the arm's success is -- it is everything except the two harm-pressure datasets. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B30
D-224,Its signal on the instructed datasets suggests that part of what any contrast of this kind reads is the shared register of role-played misbehaviour rather than deception itself.,,draft p19 App F Sycophancy contrast,"origin/paper:src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv","column auroc_syc_axis, all six datasets; cross-ref kd/docs/FINDINGS.md F-13, F-65, F-66",see level2_value,yes,"Interpretive claim, and the pattern it rests on is exactly as described: the sycophancy contrast scores 0.92-1.00 on the four role-played/instructed datasets and inverts on HP-KR (0.043-0.480) and is weak on HP-C (0.533-0.751).","re-derived from the collaborator's raw result files on origin/paper (git show, no checkout) and from the Liars' Bench PDF",origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level2.py,"The inference is sound and independently corroborated by this project: F-13's register diagnosis, and the cap bank's constructive confirmation (a capitulation axis reads 0.745 zero-shot on sycophancy_mt where the paper16 sycophancy axis reads 0.313, F-65/F-66). Cite that rather than leaving it as a suggestion -- it is the strongest form of the argument available. Note also DF-24: this contrast is not independently constructed (|cos| = 0.54 with the deception axis, fitted on the same bank object). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 2, 2026-09-24]",B30
