D-032,We release the code and results.,,draft p3 1 Contributions,git ls-tree -r origin/paper -- src/probes/deception-detection/paper/,"generated/numbers.tex, tab_*.tex, fig_*.pdf","RESOLVED 2026-09-24. Code released: paper/make_numbers.py (28,232 B) and paper/make_figures.py at 8fd071b2. Results released: paper/generated/ holds numbers.tex (1,162 generated \setV macros), eight tab_*.tex and five fig_*.pdf, beside the full persona_ood_ext_L* result CSVs.",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"REVISED UP TWICE. My first reading called this PARTLY because Figure 2's numbers and the cosine were in no committed result file -- they ARE, in paper/generated/numbers.tex, which is generated by make_numbers.py and committed. I had looked only in the result CSVs. **One real residual, and it is about re-RUNNING rather than reading:** make_figures.py's personas() needs pcs.EXTENDED_VECTORS_DIR, and those 36 vectors are not on the branch, so Figure 2 cannot be regenerated from the repository even though its numbers are published there. Shipping the vectors (small) would close it. The pipeline's own results tables are also absent (D-030/D-063) and are absent from the lab PC too. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B02
