D-014,"On Llama 3.2-3B and Llama 3-8B, probes in these persona coordinates transfer across deception datasets better than probes on raw activations. Among the directions they name for future work are larger ",,draft p1 1 Introduction,papers/Do Linear Probes Generalize Better in Persona Coordinates.pdf,"pp.1-5, contribution bullets and Section 5","faithful to the cited paper: main model Llama-3.2-3B, 'additional replications on Llama 3-8B' (p.4); contribution bullets claim persona-PC projections generalise better than raw activations (p.2)",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Accurate as a report of the cited work. Two things belong beside it: the paper's own words for 8B are 'auxiliary comparisons ... broadly supportive' (p.5), not a full replication; and this project's three-rung ladder finds the gain DECLINES with scale on both banks (F-121), so it does not extend to 70B. That is this paper's contribution and is worth saying here. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B03
