D-036,"Their protocol sets the decision threshold to a 1% false-positive rate on benign chat, and it is the protocol we follow.",1%,draft p3 2 Related work,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,"Tables 6-8 captions, 'at a 1% false-positive rate on alpaca'",Liars' Bench sets the threshold at 1% FPR on benign chat (Alpaca) -- CONFIRMED,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Accurate as a description of the benchmark's protocol, and it is the protocol followed. The realised FPR on the evaluation sets is another matter (D-011, section 1(b) of the chapter). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B04
D-037,Most methods perform near chance on the harm-pressure datasets. On HP-KR ... the benchmark reports recalls near zero for every method.,,draft p3 2 Related work,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,"Tables 6/7/8 p.54-56, RECALL blocks, row 'Llama 3.3 70B', col HP-KR",Mean Probe recall on HP-KR (Llama-3.3-70B) = 0.00 -- EXACT. But Follow-Up Probe recall = 0.37 and Upper-Bound Probe recall = 0.97 on the same cell.,partial,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"'Recalls near zero for EVERY method' is false as written. It holds for the Mean Probe (0.00) and for the cross-model averages of the non-privileged probes (0.00 and 0.12), but the Follow-Up Probe reads 0.37 on Llama-3.3-70B and the privileged upper bound 0.97. Confirms DF-13 at Level 1. The fix is one clause -- 'near zero for every non-privileged method on the cross-model average' -- and the Follow-Up Probe's 0.37 is bought at an 84% FPR, which makes the paper's point better than the overstatement does. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B04
