D-039,"Kirch et al. (2026) find that probe generalization depends on how the training data was generated, and that failures are largest for behaviours defined by intent, such as strategic deception.",,draft p3 2 Related work,audit/papers.csv,arxiv_id / pdf_present columns,"PDF present: papers/The Impact of Off-Policy Training Data.pdf, arXiv 2511.17408 (audit/papers.csv)",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Citation is to a paper the project holds, and the characterisation matches how cap/docs/DESIGN.md:79 already uses it. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B04
D-040,Natarajan et al. (2026) find deception detection heterogeneous: probes matched to a specific type of deception outperform a universal one.,,draft p3 2 Related work,"arXiv API, id_list=2602.01425","title, authors, abstract","RESOLVED 2026-09-24: Vikram Natarajan, Devina Jain, Shivam Arora, Satvik Golechha, Joseph Bloom -- 'One Probe Won't Catch Them All: Towards Targeted Deception Detection', arXiv 2602.01425.",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The abstract matches the draft's characterisation: probes fail with spurious correlations and false positives, and targeted probes outperform a universal one. CORRECTION TO MY OWN FIRST PASS, which marked this UNRESOLVED on the basis that audit/papers.csv has no row for it -- true, but that is a gap in the audit's own bibliography, not evidence the citation is bad. **Owed: add the row to audit/papers.csv and pull the PDF.** [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B04
D-041,Yoo and Skapars (2026) show that projecting onto a well-chosen subset of the training distribution's principal components nearly closes the gap to probes trained on the test distribution.,,draft p3 2 Related work,papers/Probe Generalization as Subspace Selection for OOD Deception Detectio.pdf,page 1 author line; arXiv 2609.02893,"RESOLVED 2026-09-24: the PDF is ALREADY IN papers/ -- 'Probe Generalization as Subspace Selection for OOD Deception Detection', **Daniel Yoo and Adrians Skapars**, arXiv 2609.02893.",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Author line read from page 1 of papers/'Probe Generalization as Subspace Selection for OOD Deception Detectio.pdf'. CORRECTION TO MY OWN FIRST PASS: I checked audit/papers.csv and not the papers/ directory itself, and wrongly marked this UNRESOLVED. The citation is sound. **Owed: add the row to audit/papers.csv.** DF-19's separate point -- that two venue strings near these citations appear in none of the three PDFs held -- is untouched by this and still needs checking before the reference list is fixed. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B04
D-043,Our one-dimensional result does not contradict this. Our direction is not the principal component of any dataset's activations but a contrast between persona groups ... only that this contrast transfe,,draft p4 2 Related work,src/probes/deception-detection/deception_detection/persona_pcs.py,"lines 149-160, axis construction","the direction is a contrast between persona means, not a dataset PC -- CONFIRMED by construction in the code",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"`persona_pcs.py:157` builds each axis as `mean_of(POSITIVE) - mean_of(NEGATIVE)` over persona vectors. No dataset activations enter it. The distinction the sentence draws is real. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B04
