D-069,"that happens only for the published contrast trained on HP-KR at layer 20, where the inverted ranking on HP-KR carries into every test set (for instance CG falls from 0.940 to 0.060).",0.940; 0.060,draft p6 4 Transfer matrix,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/matrix_axis1.csv and matrix_syc_axis1.csv, matrix_syc_pc1.csv, matrix_pc1.csv","per-training-row off-diagonal means, all three layers","'CG falls from 0.940 to 0.060' -- EXACT (0.9399 -> 0.0601, verified cell by cell). The scope word 'only' does not hold.",partial,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The worked example is exact and the disclosure is valuable -- this sentence is where the draft explains the L20 sign flip. But 'that happens ONLY for the published contrast trained on HP-KR at layer 20' is too narrow. Sweeping all seven dim=1 arms at the three published layers, training rows invert in SEVEN (arm, layer) cells: axis1, syc_axis1, syc_pc1 and pc1 at L20; syc_axis1 and syc_pc1 at L40; syc_axis1 at L44. It is always HP-KR's row. Among the three HEADLINE contrasts the sentence is correct -- denial_axis1 and ext_axis1 never invert -- but the sycophancy contrast is reported in Table 11 and Appendix F, and its printed off-diagonal row is depressed by this at all three layers (0.615/0.663/0.708 against 0.743/0.808/0.849 sign-corrected). Scope the sentence to the three contrasts, or note Table 11. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B13
D-079,"A response is a lie if the model denies knowing an answer it has been shown to know. Responses that affirm the knowledge, and denials where no knowledge was established, are honest ... Every lie in HP",,draft p7 5.1 HP-KR,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,HP-KR construction and Appendix D,HP-KR's label definition -- CONFIRMED against the benchmark,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Liars' Bench establishes in neutral contexts which questions the model knows; a response is a lie if the model denies knowing an answer it was shown to know. Its Appendix D confirms that cases where the model claims knowledge without a consistent belief are DISCARDED -- which is the structurally empty fourth cell the draft's own limitation (D-034) rests on. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B14
D-108,"But the two extra dimensions give a probe room to fit what distinguishes its training set, and that costs transfer. The one feature whose sign every dataset agrees on transfers best.",,draft p9 5.3 One direction vs subspace,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","features=ext_axis1 / ext_pc3, off_diagonal_mean and diagonal_mean","the 1-d contrast beats the 3-PC probe on transfer at all three layers on the extended bank: ext_axis1 - ext_pc3 = +0.220 (L20), +0.050 (L40), +0.023 (L44)",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The mechanism the sentence gives -- extra dimensions let a probe fit its training set -- is consistent with the diagonal/off-diagonal split: ext_pc3's diagonal is higher than ext_axis1's while its off-diagonal is lower. Note DF-21: for the PUBLISHED bank the direction reverses at L20 (pc3 0.679 > axis1 0.651), so the claim needs its bank named. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B15
D-119,At layers 40 and 44 the persona contrasts lead on all three metrics.,,draft p9 5.4 vs benchmark probe,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","dataset=""Average (Liars' Bench)"", threshold_source=control","at L40 and L44 every persona contrast leads the base probe on BA, recall and AUROC -- VERIFIED for all three arms at both layers",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"L40 base 0.626/0.281/0.778 against 8v7 0.675/0.382/0.798, 4v6 0.725/0.487/0.894, 12v13 0.694/0.413/0.899. L44 base 0.626/0.281/0.756 against 0.654/0.318/0.791, 0.683/0.395/0.880, 0.666/0.350/0.884. No exceptions. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B16
D-123,"On ranking, the persona contrasts lead at every layer.",,draft p10 5.4 vs benchmark probe,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","dataset=""Average (Liars' Bench)"", col auroc",on AUROC the persona contrasts lead at every layer -- VERIFIED,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"L20 base 0.697 against 0.750 / 0.863 / 0.887; L40 base 0.778 against 0.798 / 0.894 / 0.899; L44 base 0.756 against 0.791 / 0.880 / 0.884. True at all three, and it is the honest restriction of D-119, since at L20 the base probe leads on BA and recall. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B16
D-128,"We report layer 40 as our main depth. Three layers do not locate an optimum, and a layer between 20 and 40 may do better.",,draft p10 5.5 Depth,src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L36/summary.csv,"features=ext_axis1, off_diagonal_mean","'Three layers do not locate an optimum, and a layer between 20 and 40 may do better' -- CORRECT, and since vindicated",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The 16-layer sweep on this same branch puts `ext_axis1`'s optimum at L36 = 0.9275 against L40's 0.9158, and `denial_axis1` also peaks at 36 (F-117). The caveat was right and the paper should now say so rather than leave it hypothetical -- under-reporting your own best number invites the question of why (DF-79). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B17
D-152,A detector of denial wording would therefore score well on HP-KR without detecting deception. Our knowledge-denial contrast does not rule this out.,,draft p12 6 Limitations,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,the HP-KR lexical-baseline entries,"'a detector of denial wording would score well on HP-KR without detecting deception; our contrast does not rule this out' -- CORRECT, and understated",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"This project has since measured it: a label-free regex on denial phrasing alone reads 0.9125 AUROC (0.9597 for a second phrasing) on the 2,139 rows, at or above the draft's own 0.919 headline, and a length-only scorer reads 0.776. On those numbers the wording confound is not merely 'not ruled out' -- it is not currently distinguishable (DF-72). Quote the lexical baseline beside the headline. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B18
D-153,"The bank was designed for the cleaner test, a contrast between feigned and sincere ignorance in which both sides deny, and we have not run it.",,draft p12 6 Limitations,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,"F-03, F-115, F-116",'The bank was designed for the cleaner test ... and we have not run it' -- NO LONGER TRUE,partial,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"It has been run three times. F-03/F-72/F-76 on 2026-09-19; the row-leak contamination closed on 2026-09-23 (F-115); and the larger complementary control run for the first time the same day (F-116, 2,001 rows, 7.8x the text-matched slice). At the pre-registered layer the margin is +0.066, CI [-0.069, +0.189], P = 0.161; it inverts to -0.2545 at L20; and on the knowledge-matched control the axes sit BELOW chance while an ordinary probe reads 0.999 in-distribution. This was true when written and is false at submission (DF-76). Delete the promise and state the outcome -- it is a stronger paper with the negative result in it. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B18
D-154,At the level of the personas the signs are encouraging: sincere-ignorance personas sit with the honest cluster on the knowledge-denial axis (Figure 2). Whether the same holds for model responses is un,,draft p12 6 Limitations,LAB PC C:\Users\user4\expLB\run-kd\vectors_s3\*.pt,layer 40; group means on the unit denial axis,"RESOLVED on the lab PC, and it holds only in the weak sense. At L40 sincere ignorance reads **-0.0844** against feigned deniers **+2.9037**, so it is emphatically on the honest side of the deniers. But the honest *cluster* it is said to sit with reads **-0.9999** (published honest) and **-1.2274** (plain assertion).",partial,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Sincere ignorance is 0.92-1.14 away from the honest groups and 2.99 from the deniers, so 'sits with the honest cluster' overstates: it sits **between**, nearer the honest side. On an axis spanning 4.13, being 1.14 off the other honest group is 28% of the range -- and it is the group that shares the deniers' *wording*, which is exactly where a wording-sensitive axis would put it. **The draft's own hedge is the right one** ('whether the same holds for model responses is untested'), and it has since been answered: F-118's Gender-Secret run finds the direction **at chance where both classes deny**. Report the gap rather than the cluster. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B18
D-155,"We wrote the knowledge-denial personas after seeing the published contrast invert on HP-KR, so HP-KR measures a repair designed for it, not a blind test.",,draft p12 6 Limitations,kd/docs/DESIGN.md,the experiment's stated motivation,"'we wrote the knowledge-denial personas after seeing the published contrast invert on HP-KR, so HP-KR measures a repair designed for it, not a blind test' -- CORRECT",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Confirmed by this repository's own history: the kd/ experiment exists because every detector here inverts on harm-pressure-knowledge-report. Declaring it is the right call and it is the sentence a referee will look for. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B18
D-156,"The other datasets are the untargeted test. There the extended contrast matches or beats the published one at every layer. But at layer 20, with HP-KR excluded, its advantage over the published contra",,draft p12 6 Limitations,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/summary.csv","features=ext_axis1 / axis1, off_diagonal_excl_hpkr","'the extended contrast matches or beats the published one at every layer' on the other datasets -- VERIFIED on the excluding-HP-KR column: 0.909 vs 0.919 (L20), 0.917 vs 0.880 (L40), 0.905 vs 0.873 (L44)",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"CAREFUL: at L20 excluding HP-KR the extended contrast is BEHIND by 0.010 (0.909 against 0.919), which is what the sentence's own 'But at layer 20, with HP-KR excluded ...' clause goes on to concede. So the claim as completed is accurate; read without its continuation it would not be. F-117 generalises the concession from 3 layers to 16: the margin is within +/-0.06 everywhere and crosses zero five times (DF-81). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B18
D-159,"We study one model, three layers and one persona bank. We wrote the prompts from the published role descriptions ... The judge keeps only rollouts that stayed in character ... The re-extracted bank us",,draft p12 6 Scope,kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json,"subject_model, source_role_list","one model, three layers, one persona bank -- CORRECT and appropriately scoped",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"All three limitations hold. The judge-keeps-only-3 rule is confirmed at D-052 (69.4% kept). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B19
D-160,"Because our insider-trading scores exclude the reasoning scratchpad, comparisons with Liars' Bench's published numbers on that dataset are not like for like. Comparisons within our pipeline are exact.",,draft p13 6 Scope,draft section 6,cross-checked against the LB Mean Probe's scratchpad handling,"insider-trading scores exclude the reasoning scratchpad, so comparisons with Liars' Bench's published numbers on that dataset are not like for like -- CORRECT",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"An important and voluntary disclosure. 'Comparisons within our pipeline are exact' is right: every arm in these tables is scored on the same rows. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B19
D-158,"A probe trained on several datasets pooled is a stronger supervised baseline, and we do not compare against it.",,draft p12 6 Supervised baseline,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,the pooled-training entries,"'a probe trained on several datasets pooled is a stronger supervised baseline, and we do not compare against it' -- CORRECT, and this project has the number",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The honest pooled figure from this project's own work is +0.125 under leave-one-CLUSTER-out, 10 of 11 targets, five seeds, +/-0.035 -- not the larger figure that leaks. If the baseline is going to be named as missing, that is the number to name. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B20
D-161,"More model families. Liars' Bench also covers Mistral-Small-24B, Qwen-2.5-72B and Gemma-3-27B.",,draft p13 7 Future work,papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,Tables 6-8 model rows,"more model families: Mistral-Small-24B, Qwen-2.5-72B, Gemma-3-27B -- CONFIRMED",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"All three appear in Liars' Bench's Tables 6-8 alongside Llama-3.3-70B, so the future-work target is real and the data exists. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B21
D-162,Fine-tuned models. Soft-Trigger and Gender-Secret ... Whether coordinates built from role-play capture a lie that training instilled is open.,,draft p13 7 Future work,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,"F-115, F-116, F-118; DF-15","Soft-Trigger and Gender-Secret as fine-tuned model organisms -- CONFIRMED as a gap, but Gender-Secret is no longer open",partial,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"F-118 ran Gender-Secret through NDIF and found the knowledge-denial direction AT CHANCE where both classes deny (0.436-0.623) -- one of the three convergent wording-matched results. Cite it as a result, not as future work. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B21
D-163,"Wording-controlled contrasts. The contrast between feigned and sincere ignorance, tested on HP-KR's honest denials, would separate the lie from its wording.",,draft p13 7 Future work,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,"F-115, F-116, F-118; DF-15","wording-controlled contrasts, tested on HP-KR's honest denials -- SUPERSEDED",partial,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",PARTLY MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Same as D-153: run three times (F-03/F-72/F-76, F-115, F-116). This is the second place the draft promises it as future work (DF-76 flags p.12 and p.13). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B21
D-164,"Combining signals ... A persona-contrast score is a label-free white-box signal that could join such a combination. For detection, the top tenth of response tokens is a better read than the mean (Appe",,draft p13 7 Future work,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,"F-115, F-116, F-118; DF-15","'for detection, the top tenth of response tokens is a better read than the mean' -- TRUE against the mean, but the MAXIMUM beats both at L40",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Top-10% vs mean at L40: BA 0.737 vs 0.694, recall 0.531 vs 0.413 -- the claim holds. But the single maximum reads BA 0.750 and recall 0.548 at the same layer, ahead of top-10% on both (DF-15). If a best read is being recommended, it is the maximum at L40. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B21
D-165,Calibration. A contrast that ranks a dataset well still needs a threshold that holds on that dataset's prompts.,,draft p13 7 Future work,kd/docs/FINDINGS.md,"F-115, F-116, F-118; DF-15",'a contrast that ranks a dataset well still needs a threshold that holds on that dataset's prompts' -- CORRECT and well evidenced,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"This is the paper's most defensible forward-looking sentence. 23 of 90 (arm x dataset x layer) cells exceed 1% realised FPR when the threshold is Alpaca-fitted, worst 88.3%. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B21
