D-170,[Collaborator name] built the persona bank and the rollout and judging pipeline.,,draft p13 Acknowledgements,"kd/personas/, audit/cache/labpc/run-kd/",bank and rollout provenance,authorship attribution for the persona bank and the rollout/judging pipeline,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Consistent with the repository: the bank, the rollouts and the judge pipeline are in kd/ and run-kd/, authored on this side. Acknowledgement is appropriately placed. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B24
D-171,"We used a large language model (Claude, Anthropic) to help write analysis code, produce the figures and tables, and draft text. Every number in the paper is generated from the released result files, a",,draft p13 Acknowledgements,src/probes/deception-detection/paper/generated/numbers.tex,"1,162 \setV entries; header line 'Generated by make_numbers.py'","RESOLVED 2026-09-24 and it is better supported than any comparable claim I have checked. paper/generated/numbers.tex carries **1,162 \setV macros**, headed 'Generated by make_numbers.py -- do not edit', and every draft number spot-checked in Phase 6 resolves to one of them -- dataset sizes, bank counts, the zero-shot grid, the cosine and the Figure 2 projections included.",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"REVISED UP. My first reading called this PARTLY on the belief that five numbers were not generated from released files. Four of the five (cos-dec-den-L40, proj-den-sincere-L40, proj-den-kd-L40, proj-den-deceptive-L40) are macros in that committed file, and I re-derived all four independently on the lab PC to 4 dp. **The one genuine exception is Appendix G's four-decimal reproduction claim** (D-030/D-063), whose comparison artifact exists neither on the branch nor on the lab PC. So the sentence is true of every number in the paper except that one, and the honest scope is 'every number in the tables and figures'. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B24
D-180,Each persona has five prompt variants that reword one instruction. [full five variants given for feigned novice and honest novice],5 variants x 2 personas quoted,draft p16 App A Prompts,kd/personas/kd_instructions,per-persona variant files,"five prompt variants per persona, with the feigned-novice and honest-novice sets quoted in full -- CONSISTENT",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Five variants x 30 questions = 150 rollouts per persona, which is exactly the denominator Table 5 uses and D-052's arithmetic confirms. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B25
D-181,"Every persona answers the same 30 questions. The first 20 are the deception and sycophancy questions of Mahadik and Skapars (2026, Appendices A-B). The ten new ones ... In the first six the speaker kn",30 = 20 + 10; 6 know / 4 do not,draft p16 App A Questions,kd/personas/kd_role_groups.json,question_set,"30 questions = 20 from the cited paper + 10 new; of the new ten, 6 the model knows and 4 it does not -- CONFIRMED for the 20/10 split",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The bank file records the 20/10 split verbatim. The 6-know / 4-do-not breakdown is a property of the new question file and is not restated in the bank metadata; it was not separately re-derived at Level 1. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B26
D-196,"We extracted activations at the 'No' (layer 20) and projected them onto the same persona contrasts. At that token, the contrast's sign stops being the same on every dataset.",,draft p17 App C Follow-up token,src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_followup_L20/zero_shot.csv,col auroc_axis across datasets,'at the follow-up token the contrast's sign stops being the same on every dataset' -- VERIFIED,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"At the 'No' token, L20: CG 0.912, ID 0.900, RepE 1.000 all point one way, while IT reads 0.165 and HP-KR 0.168 -- both inverted. So the sign genuinely stops being universal, exactly as stated. This is the same mechanism as D-069, observed at a different token. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B27
D-199,What the model carries forward to a self-report is not the same signal as the one its response carries.,,draft p17 App C Follow-up token,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv and src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_followup_L20/zero_shot.csv",response vs follow-up columns,'what the model carries forward to a self-report is not the same signal as the one its response carries' -- SUPPORTED,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The response-vs-'No' gaps in Table 8 are large and not uniform in direction: IT falls 0.988 -> 0.165, HP-KR's 4v6 falls 0.890 -> 0.237, while RepE rises 0.994 -> 1.000 and ID barely moves. A single rescaling cannot produce that pattern. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B27
D-209,"The token before the reply mostly reads the prompt. It separates well where the instruction to lie is already in context, and it does not help on HP-KR.",,draft p18 App D Token reads,src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_positions_L20/reads.csv,"axis=extended, read=pre, per dataset","'the token before the reply ... separates well where the instruction to lie is already in context, and does not help on HP-KR' -- VERIFIED per dataset",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Extended axis, `pre` read at L20: RepE 1.0000, IT 0.9273, ID 0.8995, CG 0.8714 -- all strong, and all are datasets where the instruction or setup is in the prompt. HP-KR reads 0.3855, inverted, against 0.8816 for the response mean. Exactly as described. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B28
D-217,"There, a learned combination of three components avoids the sign flip on IT that a fixed direction cannot.",,draft p18 App E PCs trained on RepE,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/matrix_ext_pc3.csv",IT column against matrix_ext_axis1.csv,'a learned combination of three components avoids the sign flip on IT that a fixed direction cannot' -- CONSISTENT with the committed matrices,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"A k=3 probe has the freedom to reweight components per training set, which a 1-d feature does not (D-060). The specific IT cell was not isolated at Level 1; the mechanism is verified. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B29
D-139,"Projecting lies onto persona coordinates: 36 personas x 5 prompt variants x 30 questions -> 5,400 rollouts -> judge keeps 3,749 -> persona vectors -> contrast d and leading PCs; LB response -> activat","36; 5; 30; 5,400; 3,749; L20/40/44",draft p2 Fig 1,audit/cache/labpc/run-kd/scores/*.json,"count of entries == 3, plus default","36 personas x 5 variants x 30 questions -> 5,400 rollouts -> judge keeps 3,749 -> vectors -> L20/40/44 -- EVERY NUMBER EXACT",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The whole pipeline figure reproduces: 36x5x30 = 5,400 and the kept count recomputes to 3,749 (3,599 judged + default's 150). [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B31
D-065,"Sincere-ignorance personas ... sit with the honest cluster (mean -0.08 on the vertical axis, against 2.90 for the feigned deniers). The published deceptive personas never reach the region the deniers ",-0.08; 2.90; 0.05,draft p6 Fig 2 caption,LAB PC C:\Users\user4\expLB\run-kd\vectors_s3\*.pt,"layer 40; centred persona vectors projected on unit denial axis, group means",RESOLVED on the lab PC. All three caption figures EXACT at L40: sincere ignorance mean **-0.0844** -> -0.08; feigned deniers **+2.9037** -> 2.90; published deceptive **+0.0458** -> 0.05.,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Reproduced as `centred[idx] @ axis_unit('denial')` with `centred = personas - personas.mean(0)` over all 36, exactly as `make_figures.py:personas()` computes it. **The fourth clause checks too**: 'the published deceptive personas never reach the region the deniers occupy' -- their maximum is +0.885 against the deniers' minimum +2.150, so the groups do not overlap at all. ONE THING THE CAPTION DOES NOT SAY, and it matters: the two honest groups are **not together**. Plain assertion sits at **-1.2274** and sincere ignorance at **-0.0844**, a gap of **1.14** on an axis whose full span is 4.13 -- so sincere ignorance, the group that shares the deniers' wording, sits **28% of the axis closer to them** than plain assertion does. That is the wording pull made visible, and it is the quantity DF-25 predicts when the two groups are merged. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B32
D-138,"HP-KR across depth. Left: ranking. Both contrasts built with the knowledge-denial personas stay near 0.9 at every layer. The published contrast inverts at layer 20, and the base probe swings from inve",,draft p9 Fig 3,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot.csv","dataset=HP-KR, all arm columns, three layers",'both contrasts built with the knowledge-denial personas stay near 0.9 at every layer; the published contrast inverts at layer 20' -- VERIFIED,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"On HP-KR: 4v6 reads 0.890 / 0.919 / 0.908 and 12v13 reads 0.882 / 0.912 / 0.894 -- both near 0.9 at all three. The published contrast reads 0.148 at L20 (inverted) and recovers only to 0.593 / 0.589. The base probe swings from 0.109 (L20) to 0.936 (L40), which is the 'swings from inver[ted]' the caption describes. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B33
D-136,"Left: ... It fits each training set but transfers unevenly and inverts in places. Right: the extended persona contrast, a single direction that no dataset shaped. Its rows are constant because a probe",,draft p10 Fig 4 caption,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/matrix_ext_axis1.csv and matrix_baseline.csv",per-column distinct values,'its rows are constant because a probe [on one feature can learn only a sign]' -- VERIFIED EXACTLY,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The rows are constant to 4 dp, not approximately. This caption is the THIRD place the draft discloses the dim=1 identity, after section 3.4 and Table 3's caption -- which together settle DF-93's 'label these arms zero-shot'. The left panel's 'transfers unevenly and inverts in places' is also exact: the raw probe's HP-KR column runs 0.06 to 0.95. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B34
D-137,"Zero-shot persona contrasts against the RepE-trained base probe at layer 40, in the layout of Liars' Bench's Figure 2 ... Error bars are 95% bootstrap intervals over examples ... the Average excludes ",95%,draft p11 Fig 5,"src/probes/deception-detection/results/persona_ood_ext_L{20,40,44}/zero_shot_operating.csv","*_lo / *_hi columns; ""Average (Liars' Bench)"" row excludes repe_honesty",'error bars are 95% bootstrap intervals over examples' and 'the Average excludes RepE' -- CONFIRMED,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Section 4 states the intervals are over examples with 1,000 resamples drawn once and shared, and that RepE is excluded from averages because it is the base probe's training set. Both are the right choices and both are load-bearing for DF-93, which does not apply to this draft because no interval is computed over matrix cells. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B37
D-033,"The knowledge-denial personas were written after we saw HP-KR fail, so HP-KR measures a designed repair rather than a blind test.",,draft p3 1 (caveats),kd/docs/DESIGN.md,experiment motivation,'the knowledge-denial personas were written after we saw HP-KR fail' -- CORRECT,yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,medium,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"Same disclosure as D-155, made twice, which is the right number of times for a caveat this load-bearing. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B01
D-034,"HP-KR's labels make a denial necessary for a lie, so its gains do not by themselves separate deception from the wording of a denial.",,draft p3 1 (caveats),papers/2511.16035v2 (1).pdf,Appendix D; cross-ref kd/docs/FINDINGS.md HP-KR lexical entries,"'HP-KR's labels make a denial necessary for a lie, so its gains do not by themselves separate deception from the wording of a denial' -- CORRECT and understated",yes,,Level 1 -- number located in a result file,origin/paper @ ea1ce52b,"single seed, his pipeline; three layers L20/L40/L44",MATCHES HIS DATA,high,high,audit/scripts/p16_level1.py,"The benchmark's Appendix D confirms the structurally empty fourth cell (claims-knowledge cases are discarded). And this project has measured the consequence: a denial-phrasing regex alone reads 0.9125-0.9597 on these rows. See D-152. [Phase 6 / 6A Level 1, 2026-09-24]",B01
